#: content/about-tor/alt-design/contents.lr:section.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/alt-design/
msgid "Alternate Designs We Don't Do (Yet)"
msgstr "Alternativa lösningar som vi inte använder (ännu)"

#: content/about-tor/alt-design/contents.lr:section.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/alt-design/
msgid "Alternate Designs"
msgstr "Alternativa lösningar"

#: content/about-tor/alt-design/exit-blocking-sites/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/alt-design/exit-blocking-sites/
msgid ""
"While it may seem useful for relay operators to block websites by hostname, "
"Tor exit policies only support IP-based rules to prevent censorship and "
"abuse through DNS manipulation."
msgstr ""
"Även om det kan verka användbart att låta reläoperatörer blockera "
"webbplatser efter värdnamn stöder Tors utgångspolicyer endast IP-baserade "
"regler, för att förhindra censur och missbruk genom DNS-manipulation."

#: content/about-tor/alt-design/exit-blocking-sites/contents.lr:article.longer_title
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/alt-design/exit-blocking-sites/
msgid "Why Tor exit policies block IP addresses instead of domain names"
msgstr ""
"Varför Tors utgångspolicyer blockerar IP-adresser i stället för domännamn"

#: content/about-tor/alt-design/exit-blocking-sites/contents.lr:article.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/alt-design/exit-blocking-sites/
msgid "Exit policies should be able to block websites, not just IP addresses"
msgstr ""
"Utgångspolicyer borde kunna blockera webbplatser, inte bara IP-adresser"

#: content/about-tor/alt-design/exit-blocking-sites/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/alt-design/exit-blocking-sites/
msgid "First, users could still get around these blocks."
msgstr ""
"För det första skulle användare fortfarande kunna kringgå blockeringarna."

#: content/about-tor/alt-design/exit-blocking-sites/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/alt-design/exit-blocking-sites/
msgid ""
"For example, if a Tor operator blocks www1.slashdot.org, and then some "
"attacker poisons the Tor relay's DNS or otherwise changes that hostname to "
"resolve to the IP address for a major news site, then suddenly that Tor "
"relay is blocking the news site."
msgstr ""
"Om en Tor-operatör till exempel blockerar www1.slashdot.org och en angripare "
"sedan förgiftar Tor-reläets DNS eller på annat sätt får värdnamnet att peka "
"på IP-adressen till en stor nyhetswebbplats, börjar Tor-reläet plötsligt "
"blockera nyhetswebbplatsen."

#: content/about-tor/alt-design/exit-blocking-sites/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/alt-design/exit-blocking-sites/
msgid ""
"For example, they could request the IP address rather than the hostname when "
"they exit from the Tor network."
msgstr ""
"De skulle till exempel kunna begära IP-adressen i stället för värdnamnet när "
"de lämnar Tor-nätverket."

#: content/about-tor/alt-design/exit-blocking-sites/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/alt-design/exit-blocking-sites/
msgid ""
"It would be nice to let relay operators say things like `reject "
"www.slashdot.org` in their exit policies, rather than requiring them to "
"learn all the IP address space that could be covered by the site (and then "
"also blocking other sites at those IP addresses)."
msgstr ""
"Det vore praktiskt om reläoperatörer kunde skriva exempelvis `reject "
"www.slashdot.org` i sina utgångspolicyer, i stället för att behöva ta reda "
"på hela det IP-adressutrymme som webbplatsen kan använda (och samtidigt "
"blockera andra webbplatser på samma IP-adresser)."

#: content/about-tor/alt-design/exit-blocking-sites/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/alt-design/exit-blocking-sites/
msgid ""
"The second problem is that it would allow remote attackers to censor "
"arbitrary sites."
msgstr ""
"Det andra problemet är att detta skulle göra det möjligt för fjärrangripare "
"att censurera godtyckliga webbplatser."

#: content/about-tor/alt-design/exit-blocking-sites/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/alt-design/exit-blocking-sites/
msgid "There are two problems, though."
msgstr "Det finns dock två problem."

#: content/about-tor/alt-design/exit-blocking-sites/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/alt-design/exit-blocking-sites/
msgid ""
"This means operators would still need to learn all the IP addresses for the "
"destinations in question."
msgstr ""
"Det innebär att operatörerna ändå skulle behöva ta reda på alla IP-adresser "
"för de aktuella destinationerna."

#: content/about-tor/alt-design/exit-blocking-sites/contents.lr:tab.title
#: content/about-tor/alt-design/hide-list-of-exits/contents.lr:tab.title
#: content/about-tor/alt-design/let-the-network-pick-the-path/contents.lr:tab.title
#: content/contents.lr:nav_item.title https://support.torproject.org/
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/alt-design/exit-blocking-sites/
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/alt-design/hide-list-of-exits/
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/alt-design/let-the-network-pick-the-path/
msgid "About"
msgstr "Om"

#: content/about-tor/alt-design/hide-list-of-exits/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/alt-design/hide-list-of-exits/
msgid ""
"This article explains why it can't be hidden and how transparency benefits "
"both security and constructive dialogue with websites."
msgstr ""
"Artikeln förklarar varför listan inte kan döljas och hur öppenhet gynnar "
"både säkerheten och en konstruktiv dialog med webbplatser."

#: content/about-tor/alt-design/hide-list-of-exits/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/alt-design/hide-list-of-exits/
msgid "Tor's relay list is public by design."
msgstr "Tors relälista är avsiktligt offentlig."

#: content/about-tor/alt-design/hide-list-of-exits/contents.lr:article.longer_title
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/alt-design/hide-list-of-exits/
msgid "Why Tor's relay list is public and cannot be hidden"
msgstr "Varför Tors relälista är offentlig och inte kan döljas"

#: content/about-tor/alt-design/hide-list-of-exits/contents.lr:article.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/alt-design/hide-list-of-exits/
msgid ""
"You should hide the list of Tor relays, so people can't block the exits."
msgstr ""
"Ni borde dölja listan över Tor-reläer så att utgångarna inte kan blockeras."

#: content/about-tor/alt-design/hide-list-of-exits/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/alt-design/hide-list-of-exits/
msgid ""
"1. Being blockable also has tactical advantages: it may be a persuasive "
"response to website maintainers who feel threatened by Tor."
msgstr ""
"1. Att kunna blockeras har också taktiska fördelar: det kan vara ett "
"övertygande svar till webbplatsansvariga som känner sig hotade av Tor."

#: content/about-tor/alt-design/hide-list-of-exits/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/alt-design/hide-list-of-exits/
msgid ""
"1. If people want to block us, we believe that they should be allowed to do "
"so."
msgstr "1. Om människor vill blockera oss anser vi att de bör få göra det."

#: content/about-tor/alt-design/hide-list-of-exits/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/alt-design/hide-list-of-exits/
msgid ""
"1. We can't help but make the information available, since Tor clients need "
"to use it to pick their paths."
msgstr ""
"1. Vi kan inte undvika att göra informationen tillgänglig, eftersom Tor-"
"klienterna behöver den för att välja sina vägar."

#: content/about-tor/alt-design/hide-list-of-exits/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/alt-design/hide-list-of-exits/
msgid ""
"Further, even if we didn't tell clients about the list of relays directly, "
"somebody could still make a lot of connections through Tor to a test site "
"and build a list of the addresses they see."
msgstr ""
"Även om vi inte gav klienterna relälistan direkt skulle någon ändå kunna "
"skapa många anslutningar genom Tor till en testwebbplats och bygga upp en "
"lista över de adresser som syns."

#: content/about-tor/alt-design/hide-list-of-exits/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/alt-design/hide-list-of-exits/
msgid ""
"Giving them the option may inspire them to stop and think about whether they "
"really want to eliminate private access to their system, and if not, what "
"other options they might have."
msgstr ""
"Möjligheten kan få dem att stanna upp och fundera över om de verkligen vill "
"undanröja privat åtkomst till sitt system och, om inte, vilka andra "
"alternativ som finns."

#: content/about-tor/alt-design/hide-list-of-exits/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/alt-design/hide-list-of-exits/
msgid ""
"Obviously, we would prefer for everybody to allow Tor users to connect to "
"them, but people have the right to decide who their services should allow "
"connections from, and if they want to block anonymous users, they can."
msgstr ""
"Vi skulle naturligtvis föredra att alla tillät Tor-användare att ansluta, "
"men människor har rätt att bestämma vilka deras tjänster ska ta emot "
"anslutningar från. Om de vill blockera anonyma användare kan de göra det."

#: content/about-tor/alt-design/hide-list-of-exits/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/alt-design/hide-list-of-exits/
msgid "So if the \"blockers\" want it, they can get it anyway."
msgstr ""
"Om de som vill blockera Tor vill ha listan kan de alltså få fram den ändå."

#: content/about-tor/alt-design/hide-list-of-exits/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/alt-design/hide-list-of-exits/
msgid ""
"The time they might otherwise have spent blocking Tor, they may instead "
"spend rethinking their overall approach to privacy and anonymity."
msgstr ""
"Den tid de annars hade lagt på att blockera Tor kan de i stället använda "
"till att ompröva sin övergripande syn på integritet och anonymitet."

#: content/about-tor/alt-design/hide-list-of-exits/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/alt-design/hide-list-of-exits/
msgid "There are a few reasons we don't hide the list of relays:"
msgstr "Det finns flera skäl till att vi inte döljer relälistan:"

#: content/about-tor/alt-design/let-the-network-pick-the-path/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/alt-design/let-the-network-pick-the-path/
msgid "In Tor, the client - not the network - selects the relays in a circuit."
msgstr "I Tor är det klienten, inte nätverket, som väljer reläerna i en krets."

#: content/about-tor/alt-design/let-the-network-pick-the-path/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/alt-design/let-the-network-pick-the-path/
msgid ""
"This prevents malicious relays from colluding to control your entire path "
"and deanonymize your traffic."
msgstr ""
"Det hindrar skadliga reläer från att samarbeta för att styra hela din väg "
"och avanonymisera din trafik."

#: content/about-tor/alt-design/let-the-network-pick-the-path/contents.lr:article.longer_title
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/alt-design/let-the-network-pick-the-path/
msgid "Why Tor clients, not the network, choose the path"
msgstr "Varför Tor-klienterna, inte nätverket, väljer vägen"

#: content/about-tor/alt-design/let-the-network-pick-the-path/contents.lr:article.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/alt-design/let-the-network-pick-the-path/
msgid "You should let the network pick the path, not the client."
msgstr "Ni borde låta nätverket välja vägen, inte klienten."

#: content/about-tor/alt-design/let-the-network-pick-the-path/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/alt-design/let-the-network-pick-the-path/
msgid "Malicious relays could route you through their colluding friends."
msgstr ""
"Skadliga reläer skulle kunna leda dig genom reläer som drivs av deras "
"samarbetspartner."

#: content/about-tor/alt-design/let-the-network-pick-the-path/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/alt-design/let-the-network-pick-the-path/
msgid ""
"This would give an adversary the ability to watch all of your traffic end to "
"end."
msgstr ""
"Det skulle ge en angripare möjlighet att övervaka all din trafik från början "
"till slut."

#: content/about-tor/alt-design/let-the-network-pick-the-path/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/alt-design/let-the-network-pick-the-path/
msgid ""
"Tor instead uses a **distributed trust model**: the client chooses relays "
"for each circuit, ensuring no single relay or operator can both identify who "
"you are and see where your traffic is going."
msgstr ""
"Tor använder i stället en **distribuerad tillitsmodell**: klienten väljer "
"reläer för varje krets, vilket säkerställer att inget enskilt relä eller "
"ingen enskild operatör både kan identifiera vem du är och se vart trafiken "
"går."

#: content/about-tor/alt-design/let-the-network-pick-the-path/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/alt-design/let-the-network-pick-the-path/
msgid "You cannot trust the network to pick the path."
msgstr "Du kan inte lita på att nätverket väljer vägen."

#: content/about-tor/alt-design/make-every-user-a-relay/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/alt-design/make-every-user-a-relay/
msgid ""
"Tor instead focuses on making relay operation easier, safer, and more "
"attractive for those who can contribute."
msgstr ""
"Tor fokuserar i stället på att göra det enklare, säkrare och mer attraktivt "
"att driva reläer för dem som kan bidra."

#: content/about-tor/alt-design/make-every-user-a-relay/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/alt-design/make-every-user-a-relay/
msgid ""
"While having every Tor user act as a relay might improve network capacity, "
"in practice many users cannot safely or reliably relay traffic."
msgstr ""
"Även om nätverkskapaciteten skulle kunna förbättras om alla Tor-användare "
"fungerade som reläer kan många användare i praktiken inte vidarebefordra "
"trafik på ett säkert eller tillförlitligt sätt."

#: content/about-tor/alt-design/make-every-user-a-relay/contents.lr:article.longer_title
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/alt-design/make-every-user-a-relay/
msgid "Why not every Tor user can (or should) be a relay"
msgstr "Varför inte alla Tor-användare kan (eller bör) vara reläer"

#: content/about-tor/alt-design/make-every-user-a-relay/contents.lr:article.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/alt-design/make-every-user-a-relay/
msgid "You should make every Tor user be a relay"
msgstr "Ni borde göra alla Tor-användare till reläer"

#: content/about-tor/alt-design/make-every-user-a-relay/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/alt-design/make-every-user-a-relay/
msgid "Again, UDP transport would help here."
msgstr "Även här skulle UDP-transport vara till hjälp."

#: content/about-tor/alt-design/make-every-user-a-relay/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/alt-design/make-every-user-a-relay/
msgid ""
"But if we're trying to encourage more clients to turn on relay functionality "
"too (whether as bridge relays or as normal relays), then we need to "
"understand this threat better and learn how to mitigate it."
msgstr ""
"Om vi vill uppmuntra fler klienter att även aktivera reläfunktionen (som "
"broreläer eller vanliga reläer) måste vi dock förstå hotet bättre och lära "
"oss att begränsa det."

#: content/about-tor/alt-design/make-every-user-a-relay/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/alt-design/make-every-user-a-relay/
msgid ""
"Changes like this can have large impact on potential and actual anonymity."
msgstr ""
"Sådana förändringar kan få stor betydelse för både möjlig och faktisk "
"anonymitet."

#: content/about-tor/alt-design/make-every-user-a-relay/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/alt-design/make-every-user-a-relay/
msgid ""
"First, we still need to get better at automatically estimating the right "
"amount of bandwidth to allow."
msgstr ""
"För det första måste vi bli bättre på att automatiskt uppskatta hur mycket "
"bandbredd som bör tillåtas."

#: content/about-tor/alt-design/make-every-user-a-relay/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/alt-design/make-every-user-a-relay/
msgid ""
"Fourth, we might need some sort of incentive scheme to encourage people to "
"relay traffic for others, and/or to become exit nodes."
msgstr ""
"För det fjärde kan vi behöva något slags incitamentssystem för att uppmuntra "
"människor att vidarebefordra trafik åt andra och/eller bli utgångsreläer."

#: content/about-tor/alt-design/make-every-user-a-relay/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/alt-design/make-every-user-a-relay/
msgid ""
"However, many Tor users cannot be good relays — for example, some Tor "
"clients operate from behind restrictive firewalls, connect via modem, or "
"otherwise aren't in a position where they can relay traffic."
msgstr ""
"Många Tor-användare kan dock inte vara bra reläer. Vissa Tor-klienter körs "
"till exempel bakom restriktiva brandväggar, ansluter via modem eller "
"befinner sig på annat sätt i en situation där de inte kan vidarebefordra "
"trafik."

#: content/about-tor/alt-design/make-every-user-a-relay/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/alt-design/make-every-user-a-relay/
msgid ""
"It might be that [switching to UDP transport](../transport-all-ip-packets) "
"is the simplest answer here — which alas is not a very simple answer at all."
msgstr ""
"Det kan vara så att [en övergång till UDP-transport](../transport-all-ip-"
"packets) är den enklaste lösningen – vilket tyvärr inte alls är en enkel "
"lösning."

#: content/about-tor/alt-design/make-every-user-a-relay/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/alt-design/make-every-user-a-relay/
msgid "Please help on all of these!"
msgstr "Hjälp gärna till med allt detta!"

#: content/about-tor/alt-design/make-every-user-a-relay/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/alt-design/make-every-user-a-relay/
msgid ""
"Providing service to these clients is a critical part of providing effective "
"anonymity for everyone, since many Tor users are subject to these or similar "
"constraints and including these clients increases the size of the anonymity "
"set."
msgstr ""
"Att tillhandahålla tjänsten för dessa klienter är avgörande för att alla ska "
"få effektiv anonymitet, eftersom många Tor-användare omfattas av sådana "
"eller liknande begränsningar och fler klienter ökar anonymitetsmängdens "
"storlek."

#: content/about-tor/alt-design/make-every-user-a-relay/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/alt-design/make-every-user-a-relay/
msgid ""
"Requiring every Tor user to be a relay would help with scaling the network "
"to handle all our users, and running a Tor relay may help your anonymity."
msgstr ""
"Om alla Tor-användare måste vara reläer skulle det underlätta skalningen av "
"nätverket så att det klarar alla användare, och att driva ett Tor-relä kan "
"förbättra din anonymitet."

#: content/about-tor/alt-design/make-every-user-a-relay/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/alt-design/make-every-user-a-relay/
msgid ""
"Second, we need to work on scalability, both of the network (how to stop "
"requiring that all Tor relays be able to connect to all Tor relays) and of "
"the directory (how to stop requiring that all Tor users know about all Tor "
"relays)."
msgstr ""
"För det andra måste vi förbättra skalbarheten, både i nätverket (så att alla "
"Tor-reläer inte behöver kunna ansluta till alla andra Tor-reläer) och i "
"katalogen (så att alla Tor-användare inte behöver känna till alla Tor-"
"reläer)."

#: content/about-tor/alt-design/make-every-user-a-relay/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/alt-design/make-every-user-a-relay/
msgid ""
"See Section 5 of the [Challenges](https://svn.torproject.org/svn/projects/"
"design-paper/challenges.pdf) paper for details."
msgstr ""
"Mer information finns i avsnitt 5 i artikeln [Challenges](https://"
"svn.torproject.org/svn/projects/design-paper/challenges.pdf)."

#: content/about-tor/alt-design/make-every-user-a-relay/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/alt-design/make-every-user-a-relay/
msgid ""
"That said, we do want to encourage Tor users to run relays, so what we "
"really want to do is simplify the process of setting up and maintaining a "
"relay."
msgstr ""
"Vi vill trots detta uppmuntra Tor-användare att driva reläer, så det vi "
"egentligen vill göra är att förenkla konfigureringen och underhållet av ett "
"relä."

#: content/about-tor/alt-design/make-every-user-a-relay/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/alt-design/make-every-user-a-relay/
msgid "There are four steps we need to address before we can do this though:"
msgstr "Innan vi kan göra detta måste vi dock hantera fyra steg:"

#: content/about-tor/alt-design/make-every-user-a-relay/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/alt-design/make-every-user-a-relay/
msgid ""
"These clogging attacks are not that scary in the Tor context so long as "
"relays are never clients too."
msgstr ""
"Dessa överbelastningsattacker är inte särskilt skrämmande i Tor-sammanhang "
"så länge reläer aldrig samtidigt är klienter."

#: content/about-tor/alt-design/make-every-user-a-relay/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/alt-design/make-every-user-a-relay/
msgid ""
"Third, we need to better understand the risks from letting the attacker send "
"traffic through your relay while you're also initiating your own anonymized "
"traffic."
msgstr ""
"För det tredje måste vi förstå riskerna bättre när en angripare kan skicka "
"trafik genom ditt relä samtidigt som du själv initierar anonymiserad trafik."

#: content/about-tor/alt-design/make-every-user-a-relay/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/alt-design/make-every-user-a-relay/
msgid ""
"We've made a lot of progress with easy configuration in the past few years: "
"Tor is good at automatically detecting whether it's reachable and how much "
"bandwidth it can offer."
msgstr ""
"Under de senaste åren har vi gjort stora framsteg med enkel konfigurering: "
"Tor är bra på att automatiskt avgöra om reläet är nåbart och hur mycket "
"bandbredd det kan erbjuda."

#: content/about-tor/alt-design/make-every-user-a-relay/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/alt-design/make-every-user-a-relay/
msgid ""
"[Here are our current thoughts on Tor incentives](https://"
"blog.torproject.org/blog/two-incentive-designs-tor)."
msgstr ""
"[Här är våra nuvarande tankar om incitament i Tor](https://"
"blog.torproject.org/blog/two-incentive-designs-tor)."

#: content/about-tor/alt-design/make-every-user-a-relay/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/alt-design/make-every-user-a-relay/
msgid ""
"[Three](https://www.freehaven.net/anonbib/#back01) [different](https://"
"www.freehaven.net/anonbib/#clog-the-queue) [research](https://"
"www.freehaven.net/anonbib/#torta05) papers describe ways to identify the "
"relays in a circuit by running traffic through candidate relays and looking "
"for dips in the traffic while the circuit is active."
msgstr ""
"[Tre](https://www.freehaven.net/anonbib/#back01) [olika](https://"
"www.freehaven.net/anonbib/#clog-the-queue) [forskningsartiklar](https://"
"www.freehaven.net/anonbib/#torta05) beskriver sätt att identifiera reläerna "
"i en krets genom att skicka trafik genom tänkbara reläer och leta efter "
"nedgångar i trafiken medan kretsen är aktiv."

#: content/about-tor/alt-design/make-every-user-a-relay/contents.lr:tab.title
#: content/about-tor/alt-design/transport-all-ip-packets/contents.lr:tab.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/alt-design/make-every-user-a-relay/
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/alt-design/transport-all-ip-packets/
msgid "About design"
msgstr "Om utformningen"

#: content/about-tor/alt-design/transport-all-ip-packets/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/alt-design/transport-all-ip-packets/
msgid ""
"Extending Tor to transport all IP packets - not just TCP streams - could "
"improve flexibility and support new protocols, but it also introduces "
"complex challenges such as fingerprinting risks, protocol-level leaks, and "
"more difficult exit policies."
msgstr ""
"Om Tor utökades till att transportera alla IP-paket, inte bara TCP-strömmar, "
"skulle flexibiliteten och stödet för nya protokoll kunna förbättras. Det "
"skulle dock även medföra komplexa problem, såsom risker för fingeravtryck, "
"läckor på protokollnivå och mer komplicerade utgångspolicyer."

#: content/about-tor/alt-design/transport-all-ip-packets/contents.lr:article.longer_title
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/alt-design/transport-all-ip-packets/
msgid "Challenges and implications of supporting all IP packets in Tor"
msgstr "Utmaningar och konsekvenser av att stödja alla IP-paket i Tor"

#: content/about-tor/alt-design/transport-all-ip-packets/contents.lr:article.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/alt-design/transport-all-ip-packets/
msgid "You should transport all IP packets, not just TCP packets"
msgstr "Ni borde transportera alla IP-paket, inte bara TCP-paket"

#: content/about-tor/alt-design/transport-all-ip-packets/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/alt-design/transport-all-ip-packets/
msgid "1. IP packets reveal OS characteristics."
msgstr "1. IP-paket avslöjar egenskaper hos operativsystemet."

#: content/about-tor/alt-design/transport-all-ip-packets/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/alt-design/transport-all-ip-packets/
msgid "2. Application-level streams still need scrubbing."
msgstr "2. Strömmar på programnivå måste fortfarande rensas."

#: content/about-tor/alt-design/transport-all-ip-packets/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/alt-design/transport-all-ip-packets/
msgid "3. Certain protocols will still leak information."
msgstr "3. Vissa protokoll kommer fortfarande att läcka information."

#: content/about-tor/alt-design/transport-all-ip-packets/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/alt-design/transport-all-ip-packets/
msgid "4. DTLS (datagram TLS) basically has no users, and IPsec sure is big."
msgstr ""
"4. DTLS (datagram-TLS) har i princip inga användare, och IPsec är onekligen "
"omfattande."

#: content/about-tor/alt-design/transport-all-ip-packets/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/alt-design/transport-all-ip-packets/
msgid ""
"5. Exit policies for arbitrary IP packets mean building a secure Intrusion "
"Detection System (IDS)."
msgstr ""
"5. Utgångspolicyer för godtyckliga IP-paket kräver att ett säkert "
"intrångsdetekteringssystem (IDS) byggs."

#: content/about-tor/alt-design/transport-all-ip-packets/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/alt-design/transport-all-ip-packets/
msgid "6. The Tor-internal name spaces would need to be redesigned."
msgstr "6. Tors interna namnrymder skulle behöva göras om."

#: content/about-tor/alt-design/transport-all-ip-packets/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/alt-design/transport-all-ip-packets/
msgid ""
"Adding an IDS to handle exit policies would increase the security complexity "
"of Tor, and would likely not work anyway, as evidenced by the entire field "
"of IDS and counter-IDS papers."
msgstr ""
"Ett IDS för att hantera utgångspolicyer skulle öka Tors säkerhetskomplexitet "
"och sannolikt ändå inte fungera, vilket hela forskningsområdet kring IDS och "
"motåtgärder mot IDS visar."

#: content/about-tor/alt-design/transport-all-ip-packets/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/alt-design/transport-all-ip-packets/
msgid ""
"Clients also need to predict all the packets they will want to send in a "
"session before picking their exit node!"
msgstr ""
"Klienterna måste dessutom förutse alla paket de kommer att vilja skicka "
"under en session innan de väljer utgångsrelä!"

#: content/about-tor/alt-design/transport-all-ip-packets/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/alt-design/transport-all-ip-packets/
msgid ""
"Doing so at the IP level will require a more complex interface between Tor "
"and the local DNS resolver."
msgstr ""
"Att göra detta på IP-nivå kräver ett mer komplext gränssnitt mellan Tor och "
"den lokala DNS-resolvern."

#: content/about-tor/alt-design/transport-all-ip-packets/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/alt-design/transport-all-ip-packets/
msgid ""
"Exit policies become even more important as we become able to transport IP "
"packets."
msgstr ""
"Utgångspolicyerna blir ännu viktigare när vi kan transportera IP-paket."

#: content/about-tor/alt-design/transport-all-ip-packets/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/alt-design/transport-all-ip-packets/
msgid ""
"Exit relays would also not need to allocate a lot of file descriptors for "
"all the exit connections."
msgstr ""
"Utgångsreläerna skulle dessutom inte behöva avsätta ett stort antal "
"filbeskrivare för alla utgående anslutningar."

#: content/about-tor/alt-design/transport-all-ip-packets/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/alt-design/transport-all-ip-packets/
msgid ""
"For example, we must rewrite DNS requests so they are delivered to an "
"unlinkable DNS server rather than the DNS server at a user's ISP; thus, we "
"must understand the protocols we are transporting."
msgstr ""
"Vi måste till exempel skriva om DNS-förfrågningar så att de skickas till en "
"DNS-server som inte kan kopplas till användaren, i stället för till DNS-"
"servern hos användarens internetleverantör. Därför måste vi förstå de "
"protokoll som transporteras."

#: content/about-tor/alt-design/transport-all-ip-packets/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/alt-design/transport-all-ip-packets/
msgid ""
"Given the diversity and complexity of TCP stacks, along with device "
"fingerprinting attacks, it looks like our best bet is shipping our own user-"
"space TCP stack."
msgstr ""
"Med tanke på mångfalden och komplexiteten hos TCP-stackar samt attacker med "
"enhetsfingeravtryck verkar det bästa alternativet vara att leverera en egen "
"TCP-stack i användarrymden."

#: content/about-tor/alt-design/transport-all-ip-packets/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/alt-design/transport-all-ip-packets/
msgid "It could solve the whole need to socksify applications."
msgstr "Det skulle kunna undanröja hela behovet av att SOCKS-anpassa program."

#: content/about-tor/alt-design/transport-all-ip-packets/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/alt-design/transport-all-ip-packets/
msgid "It would make Tor better able to handle new protocols like VoIP."
msgstr "Det skulle göra Tor bättre på att hantera nya protokoll som VoIP."

#: content/about-tor/alt-design/transport-all-ip-packets/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/alt-design/transport-all-ip-packets/
msgid ""
"Many potential abuse issues are resolved by the fact that Tor only "
"transports valid TCP streams (as opposed to arbitrary IP including malformed "
"packets and IP floods.)"
msgstr ""
"Många möjliga missbruksproblem undviks genom att Tor endast transporterar "
"giltiga TCP-strömmar (i motsats till godtycklig IP-trafik, inklusive "
"felaktiga paket och IP-översvämningsattacker)."

#: content/about-tor/alt-design/transport-all-ip-packets/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/alt-design/transport-all-ip-packets/
msgid ""
"Once we've picked a transport mechanism, we need to design a new end-to-end "
"Tor protocol for avoiding tagging attacks and other potential anonymity and "
"integrity issues now that we allow drops, resends, et cetera."
msgstr ""
"När vi har valt en transportmekanism måste vi utforma ett nytt Tor-protokoll "
"från ände till ände som motverkar märkningsattacker och andra möjliga "
"anonymitets- och integritetsproblem, nu när paket kan tappas, skickas om och "
"så vidare."

#: content/about-tor/alt-design/transport-all-ip-packets/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/alt-design/transport-all-ip-packets/
msgid ""
"Our node operators tell us that exit policies are one of the main reasons "
"they're willing to run Tor."
msgstr ""
"Våra nodoperatörer säger att utgångspolicyerna är ett av de främsta skälen "
"till att de är villiga att driva Tor."

#: content/about-tor/alt-design/transport-all-ip-packets/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/alt-design/transport-all-ip-packets/
msgid ""
"So it won't become just a matter of capturing packets and anonymizing them "
"at the IP layer."
msgstr ""
"Det blir alltså inte bara en fråga om att fånga paket och anonymisera dem på "
"IP-nivå."

#: content/about-tor/alt-design/transport-all-ip-packets/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/alt-design/transport-all-ip-packets/
msgid "This would be handy for a number of reasons:"
msgstr "Detta vore praktiskt av flera skäl:"

#: content/about-tor/alt-design/transport-all-ip-packets/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/alt-design/transport-all-ip-packets/
msgid ""
"We also need to compactly describe exit policies in the Tor directory, so "
"clients can predict which nodes will allow their packets to exit."
msgstr ""
"Vi måste också beskriva utgångspolicyerna kompakt i Tor-katalogen, så att "
"klienterna kan förutse vilka noder som tillåter deras paket att lämna "
"nätverket."

#: content/about-tor/alt-design/transport-all-ip-packets/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/alt-design/transport-all-ip-packets/
msgid ""
"We support onion service \".onion\" addresses by intercepting the addresses "
"when they are passed to the Tor client."
msgstr ""
"Vi stöder onion-tjänstadresser med ändelsen ”.onion” genom att fånga upp "
"adresserna när de skickas till Tor-klienten."

#: content/about-tor/alt-design/transport-all-ip-packets/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/alt-design/transport-all-ip-packets/
msgid "We will still need user-side applications like Torbutton."
msgstr "Vi skulle fortfarande behöva program på användarsidan, som Torbutton."

#: content/about-tor/alt-design/transport-all-ip-packets/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/alt-design/transport-all-ip-packets/
msgid ""
"We would still need to do IP-level packet normalization, to stop things like "
"TCP fingerprinting attacks."
msgstr ""
"Vi skulle fortfarande behöva normalisera paket på IP-nivå för att stoppa "
"exempelvis attacker med TCP-fingeravtryck."

#: content/about-tor/alt-design/transport-all-ip-packets/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/alt-design/transport-all-ip-packets/
msgid "We're heading in this direction. Some of the hard problems are:"
msgstr "Vi är på väg i den riktningen. Några av de svåra problemen är:"

#: content/about-tor/contents.lr:product.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/
msgid ""
"This section explains Tor's design choices, security protections, entry "
"guards, key management, and how Tor differs from other proxies."
msgstr ""
"Det här avsnittet förklarar Tors designval, säkerhetsskydd, ingångsvakter, "
"nyckelhantering och hur Tor skiljer sig från andra proxyservrar."

#: content/about-tor/contents.lr:product.title
#: content/about-tor/introduction/protections/contents.lr:tab.title
#: content/about-tor/introduction/tor-vs-other-proxies/contents.lr:tab.title
#: content/about-tor/introduction/what-is-tor/contents.lr:tab.title
#: content/about-tor/introduction/who-funds-tor/contents.lr:tab.title
#: content/about-tor/introduction/why-is-it-called-tor/contents.lr:tab.title
