#: content/contents.lr:pagenav_item.title https://support.torproject.org/
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/introduction/protections/
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/introduction/tor-vs-other-proxies/
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/introduction/what-is-tor/
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/introduction/who-funds-tor/
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/introduction/why-is-it-called-tor/
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/security/attacks-on-onion-routing/
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/security/no-backdoor/
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/using-and-sharing/distributing/
msgid "About Tor"
msgstr "Om Tor"

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/contents.lr:section.title
#: content/tor-browser/getting-started/about-tor-browser/contents.lr:content.content
#: content/tor-browser/getting-started/about-tor-browser/contents.lr:figure.text
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/getting-started/about-tor-browser/
msgid "How Tor works"
msgstr "Så fungerar Tor"

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/entry-guards/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/entry-guards/
msgid "Entry guards are the first relays your Tor client connects to."
msgstr "Ingångsvakter är de första reläerna som Tor-klienten ansluter till."

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/entry-guards/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/entry-guards/
msgid ""
"Instead of picking a new entry each time, Tor selects a small set of guards "
"and reuses them, reducing the chances of an attacker correlating your "
"traffic and deanonymizing you."
msgstr ""
"I stället för att välja en ny ingång varje gång väljer Tor en liten "
"uppsättning vakter och återanvänder dem. Det minskar sannolikheten för att "
"en angripare ska kunna korrelera din trafik och avanonymisera dig."

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/entry-guards/contents.lr:article.longer_title
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/entry-guards/
msgid "How Tor uses entry guards to protect users from correlation attacks"
msgstr ""
"Så använder Tor ingångsvakter för att skydda användare mot "
"korrelationsattacker"

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/entry-guards/contents.lr:article.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/entry-guards/
msgid "What are Entry Guards?"
msgstr "Vad är ingångsvakter?"

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/entry-guards/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/entry-guards/
msgid ""
"(Even though they can't learn what destinations the users are talking to, "
"they still might be able to do bad things with just a list of users.)"
msgstr ""
"(Även om de inte kan ta reda på vilka destinationer användarna kommunicerar "
"med kan de ändå göra skada med enbart en lista över användare.)"

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/entry-guards/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/entry-guards/
msgid ""
"But profiling is, for most users, as bad as being traced all the time: they "
"want to do something often without an attacker noticing, and the attacker "
"noticing once is as bad as the attacker noticing more often."
msgstr ""
"För de flesta användare är profilering dock lika illa som att spåras hela "
"tiden: de vill kunna göra något ofta utan att en angripare märker det, och "
"att angriparen märker det en enda gång är lika illa som att det sker flera "
"gånger."

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/entry-guards/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/entry-guards/
msgid ""
"For example, suppose the attacker controls or watches the Tor relay you "
"choose to enter the network, and also controls or watches the website you "
"visit."
msgstr ""
"Anta till exempel att angriparen styr eller övervakar Tor-reläet som du "
"väljer för att gå in i nätverket och även styr eller övervakar webbplatsen "
"du besöker."

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/entry-guards/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/entry-guards/
msgid ""
"However, that feature won't really become useful until we move to a "
"\"directory guard\" design as well."
msgstr ""
"Den funktionen blir dock inte särskilt användbar förrän vi även går över "
"till en utformning med ”katalogvakter”."

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/entry-guards/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/entry-guards/
msgid ""
"If those relays are not controlled or observed, the attacker can't win, "
"ever, and the user is secure."
msgstr ""
"Om dessa reläer varken styrs eller övervakas av angriparen kan angriparen "
"aldrig lyckas, och användaren är säker."

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/entry-guards/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/entry-guards/
msgid ""
"If those relays are observed or controlled by the attacker, the attacker "
"sees a larger fraction of the user's traffic - but still the user is no more "
"profiled than before."
msgstr ""
"Om reläerna övervakas eller styrs av angriparen ser angriparen en större "
"andel av användarens trafik, men användaren profileras ändå inte mer än "
"tidigare."

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/entry-guards/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/entry-guards/
msgid ""
"If you select new entry and exit relays each time you use the network, the "
"attacker will be able to correlate all traffic you send with probability "
"around (c/n)^2."
msgstr ""
"Om du väljer nya ingångs- och utgångsreläer varje gång du använder nätverket "
"kan angriparen korrelera all trafik du skickar med en sannolikhet på ungefär "
"(c/n)^2."

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/entry-guards/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/entry-guards/
msgid ""
"In this case, the research community knows no practical low-latency design "
"that can reliably stop the attacker from correlating volume and timing "
"information on the two sides."
msgstr ""
"I detta fall känner forskarvärlden inte till någon praktisk design med låg "
"latens som på ett tillförlitligt sätt kan hindra angriparen från att "
"korrelera volym- och tidsinformation på kanalens båda sidor."

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/entry-guards/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/entry-guards/
msgid ""
"Restricting your entry nodes may also help against attackers who want to run "
"a few Tor nodes and easily enumerate all of the Tor user IP addresses."
msgstr ""
"Att begränsa vilka ingångsnoder du använder kan också skydda mot angripare "
"som vill driva ett fåtal Tor-noder och enkelt kartlägga alla Tor-användares "
"IP-adresser."

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/entry-guards/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/entry-guards/
msgid "So, what should we do?"
msgstr "Vad bör vi då göra?"

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/entry-guards/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/entry-guards/
msgid "Suppose the attacker controls, or can observe, C relays."
msgstr "Anta att angriparen styr eller kan övervaka C reläer."

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/entry-guards/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/entry-guards/
msgid "Suppose there are N relays total."
msgstr "Anta att det finns totalt N reläer."

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/entry-guards/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/entry-guards/
msgid ""
"The solution is \"entry guards\": each Tor client selects a few relays at "
"random to use as entry points, and uses only those relays for their first "
"hop."
msgstr ""
"Lösningen är ”ingångsvakter”: varje Tor-klient väljer slumpmässigt några få "
"reläer som ingångspunkter och använder endast dessa reläer för det första "
"hoppet."

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/entry-guards/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/entry-guards/
msgid ""
"Thus, choosing many random entries and exits gives the user no chance of "
"escaping profiling by this kind of attacker."
msgstr ""
"Att välja många slumpmässiga ingångar och utgångar ger alltså användaren "
"ingen möjlighet att undgå profilering av en sådan angripare."

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/entry-guards/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/entry-guards/
msgid ""
"Thus, the user has some chance (on the order of (n-c)/n) of avoiding "
"profiling, whereas they had none before."
msgstr ""
"Användaren har därmed en viss möjlighet (i storleksordningen (n-c)/n) att "
"undvika profilering, medan möjligheten tidigare saknades helt."

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/entry-guards/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/entry-guards/
msgid ""
"Tor (like all current practical low-latency anonymity designs) fails when "
"the attacker can see both ends of the communications channel."
msgstr ""
"Tor (liksom alla nuvarande praktiska anonymitetslösningar med låg latens) "
"misslyckas när angriparen kan se kommunikationskanalens båda ändar."

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/entry-guards/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/entry-guards/
msgid ""
"You can read more at [An Analysis of the Degradation of Anonymous Protocols]"
"(https://www.freehaven.net/anonbib/#wright02), [Defending Anonymous "
"Communication Against Passive Logging Attacks](https://www.freehaven.net/"
"anonbib/#wright03), and especially [Locating Hidden Servers](https://"
"www.freehaven.net/anonbib/#hs-attack06)."
msgstr ""
"Du kan läsa mer i [An Analysis of the Degradation of Anonymous Protocols]"
"(https://www.freehaven.net/anonbib/#wright02), [Defending Anonymous "
"Communication Against Passive Logging Attacks](https://www.freehaven.net/"
"anonbib/#wright03) och särskilt [Locating Hidden Servers](https://"
"www.freehaven.net/anonbib/#hs-attack06)."

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/entry-guards/contents.lr:tab.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/entry-guards/
msgid "About Entry Guards"
msgstr "Om ingångsvakter"

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/key-management/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/key-management/
msgid ""
"These keys ensure your traffic stays private, confirm you're connecting to "
"the intended relays, and coordinate a trusted view of the network."
msgstr ""
"Dessa nycklar håller trafiken privat, bekräftar att du ansluter till de "
"avsedda reläerna och samordnar en betrodd bild av nätverket."

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/key-management/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/key-management/
msgid ""
"Tor relies on multiple types of cryptographic keys to provide privacy, "
"authentication, and trust."
msgstr ""
"Tor använder flera typer av kryptografiska nycklar för att ge integritet, "
"autentisering och tillit."

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/key-management/contents.lr:article.longer_title
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/key-management/
msgid "Tell me about all the keys Tor uses"
msgstr "Berätta om alla nycklar som Tor använder"

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/key-management/contents.lr:article.title
#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/key-management/contents.lr:tab.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/key-management/
msgid "Tor cryptographic keys"
msgstr "Tors kryptografiska nycklar"

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/key-management/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/key-management/
msgid ""
"**Authentication**: Every Tor relay has a public decryption key called the "
"\"onion key\"."
msgstr ""
"**Autentisering**: Varje Tor-relä har en offentlig dekrypteringsnyckel som "
"kallas ”onion-nyckeln”."

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/key-management/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/key-management/
msgid ""
"**Coordination**: How do clients know what the relays are, and how do they "
"know that they have the right keys for them?"
msgstr ""
"**Samordning**: Hur vet klienterna vilka reläerna är, och hur vet de att de "
"har rätt nycklar till dem?"

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/key-management/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/key-management/
msgid ""
"**Encryption**: first, all connections in Tor use TLS link encryption, so "
"observers can't look inside to see which circuit a given cell is intended "
"for."
msgstr ""
"**Kryptering**: För det första använder alla anslutningar i Tor TLS-"
"länkkryptering, så att observatörer inte kan se inuti dem och avgöra vilken "
"krets en viss cell är avsedd för."

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/key-management/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/key-management/
msgid ""
"Because the Tor client chooses the path, it can make sure to get Tor's "
"\"distributed trust\" property: no single relay in the path can know about "
"both the client and what the client is doing."
msgstr ""
"Eftersom Tor-klienten väljer vägen kan den säkerställa Tors egenskap med "
"”distribuerad tillit”: inget enskilt relä i vägen kan känna till både "
"klienten och vad klienten gör."

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/key-management/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/key-management/
msgid ""
"Both sides discard the circuit key when the circuit ends, so logging traffic "
"and then breaking into the relay to discover the key won't work."
msgstr ""
"Båda sidor kasserar kretsnyckeln när kretsen avslutas, så det fungerar inte "
"att logga trafiken och senare göra intrång i reläet för att hitta nyckeln."

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/key-management/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/key-management/
msgid "Each directory authority additionally has a \"directory signing key\"."
msgstr "Varje katalogauktoritet har dessutom en ”katalogsigneringsnyckel”."

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/key-management/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/key-management/
msgid ""
"Each relay has a long-term public signing key called the \"identity key\"."
msgstr ""
"Varje relä har en långsiktig offentlig signeringsnyckel som kallas "
"”identitetsnyckeln”."

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/key-management/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/key-management/
msgid "Each relay rotates its onion key every four weeks."
msgstr "Varje relä byter sin onion-nyckel var fjärde vecka."

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/key-management/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/key-management/
msgid ""
"Further, the Tor client establishes an ephemeral encryption key with each "
"relay in the circuit; these extra layers of encryption mean that only the "
"exit relay can read the cells."
msgstr ""
"Tor-klienten upprättar dessutom en tillfällig krypteringsnyckel med varje "
"relä i kretsen. De extra krypteringslagren innebär att endast utgångsreläet "
"kan läsa cellerna."

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/key-management/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/key-management/
msgid "How do clients know what the directory authorities are?"
msgstr "Hur vet klienterna vilka katalogauktoriteterna är?"

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/key-management/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/key-management/
msgid "How do users know they've got the right software?"
msgstr "Hur vet användarna att de har rätt programvara?"

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/key-management/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/key-management/
msgid ""
"If you're concerned about an attack on this level, we recommend you get "
"involved with the security community and start meeting people."
msgstr ""
"Om du oroar dig för en attack på den här nivån rekommenderar vi att du "
"engagerar dig i säkerhetsgemenskapen och börjar lära känna människor där."

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/key-management/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/key-management/
msgid ""
"In order to be certain that it's really signed by us, you need to have met "
"us in person and gotten a copy of our GPG key fingerprint, or you need to "
"know somebody who has."
msgstr ""
"För att vara säker på att programmet verkligen har signerats av oss måste du "
"ha träffat oss personligen och fått ett exemplar av fingeravtrycket för vår "
"GPG-nyckel, eller känna någon som har gjort det."

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/key-management/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/key-management/
msgid ""
"See the [instructions on how to check Tor Browser's signature](../../../tor-"
"browser/getting-started/verifying-tor-browser/)."
msgstr ""
"Se [anvisningarna för att kontrollera Tor Browsers signatur](../../../tor-"
"browser/getting-started/verifying-tor-browser/)."

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/key-management/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/key-management/
msgid ""
"So the only way to trick users into using a fake Tor network is to give them "
"a specially modified version of the software."
msgstr ""
"Det enda sättet att lura användare att använda ett falskt Tor-nätverk är "
"alltså att ge dem en särskilt modifierad version av programvaran."

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/key-management/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/key-management/
msgid ""
"So unless the adversary can control a majority of the directory authorities "
"(as of 2025 there are 9 directory authorities), they can't trick the Tor "
"client into using other Tor relays."
msgstr ""
"Om inte angriparen kan styra en majoritet av katalogauktoriteterna (år 2025 "
"finns det nio) kan angriparen därför inte lura Tor-klienten att använda "
"andra Tor-reläer."

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/key-management/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/key-management/
msgid ""
"That way the first node in the path can't just spoof the rest of the path."
msgstr ""
"På så sätt kan den första noden i vägen inte bara förfalska resten av vägen."

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/key-management/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/key-management/
msgid ""
"The Tor software comes with a built-in list of location and public key for "
"each directory authority."
msgstr ""
"Tor-programvaran innehåller en inbyggd lista med plats och offentlig nyckel "
"för varje katalogauktoritet."

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/key-management/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/key-management/
msgid ""
"The directory authorities [provide a signed list](https://"
"spec.torproject.org/dir-spec) of all the known relays, and in that list are "
"a set of certificates from each relay (self-signed by their identity key) "
"specifying their keys, locations, exit policies, and so on."
msgstr ""
"Katalogauktoriteterna [tillhandahåller en signerad lista](https://"
"spec.torproject.org/dir-spec) över alla kända reläer. Listan innehåller en "
"uppsättning certifikat från varje relä (självsignerade med reläets "
"identitetsnyckel) som anger dess nycklar, plats, utgångspolicy och så vidare."

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/key-management/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/key-management/
msgid ""
"Tor uses a variety of different keys, with three goals in mind: 1) "
"encryption to ensure privacy of data within the Tor network, 2) "
"authentication so clients know they're talking to the relays they meant to "
"talk to, and 3) signatures to make sure all clients know the same set of "
"relays."
msgstr ""
"Tor använder flera olika nycklar med tre syften: 1) kryptering för att "
"skydda data i Tor-nätverket, 2) autentisering så att klienterna vet att de "
"kommunicerar med de avsedda reläerna och 3) signaturer så att alla klienter "
"känner till samma uppsättning reläer."

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/key-management/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/key-management/
msgid ""
"When the Tor client establishes circuits, at each step it [demands that the "
"Tor relay prove knowledge of its onion key](https://svn-"
"archive.torproject.org/svn/projects/design-paper/tor-"
"design.html#subsec:circuits)."
msgstr ""
"När Tor-klienten upprättar kretsar [kräver den i varje steg att Tor-reläet "
"visar att det känner till sin onion-nyckel](https://svn-"
"archive.torproject.org/svn/projects/design-paper/tor-"
"design.html#subsec:circuits)."

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/key-management/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/key-management/
msgid ""
"When we distribute the source code or a package, we digitally sign it with "
"[GNU Privacy Guard](https://www.gnupg.org/)."
msgstr ""
"När vi distribuerar källkoden eller ett paket signerar vi det digitalt med "
"[GNU Privacy Guard](https://www.gnupg.org/)."

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/
msgid ""
"It explains what Tor does, why it's needed, and how its distributed design "
"keeps users safe."
msgstr ""
"Den förklarar vad Tor gör, varför Tor behövs och hur den distribuerade "
"utformningen skyddar användarna."

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/
msgid ""
"This page introduces the Tor network - a volunteer-run system that protects "
"privacy, resists censorship, and helps people communicate and browse "
"anonymously."
msgstr ""
"Den här sidan presenterar Tor-nätverket – ett system som drivs av volontärer "
"och skyddar integriteten, motstår censur och hjälper människor att "
"kommunicera och surfa anonymt."

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/contents.lr:article.longer_title
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/
msgid "What Tor is, how it works, and why people use it"
msgstr "Vad Tor är, hur det fungerar och varför människor använder det"

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/contents.lr:article.title
#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/contents.lr:tab.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/
msgid "Overview"
msgstr "Översikt"

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/
msgid ""
"A basic problem for the privacy minded is that the recipient of your "
"communications can see that you sent it by looking at headers."
msgstr ""
"Ett grundläggande problem för den som värnar om sin integritet är att "
"mottagaren av kommunikationen kan se att du skickade den genom att granska "
"rubrikerna."

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/
msgid ""
"A very simple form of traffic analysis might involve sitting somewhere "
"between sender and recipient on the network, looking at headers."
msgstr ""
"En mycket enkel form av trafikanalys kan bestå i att någon befinner sig "
"någonstans mellan avsändaren och mottagaren i nätverket och granskar "
"rubrikerna."

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/
msgid ""
"Activist groups like the Electronic Frontier Foundation (EFF) recommend Tor "
"as a mechanism for maintaining civil liberties online."
msgstr ""
"Aktivistgrupper som Electronic Frontier Foundation (EFF) rekommenderar Tor "
"som ett sätt att bevara medborgerliga fri- och rättigheter på nätet."

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/
msgid ""
"Along the same line, Tor is an effective censorship circumvention tool, "
"allowing its users to reach otherwise blocked destinations or content."
msgstr ""
"På samma sätt är Tor ett effektivt verktyg för att kringgå censur och gör "
"det möjligt för användarna att nå destinationer eller innehåll som annars är "
"blockerat."

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/
msgid ""
"Because each relay sees no more than one hop in the circuit, neither an "
"eavesdropper nor a compromised relay can use traffic analysis to link the "
"connection's source and destination."
msgstr ""
"Eftersom varje relä inte ser mer än ett hopp i kretsen kan varken en "
"avlyssnare eller ett komprometterat relä använda trafikanalys för att koppla "
"samman anslutningens källa och destination."

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/
msgid "But there are also more powerful kinds of traffic analysis."
msgstr "Det finns dock även kraftfullare former av trafikanalys."

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/
msgid ""
"Corporations use Tor as a safe way to conduct competitive analysis, and to "
"protect sensitive procurement patterns from eavesdroppers."
msgstr ""
"Företag använder Tor som ett säkert sätt att genomföra konkurrensanalyser "
"och skydda känsliga inköpsmönster från avlyssnare."

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/
msgid ""
"Even if you encrypt the data payload of your communications, traffic "
"analysis still reveals a great deal about what you're doing and, possibly, "
"what you're saying."
msgstr ""
"Även om du krypterar kommunikationens datainnehåll avslöjar trafikanalys "
"fortfarande mycket om vad du gör och möjligen vad du säger."

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/
msgid ""
"For efficiency, the Tor software uses the same circuit for connections that "
"happen within the same ten minutes or so."
msgstr ""
"För effektivitetens skull använder Tor-programvaran samma krets för "
"anslutningar som sker inom ungefär samma tiominutersperiod."

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/
msgid ""
"For example, if you're travelling abroad and you connect to your employer's "
"computers to check or send mail, you can inadvertently reveal your national "
"origin and professional affiliation to anyone observing the network, even if "
"the connection is encrypted."
msgstr ""
"Om du till exempel reser utomlands och ansluter till arbetsgivarens datorer "
"för att läsa eller skicka e-post kan du oavsiktligt avslöja ditt "
"ursprungsland och din yrkesmässiga anknytning för den som övervakar "
"nätverket, även om anslutningen är krypterad."

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/
msgid "How does traffic analysis work?"
msgstr "Hur fungerar trafikanalys?"

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/
msgid ""
"Individuals also use Tor for socially sensitive communication: chat rooms "
"and web forums for rape and abuse survivors, or people with illnesses."
msgstr ""
"Enskilda personer använder också Tor för socialt känslig kommunikation, till "
"exempel chattrum och webbforum för personer som har utsatts för våldtäkt "
"eller övergrepp eller lever med sjukdomar."

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/
msgid ""
"Individuals use Tor to keep websites from tracking them and their family "
"members, or to connect to news sites, instant messaging services, or the "
"like when these are blocked by their local Internet providers."
msgstr ""
"Enskilda personer använder Tor för att hindra webbplatser från att spåra dem "
"och deras familjer, eller för att ansluta till nyhetswebbplatser, "
"snabbmeddelandetjänster och liknande när dessa blockeras av lokala "
"internetleverantörer."

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/
msgid ""
"Internet data packets have two parts: a data payload and a header used for "
"routing."
msgstr ""
"Internetdatapaket består av två delar: ett datainnehåll och en rubrik som "
"används för routning."

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/
msgid ""
"It can even threaten your job and physical safety by revealing who and where "
"you are."
msgstr ""
"Det kan till och med hota ditt arbete och din fysiska säkerhet genom att "
"avslöja vem och var du är."

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/
msgid ""
"Journalists use Tor to communicate more safely with whistleblowers and "
"dissidents."
msgstr ""
"Journalister använder Tor för att kommunicera säkrare med visselblåsare och "
"dissidenter."

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/
msgid ""
"Knowing the source and destination of your Internet traffic allows others to "
"track your behavior and interests."
msgstr ""
"Om andra känner till källan och destinationen för din internettrafik kan de "
"spåra ditt beteende och dina intressen."

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/
msgid ""
"Later requests are given a new circuit, to keep people from linking your "
"earlier actions to the new ones."
msgstr ""
"Senare förfrågningar får en ny krets, så att ingen kan koppla dina tidigare "
"handlingar till de nya."

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/
msgid ""
"No individual relay ever knows the complete path that a data packet has "
"taken."
msgstr ""
"Inget enskilt relä känner någonsin till hela den väg som ett datapaket har "
"tagit."

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/
msgid ""
"Non-governmental organizations (NGOs) use Tor to allow their workers to "
"connect to their home website while they're in a foreign country, without "
"notifying everybody nearby that they're working with that organization."
msgstr ""
"Icke-statliga organisationer använder Tor för att låta sina medarbetare "
"ansluta till organisationens webbplats i hemlandet när de befinner sig "
"utomlands, utan att avslöja för alla i närheten att de arbetar för "
"organisationen."

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/
msgid ""
"Once a circuit has been established, many kinds of data can be exchanged and "
"several different sorts of software applications can be deployed over the "
"Tor network."
msgstr ""
"När en krets har upprättats kan många typer av data utbytas och flera olika "
"slags program användas över Tor-nätverket."

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/
msgid ""
"So can authorized intermediaries like Internet service providers, and "
"sometimes unauthorized intermediaries as well."
msgstr ""
"Det kan även behöriga mellanhänder, såsom internetleverantörer, och ibland "
"också obehöriga mellanhänder göra."

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/
msgid ""
"Some attackers spy on multiple parts of the Internet and use sophisticated "
"statistical techniques to track the communications patterns of many "
"different organizations and individuals. Encryption does not help against "
"these attackers, since it only hides the content of Internet traffic, not "
"the headers."
msgstr ""
"Vissa angripare övervakar flera delar av internet och använder avancerade "
"statistiska metoder för att spåra kommunikationsmönster hos många olika "
"organisationer och personer. Kryptering hjälper inte mot dessa angripare, "
"eftersom den bara döljer internettrafikens innehåll, inte rubrikerna."

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/
msgid ""
"That's because it focuses on the header, which discloses source, "
"destination, size, timing, and so on."
msgstr ""
"Det beror på att analysen fokuserar på rubriken, som avslöjar källa, "
"destination, storlek, tidpunkter och så vidare."

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/
msgid ""
"The Tor network is a group of volunteer-operated servers that allows people "
"to improve their privacy and security on the Internet."
msgstr ""
"Tor-nätverket är en grupp servrar som drivs av volontärer och gör det "
"möjligt för människor att förbättra sin integritet och säkerhet på internet."

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/
msgid ""
"The circuit is extended one hop at a time, and each relay along the way "
"knows only which relay gave it data and which relay it is giving data to."
msgstr ""
"Kretsen förlängs ett hopp i taget, och varje relä längs vägen vet bara "
"vilket relä det fick data från och vilket relä det skickar data till."

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/
msgid ""
"The client negotiates a separate set of encryption keys for each hop along "
"the circuit to ensure that each hop can't trace these connections as they "
"pass through."
msgstr ""
"Klienten förhandlar fram en separat uppsättning krypteringsnycklar för varje "
"hopp i kretsen, så att inget enskilt hopp kan spåra anslutningarna när de "
"passerar."

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/
msgid ""
"The data payload is whatever is being sent, whether that's an email message, "
"a web page, or an audio file."
msgstr ""
"Datainnehållet är det som skickas, oavsett om det är ett e-postmeddelande, "
"en webbsida eller en ljudfil."

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/
msgid ""
"The idea is similar to using a twisty, hard-to-follow route in order to "
"throw off somebody who is tailing you - and then periodically erasing your "
"footprints. Instead of taking a direct route from source to destination, "
"data packets on the Tor network take a random pathway through several relays "
"that cover your tracks so no observer at any single point can tell where the "
"data came from or where it's going."
msgstr ""
"Idén liknar att ta en slingrande och svårföljd väg för att skaka av sig "
"någon som följer efter och sedan regelbundet sudda ut sina spår. I stället "
"för att ta en direkt väg från källa till destination tar datapaket i Tor-"
"nätverket en slumpmässig väg genom flera reläer som döljer spåren. Ingen "
"observatör vid en enskild punkt kan därför avgöra varifrån data kom eller "
"vart de är på väg."

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/
msgid ""
"The variety of people who use Tor is actually part of what makes it so "
"secure."
msgstr ""
"Mångfalden bland dem som använder Tor är faktiskt en del av det som gör "
"nätverket så säkert."

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/
msgid ""
"They also use it to replace traditional VPNs, which reveal the exact amount "
"and timing of communication."
msgstr ""
"De använder också Tor i stället för traditionella VPN-tjänster, som avslöjar "
"kommunikationens exakta omfattning och tidpunkter."

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/
msgid ""
"This can impact your checkbook if, for example, an e-commerce site uses "
"price discrimination based on your country or institution of origin."
msgstr ""
"Det kan påverka din ekonomi om en e-handelswebbplats till exempel använder "
"prisdiskriminering utifrån ditt land eller den institution du kommer från."

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/
msgid ""
"To create a private network pathway with Tor, the user's software or client "
"incrementally builds a circuit of encrypted connections through relays on "
"the network."
msgstr ""
"För att skapa en privat nätverksväg med Tor bygger användarens programvara "
"eller klient stegvis en krets av krypterade anslutningar genom reläer i "
"nätverket."

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/
msgid ""
"Tor can also be used as a building block for software developers to create "
"new communication tools with built-in privacy features."
msgstr ""
"Programutvecklare kan också använda Tor som byggsten för att skapa nya "
"kommunikationsverktyg med inbyggt integritetsskydd."

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/
msgid ""
"Tor helps to reduce the risks of both simple and sophisticated traffic "
"analysis by distributing your transactions over several places on the "
"Internet, so no single point can link you to your destination."
msgstr ""
"Tor minskar riskerna med både enkel och avancerad trafikanalys genom att "
"fördela dina transaktioner över flera platser på internet, så att ingen "
"enskild punkt kan koppla dig till destinationen."

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/
msgid ""
"Tor hides you among the other users on the network, so the more populous and "
"diverse the user base for Tor is, the more your anonymity will be protected."
msgstr ""
"Tor döljer dig bland nätverkets andra användare. Ju större och mer varierad "
"användarbasen är, desto bättre skyddas din anonymitet."

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/
msgid ""
"Tor only works for TCP streams and can be used by any application with SOCKS "
"support."
msgstr ""
"Tor fungerar endast för TCP-strömmar och kan användas av alla program med "
"SOCKS-stöd."

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/
msgid ""
"Tor's onion services let users publish web sites and other services without "
"needing to reveal the location of the site."
msgstr ""
"Tors onion-tjänster gör det möjligt för användare att publicera webbplatser "
"och andra tjänster utan att avslöja var webbplatsen finns."

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/
msgid ""
"Tor's users employ this network by connecting through a series of virtual "
"tunnels rather than making a direct connection, thus allowing both "
"organizations and individuals to share information over public networks "
"without compromising their privacy."
msgstr ""
"Tor-användare använder nätverket genom att ansluta via en serie virtuella "
"tunnlar i stället för en direkt anslutning. Det gör att både organisationer "
"och enskilda personer kan dela information över offentliga nätverk utan att "
"äventyra sin integritet."

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/
msgid ""
"Traffic analysis can be used to infer who is talking to whom over a public "
"network."
msgstr ""
"Trafikanalys kan användas för att dra slutsatser om vem som kommunicerar med "
"vem över ett offentligt nätverk."

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/
msgid ""
"Using Tor protects you against a common form of Internet surveillance known "
"as \"traffic analysis.\""
msgstr ""
"När du använder Tor skyddas du mot en vanlig form av internetövervakning som "
"kallas ”trafikanalys”."

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/
msgid ""
"Which locations have employees working late? Which locations have employees "
"consulting job-hunting websites?"
msgstr ""
"På vilka platser arbetar personalen sent? På vilka platser besöker "
"personalen webbplatser för arbetssökande?"

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/
msgid ""
"Which research divisions are communicating with the company's patent lawyers?"
msgstr ""
"Vilka forskningsavdelningar kommunicerar med företagets patentjurister?"

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/contents.lr:tab.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/
msgid "Distributed network"
msgstr "Distribuerat nätverk"

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/contents.lr:tab.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/overview/
msgid "Why we need Tor"
msgstr "Varför vi behöver Tor"

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/path-selection/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/path-selection/
msgid ""
"Tor may reuse a circuit before building a new one, balancing anonymity with "
"performance."
msgstr ""
"Tor kan återanvända en krets innan en ny byggs och balanserar därmed "
"anonymitet mot prestanda."

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/path-selection/contents.lr:article.longer_title
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/path-selection/
msgid "How often does Tor change its paths?"
msgstr "Hur ofta ändrar Tor sina vägar?"

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/path-selection/contents.lr:article.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/path-selection/
msgid "Tor path selection"
msgstr "Tors vägval"

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/path-selection/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/path-selection/
msgid "(If the circuit fails, Tor will switch to a new circuit immediately.)"
msgstr "(Om kretsen slutar fungera byter Tor omedelbart till en ny krets.)"

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/path-selection/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/path-selection/
msgid ""
"But note that a single TCP stream (e.g. a long IRC connection) will stay on "
"the same circuit forever."
msgstr ""
"Observera dock att en enskild TCP-ström (till exempel en lång IRC-"
"anslutning) stannar i samma krets så länge den pågår."

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/path-selection/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/path-selection/
msgid ""
"Otherwise, an adversary with a partial view of the network would be given "
"many chances over time to link you to your destination, rather than just one "
"chance."
msgstr ""
"Annars skulle en angripare med begränsad insyn i nätverket med tiden få "
"många chanser att koppla dig till destinationen, i stället för en enda chans."

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/path-selection/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/path-selection/
msgid ""
"Tor will reuse the same circuit for new TCP streams for 10 minutes, as long "
"as the circuit is working fine."
msgstr ""
"Tor återanvänder samma krets för nya TCP-strömmar i tio minuter, så länge "
"kretsen fungerar som den ska."

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/path-selection/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/path-selection/
msgid "We don't rotate individual streams from one circuit to the next."
msgstr "Vi flyttar inte enskilda strömmar från en krets till nästa."

#: content/about-tor/how-tor-works/path-selection/contents.lr:tab.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/how-tor-works/path-selection/
msgid "About path selection"
msgstr "Om vägval"

#: content/about-tor/introduction/contents.lr:section.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/introduction/
msgid "Understand the basics of Tor"
msgstr "Förstå grunderna i Tor"

#: content/about-tor/introduction/contents.lr:section.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/introduction/
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr "Introduktion"

#: content/about-tor/introduction/protections/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/introduction/protections/
msgid ""
"Tor encrypts your traffic in layers and routes it through different servers "
"so that no single point can reveal both who you are and what you're doing "
"online."
msgstr ""
"Tor krypterar trafiken i lager och leder den genom olika servrar, så att "
"ingen enskild punkt kan avslöja både vem du är och vad du gör på nätet."

#: content/about-tor/introduction/protections/contents.lr:article.longer_title
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/introduction/protections/
msgid "The privacy and anonymity protections Tor offers"
msgstr "Tors skydd för integritet och anonymitet"

#: content/about-tor/introduction/protections/contents.lr:article.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/introduction/protections/
msgid "What protections does Tor provide?"
msgstr "Vilket skydd ger Tor?"

#: content/about-tor/introduction/protections/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/introduction/protections/
msgid ""
"Because these relays are run by different individuals or organizations, "
"distributing trust provides more security than the old [one hop proxy](../"
"tor-vs-other-proxies/) approach."
msgstr ""
"Eftersom reläerna drivs av olika personer eller organisationer ger "
"distribuerad tillit bättre säkerhet än den äldre metoden med en [proxy med "
"ett enda hopp](../tor-vs-other-proxies/)."

#: content/about-tor/introduction/protections/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/introduction/protections/
msgid ""
"Every packet includes a source IP address (of the sender) and a destination "
"IP address (of the receiver), just as ordinary letters contain postal "
"addresses of sender and receiver."
msgstr ""
"Varje paket innehåller en IP-källadress (avsändarens) och en IP-"
"destinationsadress (mottagarens), precis som vanliga brev har avsändarens "
"och mottagarens postadresser."

#: content/about-tor/introduction/protections/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/introduction/protections/
msgid ""
"First, Tor prevents websites and other services from learning your location, "
"which they can use to build databases about your habits and interests."
msgstr ""
"För det första hindrar Tor webbplatser och andra tjänster från att ta reda "
"på var du befinner dig, vilket de annars kan använda för att bygga databaser "
"över dina vanor och intressen."

#: content/about-tor/introduction/protections/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/introduction/protections/
msgid "Generally speaking, Tor aims to solve three privacy problems:"
msgstr "I stora drag är Tors mål att lösa tre integritetsproblem:"

#: content/about-tor/introduction/protections/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/introduction/protections/
msgid ""
"In addition, every server in the Internet that can see any of the packets "
"can profile your behavior."
msgstr ""
"Alla servrar på internet som kan se något av paketen kan dessutom profilera "
"ditt beteende."

#: content/about-tor/introduction/protections/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/introduction/protections/
msgid ""
"In particular, your local ISP is in the position to build a complete profile "
"of your Internet usage."
msgstr ""
"Din lokala internetleverantör har i synnerhet möjlighet att bygga en "
"fullständig profil över din internetanvändning."

#: content/about-tor/introduction/protections/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/introduction/protections/
msgid ""
"Internet communication is based on a store-and-forward model that can be "
"understood in analogy to postal mail: Data is transmitted in blocks called "
"IP datagrams or packets."
msgstr ""
"Internetkommunikation bygger på en modell där data lagras och "
"vidarebefordras, vilket kan liknas vid postgång: data överförs i block som "
"kallas IP-datagram eller paket."

#: content/about-tor/introduction/protections/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/introduction/protections/
msgid ""
"It also stops them from deciding what you're allowed to learn and publish -- "
"if you can get to any part of the Tor network, you can reach any site on the "
"Internet."
msgstr ""
"Tor hindrar dem också från att bestämma vad du får läsa och publicera – om "
"du kan nå någon del av Tor-nätverket kan du nå vilken webbplats som helst på "
"internet."

#: content/about-tor/introduction/protections/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/introduction/protections/
msgid ""
"Note that all your local ISP can observe now is that you are communicating "
"with Tor nodes."
msgstr ""
"Observera att det enda din lokala internetleverantör nu kan se är att du "
"kommunicerar med Tor-noder."

#: content/about-tor/introduction/protections/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/introduction/protections/
msgid ""
"Note, however, that there are situations where Tor fails to solve these "
"privacy problems entirely: see the entry below on [remaining attacks](../../"
"security/attacks-on-onion-routing/)."
msgstr ""
"Observera dock att det finns situationer där Tor inte löser "
"integritetsproblemen fullständigt. Se posten nedan om [kvarstående attacker]"
"(../../security/attacks-on-onion-routing/)."

#: content/about-tor/introduction/protections/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/introduction/protections/
msgid ""
"Second, Tor prevents people watching your traffic locally (such as your ISP "
"or someone with access to your home wifi or router) from learning what "
"information you're fetching and where you're fetching it from."
msgstr ""
"För det andra hindrar Tor personer som övervakar trafiken lokalt (till "
"exempel din internetleverantör eller någon med åtkomst till hemmets Wi-Fi "
"eller router) från att ta reda på vilken information du hämtar och varifrån "
"du hämtar den."

#: content/about-tor/introduction/protections/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/introduction/protections/
msgid ""
"Similarly, servers in the Internet just see that they are being contacted by "
"Tor nodes."
msgstr ""
"På motsvarande sätt ser servrar på internet bara att de kontaktas av Tor-"
"noder."

#: content/about-tor/introduction/protections/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/introduction/protections/
msgid ""
"The aim of Tor is to improve your privacy by sending your traffic through a "
"series of proxies."
msgstr ""
"Tors mål är att förbättra din integritet genom att skicka trafiken genom en "
"serie proxyservrar."

#: content/about-tor/introduction/protections/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/introduction/protections/
msgid ""
"The way from sender to receiver involves multiple hops of routers, where "
"each router inspects the destination IP address and forwards the packet "
"closer to its destination."
msgstr ""
"Vägen från avsändare till mottagare omfattar flera hopp genom routrar. Varje "
"router granskar destinations-IP-adressen och vidarebefordrar paketet närmare "
"destinationen."

#: content/about-tor/introduction/protections/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/introduction/protections/
msgid ""
"Third, Tor routes your connection through more than one Tor relay so no "
"single relay can learn what you're up to."
msgstr ""
"För det tredje leder Tor anslutningen genom mer än ett Tor-relä, så att "
"inget enskilt relä kan ta reda på vad du gör."

#: content/about-tor/introduction/protections/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/introduction/protections/
msgid ""
"Thus, every router between sender and receiver learns that the sender is "
"communicating with the receiver."
msgstr ""
"Varje router mellan avsändaren och mottagaren får därmed veta att avsändaren "
"kommunicerar med mottagaren."

#: content/about-tor/introduction/protections/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/introduction/protections/
msgid ""
"With Tor, your Internet connections don't give you away by default -- now "
"you can have the ability to choose, for each connection, how much "
"information to reveal."
msgstr ""
"Med Tor avslöjar dina internetanslutningar dig inte som standard. Du kan i "
"stället välja för varje anslutning hur mycket information som ska avslöjas."

#: content/about-tor/introduction/protections/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/introduction/protections/
msgid ""
"Your communication is encrypted in multiple layers and routed via multiple "
"hops through the Tor network to the final receiver."
msgstr ""
"Kommunikationen krypteras i flera lager och leds genom flera hopp i Tor-"
"nätverket till den slutliga mottagaren."

#: content/about-tor/introduction/tor-vs-other-proxies/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/introduction/tor-vs-other-proxies/
msgid ""
"This prevents any single relay or provider from knowing both your identity "
"and your online activity."
msgstr ""
"Det hindrar ett enskilt relä eller en enskild leverantör från att känna till "
"både din identitet och din aktivitet på nätet."

#: content/about-tor/introduction/tor-vs-other-proxies/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/introduction/tor-vs-other-proxies/
msgid ""
"Unlike regular proxy servers, which create a single point of trust and "
"failure, Tor routes your traffic through multiple relays with layered "
"encryption."
msgstr ""
"Till skillnad från vanliga proxyservrar, som skapar en enda tillits- och "
"felpunkt, leder Tor trafiken genom flera reläer med kryptering i lager."

#: content/about-tor/introduction/tor-vs-other-proxies/contents.lr:article.longer_title
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/introduction/tor-vs-other-proxies/
msgid "Tor provides stronger privacy than simple proxy services"
msgstr "Tor ger starkare integritetsskydd än enkla proxytjänster"

#: content/about-tor/introduction/tor-vs-other-proxies/contents.lr:article.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/introduction/tor-vs-other-proxies/
msgid "How is Tor different from other proxies?"
msgstr "Hur skiljer sig Tor från andra proxyservrar?"

#: content/about-tor/introduction/tor-vs-other-proxies/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/introduction/tor-vs-other-proxies/
msgid ""
"A bad first of three servers can see encrypted Tor traffic coming from your "
"computer."
msgstr ""
"En illvillig första server av tre kan se krypterad Tor-trafik som kommer "
"från din dator."

#: content/about-tor/introduction/tor-vs-other-proxies/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/introduction/tor-vs-other-proxies/
msgid "A bad third of three servers can see the traffic you sent into Tor."
msgstr ""
"En illvillig tredje server av tre kan se trafiken som du skickade in i Tor."

#: content/about-tor/introduction/tor-vs-other-proxies/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/introduction/tor-vs-other-proxies/
msgid ""
"A typical proxy provider sets up a server somewhere on the Internet and "
"allows you to use it to relay your traffic."
msgstr ""
"En vanlig proxyleverantör sätter upp en server någonstans på internet och "
"låter dig använda den för att vidarebefordra trafik."

#: content/about-tor/introduction/tor-vs-other-proxies/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/introduction/tor-vs-other-proxies/
msgid ""
"Because there's a separate layer of encryption for each of the three relays, "
"somebody watching your Internet connection can't modify, or read, what you "
"are sending into the Tor network."
msgstr ""
"Eftersom det finns ett separat krypteringslager för vart och ett av de tre "
"reläerna kan någon som övervakar din internetanslutning varken ändra eller "
"läsa det du skickar in i Tor-nätverket."

#: content/about-tor/introduction/tor-vs-other-proxies/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/introduction/tor-vs-other-proxies/
msgid "Can't the third server see my traffic?"
msgstr "Kan inte den tredje servern se min trafik?"

#: content/about-tor/introduction/tor-vs-other-proxies/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/introduction/tor-vs-other-proxies/
msgid "Doesn't the first server see who I am?"
msgstr "Ser inte den första servern vem jag är?"

#: content/about-tor/introduction/tor-vs-other-proxies/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/introduction/tor-vs-other-proxies/
msgid ""
"If you're using encryption (like HTTPS), it will only know the destination."
msgstr ""
"Om du använder kryptering (som HTTPS) känner den bara till destinationen."

#: content/about-tor/introduction/tor-vs-other-proxies/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/introduction/tor-vs-other-proxies/
msgid ""
"In some cases, they can even see inside your encrypted traffic as they relay "
"it to your banking site or to ecommerce stores."
msgstr ""
"I vissa fall kan de till och med se inuti den krypterade trafiken när den "
"vidarebefordras till din bank eller e-handelsbutiker."

#: content/about-tor/introduction/tor-vs-other-proxies/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/introduction/tor-vs-other-proxies/
msgid "In the simplest configuration, you don't have to install anything."
msgstr "I den enklaste konfigurationen behöver du inte installera något."

#: content/about-tor/introduction/tor-vs-other-proxies/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/introduction/tor-vs-other-proxies/
msgid "It merely sees \"This IP address is using Tor\"."
msgstr "Den ser bara: ”Den här IP-adressen använder Tor.”"

#: content/about-tor/introduction/tor-vs-other-proxies/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/introduction/tor-vs-other-proxies/
msgid "It still doesn't know who you are and what you are doing over Tor."
msgstr "Den vet fortfarande inte vem du är eller vad du gör via Tor."

#: content/about-tor/introduction/tor-vs-other-proxies/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/introduction/tor-vs-other-proxies/
msgid "It won't know who sent this traffic."
msgstr "Den vet inte vem som skickade trafiken."

#: content/about-tor/introduction/tor-vs-other-proxies/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/introduction/tor-vs-other-proxies/
msgid "Possibly."
msgstr "Möjligen."

#: content/about-tor/introduction/tor-vs-other-proxies/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/introduction/tor-vs-other-proxies/
msgid "Simple proxy providers also create a single point of failure."
msgstr "Enkla proxyleverantörer skapar också en enda felpunkt."

#: content/about-tor/introduction/tor-vs-other-proxies/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/introduction/tor-vs-other-proxies/
msgid ""
"Simple proxy providers are fine solutions if you do not want protections for "
"your privacy and anonymity online and you trust the provider to not do bad "
"things."
msgstr ""
"Enkla proxyleverantörer kan vara tillräckliga om du inte vill skydda din "
"integritet och anonymitet på nätet och litar på att leverantören inte "
"missbrukar sin ställning."

#: content/about-tor/introduction/tor-vs-other-proxies/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/introduction/tor-vs-other-proxies/
msgid ""
"Some simple proxy providers use SSL to secure your connection to them, which "
"protects you against local eavesdroppers, such as those at a cafe with free "
"wifi Internet."
msgstr ""
"Vissa enkla proxyleverantörer använder SSL för att skydda din anslutning "
"till dem, vilket skyddar mot lokala avlyssnare, till exempel på ett kafé med "
"kostnadsfritt Wi-Fi."

#: content/about-tor/introduction/tor-vs-other-proxies/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/introduction/tor-vs-other-proxies/
msgid ""
"The provider knows both who you are and what you browse on the Internet."
msgstr "Leverantören vet både vem du är och vad du besöker på internet."

#: content/about-tor/introduction/tor-vs-other-proxies/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/introduction/tor-vs-other-proxies/
msgid ""
"The provider may charge for use of the proxy, or fund their costs through "
"advertisements on the server."
msgstr ""
"Leverantören kan ta betalt för proxyn eller finansiera kostnaderna genom "
"annonser på servern."

#: content/about-tor/introduction/tor-vs-other-proxies/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/introduction/tor-vs-other-proxies/
msgid "The users all enter and leave through the same server."
msgstr "Alla användare går in och ut genom samma server."

#: content/about-tor/introduction/tor-vs-other-proxies/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/introduction/tor-vs-other-proxies/
msgid "They can see your traffic as it passes through their server."
msgstr "De kan se trafiken när den passerar genom deras server."

#: content/about-tor/introduction/tor-vs-other-proxies/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/introduction/tor-vs-other-proxies/
msgid "This creates a simple, easy to maintain architecture."
msgstr "Det skapar en enkel arkitektur som är lätt att underhålla."

#: content/about-tor/introduction/tor-vs-other-proxies/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/introduction/tor-vs-other-proxies/
msgid ""
"Tor passes your traffic through at least 3 different servers before sending "
"it on to the destination."
msgstr ""
"Tor leder trafiken genom minst tre olika servrar innan den skickas vidare "
"till destinationen."

#: content/about-tor/introduction/tor-vs-other-proxies/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/introduction/tor-vs-other-proxies/
msgid ""
"You are still protected from this node figuring out both who you are and "
"where you are going on the Internet."
msgstr ""
"Du är fortfarande skyddad mot att den här noden tar reda på både vem du är "
"och vart du går på internet."

#: content/about-tor/introduction/tor-vs-other-proxies/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/introduction/tor-vs-other-proxies/
msgid ""
"You have to trust the provider isn't watching your traffic, injecting their "
"own advertisements into your traffic stream, or recording your personal "
"details."
msgstr ""
"Du måste lita på att leverantören inte övervakar trafiken, lägger in egna "
"annonser i trafikströmmen eller registrerar dina personuppgifter."

#: content/about-tor/introduction/tor-vs-other-proxies/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/introduction/tor-vs-other-proxies/
msgid "You just have to point your browser at their proxy server."
msgstr ""
"Du behöver bara ställa in webbläsaren så att den använder deras proxyserver."

#: content/about-tor/introduction/tor-vs-other-proxies/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/introduction/tor-vs-other-proxies/
msgid ""
"Your traffic is encrypted between the Tor client (on your computer) and "
"where it pops out somewhere else in the world."
msgstr ""
"Trafiken är krypterad mellan Tor-klienten på din dator och den plats någon "
"annanstans i världen där den lämnar Tor."

#: content/about-tor/introduction/what-is-tor/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/introduction/what-is-tor/
msgid "The name \"Tor\" can refer to several different components."
msgstr "Namnet ”Tor” kan syfta på flera olika komponenter."

#: content/about-tor/introduction/what-is-tor/contents.lr:article.longer_title
#: content/about-tor/introduction/what-is-tor/contents.lr:article.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/introduction/what-is-tor/
msgid "What is Tor?"
msgstr "Vad är Tor?"

#: content/about-tor/introduction/what-is-tor/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/introduction/what-is-tor/
msgid ""
"It protects you by bouncing your communications around a distributed network "
"of relays run by volunteers all around the world: it prevents somebody "
"watching your Internet connection from learning what sites you visit, and it "
"prevents the sites you visit from learning your physical location."
msgstr ""
"Tor skyddar dig genom att låta kommunikationen studsa genom ett distribuerat "
"nätverk av reläer som drivs av volontärer över hela världen. Det hindrar den "
"som övervakar din internetanslutning från att ta reda på vilka webbplatser "
"du besöker och hindrar webbplatserna från att ta reda på var du befinner dig "
"fysiskt."

#: content/about-tor/introduction/what-is-tor/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/introduction/what-is-tor/
msgid ""
"The Tor Project is a non-profit (charity) organization that maintains and "
"develops the Tor software."
msgstr ""
"The Tor Project är en ideell organisation som underhåller och utvecklar Tor-"
"programvaran."

#: content/about-tor/introduction/what-is-tor/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/introduction/what-is-tor/
msgid ""
"The way most people use Tor is with Tor Browser, which is a version of "
"Firefox that fixes many privacy issues."
msgstr ""
"De flesta använder Tor med Tor Browser, en version av Firefox där många "
"integritetsproblem har åtgärdats."

#: content/about-tor/introduction/what-is-tor/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/introduction/what-is-tor/
msgid "This set of volunteer relays is called the Tor network."
msgstr "Denna uppsättning reläer som drivs av volontärer kallas Tor-nätverket."

#: content/about-tor/introduction/what-is-tor/contents.lr:content.content
#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/introduction/what-is-tor/
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"Tor is a program you can run on your computer that helps keep you safe on "
"the Internet."
msgstr ""
"Tor är ett program som du kan köra på datorn och som hjälper dig att vara "
"säker på internet."

#: content/about-tor/introduction/what-is-tor/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/introduction/what-is-tor/
msgid ""
"You can read more about Tor on our [about](https://www.torproject.org/about/"
"history/) page."
msgstr ""
"Du kan läsa mer om Tor på vår sida [om Tor](https://www.torproject.org/about/"
"history/)."

#: content/about-tor/introduction/who-funds-tor/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/introduction/who-funds-tor/
msgid ""
"The Tor Project is supported by a mix of government grants, private "
"foundations, and individual donors."
msgstr ""
"The Tor Project finansieras genom en blandning av statliga anslag, privata "
"stiftelser och enskilda givare."

#: content/about-tor/introduction/who-funds-tor/contents.lr:article.longer_title
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/introduction/who-funds-tor/
msgid "Who funds the Tor Project?"
msgstr "Vem finansierar The Tor Project?"

#: content/about-tor/introduction/who-funds-tor/contents.lr:article.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/introduction/who-funds-tor/
msgid "Funding the Tor Project"
msgstr "Finansiering av The Tor Project"

#: content/about-tor/introduction/who-funds-tor/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/introduction/who-funds-tor/
msgid ""
"Check out a list of all [our supporters](https://www.torproject.org/about/"
"supporters/) and a series of [blog posts](https://blog.torproject.org/"
"category/financials/) on our financial reports."
msgstr ""
"Se en lista över [alla våra bidragsgivare](https://www.torproject.org/about/"
"supporters/) och en serie [blogginlägg](https://blog.torproject.org/category/"
"financials/) om våra ekonomiska rapporter."

#: content/about-tor/introduction/who-funds-tor/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/introduction/who-funds-tor/
msgid ""
"The Tor Project is funded by a number of different sponsors including US "
"federal agencies, private foundations, and individual donors."
msgstr ""
"The Tor Project finansieras av flera olika sponsorer, däribland amerikanska "
"federala myndigheter, privata stiftelser och enskilda givare."

#: content/about-tor/introduction/who-funds-tor/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/introduction/who-funds-tor/
msgid ""
"We are always seeking more diversity in our funding sources, especially from "
"foundations and individuals."
msgstr ""
"Vi strävar alltid efter större mångfald bland finansieringskällorna, "
"särskilt genom stöd från stiftelser och enskilda personer."

#: content/about-tor/introduction/who-funds-tor/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/introduction/who-funds-tor/
msgid ""
"We feel that talking openly about our sponsors and funding model is the best "
"way to maintain trust with our community."
msgstr ""
"Vi anser att öppenhet om våra sponsorer och vår finansieringsmodell är det "
"bästa sättet att bevara gemenskapens förtroende."

#: content/about-tor/introduction/why-is-it-called-tor/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/introduction/why-is-it-called-tor/
msgid "Tor is not spelled \"TOR\", only the first letter is capitalized."
msgstr "Tor skrivs inte ”TOR”; bara den första bokstaven är versal."

#: content/about-tor/introduction/why-is-it-called-tor/contents.lr:article.longer_title
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/introduction/why-is-it-called-tor/
msgid "The origin of the name \"Tor\""
msgstr "Ursprunget till namnet ”Tor”"

#: content/about-tor/introduction/why-is-it-called-tor/contents.lr:article.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/introduction/why-is-it-called-tor/
msgid "Why is it called Tor?"
msgstr "Varför heter det Tor?"

#: content/about-tor/introduction/why-is-it-called-tor/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/introduction/why-is-it-called-tor/
msgid "(It's also got a fine meaning in German and Turkish.)"
msgstr "(Namnet har dessutom en bra betydelse på tyska och turkiska.)"

#: content/about-tor/introduction/why-is-it-called-tor/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/introduction/why-is-it-called-tor/
msgid ""
"Even if onion routing has become a standard household term, Tor was born out "
"of the actual [onion routing project](https://www.onion-router.net/) run by "
"the Naval Research Lab."
msgstr ""
"Även om onion-routing har blivit ett välkänt begrepp har Tor sitt ursprung i "
"det faktiska [onion-routingprojektet](https://www.onion-router.net/) vid "
"Naval Research Laboratory."

#: content/about-tor/introduction/why-is-it-called-tor/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/introduction/why-is-it-called-tor/
msgid ""
"In fact, we can usually spot people who haven't read any of our website (and "
"have instead learned everything they know about Tor from news articles) by "
"the fact that they spell it wrong."
msgstr ""
"Vi kan faktiskt ofta känna igen personer som inte har läst något på vår "
"webbplats (utan har lärt sig allt de vet om Tor från nyhetsartiklar) genom "
"att de skriver namnet fel."

#: content/about-tor/introduction/why-is-it-called-tor/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/introduction/why-is-it-called-tor/
msgid ""
"Note: even though it originally came from an acronym, Tor is not spelled "
"\"TOR\"."
msgstr ""
"Observera: även om namnet ursprungligen kommer från en akronym skrivs Tor "
"inte ”TOR”."

#: content/about-tor/introduction/why-is-it-called-tor/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/introduction/why-is-it-called-tor/
msgid "Only the first letter is capitalized."
msgstr "Endast den första bokstaven är versal."

#: content/about-tor/introduction/why-is-it-called-tor/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/introduction/why-is-it-called-tor/
msgid "Tor is the onion routing network."
msgstr "Tor är nätverket för onion-routing."

#: content/about-tor/introduction/why-is-it-called-tor/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/introduction/why-is-it-called-tor/
msgid ""
"When we were starting the new next-generation design and implementation of "
"onion routing in 2001-2002, we would tell people we were working on onion "
"routing, and they would say \"Neat. Which one?\""
msgstr ""
"När vi 2001–2002 började arbeta med nästa generations utformning och "
"implementering av onion-routing berättade vi för människor att vi arbetade "
"med onion-routing, och de svarade: ”Intressant. Vilken?”"

#: content/about-tor/onion-services/contents.lr:section.title
#: content/about-tor/onion-services/what-is-a-dot-onion/contents.lr:tab.title
#: content/contents.lr:internal_nav_item.title
#: content/tor-browser/features/onion-services/contents.lr:tab.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/onion-services/
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/onion-services/what-is-a-dot-onion/
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/features/onion-services/
msgid "Onion Services"
msgstr "Oniontjänster"

#: content/about-tor/onion-services/what-is-a-dot-onion/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/onion-services/what-is-a-dot-onion/
msgid ""
"Onion services use the special .onion domain to let people browse and "
"publish content anonymously through the Tor network."
msgstr ""
"Onion-tjänster använder den särskilda domänen .onion för att låta människor "
"surfa och publicera innehåll anonymt genom Tor-nätverket."

#: content/about-tor/onion-services/what-is-a-dot-onion/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/onion-services/what-is-a-dot-onion/
msgid ""
"They provide more private ways to host websites, share files, communicate, "
"and even access popular sites over secure Tor connections."
msgstr ""
"De ger mer privata sätt att vara värd för webbplatser, dela filer, "
"kommunicera och till och med nå populära webbplatser via säkra Tor-"
"anslutningar."

#: content/about-tor/onion-services/what-is-a-dot-onion/contents.lr:article.longer_title
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/onion-services/what-is-a-dot-onion/
msgid "Understanding .onion addresses and how onion services work"
msgstr "Förstå .onion-adresser och hur onion-tjänster fungerar"

#: content/about-tor/onion-services/what-is-a-dot-onion/contents.lr:article.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/onion-services/what-is-a-dot-onion/
msgid "What are .onion sites and onion services?"
msgstr "Vad är .onion-webbplatser och onion-tjänster?"

#: content/about-tor/onion-services/what-is-a-dot-onion/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/onion-services/what-is-a-dot-onion/
msgid ""
"A list of the Tor Project Onion Services is available at "
"[onion.torproject.org](https://onion.torproject.org)."
msgstr ""
"En lista över The Tor Projects onion-tjänster finns på [onion.torproject.org]"
"(https://onion.torproject.org)."

#: content/about-tor/onion-services/what-is-a-dot-onion/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/onion-services/what-is-a-dot-onion/
msgid ""
"Developers, researchers, and anyone curious about onion services can explore "
"the [Onion Services Ecosystem Documentation](https://"
"onionservices.torproject.org/), which brings together content from many "
"projects into a single searchable website for the wider Tor community."
msgstr ""
"Utvecklare, forskare och andra som är nyfikna på onion-tjänster kan utforska "
"[dokumentationen om ekosystemet för onion-tjänster](https://"
"onionservices.torproject.org/), som samlar innehåll från många projekt på en "
"enda sökbar webbplats för hela Tor-gemenskapen."

#: content/about-tor/onion-services/what-is-a-dot-onion/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/onion-services/what-is-a-dot-onion/
msgid ""
"Onion services allow people to browse but also to publish anonymously, "
"including publishing anonymous websites."
msgstr ""
"Onion-tjänster gör det möjligt för människor att både surfa och publicera "
"anonymt, inklusive att publicera anonyma webbplatser."

#: content/about-tor/onion-services/what-is-a-dot-onion/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/onion-services/what-is-a-dot-onion/
msgid ""
"Onion services are also relied on for metadata-free chat and file sharing, "
"safer interaction between journalists and their sources like with "
"[SecureDrop](https://securedrop.org/) or [OnionShare](https://"
"onionshare.org/), safer software updates, and more secure ways to reach "
"popular websites like [Facebook](https://www.facebook.com/notes/protect-the-"
"graph/making-connections-to-facebook-more-secure/1526085754298237/)."
msgstr ""
"Onion-tjänster används också för chatt och fildelning utan metadata, säkrare "
"kommunikation mellan journalister och deras källor genom exempelvis "
"[SecureDrop](https://securedrop.org/) och [OnionShare](https://"
"onionshare.org/), säkrare programuppdateringar och säkrare åtkomst till "
"populära webbplatser som [Facebook](https://www.facebook.com/notes/protect-"
"the-graph/making-connections-to-facebook-more-secure/1526085754298237/)."

#: content/about-tor/onion-services/what-is-a-dot-onion/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/onion-services/what-is-a-dot-onion/
msgid ""
"These services use the special-use top level domain (TLD) .onion (instead "
"of .com, .net, .org, etc.) and are only accessible through the Tor network."
msgstr ""
"Dessa tjänster använder den särskilda toppdomänen .onion (i stället "
"för .com, .net, .org och så vidare) och är endast åtkomliga genom Tor-"
"nätverket."

#: content/about-tor/onion-services/what-is-a-dot-onion/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/onion-services/what-is-a-dot-onion/
msgid ""
"To learn more about onion services, read [How do Onion Services work?]"
"(https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/overview/)"
msgstr ""
"Läs [Hur fungerar onion-tjänster?](https://community.torproject.org/onion-"
"services/overview/) om du vill veta mer"

#: content/about-tor/onion-services/what-is-a-dot-onion/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/onion-services/what-is-a-dot-onion/
msgid ""
"When accessing a website that uses an onion service, Tor Browser will show "
"at the URL bar an icon of an onion displaying the state of your connection: "
"secure and using an onion service."
msgstr ""
"När du besöker en webbplats som använder en onion-tjänst visar Tor Browser "
"en onion-ikon i adressfältet som anger anslutningens status: säker och "
"ansluten via en onion-tjänst."

#: content/about-tor/onion-services/what-is-a-dot-onion/contents.lr:figure.text
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/onion-services/what-is-a-dot-onion/
msgid ""
"Tor Browser's address bar showing an .onion address and the .onion security "
"icon."
msgstr ""
"Tor Browsers adressfält med en .onion-adress och säkerhetsikonen för .onion."

#: content/about-tor/security/attacks-on-onion-routing/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/security/attacks-on-onion-routing/
msgid ""
"While Tor significantly improves privacy and anonymity online, certain "
"attacks - such as traffic correlation, timing analysis, and circuit reuse - "
"can still pose risks under strong adversaries."
msgstr ""
"Tor förbättrar integriteten och anonymiteten på nätet avsevärt, men vissa "
"attacker – såsom trafikkorrelation, tidsanalys och återanvändning av kretsar "
"– kan fortfarande medföra risker när angriparen är stark."

#: content/about-tor/security/attacks-on-onion-routing/contents.lr:article.longer_title
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/security/attacks-on-onion-routing/
msgid "Limitations and remaining attacks against Tor's anonymity"
msgstr "Begränsningar och kvarstående attacker mot Tors anonymitet"

#: content/about-tor/security/attacks-on-onion-routing/contents.lr:article.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/security/attacks-on-onion-routing/
msgid "What attacks remain against onion routing?"
msgstr "Vilka attacker mot onion-routing återstår?"

#: content/about-tor/security/attacks-on-onion-routing/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/security/attacks-on-onion-routing/
msgid ""
"Again, this is only useful to verify that parties already suspected of "
"communicating with one another are doing so."
msgstr ""
"Även detta är endast användbart för att bekräfta att parter som redan "
"misstänks kommunicera med varandra faktiskt gör det."

#: content/about-tor/security/attacks-on-onion-routing/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/security/attacks-on-onion-routing/
msgid ""
"Furthermore, since Tor reuses circuits for multiple TCP connections, it is "
"possible to associate non anonymous and anonymous traffic at a given exit "
"node, so be careful about what applications you run concurrently over Tor."
msgstr ""
"Eftersom Tor återanvänder kretsar för flera TCP-anslutningar kan icke-anonym "
"och anonym trafik dessutom kopplas samman vid ett visst utgångsrelä. Var "
"därför försiktig med vilka program du kör samtidigt över Tor."

#: content/about-tor/security/attacks-on-onion-routing/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/security/attacks-on-onion-routing/
msgid ""
"In a more limited sense, note that if a censor or law enforcement agency has "
"the ability to obtain specific observation of parts of the network, it is "
"possible for them to verify a suspicion that you talk regularly to your "
"friend by observing traffic at both ends and correlating the timing of only "
"that traffic."
msgstr ""
"I en mer begränsad mening kan en censor eller brottsbekämpande myndighet som "
"kan övervaka specifika delar av nätverket bekräfta en misstanke om att du "
"regelbundet kommunicerar med en vän genom att observera trafiken i båda "
"ändarna och korrelera enbart tidpunkterna."

#: content/about-tor/security/attacks-on-onion-routing/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/security/attacks-on-onion-routing/
msgid ""
"In most countries, the suspicion required to obtain a warrant already "
"carries more weight than timing correlation would provide."
msgstr ""
"I de flesta länder har misstanken som krävs för att få ett beslut om "
"övervakning redan större bevisvärde än vad tidskorrelationen skulle ge."

#: content/about-tor/security/attacks-on-onion-routing/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/security/attacks-on-onion-routing/
msgid ""
"It is possible for an observer who can view both you and either the "
"destination website or your Tor exit node to correlate timings of your "
"traffic as it enters the Tor network and also as it exits."
msgstr ""
"En observatör som kan se både dig och antingen destinationswebbplatsen eller "
"ditt Tor-utgångsrelä kan korrelera tidpunkterna för trafiken när den går in "
"i och ut ur Tor-nätverket."

#: content/about-tor/security/attacks-on-onion-routing/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/security/attacks-on-onion-routing/
msgid "Perhaps even run separate Tor clients for these applications."
msgstr "Överväg till och med att köra separata Tor-klienter för dessa program."

#: content/about-tor/security/attacks-on-onion-routing/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/security/attacks-on-onion-routing/
msgid "Tor does not defend against such a threat model."
msgstr "Tor skyddar inte mot en sådan hotmodell."

#: content/about-tor/security/contents.lr:section.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/security/
msgid "Tor security"
msgstr "Tors säkerhet"

