#: content/about-tor/security/no-backdoor/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/security/no-backdoor/
msgid ""
"Tor has no backdoors. The software is open source, its code can be "
"independently audited, and every release is signed to protect against "
"tampering."
msgstr ""
"Tor har inga bakdörrar. Programvaran har öppen källkod, koden kan granskas "
"oberoende och varje utgåva signeras för att skydda mot manipulering."

#: content/about-tor/security/no-backdoor/contents.lr:article.longer_title
#: content/about-tor/security/no-backdoor/contents.lr:article.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/security/no-backdoor/
msgid "Is there a backdoor in Tor?"
msgstr "Finns det en bakdörr i Tor?"

#: content/about-tor/security/no-backdoor/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/security/no-backdoor/
msgid ""
"Also, there might be accidental bugs in Tor that could affect your anonymity."
msgstr ""
"Det kan också finnas oavsiktliga fel i Tor som påverkar din anonymitet."

#: content/about-tor/security/no-backdoor/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/security/no-backdoor/
msgid ""
"But that said, there are still plenty of subtle attacks people might try."
msgstr ""
"Trots detta finns det fortfarande många subtila attacker som människor kan "
"försöka genomföra."

#: content/about-tor/security/no-backdoor/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/security/no-backdoor/
msgid ""
"If they do ask us, we will fight them, and (the lawyers say) probably win."
msgstr ""
"Om någon ändå kräver det av oss kommer vi att bestrida det och, enligt "
"juristerna, sannolikt vinna."

#: content/about-tor/security/no-backdoor/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/security/no-backdoor/
msgid ""
"If we (or the distributors that gave you Tor) don't give you access to the "
"source code, that's a sure sign something funny might be going on."
msgstr ""
"Om vi (eller distributören som gav dig Tor) inte ger dig tillgång till "
"källkoden är det ett tydligt tecken på att något misstänkt kan pågå."

#: content/about-tor/security/no-backdoor/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/security/no-backdoor/
msgid ""
"If we ever put a deliberate backdoor in our security software, it would ruin "
"our professional reputation."
msgstr ""
"Om vi någonsin avsiktligt lade in en bakdörr i vår säkerhetsprogramvara "
"skulle det förstöra vårt professionella anseende."

#: content/about-tor/security/no-backdoor/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/security/no-backdoor/
msgid "Nobody would trust our software ever again - for excellent reasons!"
msgstr ""
"Ingen skulle någonsin lita på vår programvara igen – av mycket goda skäl!"

#: content/about-tor/security/no-backdoor/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/security/no-backdoor/
msgid ""
"Somebody might impersonate us, or break into our computers, or something "
"like that."
msgstr ""
"Någon kan utge sig för att vara oss, göra intrång i våra datorer eller göra "
"något liknande."

#: content/about-tor/security/no-backdoor/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/security/no-backdoor/
msgid "There is absolutely no backdoor in Tor."
msgstr "Det finns absolut ingen bakdörr i Tor."

#: content/about-tor/security/no-backdoor/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/security/no-backdoor/
msgid ""
"Tor is open source, and you should always check the source (or at least the "
"diffs since the last release) for suspicious things."
msgstr ""
"Tor har öppen källkod, och du bör alltid kontrollera källkoden (eller "
"åtminstone skillnaderna sedan den förra utgåvan) efter misstänkta ändringar."

#: content/about-tor/security/no-backdoor/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/security/no-backdoor/
msgid ""
"We know some smart lawyers who say that it is unlikely that anybody will try "
"to make us add one in our jurisdiction (United States)."
msgstr ""
"Vi känner skickliga jurister som säger att det är osannolikt att någon inom "
"vår jurisdiktion (USA) försöker tvinga oss att lägga till en bakdörr."

#: content/about-tor/security/no-backdoor/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/security/no-backdoor/
msgid ""
"We periodically find and fix anonymity-related bugs, so make sure you keep "
"your Tor versions up-to-date."
msgstr ""
"Vi hittar och rättar regelbundet fel som rör anonymitet, så se till att "
"hålla din Tor-version uppdaterad."

#: content/about-tor/security/no-backdoor/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/security/no-backdoor/
msgid ""
"We think that putting a backdoor in Tor would be tremendously irresponsible "
"to our users, and a bad precedent for security software in general."
msgstr ""
"Vi anser att en bakdörr i Tor skulle vara ytterst oansvarig gentemot "
"användarna och skapa ett dåligt prejudikat för säkerhetsprogramvara i "
"allmänhet."

#: content/about-tor/security/no-backdoor/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/security/no-backdoor/
msgid "We will never put a backdoor in Tor."
msgstr "Vi kommer aldrig att lägga in en bakdörr i Tor."

#: content/about-tor/security/no-backdoor/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/security/no-backdoor/
msgid ""
"You should also check the PGP signatures on the releases, to make sure "
"nobody messed with the distribution sites."
msgstr ""
"Du bör också kontrollera utgåvornas PGP-signaturer för att säkerställa att "
"ingen har manipulerat distributionswebbplatserna."

#: content/about-tor/using-and-sharing/circuit-length/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/using-and-sharing/circuit-length/
msgid ""
"This article explains why the path length is fixed and why making it longer "
"doesn't improve security."
msgstr ""
"Artikeln förklarar varför vägens längd är fast och varför en längre väg inte "
"förbättrar säkerheten."

#: content/about-tor/using-and-sharing/circuit-length/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/using-and-sharing/circuit-length/
msgid "Tor circuits normally use three relays by design."
msgstr "Tor-kretsar använder normalt tre reläer, avsiktligt."

#: content/about-tor/using-and-sharing/circuit-length/contents.lr:article.longer_title
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/using-and-sharing/circuit-length/
msgid "Can I change the number of hops Tor uses?"
msgstr "Kan jag ändra antalet hopp som Tor använder?"

#: content/about-tor/using-and-sharing/circuit-length/contents.lr:article.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/using-and-sharing/circuit-length/
msgid "Changing the number of Tor hops"
msgstr "Ändra antalet Tor-hopp"

#: content/about-tor/using-and-sharing/circuit-length/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/using-and-sharing/circuit-length/
msgid ""
"Also, using paths longer than three could harm anonymity, first because it "
"makes [denial of security](https://www.freehaven.net/anonbib/#ccs07-doa) "
"attacks easier, and second because it could act as an identifier if only a "
"small number of users have the same path length as you."
msgstr ""
"Vägar med fler än tre hopp kan dessutom försämra anonymiteten, dels eftersom "
"de gör attacker med [förnekad säkerhet](https://www.freehaven.net/anonbib/"
"#ccs07-doa) enklare, dels eftersom väglängden kan fungera som identifierare "
"om få användare har samma längd som du."

#: content/about-tor/using-and-sharing/circuit-length/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/using-and-sharing/circuit-length/
msgid ""
"If we made two-hop paths, then a relay on either end of the circuit would "
"know which relay it needs to attack (whether break into, collaborate with, "
"or maybe just surveil) in order to identify the user."
msgstr ""
"Om vi använde vägar med två hopp skulle ett relä i någon av kretsens ändar "
"veta vilket annat relä som måste angripas (genom intrång, samarbete eller "
"kanske bara övervakning) för att identifiera användaren."

#: content/about-tor/using-and-sharing/circuit-length/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/using-and-sharing/circuit-length/
msgid ""
"Right now the path length is hard-coded at three (except if you're accessing "
"an onion service)."
msgstr ""
"För närvarande är väglängden hårdkodad till tre hopp (utom när du ansluter "
"till en onion-tjänst)."

#: content/about-tor/using-and-sharing/circuit-length/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/using-and-sharing/circuit-length/
msgid ""
"We don't want to encourage people to use paths longer than this as it "
"increases load on the network without (as far as we can tell) providing any "
"more security."
msgstr ""
"Vi vill inte uppmuntra människor att använda längre vägar eftersom det ökar "
"belastningen på nätverket utan att, såvitt vi kan se, ge bättre säkerhet."

#: content/about-tor/using-and-sharing/circuit-length/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/using-and-sharing/circuit-length/
msgid ""
"Whereas with three-hop paths, a relay on one end doesn't immediately know "
"which relay they would need to attack, increasing the cost, effort, and "
"uncertainty of an attack."
msgstr ""
"Med vägar på tre hopp vet ett relä i ena änden däremot inte omedelbart "
"vilket relä som måste angripas, vilket ökar kostnaden, arbetsinsatsen och "
"osäkerheten för angriparen."

#: content/about-tor/using-and-sharing/circuit-length/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/using-and-sharing/circuit-length/
msgid "Why not longer?"
msgstr "Varför inte längre?"

#: content/about-tor/using-and-sharing/circuit-length/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/using-and-sharing/circuit-length/
msgid "Why not shorter?"
msgstr "Varför inte kortare?"

#: content/about-tor/using-and-sharing/circuit-length/contents.lr:tab.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/using-and-sharing/circuit-length/
msgid "Tor circuit"
msgstr "Tor-krets"

#: content/about-tor/using-and-sharing/contents.lr:section.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/using-and-sharing/
msgid "Using Tor and redistributing it"
msgstr "Använda och vidaredistribuera Tor"

#: content/about-tor/using-and-sharing/contents.lr:section.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/using-and-sharing/
msgid "Using and sharing"
msgstr "Användning och delning"

#: content/about-tor/using-and-sharing/distributing/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/using-and-sharing/distributing/
msgid "Tor is free software."
msgstr "Tor är fri programvara."

#: content/about-tor/using-and-sharing/distributing/contents.lr:article.longer_title
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/using-and-sharing/distributing/
msgid "Can I distribute Tor?"
msgstr "Får jag distribuera Tor?"

#: content/about-tor/using-and-sharing/distributing/contents.lr:article.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/using-and-sharing/distributing/
msgid "Distributing Tor"
msgstr "Distribuera Tor"

#: content/about-tor/using-and-sharing/distributing/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/using-and-sharing/distributing/
msgid ""
"Also, you should make sure not to confuse your readers about what Tor is, "
"who makes it, and what properties it provides (and doesn't provide)."
msgstr ""
"Du bör också se till att läsarna inte får en felaktig bild av vad Tor är, "
"vem som utvecklar det och vilket skydd det ger (och inte ger)."

#: content/about-tor/using-and-sharing/distributing/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/using-and-sharing/distributing/
msgid ""
"Essentially this means that you need to include our LICENSE file along with "
"whatever part of the Tor software you're distributing."
msgstr ""
"I praktiken innebär det att filen LICENSE måste följa med den del av Tor-"
"programvaran som du distribuerar."

#: content/about-tor/using-and-sharing/distributing/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/using-and-sharing/distributing/
msgid ""
"However, if you want to redistribute the Tor software you must follow our "
"[LICENSE](https://gitlab.torproject.org/tpo/core/tor/-/raw/HEAD/LICENSE)."
msgstr ""
"Om du vill vidaredistribuera Tor-programvaran måste du dock följa vår "
"[LICENS](https://gitlab.torproject.org/tpo/core/tor/-/raw/HEAD/LICENSE)."

#: content/about-tor/using-and-sharing/distributing/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/using-and-sharing/distributing/
msgid ""
"Most people who ask us this question don't want to distribute just the Tor "
"software, though."
msgstr ""
"De flesta som ställer frågan vill dock inte bara distribuera Tor-"
"programvaran."

#: content/about-tor/using-and-sharing/distributing/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/using-and-sharing/distributing/
msgid ""
"NoScript extension is distributed under the [GNU General Public License]"
"(https://github.com/hackademix/noscript/blob/main/LICENSE), while Firefox "
"ESR is released under the [Mozilla Public License](https://www.mozilla.org/"
"MPL/)."
msgstr ""
"Tillägget NoScript distribueras under [GNU General Public License](https://"
"github.com/hackademix/noscript/blob/main/LICENSE), medan Firefox ESR ges ut "
"under [Mozilla Public License](https://www.mozilla.org/MPL/)."

#: content/about-tor/using-and-sharing/distributing/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/using-and-sharing/distributing/
msgid ""
"See our [trademark FAQ](https://www.torproject.org/about/trademark/) for "
"details."
msgstr ""
"Mer information finns i våra [vanliga frågor om varumärken](https://"
"www.torproject.org/about/trademark/)."

#: content/about-tor/using-and-sharing/distributing/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/using-and-sharing/distributing/
msgid ""
"The Tor software is [free software](https://wikipedia.org/wiki/"
"Free_software)."
msgstr ""
"Tor-programvaran är [fri programvara](https://wikipedia.org/wiki/"
"Free_software)."

#: content/about-tor/using-and-sharing/distributing/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/using-and-sharing/distributing/
msgid ""
"The simplest way to obey their licenses is to include the source code for "
"these programs everywhere you include the bundles themselves."
msgstr ""
"Det enklaste sättet att följa licenserna är att inkludera källkoden till "
"dessa program överallt där programpaketen ingår."

#: content/about-tor/using-and-sharing/distributing/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/using-and-sharing/distributing/
msgid "They want to distribute Tor Browser."
msgstr "De vill distribuera Tor Browser."

#: content/about-tor/using-and-sharing/distributing/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/using-and-sharing/distributing/
msgid ""
"This includes [Firefox Extended Support Release](https://www.mozilla.org/en-"
"US/firefox/organizations/) and the [NoScript](https://noscript.net/) "
"extension."
msgstr ""
"Det omfattar [Firefox Extended Support Release](https://www.mozilla.org/en-"
"US/firefox/organizations/) och tillägget [NoScript](https://noscript.net/)."

#: content/about-tor/using-and-sharing/distributing/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/using-and-sharing/distributing/
msgid ""
"This means we give you the rights to redistribute the Tor software, either "
"modified or unmodified, either for a fee or gratis."
msgstr ""
"Det innebär att vi ger dig rätt att vidaredistribuera Tor-programvaran, "
"ändrad eller oförändrad, mot betalning eller kostnadsfritt."

#: content/about-tor/using-and-sharing/distributing/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/using-and-sharing/distributing/
msgid "You don't have to ask us for specific permission."
msgstr "Du behöver inte be oss om särskilt tillstånd."

#: content/about-tor/using-and-sharing/distributing/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/using-and-sharing/distributing/
msgid "You will need to follow the license for those programs as well."
msgstr "Du måste även följa licenserna för de programmen."

#: content/about-tor/using-and-sharing/hosting/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/using-and-sharing/hosting/
msgid ""
"The Tor Project develops privacy and anonymity software, but it does not run "
"email, hosting, or other online services."
msgstr ""
"The Tor Project utvecklar programvara för integritet och anonymitet men "
"driver inte e-post-, webbhotells- eller andra nättjänster."

#: content/about-tor/using-and-sharing/hosting/contents.lr:article.longer_title
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/using-and-sharing/hosting/
msgid ""
"Does Tor Project offer email service or other privacy protecting web "
"services?"
msgstr ""
"Erbjuder The Tor Project e-post eller andra integritetsskyddande "
"webbtjänster?"

#: content/about-tor/using-and-sharing/hosting/contents.lr:article.title
#: content/about-tor/using-and-sharing/hosting/contents.lr:tab.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/using-and-sharing/hosting/
msgid "About our services"
msgstr "Om våra tjänster"

#: content/about-tor/using-and-sharing/hosting/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/using-and-sharing/hosting/
msgid ""
"A list of all of our software projects can be found on our [projects page]"
"(https://www.torproject.org/projects/projects.html.en)."
msgstr ""
"En lista över alla våra programvaruprojekt finns på vår [projektsida]"
"(https://www.torproject.org/projects/projects.html.en)."

#: content/about-tor/using-and-sharing/hosting/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/using-and-sharing/hosting/
msgid ""
"Our work focuses on developing and maintaining privacy-enhancing software "
"like Tor Browser and related tools."
msgstr ""
"Vårt arbete är inriktat på att utveckla och underhålla "
"integritetsförbättrande programvara som Tor Browser och närliggande verktyg."

#: content/about-tor/using-and-sharing/hosting/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/using-and-sharing/hosting/
msgid ""
"The Tor Project does not provide hosting, messaging app, email solutions, or "
"any other online services."
msgstr ""
"The Tor Project tillhandahåller inte webbhotell, meddelandeappar, e-"
"postlösningar eller andra nättjänster."

#: content/about-tor/using-and-sharing/no-logs/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/using-and-sharing/no-logs/
msgid ""
"Only limited, privacy-preserving measurements are gathered to monitor the "
"health of the Tor network."
msgstr ""
"Endast begränsade mätningar som bevarar integriteten samlas in för att "
"övervaka Tor-nätverkets hälsa."

#: content/about-tor/using-and-sharing/no-logs/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/using-and-sharing/no-logs/
msgid ""
"The Tor Project does not collect logs that could identify a particular user."
msgstr ""
"The Tor Project samlar inte in loggar som kan identifiera en viss användare."

#: content/about-tor/using-and-sharing/no-logs/contents.lr:article.longer_title
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/using-and-sharing/no-logs/
msgid "Does the Tor Project keep logs of its users?"
msgstr "Sparar The Tor Project loggar över sina användare?"

#: content/about-tor/using-and-sharing/no-logs/contents.lr:article.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/using-and-sharing/no-logs/
msgid "Does Tor Project keep logs?"
msgstr "Sparar The Tor Project loggar?"

#: content/about-tor/using-and-sharing/no-logs/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/using-and-sharing/no-logs/
msgid ""
"The Tor Project doesn't keep any logs that could identify a particular user."
msgstr ""
"The Tor Project sparar inga loggar som kan identifiera en viss användare."

#: content/about-tor/using-and-sharing/no-logs/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/using-and-sharing/no-logs/
msgid ""
"We do take some safe measurements of how the network functions, which you "
"can check out at [Tor Metrics](https://metrics.torproject.org/)."
msgstr ""
"Vi gör vissa säkra mätningar av hur nätverket fungerar. Du kan se dem på "
"[Tor Metrics](https://metrics.torproject.org/)."

#: content/about-tor/using-and-sharing/no-logs/contents.lr:tab.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/using-and-sharing/no-logs/
msgid "No logs"
msgstr "Inga loggar"

#: content/about-tor/using-and-sharing/onionshare/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/using-and-sharing/onionshare/
msgid ""
"OnionShare lets you securely and anonymously send or receive files over Tor "
"for free and without third-party services or accounts."
msgstr ""
"Med OnionShare kan du säkert och anonymt skicka eller ta emot filer över "
"Tor, kostnadsfritt och utan tredjepartstjänster eller konton."

#: content/about-tor/using-and-sharing/onionshare/contents.lr:article.longer_title
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/using-and-sharing/onionshare/
msgid "How can I share files anonymously through Tor?"
msgstr "Hur kan jag dela filer anonymt genom Tor?"

#: content/about-tor/using-and-sharing/onionshare/contents.lr:article.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/using-and-sharing/onionshare/
msgid "Sharing files with OnionShare"
msgstr "Dela filer med OnionShare"

#: content/about-tor/using-and-sharing/onionshare/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/using-and-sharing/onionshare/
msgid ""
"For sharing files over Tor, [OnionShare](https://onionshare.org/) is a good "
"option."
msgstr ""
"[OnionShare](https://onionshare.org/) är ett bra alternativ för att dela "
"filer över Tor."

#: content/about-tor/using-and-sharing/onionshare/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/using-and-sharing/onionshare/
msgid ""
"It doesn't require setting up a separate server, using a third party file-"
"sharing service, or even logging into an account."
msgstr ""
"Du behöver inte konfigurera en separat server, använda en fildelningstjänst "
"från tredje part eller ens logga in på ett konto."

#: content/about-tor/using-and-sharing/onionshare/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/using-and-sharing/onionshare/
msgid ""
"It works by starting a web server directly on your computer and making it "
"accessible as an unguessable Tor web address that others can load in Tor "
"Browser to download files from you, or upload files to you."
msgstr ""
"OnionShare startar en webbserver direkt på datorn och gör den åtkomlig via "
"en Tor-URL som inte går att gissa. Andra kan öppna URL:en i Tor Browser för "
"att hämta filer från dig eller överföra filer till dig."

#: content/about-tor/using-and-sharing/onionshare/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/using-and-sharing/onionshare/
msgid ""
"OnionShare is an open source tool for securely and anonymously sending and "
"receiving files using Tor onion services."
msgstr ""
"OnionShare är ett verktyg med öppen källkod för att säkert och anonymt "
"skicka och ta emot filer med hjälp av Tors onion-tjänster."

#: content/about-tor/using-and-sharing/onionshare/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/using-and-sharing/onionshare/
msgid ""
"OnionShare is developed by [Micah Lee](https://github.com/micahflee/"
"onionshare)."
msgstr ""
"OnionShare utvecklas av [Micah Lee](https://github.com/micahflee/onionshare)."

#: content/about-tor/using-and-sharing/onionshare/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/using-and-sharing/onionshare/
msgid ""
"So long as you share the unguessable web address in a secure way (like "
"pasting it in an encrypted messaging app), no one but you and the person "
"you're sharing with can access the files."
msgstr ""
"Så länge du delar den svårgissade URL:en på ett säkert sätt, exempelvis "
"genom en krypterad meddelandeapp, kan endast du och personen du delar med "
"komma åt filerna."

#: content/about-tor/using-and-sharing/onionshare/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/using-and-sharing/onionshare/
msgid ""
"Unlike services like email, Google Drive, DropBox, WeTransfer, or nearly any "
"other way people typically send files to each other, when you use OnionShare "
"you don't give any companies access to the files that you're sharing."
msgstr ""
"Till skillnad från e-post, Google Drive, Dropbox, WeTransfer och nästan alla "
"andra vanliga sätt att skicka filer ger OnionShare inga företag åtkomst till "
"filerna du delar."

#: content/about-tor/using-and-sharing/onionshare/contents.lr:tab.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/using-and-sharing/onionshare/
msgid "OnionShare"
msgstr "OnionShare"

#: content/about-tor/using-and-sharing/torifying/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/using-and-sharing/torifying/
msgid ""
"Other programs may work with Tor, but they require careful setup and can "
"introduce anonymity risks."
msgstr ""
"Andra program kan fungera med Tor, men de kräver noggrann konfigurering och "
"kan medföra risker för anonymiteten."

#: content/about-tor/using-and-sharing/torifying/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/using-and-sharing/torifying/
msgid ""
"While Tor can be used with many applications, only Tor Browser is configured "
"for safe browsing by default."
msgstr ""
"Tor kan användas med många program, men endast Tor Browser är som standard "
"konfigurerad för säker webbsurfning."

#: content/about-tor/using-and-sharing/torifying/contents.lr:article.longer_title
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/using-and-sharing/torifying/
msgid "What programs can I use with Tor?"
msgstr "Vilka program kan jag använda med Tor?"

#: content/about-tor/using-and-sharing/torifying/contents.lr:article.title
#: content/about-tor/using-and-sharing/torifying/contents.lr:tab.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/using-and-sharing/torifying/
msgid "Using Tor"
msgstr "Använda Tor"

#: content/about-tor/using-and-sharing/torifying/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/using-and-sharing/torifying/
msgid ""
"Most people use Tor Browser, which includes everything you need to browse "
"the web safely using Tor."
msgstr ""
"De flesta använder Tor Browser, som innehåller allt du behöver för att surfa "
"säkert med Tor."

#: content/about-tor/using-and-sharing/torifying/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/using-and-sharing/torifying/
msgid ""
"Our wiki has a community-maintained list of instructions for [Torifying "
"specific applications](https://gitlab.torproject.org/legacy/trac/-/wikis/doc/"
"TorifyHOWTO)."
msgstr ""
"Vår wiki innehåller en gemenskapsunderhållen lista med anvisningar för att "
"[Tor-anpassa specifika program](https://gitlab.torproject.org/legacy/trac/-/"
"wikis/doc/TorifyHOWTO)."

#: content/about-tor/using-and-sharing/torifying/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/using-and-sharing/torifying/
msgid ""
"There are plenty of other programs you can use with Tor, but we haven't "
"researched the application-level anonymity issues on all of them well enough "
"to be able to recommend a safe configuration."
msgstr ""
"Det finns många andra program som kan användas med Tor, men vi har inte "
"undersökt anonymitetsproblemen på programnivå tillräckligt väl för att kunna "
"rekommendera en säker konfiguration."

#: content/about-tor/using-and-sharing/torifying/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/using-and-sharing/torifying/
msgid "Using Tor with other browsers is dangerous and not recommended."
msgstr ""
"Det är farligt och rekommenderas inte att använda Tor med andra webbläsare."

#: content/about-tor/using-and-sharing/torrent/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/using-and-sharing/torrent/
msgid "Using Torrent clients over Tor is unsafe and not recommended."
msgstr ""
"Det är osäkert och rekommenderas inte att använda BitTorrent-klienter över "
"Tor."

#: content/about-tor/using-and-sharing/torrent/contents.lr:article.longer_title
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/using-and-sharing/torrent/
msgid "Can I use Tor with Torrent?"
msgstr "Kan jag använda Tor med BitTorrent?"

#: content/about-tor/using-and-sharing/torrent/contents.lr:article.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/using-and-sharing/torrent/
msgid "Tor with Torrent"
msgstr "Tor med BitTorrent"

#: content/about-tor/using-and-sharing/torrent/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/using-and-sharing/torrent/
msgid ""
"For further details, please see our [blog post on the subject](https://"
"blog.torproject.org/bittorrent-over-tor-isnt-good-idea)."
msgstr ""
"Mer information finns i vårt [blogginlägg om ämnet](https://"
"blog.torproject.org/bittorrent-over-tor-isnt-good-idea)."

#: content/about-tor/using-and-sharing/torrent/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/using-and-sharing/torrent/
msgid ""
"Most torrent clients reveal your real IP address to peers, which can "
"deanonymize you even if you're connected through Tor."
msgstr ""
"De flesta BitTorrent-klienter avslöjar din verkliga IP-adress för andra "
"deltagare, vilket kan avanonymisera dig även när du är ansluten genom Tor."

#: content/about-tor/using-and-sharing/torrent/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/using-and-sharing/torrent/
msgid ""
"Torrenting through Tor puts unnecessary load and potential legal issues on "
"volunteer exit relay operators."
msgstr ""
"BitTorrent-trafik genom Tor belastar volontärernas utgångsreläer i onödan "
"och kan medföra juridiska problem för operatörerna."

#: content/about-tor/using-and-sharing/torrent/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/using-and-sharing/torrent/
msgid "We do not recommend using Tor with Torrent."
msgstr "Vi rekommenderar inte att Tor används med BitTorrent."

#: content/about-tor/using-and-sharing/torrent/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/using-and-sharing/torrent/
msgid ""
"While it may seem like a way to stay anonymous, in practice it creates "
"serious problems:"
msgstr ""
"Det kan verka som ett sätt att förbli anonym, men i praktiken skapar det "
"allvarliga problem:"

#: content/about-tor/using-and-sharing/torrent/contents.lr:tab.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/using-and-sharing/torrent/
msgid "Torrent"
msgstr "BitTorrent"

#: content/abuse/ban-tor/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/ban-tor/
msgid ""
"This article explains when and how you might block Tor connections, outlines "
"alternatives to a full ban, and highlights the potential impact on "
"legitimate users and abuse management."
msgstr ""
"Artikeln förklarar när och hur du kan blockera Tor-anslutningar, beskriver "
"alternativ till en fullständig blockering och belyser den möjliga påverkan "
"på legitima användare och hantering av missbruk."

#: content/abuse/ban-tor/contents.lr:article.longer_title
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/ban-tor/
msgid "How to block or restrict Tor users from accessing your service"
msgstr "Så blockerar eller begränsar du Tor-användares åtkomst till din tjänst"

#: content/abuse/ban-tor/contents.lr:article.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/ban-tor/
msgid "Banning Tor"
msgstr "Blockera Tor"

#: content/abuse/ban-tor/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/ban-tor/
msgid ""
"(Often people don't have a good measure of how many polite Tor users are "
"connecting to their service — you never notice them until there's an "
"impolite one.)"
msgstr ""
"(Ofta har människor inget bra mått på hur många skötsamma Tor-användare som "
"ansluter till tjänsten – de märks inte förrän någon missköter sig.)"

#: content/abuse/ban-tor/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/ban-tor/
msgid ""
"(Some system administrators block ranges of IP addresses because of official "
"policy or some abuse pattern, but some have also asked about allowing Tor "
"exit relays because they want to permit access to their systems only using "
"Tor."
msgstr ""
"(Vissa systemadministratörer blockerar IP-adressintervall på grund av "
"officiella policyer eller missbruksmönster, men andra har frågat om att "
"tillåta Tor-utgångsreläer eftersom de endast vill ge åtkomst till sina "
"system genom Tor."

#: content/abuse/ban-tor/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/ban-tor/
msgid ""
"At this point, you should also ask yourself what you do about other services "
"that aggregate many users behind a few IP addresses."
msgstr ""
"Nu bör du också fråga dig hur du hanterar andra tjänster som samlar många "
"användare bakom ett fåtal IP-adresser."

#: content/abuse/ban-tor/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/ban-tor/
msgid ""
"But in many cases, there are easier solutions that can solve your problem "
"while still allowing users to access your website securely."
msgstr ""
"I många fall finns det dock enklare lösningar som kan lösa problemet och "
"samtidigt låta användare få säker åtkomst till webbplatsen."

#: content/abuse/ban-tor/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/ban-tor/
msgid ""
"First, ask yourself if there's a way to do application-level decisions to "
"separate the legitimate users from the jerks."
msgstr ""
"Fråga dig först om du kan fatta beslut på programnivå för att skilja "
"legitima användare från dem som missköter sig."

#: content/abuse/ban-tor/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/ban-tor/
msgid ""
"For example, the Freenode IRC network had a problem with a coordinated group "
"of abusers joining channels and subtly taking over the conversation; but "
"when they labeled all users coming from Tor nodes as \"anonymous users\", "
"removing the ability of the abusers to blend in, the abusers moved back to "
"using their open proxies and bot networks."
msgstr ""
"IRC-nätverket Freenode hade till exempel problem med en samordnad grupp "
"missbrukare som anslöt till kanaler och diskret tog över samtalet. När alla "
"användare från Tor-noder märktes som ”anonyma användare”, så att "
"missbrukarna inte längre kunde smälta in, återgick de till öppna "
"proxyservrar och botnät."

#: content/abuse/ban-tor/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/ban-tor/
msgid ""
"For example, you might have certain areas of the site, or certain privileges "
"like posting, available only to people who are registered."
msgstr ""
"Du kan till exempel göra vissa delar av webbplatsen eller vissa rättigheter, "
"som att publicera inlägg, tillgängliga endast för registrerade personer."

#: content/abuse/ban-tor/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/ban-tor/
msgid ""
"If you really want to do this, we provide a [Tor exit relay list](https://"
"check.torproject.org/cgi-bin/TorBulkExitList.py) or a [DNS-based list you "
"can query](https://2019.www.torproject.org/projects/tordnsel.html.en)."
msgstr ""
"Om du verkligen vill göra detta tillhandahåller vi en [lista över Tor-"
"utgångsreläer](https://check.torproject.org/cgi-bin/TorBulkExitList.py) och "
"en [DNS-baserad lista som kan frågas](https://2019.www.torproject.org/"
"projects/tordnsel.html.en)."

#: content/abuse/ban-tor/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/ban-tor/
msgid ""
"It's easy to build an up-to-date list of Tor IP addresses that allow "
"connections to your service, so you could set up this distinction only for "
"Tor users."
msgstr ""
"Det är enkelt att skapa en aktuell lista över Tor-IP-adresser som tillåter "
"anslutningar till din tjänst, så du kan använda denna åtskillnad enbart för "
"Tor-användare."

#: content/abuse/ban-tor/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/ban-tor/
msgid "Lastly, please remember that Tor relays have individual exit policies."
msgstr "Kom slutligen ihåg att Tor-reläer har individuella utgångspolicyer."

#: content/abuse/ban-tor/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/ban-tor/
msgid "Many Tor relays do not allow exiting connections at all."
msgstr "Många Tor-reläer tillåter inga utgående anslutningar alls."

#: content/abuse/ban-tor/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/ban-tor/
msgid ""
"Many of those that do allow some exit connections might already disallow "
"connections to your service."
msgstr ""
"Många av de reläer som tillåter vissa utgående anslutningar kanske redan "
"förbjuder anslutningar till din tjänst."

#: content/abuse/ban-tor/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/ban-tor/
msgid ""
"Others use Tor because it's their only way to get past restrictive local "
"firewalls."
msgstr ""
"Andra använder Tor eftersom det är deras enda sätt att ta sig förbi "
"restriktiva lokala brandväggar."

#: content/abuse/ban-tor/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/ban-tor/
msgid ""
"Second, consider that hundreds of thousands of people use Tor every day "
"simply for good data hygiene — for example, to protect against data-"
"gathering advertising companies while going about their normal activities."
msgstr ""
"Tänk också på att hundratusentals människor använder Tor varje dag enbart "
"för god datahygien, till exempel för att skydda sig mot datainsamlande "
"reklamföretag när de utför sina vanliga aktiviteter."

#: content/abuse/ban-tor/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/ban-tor/
msgid ""
"Some Tor users may be legitimately connecting to your service right now to "
"carry on normal activities."
msgstr ""
"Vissa Tor-användare kan just nu ansluta till din tjänst av helt legitima "
"skäl för att utföra vanliga aktiviteter."

#: content/abuse/ban-tor/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/ban-tor/
msgid ""
"There are some situations where it makes sense to block anonymous users for "
"an Internet service."
msgstr ""
"I vissa situationer är det rimligt att blockera anonyma användare från en "
"internettjänst."

#: content/abuse/ban-tor/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/ban-tor/
msgid "These scripts are usable for allowlisting as well.)"
msgstr "Skripten kan även användas för tillåtelselistor.)"

#: content/abuse/ban-tor/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/ban-tor/
msgid ""
"This way you can have multi-tiered access and not have to ban every aspect "
"of your service."
msgstr ""
"På så sätt kan du erbjuda åtkomst på flera nivåer utan att behöva blockera "
"alla delar av tjänsten."

#: content/abuse/ban-tor/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/ban-tor/
msgid "Tor is not so different from AOL in this respect."
msgstr "I detta avseende skiljer sig Tor inte så mycket från AOL."

#: content/abuse/ban-tor/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/ban-tor/
msgid "We're sorry to hear that."
msgstr "Vi är ledsna att höra det."

#: content/abuse/ban-tor/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/ban-tor/
msgid ""
"When you go about banning nodes, you should parse the exit policies and only "
"block the ones that allow these connections; and you should keep in mind "
"that exit policies can change (as well as the overall list of nodes in the "
"network)."
msgstr ""
"När du blockerar noder bör du tolka deras utgångspolicyer och endast "
"blockera dem som tillåter dessa anslutningar. Kom också ihåg att både "
"utgångspolicyerna och den övergripande listan över nätverkets noder kan "
"ändras."

#: content/abuse/ban-tor/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/ban-tor/
msgid ""
"You need to decide whether banning the Tor network is worth losing the "
"contributions of these users, as well as potential future legitimate users."
msgstr ""
"Du måste avgöra om en blockering av Tor-nätverket är värd att förlora "
"bidragen från dessa användare och möjliga framtida legitima användare."

#: content/abuse/contents.lr:section.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/
msgid "Abuse FAQ"
msgstr "Vanliga frågor om missbruk"

#: content/abuse/help-trace-tor-user/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/help-trace-tor-user/
msgid ""
"Tor's design prevents anyone - including its own developers - from tracing "
"users."
msgstr ""
"Tors utformning hindrar alla – även de egna utvecklarna – från att spåra "
"användare."

#: content/abuse/help-trace-tor-user/contents.lr:article.longer_title
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/help-trace-tor-user/
msgid "I have a compelling reason to trace a Tor user. Can you help?"
msgstr "Jag har ett starkt skäl att spåra en Tor-användare. Kan ni hjälpa mig?"

#: content/abuse/help-trace-tor-user/contents.lr:article.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/help-trace-tor-user/
msgid "Can the Tor Project trace users?"
msgstr "Kan The Tor Project spåra användare?"

#: content/abuse/help-trace-tor-user/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/help-trace-tor-user/
msgid "But remember that this doesn't mean that Tor is invulnerable."
msgstr "Kom dock ihåg att detta inte betyder att Tor är osårbart."

#: content/abuse/help-trace-tor-user/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/help-trace-tor-user/
msgid "First, it technically weakens the system too far."
msgstr ""
"För det första skulle det försvaga systemet alldeles för mycket rent "
"tekniskt."

#: content/abuse/help-trace-tor-user/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/help-trace-tor-user/
msgid ""
"Having a central way to link users to their activities is a gaping hole for "
"all sorts of attackers; and the policy mechanisms needed to ensure correct "
"handling of this responsibility are enormous and unsolved."
msgstr ""
"Ett centralt sätt att koppla användare till deras aktiviteter skulle vara "
"ett enormt säkerhetshål för alla slags angripare. De policy- och "
"kontrollmekanismer som skulle krävas för att hantera ansvaret korrekt är "
"dessutom mycket omfattande och olösta."

#: content/abuse/help-trace-tor-user/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/help-trace-tor-user/
msgid ""
"Second, the [bad people aren't going to get caught by this anyway](../what-"
"about-criminals/), since they will use other means to ensure their anonymity "
"(identity theft, compromising computers and using them as bounce points, "
"etc)."
msgstr ""
"För det andra skulle [de som begår brott ändå inte fångas på detta sätt](../"
"what-about-criminals/), eftersom de skulle använda andra metoder för att "
"skydda sin anonymitet, till exempel identitetsstöld, komprometterade datorer "
"som mellanhänder och så vidare."

#: content/abuse/help-trace-tor-user/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/help-trace-tor-user/
msgid "Some fans have suggested that we redesign Tor to include a backdoor."
msgstr "Vissa anhängare har föreslagit att Tor ska göras om med en bakdörr."

#: content/abuse/help-trace-tor-user/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/help-trace-tor-user/
msgid ""
"The Tor Project is also happy to work with everyone including law "
"enforcement groups to train them how to use the Tor software to safely "
"conduct investigations or anonymized activities online."
msgstr ""
"The Tor Project samarbetar gärna med alla, även brottsbekämpande "
"myndigheter, för att utbilda dem i hur Tor-programvaran kan användas för "
"säkra utredningar eller anonymiserade aktiviteter på nätet."

#: content/abuse/help-trace-tor-user/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/help-trace-tor-user/
msgid ""
"The same protections that keep bad people from breaking Tor's anonymity also "
"prevent us from figuring out what's going on."
msgstr ""
"Samma skydd som hindrar illvilliga personer från att bryta Tors anonymitet "
"hindrar även oss från att ta reda på vad som händer."

#: content/abuse/help-trace-tor-user/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/help-trace-tor-user/
msgid "There are two problems with this idea."
msgstr "Det finns två problem med idén."

#: content/abuse/help-trace-tor-user/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/help-trace-tor-user/
msgid "There is nothing the Tor developers can do to trace Tor users."
msgstr "Tor-utvecklarna kan inte göra något för att spåra Tor-användare."

#: content/abuse/help-trace-tor-user/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/help-trace-tor-user/
msgid "This is just part of signing up for the benefits of the Internet."
msgstr "Detta är helt enkelt en del av att ta del av internets fördelar."

#: content/abuse/help-trace-tor-user/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/help-trace-tor-user/
msgid ""
"This ultimately means that it is the responsibility of site owners to "
"protect themselves against compromise and security issues that can come from "
"anywhere."
msgstr ""
"I slutänden innebär det att webbplatsägare ansvarar för att skydda sig mot "
"intrång och säkerhetsproblem som kan komma från vilket håll som helst."

#: content/abuse/help-trace-tor-user/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/help-trace-tor-user/
msgid ""
"Tracking and increased surveillance are not the answer to preventing abuse."
msgstr ""
"Spårning och ökad övervakning är inte lösningen för att förhindra missbruk."

#: content/abuse/help-trace-tor-user/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/help-trace-tor-user/
msgid ""
"Traditional police techniques can still be very effective against Tor, such "
"as investigating means, motive, and opportunity, interviewing suspects, "
"writing style analysis, technical analysis of the content itself, sting "
"operations, keyboard taps, and other physical investigations."
msgstr ""
"Traditionella polismetoder kan fortfarande vara mycket effektiva mot Tor, "
"till exempel att utreda medel, motiv och tillfälle, förhöra misstänkta, "
"analysera skrivstil, göra tekniska analyser av själva innehållet, genomföra "
"provokationer, registrera tangenttryckningar och utföra andra fysiska "
"utredningar."

#: content/abuse/help-trace-tor-user/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/help-trace-tor-user/
msgid ""
"You must be prepared to secure yourself against the bad elements, wherever "
"they may come from."
msgstr ""
"Du måste vara beredd att skydda dig mot illvilliga aktörer, oavsett varifrån "
"de kommer."

#: content/abuse/irc/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/irc/
msgid ""
"Some IRC networks block Tor exit nodes due to abuse or outdated security "
"practices."
msgstr ""
"Vissa IRC-nätverk blockerar Tor-utgångsnoder på grund av missbruk eller "
"föråldrade säkerhetsmetoder."

#: content/abuse/irc/contents.lr:article.longer_title
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/irc/
msgid "What to do if the IRC network you want to use bans Tor users"
msgstr ""
"Vad du kan göra om IRC-nätverket du vill använda blockerar Tor-användare"

#: content/abuse/irc/contents.lr:article.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/irc/
msgid "Tor users blocked on IRC"
msgstr "Tor-användare blockerade på IRC"

#: content/abuse/irc/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/irc/
msgid ""
"After all, quite a few people use Tor to IRC in privacy in order to carry on "
"legitimate communications without tying them to their real-world identity."
msgstr ""
"Många använder trots allt Tor för att kommunicera legitimt och privat via "
"IRC utan att koppla kommunikationen till sin verkliga identitet."

#: content/abuse/irc/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/irc/
msgid ""
"And most individual IP addresses do equate to individual humans, on any "
"given IRC network at any given time."
msgstr ""
"På ett visst IRC-nätverk vid en viss tidpunkt motsvarar dessutom de flesta "
"enskilda IP-adresser enskilda personer."

#: content/abuse/irc/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/irc/
msgid ""
"But the real answer is to implement application-level auth systems, to let "
"in well-behaving users and keep out badly-behaving users."
msgstr ""
"Den verkliga lösningen är dock att införa autentiseringssystem på "
"programnivå som släpper in skötsamma användare och stänger ute dem som "
"missköter sig."

#: content/abuse/irc/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/irc/
msgid ""
"By responding quickly to trolls or any other social attack, it may be "
"possible to make the attack scenario less attractive to the attacker."
msgstr ""
"Genom att snabbt reagera på troll och andra sociala attacker kan "
"angreppssättet göras mindre attraktivt för angriparen."

#: content/abuse/irc/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/irc/
msgid ""
"Each IRC network needs to decide for itself if blocking a few more of the "
"millions of IPs that bad people can use is worth losing the contributions "
"from the well-behaved Tor users."
msgstr ""
"Varje IRC-nätverk måste själv avgöra om det är värt att blockera ytterligare "
"några av de miljontals IP-adresser som illvilliga personer kan använda och "
"därmed förlora bidragen från skötsamma Tor-användare."

#: content/abuse/irc/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/irc/
msgid ""
"If you explain the problem, and they conclude that Tor ought to be blocked, "
"you may want to consider moving to a network that is more open to free "
"speech."
msgstr ""
"Om du förklarar problemet och operatörerna ändå anser att Tor bör blockeras "
"kan du överväga att byta till ett nätverk som är mer öppet för "
"yttrandefrihet."

#: content/abuse/irc/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/irc/
msgid ""
"If you're being blocked, have a discussion with the network operators and "
"explain the issues to them."
msgstr ""
"Om du blockeras bör du diskutera saken med nätverksoperatörerna och förklara "
"problemen."

#: content/abuse/irc/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/irc/
msgid ""
"In reality, this is not the case — many such trolls routinely make use of "
"the literally millions of open proxies and compromised computers around the "
"Internet."
msgstr ""
"I verkligheten är det inte så – många sådana troll använder rutinmässigt de "
"bokstavligen miljontals öppna proxyservrar och komprometterade datorer som "
"finns på internet."

#: content/abuse/irc/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/irc/
msgid ""
"Maybe inviting them to #tor on irc.oftc.net will help show them that we are "
"not all evil people."
msgstr ""
"Kanske kan en inbjudan till #tor på irc.oftc.net visa dem att vi inte alla "
"är illvilliga."

#: content/abuse/irc/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/irc/
msgid "Of course, not all IRC networks are trying to ban Tor nodes."
msgstr "Alla IRC-nätverk försöker naturligtvis inte blockera Tor-noder."

#: content/abuse/irc/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/irc/
msgid ""
"On the other hand, from the viewpoint of IRC server operators, security is "
"not an all-or-nothing thing."
msgstr ""
"Ur IRC-serveroperatörernas perspektiv är säkerhet å andra sidan inte en "
"fråga om allt eller inget."

#: content/abuse/irc/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/irc/
msgid "Sometimes jerks make use of Tor to troll IRC channels."
msgstr "Ibland använder personer Tor för att trolla i IRC-kanaler."

#: content/abuse/irc/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/irc/
msgid ""
"The IRC networks are fighting a losing battle of trying to block all these "
"nodes, and an entire cottage industry of blocklists and counter-trolls has "
"sprung up based on this flawed security model (not unlike the antivirus "
"industry)."
msgstr ""
"IRC-nätverken utkämpar en hopplös kamp för att blockera alla dessa noder, "
"och en hel småindustri med blockeringslistor och mottroll har vuxit fram "
"kring denna bristfälliga säkerhetsmodell (inte helt olikt "
"antivirusbranschen)."

#: content/abuse/irc/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/irc/
msgid "The Tor network is just a drop in the bucket here."
msgstr "Tor-nätverket är bara en droppe i havet i detta sammanhang."

#: content/abuse/irc/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/irc/
msgid ""
"The exceptions include NAT gateways which may be allocated access as special "
"cases."
msgstr ""
"Undantagen omfattar NAT-gatewayservrar som i särskilda fall kan få åtkomst."

#: content/abuse/irc/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/irc/
msgid ""
"They may not be aware of the existence of Tor at all, or they may not be "
"aware that the hostnames they're klining are Tor exit nodes."
msgstr ""
"De kanske inte alls känner till Tor eller vet att värdnamnen de blockerar "
"med kline tillhör Tor-utgångsnoder."

#: content/abuse/irc/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/irc/
msgid ""
"This abuse results in IP-specific temporary bans (\"klines\" in IRC lingo), "
"as the network operators try to keep the troll off of their network."
msgstr ""
"Missbruket leder till tillfälliga IP-specifika blockeringar (”klines” på IRC-"
"språk), när nätverksoperatörerna försöker hålla trollet borta från nätverket."

#: content/abuse/irc/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/irc/
msgid ""
"This needs to be based on some property of the human (such as a password "
"they know), not some property of the way their packets are transported."
msgstr ""
"Detta måste bygga på någon egenskap hos personen, till exempel ett lösenord "
"som personen känner till, inte på hur personens paket transporteras."

#: content/abuse/irc/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/irc/
msgid "This response underscores a fundamental flaw in IRC's security model:"
msgstr "Reaktionen belyser ett grundläggande fel i IRC:s säkerhetsmodell:"

#: content/abuse/irc/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/irc/
msgid ""
"While it's a losing battle to try to stop the use of open proxies, it's not "
"generally a losing battle to keep klining a single ill-behaved IRC user "
"until that user gets bored and goes away."
msgstr ""
"Det är en hopplös kamp att försöka stoppa användningen av öppna "
"proxyservrar, men det är i allmänhet inte hopplöst att fortsätta blockera en "
"enskild IRC-användare som missköter sig tills personen tröttnar och "
"försvinner."

#: content/abuse/irc/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/irc/
msgid ""
"they assume that IP addresses equate to humans, and by banning the IP "
"address they can ban the human."
msgstr ""
"de utgår från att IP-adresser motsvarar människor och att en blockering av "
"IP-adressen därför blockerar personen."

#: content/abuse/prevent-bad-people/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/prevent-bad-people/
msgid ""
"Tor is built to protect everyone's privacy and resist censorship - even from "
"us."
msgstr ""
"Tor är byggt för att skydda allas integritet och motstå censur – även från "
"oss."

#: content/abuse/prevent-bad-people/contents.lr:article.longer_title
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/prevent-bad-people/
msgid "Why don't you prevent bad people from doing bad things when using Tor?"
msgstr ""
"Varför hindrar ni inte illvilliga personer från att göra skada med Tor?"

#: content/abuse/prevent-bad-people/contents.lr:article.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/prevent-bad-people/
msgid "Why the Tor Project can't block bad actors"
msgstr "Varför The Tor Project inte kan blockera illvilliga aktörer"

#: content/abuse/prevent-bad-people/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/prevent-bad-people/
msgid ""
"If we wanted to block certain people from using Tor, we'd basically be "
"adding a backdoor to the software, which would open up our vulnerable users "
"to attacks from bad regimes and other adversaries."
msgstr ""
"Om vi ville blockera vissa personer från att använda Tor skulle vi i "
"praktiken lägga in en bakdörr i programvaran. Det skulle utsätta våra "
"sårbara användare för attacker från repressiva regimer och andra motståndare."

#: content/abuse/prevent-bad-people/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/prevent-bad-people/
msgid ""
"Tor is designed to defend human rights and privacy by preventing anyone from "
"censoring things, even us."
msgstr ""
"Tor är utformat för att försvara mänskliga rättigheter och integritet genom "
"att hindra alla, även oss, från att censurera."

#: content/abuse/prevent-bad-people/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/prevent-bad-people/
msgid ""
"We hate that there are some people who use Tor to do terrible things, but we "
"can't do anything to get rid of them without also undermining the human "
"rights activists, journalists, abuse survivors, and other people who use Tor "
"for good things."
msgstr ""
"Vi avskyr att vissa använder Tor för fruktansvärda handlingar, men vi kan "
"inte bli av med dem utan att samtidigt underminera människorättsaktivister, "
"journalister, överlevare efter övergrepp och andra som använder Tor för goda "
"ändamål."

#: content/abuse/ransomware/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/ransomware/
msgid "Understanding why malware authors may tell you to download Tor Browser"
msgstr "Varför skadeprogramsförfattare kan uppmana dig att hämta Tor Browser"

#: content/abuse/ransomware/contents.lr:article.longer_title
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/ransomware/
msgid ""
"The files on my computer have been locked, and someone is demanding I "
"download Tor Browser to pay a ransom for my files!"
msgstr ""
"Filerna på min dator har låsts, och någon kräver att jag hämtar Tor Browser "
"för att betala en lösensumma!"

#: content/abuse/ransomware/contents.lr:article.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/ransomware/
msgid "Tor Browser and malware"
msgstr "Tor Browser och skadeprogram"

#: content/abuse/ransomware/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/ransomware/
msgid ""
"But please consider that our software is used every day for a wide variety "
"of purposes by human rights activists, journalists, domestic violence "
"survivors, whistleblowers, law enforcement officers, and many others. "
"Unfortunately, the protection that our software can provide to these groups "
"of people can also be abused by criminals and malware authors."
msgstr ""
"Tänk på att vår programvara varje dag används för många olika ändamål av "
"människorättsaktivister, journalister, personer som överlevt våld i nära "
"relationer, visselblåsare, brottsbekämpande tjänstemän och många andra. "
"Tyvärr kan skyddet som programvaran ger dessa grupper även missbrukas av "
"brottslingar och skadeprogramsförfattare."

#: content/abuse/ransomware/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/ransomware/
msgid ""
"If this is your first introduction to Tor Browser, we understand that you "
"might think we're bad people who enable even worse people."
msgstr ""
"Om detta är din första kontakt med Tor Browser förstår vi om du tror att vi "
"är dåliga människor som hjälper ännu värre personer."

#: content/abuse/ransomware/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/ransomware/
msgid ""
"The Tor Project did not create this malware. The malware authors are asking "
"you to download Tor Browser presumably to contact them anonymously with the "
"ransom they're demanding from you."
msgstr ""
"The Tor Project skapade inte skadeprogrammet. Förmodligen uppmanar "
"skadeprogramsförfattarna dig att hämta Tor Browser för att kunna kontakta "
"dem anonymt om lösensumman de kräver."

#: content/abuse/ransomware/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/ransomware/
msgid ""
"The Tor Project does not support or condone the use of our software for "
"malicious purposes."
msgstr ""
"The Tor Project stöder eller godtar inte att vår programvara används för "
"skadliga ändamål."

#: content/abuse/ransomware/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/ransomware/
msgid "We are so sorry, but you have been infected with malware."
msgstr "Vi beklagar verkligen att din dator har infekterats med skadeprogram."

#: content/abuse/remove-content-from-onion-address/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/remove-content-from-onion-address/
msgid ""
"The Tor Project does not host or control .onion services and cannot identify "
"their owners or locations."
msgstr ""
"The Tor Project är inte värd för och styr inte .onion-tjänster och kan inte "
"identifiera deras ägare eller platser."

#: content/abuse/remove-content-from-onion-address/contents.lr:article.longer_title
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/remove-content-from-onion-address/
msgid ""
"Understanding why the Tor Project can’t remove content from .onion sites"
msgstr ""
"Varför The Tor Project inte kan ta bort innehåll från .onion-webbplatser"

#: content/abuse/remove-content-from-onion-address/contents.lr:article.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/remove-content-from-onion-address/
msgid "I want some content removed from a .onion address"
msgstr "Jag vill att innehåll tas bort från en .onion-adress"

#: content/abuse/remove-content-from-onion-address/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/remove-content-from-onion-address/
msgid ""
"But remember that this doesn't mean that onion services are invulnerable."
msgstr "Kom dock ihåg att detta inte betyder att onion-tjänster är osårbara."

#: content/abuse/remove-content-from-onion-address/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/remove-content-from-onion-address/
msgid ""
"If you have a complaint about child abuse materials, you may wish to report "
"it to the National Center for Missing and Exploited Children, which serves "
"as a national coordination point for investigation of child pornography: "
"https://www.missingkids.org/."
msgstr ""
"Om ditt klagomål gäller material med sexuella övergrepp mot barn kan du "
"rapportera det till National Center for Missing and Exploited Children, som "
"fungerar som nationell samordningspunkt för utredningar av barnpornografi: "
"https://www.missingkids.org/."

#: content/abuse/remove-content-from-onion-address/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/remove-content-from-onion-address/
msgid ""
"It's an automatically generated name which can be located on any Tor relay "
"or client anywhere on the Internet."
msgstr ""
"Det är ett automatiskt genererat namn som kan finnas på vilket Tor-relä "
"eller vilken Tor-klient som helst, var som helst på internet."

#: content/abuse/remove-content-from-onion-address/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/remove-content-from-onion-address/
msgid ""
"Onion services are designed to protect both the user and service provider "
"from discovering who they are and where they are from."
msgstr ""
"Onion-tjänster är utformade för att hindra både användaren och "
"tjänsteleverantören från att ta reda på vem den andra parten är och var den "
"befinner sig."

#: content/abuse/remove-content-from-onion-address/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/remove-content-from-onion-address/
msgid ""
"The .onion address is an address from [an onion service](../../tor-browser/"
"features/onion-services)."
msgstr ""
".onion-adressen är en adress till [en onion-tjänst](../../tor-browser/"
"features/onion-services)."

#: content/abuse/remove-content-from-onion-address/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/remove-content-from-onion-address/
msgid ""
"The Tor Project does not host, control, nor have the ability to discover the "
"owner or location of a .onion address."
msgstr ""
"The Tor Project är inte värd för, styr inte och kan inte ta reda på ägaren "
"till eller platsen för en .onion-adress."

#: content/abuse/remove-content-from-onion-address/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/remove-content-from-onion-address/
msgid ""
"The design of onion services means the owner and location of the .onion site "
"is hidden even from us."
msgstr ""
"Onion-tjänsternas utformning innebär att .onion-webbplatsens ägare och plats "
"är dolda även för oss."

#: content/abuse/remove-content-from-onion-address/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/remove-content-from-onion-address/
msgid "The name you see ending in .onion is an onion service descriptor."
msgstr "Namnet som slutar på .onion är en deskriptor för en onion-tjänst."

#: content/abuse/remove-content-from-onion-address/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/remove-content-from-onion-address/
msgid ""
"Traditional police techniques can still be very effective against them, such "
"as interviewing suspects, writing style analysis, technical analysis of the "
"content itself, sting operations, keyboard taps, and other physical "
"investigations."
msgstr ""
"Traditionella polismetoder kan fortfarande vara mycket effektiva mot dem, "
"till exempel förhör med misstänkta, analys av skrivstil, teknisk analys av "
"själva innehållet, provokationer, registrering av tangenttryckningar och "
"andra fysiska utredningar."

#: content/abuse/remove-content-from-onion-address/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/remove-content-from-onion-address/
msgid "We do not view links you report."
msgstr "Vi öppnar inte länkar som du rapporterar."

#: content/abuse/tor-project-opinion-on-abusers/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/tor-project-opinion-on-abusers/
msgid ""
"The Tor Project condemns the misuse of privacy tools for harm while refusing "
"to weaken Tor with backdoors or censorship."
msgstr ""
"The Tor Project fördömer missbruk av integritetsverktyg för att skada andra, "
"men vägrar att försvaga Tor med bakdörrar eller censur."

#: content/abuse/tor-project-opinion-on-abusers/contents.lr:article.longer_title
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/tor-project-opinion-on-abusers/
msgid "Where does Tor Project stand on abusers using technology?"
msgstr ""
"Vilken är The Tor Projects ståndpunkt om personer som missbrukar teknik?"

#: content/abuse/tor-project-opinion-on-abusers/contents.lr:article.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/tor-project-opinion-on-abusers/
msgid "Tor Project's stance on abuse and technology"
msgstr "The Tor Projects syn på missbruk och teknik"

#: content/abuse/tor-project-opinion-on-abusers/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/tor-project-opinion-on-abusers/
msgid ""
"Activists and law enforcement use Tor to investigate abuse and help support "
"survivors."
msgstr ""
"Aktivister och brottsbekämpande myndigheter använder Tor för att utreda "
"övergrepp och stödja överlevare."

#: content/abuse/tor-project-opinion-on-abusers/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/tor-project-opinion-on-abusers/
msgid ""
"Because some people in survivors' communities embrace stigma instead of "
"compassion, seeking support from fellow victims requires privacy-preserving "
"technology."
msgstr ""
"Eftersom vissa i överlevargemenskaper möter människor med stigmatisering i "
"stället för medkänsla krävs integritetsskyddande teknik för att söka stöd "
"hos andra utsatta."

#: content/abuse/tor-project-opinion-on-abusers/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/tor-project-opinion-on-abusers/
msgid ""
"Finally, it is important to consider the world that children will encounter "
"as adults when enacting policy in their name."
msgstr ""
"När politiska beslut fattas i barns namn är det slutligen viktigt att tänka "
"på den värld barnen kommer att möta som vuxna."

#: content/abuse/tor-project-opinion-on-abusers/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/tor-project-opinion-on-abusers/
msgid ""
"In some cases, technological mistakes are being made and we help to correct "
"them."
msgstr "I vissa fall görs tekniska misstag, och vi hjälper till att rätta dem."

#: content/abuse/tor-project-opinion-on-abusers/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/tor-project-opinion-on-abusers/
msgid ""
"In the face of this, it is dangerous for policymakers to assume that "
"blocking and filtering is sufficient."
msgstr ""
"Mot denna bakgrund är det farligt för beslutsfattare att anta att blockering "
"och filtrering räcker."

#: content/abuse/tor-project-opinion-on-abusers/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/tor-project-opinion-on-abusers/
msgid ""
"Meanwhile, criminals would still have access to botnets, stolen phones, "
"hacked hosting accounts, the postal system, couriers, corrupt officials, and "
"whatever technology emerges to trade content."
msgstr ""
"Brottslingar skulle samtidigt fortfarande ha tillgång till botnät, stulna "
"telefoner, kapade webbhotellskonton, postsystemet, kurirer, korrupta "
"tjänstemän och den teknik som framöver utvecklas för att utbyta innehåll."

#: content/abuse/tor-project-opinion-on-abusers/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/tor-project-opinion-on-abusers/
msgid ""
"Our refusal to build backdoors and censorship into Tor is not because of a "
"lack of concern."
msgstr ""
"Vår vägran att bygga in bakdörrar och censur i Tor beror inte på bristande "
"omtanke."

#: content/abuse/tor-project-opinion-on-abusers/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/tor-project-opinion-on-abusers/
msgid ""
"The role of corruption is especially troubling; see this United Nations "
"report on [The Role of Corruption in Trafficking in Persons](https://"
"www.unodc.org/documents/human-trafficking/2011/Issue_Paper_-"
"_The_Role_of_Corruption_in_Trafficking_in_Persons.pdf)."
msgstr ""
"Korruptionens roll är särskilt oroande. Se denna FN-rapport om "
"[korruptionens roll i människohandel](https://www.unodc.org/documents/human-"
"trafficking/2011/Issue_Paper_-"
"_The_Role_of_Corruption_in_Trafficking_in_Persons.pdf)."

#: content/abuse/tor-project-opinion-on-abusers/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/tor-project-opinion-on-abusers/
msgid "They are early adopters of technology."
msgstr "De är tidiga användare av ny teknik."

#: content/abuse/tor-project-opinion-on-abusers/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/tor-project-opinion-on-abusers/
msgid ""
"We are more interested in helping efforts to halt and prevent child abuse "
"than helping politicians score points with constituents by hiding it."
msgstr ""
"Vi är mer intresserade av att stödja arbetet med att stoppa och förebygga "
"övergrepp mot barn än av att hjälpa politiker vinna poäng hos väljare genom "
"att dölja problemen."

#: content/abuse/tor-project-opinion-on-abusers/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/tor-project-opinion-on-abusers/
msgid ""
"We refuse to weaken Tor because it would harm efforts to combat child abuse "
"and human trafficking in the physical world, while removing safe spaces for "
"victims online."
msgstr ""
"Vi vägrar att försvaga Tor eftersom det skulle skada arbetet mot övergrepp "
"mot barn och människohandel i den fysiska världen och samtidigt undanröja "
"säkra platser för utsatta på nätet."

#: content/abuse/tor-project-opinion-on-abusers/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/tor-project-opinion-on-abusers/
msgid "We take abuse seriously."
msgstr "Vi tar missbruk på stort allvar."

#: content/abuse/tor-project-opinion-on-abusers/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/tor-project-opinion-on-abusers/
msgid "We work with them to help them understand how Tor can help their work."
msgstr ""
"Vi samarbetar med dem för att hjälpa dem förstå hur Tor kan stödja deras "
"arbete."

#: content/abuse/tor-project-opinion-on-abusers/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/tor-project-opinion-on-abusers/
msgid ""
"What if they are trying to expose a failure of the state to protect other "
"children?"
msgstr ""
"Tänk om de försöker avslöja att staten har misslyckats med att skydda andra "
"barn?"

#: content/abuse/tor-project-opinion-on-abusers/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/tor-project-opinion-on-abusers/
msgid ""
"Will they thank us if they are unable to voice their opinions safely as "
"adults?"
msgstr ""
"Kommer de att tacka oss om de som vuxna inte kan uttrycka sina åsikter på "
"ett säkert sätt?"

#: content/abuse/what-about-criminals/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/what-about-criminals/
msgid "Tor is built to protect privacy and fight censorship."
msgstr "Tor är byggt för att skydda integriteten och bekämpa censur."

#: content/abuse/what-about-criminals/contents.lr:article.longer_title
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/what-about-criminals/
msgid "Doesn't Tor enable criminals to do bad things?"
msgstr "Gör inte Tor det möjligt för brottslingar att begå brott?"

#: content/abuse/what-about-criminals/contents.lr:article.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/what-about-criminals/
msgid "Does Tor enable criminal activity?"
msgstr "Möjliggör Tor brottslig verksamhet?"

#: content/abuse/what-about-criminals/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/what-about-criminals/
msgid ""
"And because of other options they can use it seems unlikely that taking Tor "
"away from the world will stop them from engaging in criminal activity."
msgstr ""
"Eftersom de även har andra alternativ verkar det osannolikt att "
"brottsligheten skulle upphöra om Tor togs bort från världen."

#: content/abuse/what-about-criminals/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/what-about-criminals/
msgid ""
"At the same time, Tor and other privacy measures can fight identity theft, "
"physical crimes like stalking, and be used by law enforcement to investigate "
"crime and help support survivors."
msgstr ""
"Samtidigt kan Tor och andra integritetsskydd motverka identitetsstöld och "
"fysiska brott som förföljelse, samt användas av brottsbekämpande myndigheter "
"för att utreda brott och stödja överlevare."

#: content/abuse/what-about-criminals/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/what-about-criminals/
msgid ""
"It's essential to understand that criminal intent lies with the individuals "
"and not the tools they use."
msgstr ""
"Det är viktigt att förstå att det brottsliga uppsåtet finns hos personerna, "
"inte i verktygen de använder."

#: content/abuse/what-about-criminals/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/what-about-criminals/
msgid ""
"Just like other widely available technology, Tor can be used by individuals "
"with criminal intent."
msgstr ""
"Precis som annan allmänt tillgänglig teknik kan Tor användas av personer med "
"brottsliga avsikter."

#: content/abuse/what-about-criminals/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/what-about-criminals/
msgid ""
"Tor's mission is to advance human rights with free and open-source "
"technology, empowering users to defend against mass surveillance and "
"internet censorship."
msgstr ""
"Tors uppdrag är att främja mänskliga rättigheter med fri teknik med öppen "
"källkod och ge användare möjlighet att försvara sig mot massövervakning och "
"internetcensur."

#: content/abuse/what-about-criminals/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/abuse/what-about-criminals/
msgid ""
"We hate that there are some people who use Tor for nefarious purposes, and "
"we condemn the misuse and exploitation of our technology for criminal "
"activity."
msgstr ""
"Vi avskyr att vissa använder Tor för skadliga ändamål och fördömer att vår "
"teknik missbrukas och utnyttjas för brottslig verksamhet."

#: content/anti-censorship/contents.lr:section.title
#: content/contents.lr:internal_nav_item.title
#: content/contents.lr:section_card.title https://support.torproject.org/
#: https://support.torproject.org/anti-censorship/
msgid "Anti-censorship"
msgstr "Motverka censur"

#: content/anti-censorship/how-can-i-use-snowflake/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/anti-censorship/how-can-i-use-snowflake/
msgid ""
"A quick guide to enabling the built-in Snowflake bridge in Tor Browser (and "
"Onion Browser on iOS) so you can connect to Tor even when direct access is "
"blocked."
msgstr ""
"En snabbguide till hur du aktiverar den inbyggda Snowflake-bron i Tor "
"Browser (och Onion Browser på iOS), så att du kan ansluta till Tor även när "
"direktåtkomst blockeras."

#: content/anti-censorship/how-can-i-use-snowflake/contents.lr:article.longer_title
#: https://support.torproject.org/anti-censorship/how-can-i-use-snowflake/
msgid "How to use Snowflake in Tor Browser"
msgstr "Så använder du Snowflake i Tor Browser"

#: content/anti-censorship/how-can-i-use-snowflake/contents.lr:article.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/anti-censorship/how-can-i-use-snowflake/
msgid "How can I use Snowflake?"
msgstr "Hur använder jag Snowflake?"

#: content/anti-censorship/how-can-i-use-snowflake/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/anti-censorship/how-can-i-use-snowflake/
msgid ""
"Alternatively, you can also type `about:preferences#connection` in the URL "
"bar."
msgstr "Du kan även skriva `about:preferences#connection` i adressfältet."

#: content/anti-censorship/how-can-i-use-snowflake/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/anti-censorship/how-can-i-use-snowflake/
msgid "From the menu, select 'Snowflake'."
msgstr "Välj ”Snowflake” i menyn."

#: content/anti-censorship/how-can-i-use-snowflake/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/anti-censorship/how-can-i-use-snowflake/
msgid ""
"From within the browser, you can click on the hamburger menu (\"≡\"), then "
"go to 'Settings' and go to 'Connection'."
msgstr ""
"I webbläsaren kan du klicka på hamburgermenyn (”≡”), välja ”Inställningar” "
"och sedan ”Anslutning”."

#: content/anti-censorship/how-can-i-use-snowflake/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/anti-censorship/how-can-i-use-snowflake/
msgid ""
"If you're running Tor Browser for desktop for the first time, you can click "
"on 'Configure Connection' on the start-up screen."
msgstr ""
"Om du kör Tor Browser för dator för första gången kan du klicka på "
"”Konfigurera anslutning” på startskärmen."

#: content/anti-censorship/how-can-i-use-snowflake/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/anti-censorship/how-can-i-use-snowflake/
msgid ""
"Once you've selected Snowflake, scroll up and click 'Connect' to save your "
"settings."
msgstr ""
"När du har valt Snowflake rullar du uppåt och klickar på ”Anslut” för att "
"spara inställningarna."

#: content/anti-censorship/how-can-i-use-snowflake/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/anti-censorship/how-can-i-use-snowflake/
msgid ""
"Snowflake is available in [Tor Browser](https://www.torproject.org/"
"download/) stable for all platforms: Windows, macOS, GNU/Linux, and Android."
msgstr ""
"Snowflake finns i den stabila versionen av [Tor Browser](https://"
"www.torproject.org/download/) för alla plattformar: Windows, macOS, GNU/"
"Linux och Android."

#: content/anti-censorship/how-can-i-use-snowflake/contents.lr:content.content
#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/unblocking-tor/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/anti-censorship/how-can-i-use-snowflake/
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/unblocking-tor/
msgid ""
"Under the \"Bridges\" section, locate the option \"Choose from one of Tor "
"Browser's built-in bridges\" and click on \"Select a Built-In Bridge\" "
"option."
msgstr ""
"Under avsnittet \"Broar\" letar du upp alternativet \"Välj från en av Tor "
"Browsers inbyggda broar\" och klickar på alternativet \"Välj en inbyggd "
"bro\"."

#: content/anti-censorship/how-can-i-use-snowflake/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/anti-censorship/how-can-i-use-snowflake/
msgid ""
"You can also use Snowflake with [Onion Browser](https://apps.apple.com/us/"
"app/onion-browser/id519296448) on iOS."
msgstr ""
"Du kan också använda Snowflake med [Onion Browser](https://apps.apple.com/us/"
"app/onion-browser/id519296448) på iOS."

#: content/anti-censorship/how-can-i-use-snowflake/contents.lr:tab.title
#: content/anti-censorship/running-snowflake/contents.lr:tab.title
#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.title
#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/anti-censorship/how-can-i-use-snowflake/
#: https://support.torproject.org/anti-censorship/running-snowflake/
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/
msgid "Snowflake"
msgstr "Snowflake"

#: content/anti-censorship/how-to-check-if-tor-is-blocked/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/anti-censorship/how-to-check-if-tor-is-blocked/
msgid ""
"OONI Probe is a free, open-source app that helps you measure potential "
"blocking of the Tor network."
msgstr ""
"OONI Probe är en fri app med öppen källkod som hjälper dig att mäta möjlig "
"blockering av Tor-nätverket."

#: content/anti-censorship/how-to-check-if-tor-is-blocked/contents.lr:article.longer_title
#: https://support.torproject.org/anti-censorship/how-to-check-if-tor-is-blocked/
msgid "I suspect I may be facing internet censorship. How can I verify this?"
msgstr ""
"Jag misstänker att jag utsätts för internetcensur. Hur kan jag kontrollera "
"det?"

#: content/anti-censorship/how-to-check-if-tor-is-blocked/contents.lr:article.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/anti-censorship/how-to-check-if-tor-is-blocked/
msgid "Learn how to check if Tor is blocked using OONI Probe"
msgstr "Så kontrollerar du om Tor blockeras med OONI Probe"

#: content/anti-censorship/how-to-check-if-tor-is-blocked/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/anti-censorship/how-to-check-if-tor-is-blocked/
msgid ""
"An OONI Tor Test can serve as an indication of a potential block of the Tor "
"network, but a thorough analysis by our developers is crucial for a "
"conclusive evaluation."
msgstr ""
"Ett Tor-test i OONI kan tyda på att Tor-nätverket blockeras, men en grundlig "
"analys av våra utvecklare krävs för en säker bedömning."

#: content/anti-censorship/how-to-check-if-tor-is-blocked/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/anti-censorship/how-to-check-if-tor-is-blocked/
msgid ""
"As any other testing tool, please be aware of [false positive tests with "
"OONI](https://ooni.org/support/glossary/#false-positive)."
msgstr ""
"Precis som med andra testverktyg bör du vara medveten om [falskt positiva "
"resultat i OONI](https://ooni.org/support/glossary/#false-positive)."

#: content/anti-censorship/how-to-check-if-tor-is-blocked/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/anti-censorship/how-to-check-if-tor-is-blocked/
msgid ""
"Before you run these measurement tests, please carefully read OONI's "
"security recommendations and [risk assessment](https://ooni.org/about/"
"risks/)."
msgstr ""
"Läs OONI:s säkerhetsrekommendationer och [riskbedömning](https://ooni.org/"
"about/risks/) noggrant innan du genomför mätningarna."

#: content/anti-censorship/how-to-check-if-tor-is-blocked/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/anti-censorship/how-to-check-if-tor-is-blocked/
msgid ""
"If you suspect that your government or Internet Service Provider (ISP) has "
"implemented some form of Internet censorship or filtering, you can test "
"whether the Tor network is being blocked by using [OONI Probe](https://"
"ooni.org/)."
msgstr ""
"Om du misstänker att din regering eller internetleverantör har infört "
"internetcensur eller filtrering kan du testa om Tor-nätverket blockeras med "
"[OONI Probe](https://ooni.org/)."

#: content/anti-censorship/how-to-check-if-tor-is-blocked/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/anti-censorship/how-to-check-if-tor-is-blocked/
msgid ""
"It is designed to test and measure which websites, messaging apps, and "
"circumvention tools may be blocked."
msgstr ""
"Programmet är utformat för att testa och mäta vilka webbplatser, "
"meddelandeappar och verktyg för censurkringgående som kan vara blockerade."

#: content/anti-censorship/how-to-check-if-tor-is-blocked/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/anti-censorship/how-to-check-if-tor-is-blocked/
msgid ""
"OONI Probe is a free and open source application developed by the Open "
"Observatory of Network Interference (OONI)."
msgstr ""
"OONI Probe är ett fritt program med öppen källkod som utvecklas av Open "
"Observatory of Network Interference (OONI)."

#: content/anti-censorship/how-to-check-if-tor-is-blocked/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/anti-censorship/how-to-check-if-tor-is-blocked/
msgid ""
"To check if Tor is blocked, you can [install OONI Probe](https://ooni.org/"
"install/) on your mobile device or on your desktop, and run the [\"Tor "
"Test\"](https://ooni.org/support/ooni-probe-mobile#manually-measuring-the-"
"blocking-of-circumvention-tools)."
msgstr ""
"Kontrollera om Tor blockeras genom att [installera OONI Probe](https://"
"ooni.org/install/) på din mobila enhet eller dator och köra [”Tor Test”]"
"(https://ooni.org/support/ooni-probe-mobile#manually-measuring-the-blocking-"
"of-circumvention-tools)."

#: content/anti-censorship/how-to-check-if-tor-is-blocked/contents.lr:tab.title
#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/anti-censorship/how-to-check-if-tor-is-blocked/
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid "OONI"
msgstr "OONI"

#: content/anti-censorship/running-snowflake/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/anti-censorship/running-snowflake/
msgid ""
"By running a Snowflake extension or web page in your browser, you can help "
"users in censored countries reach the Tor network - no special setup "
"required."
msgstr ""
"Genom att köra ett Snowflake-tillägg eller en webbsida i webbläsaren kan du "
"hjälpa användare i censurerade länder att nå Tor-nätverket – ingen särskild "
"konfigurering krävs."

#: content/anti-censorship/running-snowflake/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/anti-censorship/running-snowflake/
msgid "Learn how to become a Snowflake proxy volunteer."
msgstr "Så blir du frivillig Snowflake-proxy."

#: content/anti-censorship/running-snowflake/contents.lr:article.longer_title
#: https://support.torproject.org/anti-censorship/running-snowflake/
msgid ""
"How to volunteer and run Snowflake proxies to help people in censored "
"networks"
msgstr ""
"Så kör du Snowflake-proxyservrar som volontär och hjälper människor i "
"censurerade nätverk"

#: content/anti-censorship/running-snowflake/contents.lr:article.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/anti-censorship/running-snowflake/
msgid "How to help by running Snowflake proxies"
msgstr "Hjälp till genom att köra Snowflake-proxyservrar"

#: content/anti-censorship/running-snowflake/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/anti-censorship/running-snowflake/
msgid "Add-on"
msgstr "Tillägg"

#: content/anti-censorship/running-snowflake/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/anti-censorship/running-snowflake/
msgid ""
"Due to censorship of VPN servers in some countries, we kindly ask you to not "
"run a snowflake proxy while connected to a VPN."
msgstr ""
"Eftersom VPN-servrar censureras i vissa länder ber vi dig att inte köra en "
"Snowflake-proxy när du är ansluten till en VPN-tjänst."

#: content/anti-censorship/running-snowflake/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/anti-censorship/running-snowflake/
msgid "Firstly make sure you have WebRTC enabled."
msgstr "Kontrollera först att WebRTC är aktiverat."

#: content/anti-censorship/running-snowflake/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/anti-censorship/running-snowflake/
msgid ""
"If you don't want to add Snowflake to your browser, you can go to [embed-"
"snowflake.torproject.org](https://embed-snowflake.torproject.org/) and "
"toggle the button to opt in to being a proxy."
msgstr ""
"Om du inte vill lägga till Snowflake i webbläsaren kan du gå till [embed-"
"snowflake.torproject.org](https://embed-snowflake.torproject.org/) och "
"aktivera knappen för att delta som proxy."

#: content/anti-censorship/running-snowflake/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/anti-censorship/running-snowflake/
msgid ""
"If your internet access is not censored, you should consider installing the "
"[Snowflake](https://snowflake.torproject.org) extension to help users in "
"censored networks."
msgstr ""
"Om din internetåtkomst inte censureras bör du överväga att installera "
"tillägget [Snowflake](https://snowflake.torproject.org) för att hjälpa "
"användare i censurerade nätverk."

#: content/anti-censorship/running-snowflake/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/anti-censorship/running-snowflake/
msgid "In a browser where WebRTC is enabled:"
msgstr "I en webbläsare där WebRTC är aktiverat:"

#: content/anti-censorship/running-snowflake/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/anti-censorship/running-snowflake/
msgid ""
"It can also inform you about how many people you have helped in the last 24 "
"hours."
msgstr ""
"Du kan även se hur många personer du har hjälpt under de senaste 24 timmarna."

#: content/anti-censorship/running-snowflake/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/anti-censorship/running-snowflake/
msgid ""
"Then you can install this [extension for Firefox](https://addons.mozilla.org/"
"en-US/firefox/addon/torproject-snowflake/) or the [extension for Chrome]"
"(https://chrome.google.com/webstore/detail/snowflake/"
"mafpmfcccpbjnhfhjnllmmalhifmlcie) which will let you become a Snowflake "
"proxy."
msgstr ""
"Installera sedan [tillägget för Firefox](https://addons.mozilla.org/en-US/"
"firefox/addon/torproject-snowflake/) eller [tillägget för Chrome](https://"
"chrome.google.com/webstore/detail/snowflake/"
"mafpmfcccpbjnhfhjnllmmalhifmlcie), som gör din webbläsare till en Snowflake-"
"proxy."

#: content/anti-censorship/running-snowflake/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/anti-censorship/running-snowflake/
msgid "Web page"
msgstr "Webbsida"

#: content/anti-censorship/running-snowflake/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/anti-censorship/running-snowflake/
msgid ""
"When you run Snowflake on your regular browser, you will proxy traffic "
"between censored users and an entry node in the Tor network, and that's all."
msgstr ""
"När Snowflake körs i din vanliga webbläsare fungerar den endast som proxy "
"mellan censurerade användare och en ingångsnod i Tor-nätverket."

#: content/anti-censorship/running-snowflake/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/anti-censorship/running-snowflake/
msgid "You shouldn't close that page if you want to remain a Snowflake proxy."
msgstr "Stäng inte sidan om du vill fortsätta vara en Snowflake-proxy."

#: content/anti-censorship/what-is-snowflake/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/anti-censorship/what-is-snowflake/
msgid ""
"Snowflake is a built-in Tor pluggable transport that lets people in censored "
"networks connect to the Tor network through volunteer-run proxies."
msgstr ""
"Snowflake är en inbyggd pluggbar transport i Tor som låter människor i "
"censurerade nätverk ansluta till Tor-nätverket genom proxyservrar som drivs "
"av volontärer."

#: content/anti-censorship/what-is-snowflake/contents.lr:article.longer_title
#: content/anti-censorship/what-is-snowflake/contents.lr:article.title
#: content/anti-censorship/what-is-snowflake/contents.lr:tab.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/anti-censorship/what-is-snowflake/
msgid "What is Snowflake?"
msgstr "Vad är Snowflake?"

#: content/anti-censorship/what-is-snowflake/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/anti-censorship/what-is-snowflake/
msgid ""
"For censored users, if your Snowflake proxy gets blocked, the broker will "
"find a new proxy for you, automatically."
msgstr ""
"Om din Snowflake-proxy blockeras hittar förmedlaren automatiskt en ny proxy "
"åt dig."

#: content/anti-censorship/what-is-snowflake/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/anti-censorship/what-is-snowflake/
msgid ""
"For other discussions about Snowflake, please visit the [Tor Forum](https://"
"forum.torproject.org) and follow up the [Snowflake tag](https://"
"forum.torproject.org/tag/snowflake)."
msgstr ""
"För andra diskussioner om Snowflake kan du besöka [Tor Forum](https://"
"forum.torproject.org) och följa [Snowflake-taggen](https://"
"forum.torproject.org/tag/snowflake)."

#: content/anti-censorship/what-is-snowflake/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/anti-censorship/what-is-snowflake/
msgid ""
"If you're interested in the technical details and specification, see the "
"[Snowflake Technical Overview](https://gitlab.torproject.org/tpo/anti-"
"censorship/pluggable-transports/snowflake/-/wikis/Technical%20Overview) and "
"the [project page](https://snowflake.torproject.org/)."
msgstr ""
"Teknisk information och specifikation finns i [Snowflakes tekniska översikt]"
"(https://gitlab.torproject.org/tpo/anti-censorship/pluggable-transports/"
"snowflake/-/wikis/Technical%20Overview) och på [projektsidan](https://"
"snowflake.torproject.org/)."

#: content/anti-censorship/what-is-snowflake/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/anti-censorship/what-is-snowflake/
msgid ""
"Like a Tor bridge, a user can access the open internet when even regular Tor "
"connections are censored."
msgstr ""
"Precis som med en Tor-bro kan en användare nå det öppna internet även när "
"vanliga Tor-anslutningar censureras."

#: content/anti-censorship/what-is-snowflake/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/anti-censorship/what-is-snowflake/
msgid ""
"Snowflake uses the highly effective domain fronting technique to make a "
"connection to one of the thousands of snowflake proxies run by volunteers."
msgstr ""
"Snowflake använder den mycket effektiva tekniken domänfrontning för att "
"ansluta till någon av de tusentals Snowflake-proxyservrar som drivs av "
"volontärer."

#: content/anti-censorship/what-is-snowflake/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/anti-censorship/what-is-snowflake/
msgid ""
"These proxies are lightweight, ephemeral, and easy to run, allowing us to "
"scale Snowflake more easily than previous techniques."
msgstr ""
"Proxyservrarna är lättviktiga, tillfälliga och enkla att köra, vilket gör "
"Snowflake lättare att skala än tidigare metoder."

#: content/anti-censorship/what-is-snowflake/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/anti-censorship/what-is-snowflake/
msgid ""
"This system is composed of three components: volunteers running Snowflake "
"proxies, Tor users that want to connect to the internet, and a broker, that "
"delivers snowflake proxies to users."
msgstr ""
"Systemet består av tre delar: volontärer som kör Snowflake-proxyservrar, Tor-"
"användare som vill ansluta till internet och en förmedlare som tilldelar "
"användarna Snowflake-proxyservrar."

#: content/anti-censorship/what-is-snowflake/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/anti-censorship/what-is-snowflake/
msgid ""
"To use Snowflake is as easy as to switch to a new bridge configuration in "
"Tor Browser."
msgstr ""
"Att använda Snowflake är lika enkelt som att byta brokonfiguration i Tor "
"Browser."

#: content/anti-censorship/what-is-snowflake/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/anti-censorship/what-is-snowflake/
msgid ""
"Volunteers willing to help users on censored networks can help by spinning "
"short-lived proxies on their regular browsers. Check [how can I use "
"Snowflake?](../how-can-i-use-snowflake/)."
msgstr ""
"Volontärer som vill hjälpa användare i censurerade nätverk kan köra "
"kortlivade proxyservrar i sina vanliga webbläsare. Se [hur använder jag "
"Snowflake?](../how-can-i-use-snowflake/)."

#: content/anti-censorship/what-is-snowflake/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/anti-censorship/what-is-snowflake/
msgid ""
"[Snowflake](https://snowflake.torproject.org) is a pluggable transport "
"available in Tor Browser to defeat internet censorship."
msgstr ""
"[Snowflake](https://snowflake.torproject.org) är en pluggbar transport i Tor "
"Browser som används för att kringgå internetcensur."

