msgstr "Telegram"

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"**No. Tor Browser and all services developed by the Tor Project are "
"completely free to use.**"
msgstr ""
"**Nej. Tor Browser och alla tjänster som utvecklas av The Tor Project är "
"helt kostnadsfria att använda.**"

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"Adherence to [Tor community](https://community.torproject.org/policies/"
"social_contract/) and [other applicable policies](https://www.torproject.org/"
"about/trademark/)"
msgstr ""
"Efterlevnad av [Tor-gemenskapens](https://community.torproject.org/policies/"
"social_contract/) och [andra tillämpliga policyer](https://"
"www.torproject.org/about/trademark/)"

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"After six weeks, please email us at [giving@torproject.org]"
"(mailto:giving@torproject.org) if you would like to check on the status of "
"your gift."
msgstr ""
"Efter sex veckor kan du skriva till [giving@torproject.org]"
"(mailto:giving@torproject.org) om du vill kontrollera gåvans status."

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"Alignment with [Tor community values](https://community.torproject.org/"
"policies/statement_of_values/)"
msgstr ""
"Överensstämmelse med [Tor-gemenskapens värderingar](https://"
"community.torproject.org/policies/statement_of_values/)"

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"Allow third-party cookies on donate.torproject.org only ([here's how to do "
"it in Firefox](https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/third-party-cookies-"
"firefox-tracking-protection))."
msgstr ""
"Tillåt tredjepartskakor endast på donate.torproject.org ([så gör du i "
"Firefox](https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/third-party-cookies-firefox-"
"tracking-protection))."

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"Certain U.S. states require written disclosures for nonprofit organizations "
"soliciting contributions. [Read individual state disclosures here.](https://"
"donate.torproject.org/state-disclosures/)"
msgstr ""
"Vissa amerikanska delstater kräver skriftliga upplysningar från ideella "
"organisationer som samlar in bidrag. [Läs upplysningarna för respektive "
"delstat här.](https://donate.torproject.org/state-disclosures/)"

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid "Compliance with applicable laws and regulations"
msgstr "Efterlevnad av tillämpliga lagar och föreskrifter"

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"Disabling third-party cookies blocks Stripe, our credit card payment "
"processor, from processing your donation."
msgstr ""
"Om tredjepartskakor inaktiveras kan Stripe, vår betalningsförmedlare för "
"betalkort, inte behandla donationen."

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"Donations made to Tails before 2025-03-12 are earmarked for Tails; your "
"donations will not be spent on any other activities."
msgstr ""
"Donationer till Tails före den 12 mars 2025 är öronmärkta för Tails och "
"används inte till annan verksamhet."

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"Donations to Tor are appreciated whether they are large or small, but we've "
"learned that setting a minimum donation amount is necessary to prevent "
"credit card fraud. Our minimum is USD $2."
msgstr ""
"Donationer till Tor uppskattas oavsett storlek, men vi har lärt oss att ett "
"minimibelopp behövs för att förhindra betalkortsbedrägerier. Minsta belopp "
"är 2 USD."

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"For instance, if the giving level is $75 to receive a T-shirt and you "
"donated $75, we will not process a refund; however, if you donated $100, we "
"would process a $25 refund."
msgstr ""
"Om gåvonivån för att få en T-shirt till exempel är 75 USD och du donerade 75 "
"USD betalar vi inte tillbaka något. Om du däremot donerade 100 USD kan vi "
"återbetala 25 USD."

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid "For users logging into PayPal with Tor Browser, try another browser."
msgstr ""
"Om du loggar in på PayPal med Tor Browser kan du prova en annan webbläsare."

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"From now on, all new donations to the Tor Project will support the whole "
"suite of tools developed by the Tor Project, including Tails, the Tor "
"network, and Tor Browser."
msgstr ""
"Från och med nu stöder alla nya donationer till The Tor Project hela "
"verktygssviten som projektet utvecklar, inklusive Tails, Tor-nätverket och "
"Tor Browser."

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"However, it's normal for nonprofits to redact individual donor information "
"from the copy of the 990 that's made publicly-available on our website, and "
"that's what we do."
msgstr ""
"Det är dock vanligt att ideella organisationer maskerar uppgifter om "
"enskilda givare i den offentliga kopian av deklarationsblankett 990 på "
"webbplatsen, och det gör även vi."

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"However, we must ensure that all fundraising efforts are mission-aligned and "
"directly benefit the global communities we serve."
msgstr ""
"Vi måste dock säkerställa att alla insamlingsinsatser ligger i linje med "
"vårt uppdrag och direkt gynnar de globala gemenskaper vi arbetar för."

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"However, we will never publicly identify you as a donor, unless you have "
"given us permission to do so."
msgstr ""
"Vi kommer dock aldrig att offentligt identifiera dig som givare utan ditt "
"tillstånd."

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"If someone is charging you to use their app or service, it's not a tool from "
"the Tor Project, and we cannot speak to its validity or safety."
msgstr ""
"Om någon tar betalt för att du ska använda deras app eller tjänst är det "
"inte ett verktyg från The Tor Project, och vi kan inte uttala oss om dess "
"giltighet eller säkerhet."

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"If you do not obtain approval from the Tor Project to fundraise on the "
"organization's behalf, your efforts may be considered unauthorized or "
"misaligned with the Tor mission and values."
msgstr ""
"Om du inte får The Tor Projects godkännande att samla in pengar i "
"organisationens namn kan insatsen betraktas som obehörig eller oförenlig med "
"Tors uppdrag och värderingar."

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"If you donate above a certain amount (roughly $80,000 USD as of 2020) to the "
"Tor Project in a single year, we are required to report the donation amount "
"and your name and address (if we have it) to the IRS, on Schedule B of the "
"Form 990, which is filed annually."
msgstr ""
"Om du under ett år donerar mer än ett visst belopp (ungefär 80 000 USD år "
"2020) till The Tor Project måste vi rapportera donationsbeloppet samt ditt "
"namn och din adress, om vi har dem, till den amerikanska skattemyndigheten "
"IRS i bilaga B till den årliga blankett 990."

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"If you donate by credit card, you will be asked for some information that's "
"required to process your credit card payment, including your billing address."
msgstr ""
"Om du donerar med betalkort ombeds du lämna viss information som krävs för "
"betalningen, bland annat faktureringsadress."

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"If you donate to the Tor Project, there will be some people at the Tor "
"Project who know about your donation."
msgstr ""
"Om du donerar till The Tor Project kommer vissa personer inom projektet att "
"känna till donationen."

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"If you have your monthly donation set up through PayPal, you can cancel your "
"donation by logging into PayPal."
msgstr ""
"Om din månadsdonation är konfigurerad via PayPal kan du avsluta den genom "
"att logga in på PayPal."

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"If you have your monthly donation set up to come directly from your credit "
"card, please contact [giving@torproject.org](mailto:giving@torproject.org) "
"with the following information:"
msgstr ""
"Om månadsdonationen dras direkt från betalkortet kontaktar du "
"[giving@torproject.org](mailto:giving@torproject.org) och anger följande "
"information:"

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"If you need any further help, please email [giving@torproject.org]"
"(mailto:giving@torproject.org)."
msgstr ""
"Om du behöver mer hjälp skickar du e-post till [giving@torproject.org]"
"(mailto:giving@torproject.org)."

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"If you need assistance making a gift with any of the methods above, please "
"email [giving@torproject.org](mailto:giving@torproject.org)."
msgstr ""
"Om du behöver hjälp med att ge en gåva genom någon av metoderna ovan skriver "
"du till [giving@torproject.org](mailto:giving@torproject.org)."

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"If you pay taxes in the United States, your donation is tax deductible to "
"the full extent required by law."
msgstr ""
"Om du betalar skatt i USA är donationen avdragsgill i den fulla utsträckning "
"som lagen medger."

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"If you require a receipt, contact us at [giving@torproject.org]"
"(mailto:giving@torproject.org) with verification of your transaction."
msgstr ""
"Om du behöver ett kvitto kontaktar du [giving@torproject.org]"
"(mailto:giving@torproject.org) och bifogar bekräftelse på transaktionen."

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"If you talk about your donation on social media (and we appreciate you doing "
"so!), we will take that to mean it's okay for us to engage with or amplify "
"your post."
msgstr ""
"Om du berättar om donationen i sociala medier (vilket vi uppskattar!) tolkar "
"vi det som att vi får interagera med eller sprida ditt inlägg."

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"If you were mailed a thank-you gift as a result of your monthly donation, "
"your refund will be limited to the amount of the donation above the gift "
"giving level."
msgstr ""
"Om du fick en tackgåva till följd av din månadsdonation begränsas "
"återbetalningen till den del av donationen som överstiger gåvonivån."

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"If you would like to make a bank transfer of more than $1,000 to the Tor "
"Project, please contact [giving@torproject.org]"
"(mailto:giving@torproject.org) with your name and phone number and Tor "
"Project will reach out to you to coordinate your donation."
msgstr ""
"Om du vill göra en banköverföring på mer än 1 000 USD till The Tor Project "
"kontaktar du [giving@torproject.org](mailto:giving@torproject.org) med namn "
"och telefonnummer, så kontaktar projektet dig för att samordna donationen."

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"If you'd rather not try any of the workarounds described above, we "
"understand!"
msgstr "Vi förstår om du inte vill prova någon av lösningarna ovan."

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"If you're using any third-party privacy extensions like Privacy Badger, "
"temporarily deactivate these and try again."
msgstr ""
"Om du använder integritetstillägg från tredje part, exempelvis Privacy "
"Badger, inaktiverar du dem tillfälligt och försöker igen."

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"If you've tried the above and still can't donate by credit card, [please "
"report the issue on the Tor forum](https://forum.torproject.net/t/donating-"
"via-credit-card-issue/724)."
msgstr ""
"Om du har provat ovanstående men fortfarande inte kan donera med betalkort "
"kan du [rapportera problemet i Tor-forumet](https://forum.torproject.net/t/"
"donating-via-credit-card-issue/724)."

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid "If your company sells cloud services, it could donate these to Tor."
msgstr ""
"Om ditt företag säljer molntjänster kan det donera sådana tjänster till Tor."

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"If, for any reason, we would like to publicly name you as a donor, we will "
"ask you first, and will not do it until and unless you say it's okay."
msgstr ""
"Om vi av någon anledning vill namnge dig offentligt som givare frågar vi dig "
"först och gör det endast om du samtycker."

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"In order to donate by credit card you may consider whitelisting "
"`donate.torproject.org` or temporarily enabling JavaScript."
msgstr ""
"För att donera med betalkort kan du tillåta `donate.torproject.org` eller "
"tillfälligt aktivera JavaScript."

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"In the U.S.: We can only accept donations via bank transfer for gifts more "
"than $1,000 USD."
msgstr ""
"I USA kan vi endast ta emot donationer via banköverföring när gåvan "
"överstiger 1 000 USD."

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"It may take up to 90 days to process your donation and mail an "
"acknowledgment letter. For a faster processing time, please donate online."
msgstr ""
"Det kan ta upp till 90 dagar att behandla donationen och posta ett "
"bekräftelsebrev. Donera på nätet för snabbare behandling."

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"No action is needed at this time. Your monthly donation will continue to be "
"restricted to Tails until further notice."
msgstr ""
"Ingen åtgärd krävs nu. Din månadsdonation förblir öronmärkt för Tails tills "
"vidare."

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid "No, sorry."
msgstr "Nej, tyvärr."

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"No, sorry. However, we are happy to consider your ideas and feedback about "
"our work—please send them to [giving@torproject.org]"
"(mailto:giving@torproject.org)."
msgstr ""
"Nej, tyvärr. Vi tar dock gärna emot idéer och återkoppling om vårt arbete. "
"Skicka dem till [giving@torproject.org](mailto:giving@torproject.org)."

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"No, there is no limit on your donation size. Please contact "
"[giving@torproject.org](mailto:giving@torproject.org) for any assistance "
"with large gift transfers."
msgstr ""
"Nej, det finns ingen övre gräns för donationens storlek. Kontakta "
"[giving@torproject.org](mailto:giving@torproject.org) om du behöver hjälp "
"med en större överföring."

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"Our team is happy to discuss potential partnerships and determine the best "
"path forward for implementation."
msgstr ""
"Vårt team diskuterar gärna möjliga samarbeten och hjälper till att hitta "
"bästa sättet att genomföra dem."

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"PayPal cannot process donations made via the Tor Network. We apologize for "
"the inconvenience."
msgstr ""
"PayPal kan inte behandla donationer som görs via Tor-nätverket. Vi beklagar "
"besväret."

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"Please be aware that the Tor Project does not own or endorse any "
"cryptocurrency coin at this time."
msgstr ""
"Observera att The Tor Project för närvarande varken äger eller stöder något "
"kryptovalutamynt."

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"Please contact [giving@torproject.org](mailto:giving@torproject.org) for "
"more information."
msgstr ""
"Kontakta [giving@torproject.org](mailto:giving@torproject.org) för mer "
"information."

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"Please email [giving@torproject.org](mailto:giving@torproject.org) with "
"ideas, proposals, or to start a conversation."
msgstr ""
"Skicka idéer och förslag till [giving@torproject.org]"
"(mailto:giving@torproject.org), eller skriv för att inleda ett samtal."

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid "Please email [giving@torproject.org](mailto:giving@torproject.org)."
msgstr ""
"Skicka e-post till [giving@torproject.org](mailto:giving@torproject.org)."

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid "Please make checks and money orders payable to The Tor Project, Inc."
msgstr "Ställ checkar och betalningsanvisningar till The Tor Project, Inc."

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"Please remember to re-enable your extensions after your donation has been "
"completed."
msgstr "Kom ihåg att aktivera tilläggen igen när donationen är slutförd."

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"Re-enable JavaScript. Stripe and PayPal both require JavaScript to work."
msgstr ""
"Aktivera JavaScript igen. Både Stripe och PayPal kräver JavaScript för att "
"fungera."

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"That means we won't post your name on our website, thank you on social media "
"or other public forums, nor do anything else that would publicly identify "
"you as someone who has donated to the Tor Project."
msgstr ""
"Det innebär att vi inte publicerar ditt namn på webbplatsen, tackar dig i "
"sociala medier eller andra offentliga forum eller på annat sätt offentligt "
"identifierar dig som givare till The Tor Project."

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid "The Tor Project is a 501(c)(3) organization."
msgstr "The Tor Project är en organisation enligt 501(c)(3)."

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"The Tor Project is open to experimenting with emerging funding models, "
"including quadratic funding, blockchain-based approaches, and contributions "
"from cryptocurrency and other digitally native communities."
msgstr ""
"The Tor Project är öppet för att experimentera med nya "
"finansieringsmodeller, bland annat kvadratisk finansiering, "
"blockkedjebaserade metoder och bidrag från kryptovaluta- och andra digitalt "
"inriktade gemenskaper."

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid "The amount you donate monthly"
msgstr "Beloppet du donerar varje månad"

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"The dollar amount at which we are required to report gifts changes annually, "
"as it is calculated based on the Tor Project's total revenue for the year, "
"so please contact us at [giving@torproject.org]"
"(mailto:giving@torproject.org) if you have questions about ensuring that "
"your gift falls under this threshold."
msgstr ""
"Det dollarbelopp över vilket vi måste rapportera gåvor ändras varje år, "
"eftersom det beräknas utifrån The Tor Projects totala intäkter för året. "
"Kontakta [giving@torproject.org](mailto:giving@torproject.org) om du har "
"frågor om hur du säkerställer att gåvan ligger under gränsen."

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"The easiest way to support the Tor Project financially as a company is "
"through the [Tor Project Membership Program](https://torproject.org/about/"
"membership/)."
msgstr ""
"Det enklaste sättet för ett företag att stödja The Tor Project ekonomiskt är "
"genom [The Tor Projects medlemsprogram](https://torproject.org/about/"
"membership/)."

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid "The email address used when you set up the monthly donation"
msgstr "E-postadressen som användes när månadsdonationen skapades"

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"The fastest way to find out if your company matches donations is by checking "
"with your HR department."
msgstr ""
"Det snabbaste sättet att ta reda på om ditt företag matchar donationer är "
"att fråga personalavdelningen."

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid "There are many ways you can make a donation from outside of the U.S.:"
msgstr "Du kan donera från ett land utanför USA på många olika sätt:"

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"There are probably other ways to donate anonymously that we haven't thought "
"of—maybe you will."
msgstr ""
"Det finns förmodligen fler sätt att donera anonymt som vi inte har tänkt på "
"– kanske hittar du ett."

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"These organizations are not the same as The Tor Project, Inc., but we "
"consider that a good thing."
msgstr ""
"Organisationerna är inte desamma som The Tor Project, Inc., vilket vi ser "
"som något positivt."

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"They're run by nice people who are part of the Tor community, and your "
"donation may be tax-deductible in your country."
msgstr ""
"De drivs av trevliga personer som ingår i Tor-gemenskapen, och donationen "
"kan vara avdragsgill i ditt land."

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"This allows our payment processor to verify your identity, process your "
"payment, and prevent fraudulent charges to your credit card."
msgstr ""
"Det gör att vår betalningsförmedlare kan verifiera din identitet, behandla "
"betalningen och förhindra bedrägliga debiteringar av betalkortet."

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"Tor Browser users on the Safest security level can do so by downgrading to "
"Safer in `about:preferences#privacy`."
msgstr ""
"Tor Browser-användare med säkerhetsnivån Säkrast kan sänka nivån till "
"Säkrare i `about:preferences#privacy`."

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"Unfortunately, some efforts have used the Tor name without proper "
"authorization and have not supported our mission."
msgstr ""
"Tyvärr har vissa insatser använt namnet Tor utan rätt tillstånd och utan att "
"stödja vårt uppdrag."

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid "Verification of your transaction"
msgstr "Bekräftelse på transaktionen"

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid "Visit our [support FAQ](/about-tor/)."
msgstr "Besök våra [vanliga supportfrågor](/about-tor/)."

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"We appreciate the time and good intentions of those who wish to support the "
"Tor Project."
msgstr ""
"Vi uppskattar tiden och de goda avsikterna hos dem som vill stödja The Tor "
"Project."

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"We are a small nonprofit. It can take a few weeks to receive your gift—and "
"more if you are outside of the U.S."
msgstr ""
"Vi är en liten ideell organisation. Det kan ta några veckor innan vi får din "
"gåva, och längre tid om du befinner dig utanför USA."

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"We don't ask for information beyond what's required by the payment processor."
msgstr "Vi ber inte om mer information än vad betalningsförmedlaren kräver."

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid "We encourage you to reach out to us directly with your ideas."
msgstr "Vi uppmuntrar dig att kontakta oss direkt med dina idéer."

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid "We evaluate funding opportunities based on three key factors:"
msgstr "Vi bedömer finansieringsmöjligheter utifrån tre huvudfaktorer:"

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"We use unrestricted donations to keep Tor strong, improve our software, and "
"help millions of people browse the internet privately and anonymously."
msgstr ""
"Vi använder donationer utan begränsat ändamål för att hålla Tor starkt, "
"förbättra programvaran och hjälpa miljontals människor att surfa privat och "
"anonymt."

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"We welcome community interest in supporting us through innovative "
"fundraising methods or by hosting a fundraisers on behalf of the Tor Project."
msgstr ""
"Vi välkomnar gemenskapens intresse för att stödja oss genom innovativa "
"insamlingsmetoder eller genom att anordna insamlingar för The Tor Project."

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"We will contact you directly before any changes are made to your automatic "
"monthly donation to Tails."
msgstr ""
"Vi kontaktar dig direkt innan några ändringar görs i din automatiska "
"månadsdonation till Tails."

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"We're aware of a few issues with our current donation form that may prevent "
"you from giving by credit card."
msgstr ""
"Vi känner till några problem med vårt nuvarande donationsformulär som kan "
"hindra dig från att donera med betalkort."

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"While we're working on fixing these, there are a few workarounds you can try "
"in the meantime:"
msgstr ""
"Medan vi arbetar med att åtgärda problemen kan du prova några tillfälliga "
"lösningar:"

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"Yes! Many companies—such as Google, Microsoft, eBay, PayPal, Apple, Verizon, "
"Red Hat, many universities, and others—will match donations made by their "
"employees."
msgstr ""
"Ja! Många företag, bland annat Google, Microsoft, eBay, PayPal, Apple, "
"Verizon, Red Hat och flera universitet, matchar sina anställdas donationer."

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"Yes. Contact us at [giving@torproject.org](mailto:giving@torproject.org) "
"with the following:"
msgstr ""
"Ja. Kontakta oss på [giving@torproject.org](mailto:giving@torproject.org) "
"och ange följande:"

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"Yes. Please contact us in advance at [giving@torproject.org]"
"(mailto:giving@torproject.org) if you are transmitting securities via DTC."
msgstr ""
"Ja. Kontakta oss i förväg på [giving@torproject.org]"
"(mailto:giving@torproject.org) om du överför värdepapper via DTC."

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid "Yes. Send checks, money orders, or gift cards to:"
msgstr "Ja. Skicka checkar, postanvisningar eller presentkort till:"

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"Yes. You can donate through Donor Advised Fund (DAF). Contact your financial "
"advisor or financial institution to select **The Tor Project Inc.**. (Tax-ID "
"# 20-8096820) as a grant recipient."
msgstr ""
"Ja. Du kan donera via en donationsfond (DAF). Kontakta din finansiella "
"rådgivare eller finansiella institution för att välja **The Tor Project "
"Inc.** (organisationsnummer 20-8096820) som mottagare av bidraget."

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"Yes. [Learn more about joining the Tor community](https://"
"community.torproject.org/) or [fundraise on behalf of the Tor Project](#)."
msgstr ""
"Ja. [Läs mer om hur du går med i Tor-gemenskapen](https://"
"community.torproject.org/) eller [samlar in pengar för The Tor Project](#)."

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"You can donate by sending us a cash gift card or a money order via mail."
msgstr ""
"Du kan donera genom att skicka oss ett presentkort med kontantbelopp eller "
"en postanvisning per post."

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"You can donate via cryptocurrency if you have it set up in a way that "
"preserves your anonymity."
msgstr ""
"Du kan donera kryptovaluta om du har konfigurerat den på ett sätt som "
"bevarar din anonymitet."

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"You can learn more about the Tor Project's funding on our [Reports page]"
"(https://www.torproject.org/about/reports/) by viewing U.S. 990 Tax Forms "
"and audited financial statements."
msgstr ""
"Du kan läsa mer om The Tor Projects finansiering på vår [rapportsida]"
"(https://www.torproject.org/about/reports/) genom att granska amerikanska "
"990-deklarationer och reviderade bokslut."

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"You can still donate cryptocurrency, send checks and money orders by mail, "
"or and make a donation via Open Collective in USD or EUR."
msgstr ""
"Du kan fortfarande donera kryptovaluta, skicka checkar och "
"betalningsanvisningar per post eller donera via Open Collective i USD eller "
"EUR."

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid "You may need the following information for reporting purposes:"
msgstr "Du kan behöva följande uppgifter för rapporteringen:"

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"You will not receive an automatically generated receipt if you donate any "
"form of cryptocurrency."
msgstr "Du får inget automatiskt genererat kvitto om du donerar kryptovaluta."

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid "Your company can also run a Tor relay or bridge."
msgstr "Ditt företag kan också driva ett Tor-relä eller en Tor-bro."

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid "Your mailing address"
msgstr "Din postadress"

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid "Your name"
msgstr "Ditt namn"

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"Your swag selection, including size (see [donate.torproject.org](https://"
"donate.torproject.org) for current options)"
msgstr ""
"Val av profilprodukt, inklusive storlek (aktuella alternativ finns på "
"[donate.torproject.org](https://donate.torproject.org))"

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid "[Bank Transfer (in the United States only)](#bank-transfer)"
msgstr "[Banköverföring (endast i USA)](#bank-transfer)"

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid "[Check, Money Order, or Gift Card](#check-money-order-gift-card)"
msgstr "[Check, postanvisning eller presentkort](#check-money-order-gift-card)"

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"[Copyright, Trademark and Brand Policy for The Tor Project (\"Tor\")]"
"(https://www.torproject.org/about/trademark/)"
msgstr ""
"[The Tor Projects policy för upphovsrätt, varumärken och varumärkesprofil "
"(”Tor”)](https://www.torproject.org/about/trademark/)"

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid "[Credit Card](https://donate.torproject.org/)"
msgstr "[Betalkort](https://donate.torproject.org/)"

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"[Cryptocurrency via BTCPayServer](https://donate.torproject.org/"
"cryptocurrency)"
msgstr ""
"[Kryptovaluta via BTCPayServer](https://donate.torproject.org/cryptocurrency)"

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"[Cryptocurrency via wallet address](https://donate.torproject.org/"
"cryptocurrency)"
msgstr ""
"[Kryptovaluta via plånboksadress](https://donate.torproject.org/"
"cryptocurrency)"

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid "[Donor Advised Fund (DAF)](#donor-advised-fund)"
msgstr "[Donationsfond (DAF)](#donor-advised-fund)"

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"[Here is the Tor Project donor privacy policy.](https://"
"donate.torproject.org/privacy-policy/)"
msgstr ""
"[Här är The Tor Projects integritetspolicy för givare.](https://"
"donate.torproject.org/privacy-policy/)"

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid "[Hosting a Fundraiser](#community-how-to)"
msgstr "[Anordna en insamling](#community-how-to)"

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"[Open Collective (USD $), Open Collective (EUR €)](https://"
"opencollective.com/thetorproject)"
msgstr ""
"[Open Collective (USD $), Open Collective (EUR €)](https://"
"opencollective.com/thetorproject)"

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid "[PayPal](https://donate.torproject.org)"
msgstr "[PayPal](https://donate.torproject.org)"

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"[Read our refund policy for fiat, cryptocurrency, and other circumstances.]"
"(https://donate.torproject.org/refund-policy/)"
msgstr ""
"[Läs vår återbetalningspolicy för fiatvaluta, kryptovaluta och andra "
"omständigheter.](https://donate.torproject.org/refund-policy/)"

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid "[Stock Donation](#donate-stock)"
msgstr "[Aktiedonation](#donate-stock)"

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"[You can donate directly to the Tor Project in USD ($) via our donate page]"
"(https://donate.torproject.org/), but your donation won't be tax-deductible "
"unless you pay taxes on U.S. income."
msgstr ""
"[Du kan donera direkt till The Tor Project i USD ($) via vår donationssida]"
"(https://donate.torproject.org/), men donationen är endast avdragsgill om du "
"betalar skatt på inkomster i USA."

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"[You can donate to a relay operator association organization in your region]"
"(https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/relay-"
"associations/)."
msgstr ""
"[Du kan donera till en organisation för reläoperatörer i din region](https://"
"community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/relay-associations/)."

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"[You can donate to the Tor Project in EUR (€) via Open Collective](https://"
"opencollective.com/thetorproject-europe), who will issue a receipt for tax "
"purposes for donations of €10,000 or more."
msgstr ""
"[Du kan donera till The Tor Project i EUR (€) via Open Collective](https://"
"opencollective.com/thetorproject-europe), som utfärdar ett skattekvitto för "
"donationer på minst 10 000 euro."

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid "Can I donate hardware?"
msgstr "Kan jag donera maskinvara?"

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid "Can I donate my airline miles, flight vouchers, or hotel points?"
msgstr "Kan jag donera flygpoäng, flygvärdebevis eller hotellpoäng?"

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid "Can I donate my time?"
msgstr "Kan jag donera min tid?"

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid "Can I donate stock?"
msgstr "Kan jag donera aktier?"

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid "Can I donate through a Donor Advised Fund (DAF)?"
msgstr "Kan jag donera via en donationsfond (DAF)?"

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid "Can I donate with a check, money order, or gift card?"
msgstr "Kan jag donera med check, postanvisning eller presentkort?"

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid "Can I make a donation if I don't live in the United States?"
msgstr "Kan jag donera om jag inte bor i USA?"

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid "Can I make a donation via bank transfer?"
msgstr "Kan jag donera via banköverföring?"

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid "Can I restrict my donation to a particular purpose or project?"
msgstr "Kan jag begränsa donationen till ett visst ändamål eller projekt?"

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid "Can I still restrict my donation to Tails?"
msgstr "Kan jag fortfarande öronmärka donationen för Tails?"

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.title
#: content/donation/contents.lr:nav_item.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid "Community fundraising"
msgstr "Insamling i gemenskapen"

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.title
#: content/donation/contents.lr:nav_item.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid "Companies"
msgstr "Företag"

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid "Do I need to make a donation to use Tor?"
msgstr "Måste jag donera för att använda Tor?"

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid "Does Tor Project accept matching donations?"
msgstr "Tar The Tor Project emot matchade donationer?"

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.title
#: content/donation/contents.lr:nav_item.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid "Gifts"
msgstr "Gåvor"

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid "Help! Donating by credit card isn't working"
msgstr "Hjälp! Det går inte att donera med betalkort"

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid "How can I donate to the Tor Project?"
msgstr "Hur kan jag donera till The Tor Project?"

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid "How can I get a refund for my donation?"
msgstr "Hur kan jag få en donation återbetalad?"

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid "How can I propose a new fundraising idea?"
msgstr "Hur föreslår jag en ny insamlingsidé?"

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid "How do I cancel my monthly donation?"
msgstr "Hur avslutar jag min månadsdonation?"

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid "How to fundraise on behalf of the Tor Project?"
msgstr "Hur samlar jag in pengar för The Tor Project?"

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid "How will you use my donation?"
msgstr "Hur använder ni min donation?"

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid "I donated cryptocurrency, can I get stickers, t-shirts, or hoodies?"
msgstr ""
"Jag donerade kryptovaluta. Kan jag få klistermärken, T-shirt eller huvtröja?"

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid "I donated cryptocurrency, where is my receipt?"
msgstr "Jag donerade kryptovaluta. Var är mitt kvitto?"

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid "I have questions about how Tor works, where can I learn more?"
msgstr "Jag har frågor om hur Tor fungerar. Var kan jag läsa mer?"

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid "I would like my company to support Tor. What can we do to help?"
msgstr "Mitt företag vill stödja Tor. Hur kan vi hjälpa till?"

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"If I want my donation to be anonymous, what is the best way for me to donate?"
msgstr "Hur donerar jag bäst om jag vill vara anonym?"

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"In your privacy policy, you say you will never publicly identify me as a "
"donor without my permission. What does that mean?"
msgstr ""
"I integritetspolicyn står det att ni aldrig offentligt identifierar mig som "
"givare utan mitt tillstånd. Vad innebär det?"

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid "Is my donation tax-deductible?"
msgstr "Är min donation avdragsgill?"

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"Is the Tor Project required to identify me as a donor to the United States "
"government, or to any other authority?"
msgstr ""
"Måste The Tor Project identifiera mig som givare för USA:s regering eller "
"någon annan myndighet?"

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid "Is there a maximum donation?"
msgstr "Finns det ett högsta donationsbelopp?"

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.title
#: content/donation/contents.lr:nav_item.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid "Other questions"
msgstr "Andra frågor"

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.title
#: content/donation/contents.lr:nav_item.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid "Privacy"
msgstr "Integritet"

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.title
#: content/donation/contents.lr:nav_item.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid "Ways to give"
msgstr "Sätt att ge"

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"What are your criteria for hosting a fundraiser on behalf of the Tor Project?"
msgstr ""
"Vilka kriterier använder ni för att godkänna en insamling för The Tor "
"Project?"

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"What happens if I do not get approval from the Tor Project to fundraise?"
msgstr "Vad händer om jag samlar in pengar utan The Tor Projects godkännande?"

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid "What is your donor privacy policy?"
msgstr "Vilken integritetspolicy gäller för givare?"

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid "What should I do if I make an automatic monthly donation to Tails?"
msgstr "Vad ska jag göra om jag har en automatisk månadsdonation till Tails?"

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid "What will happen to my donations to Tails made in the past?"
msgstr "Vad händer med donationer som jag tidigare har gjort till Tails?"

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid "When will I get my stickers, t-shirt, or hoodie?"
msgstr "När får jag klistermärken, T-shirt eller huvtröja?"

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid "Where can I view U.S. state disclosure statements?"
msgstr "Var hittar jag amerikanska delstaters informationsmeddelanden?"

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid "Why do you ask for my address and similar information?"
msgstr "Varför frågar ni efter min adress och liknande uppgifter?"

#: content/donation/contents.lr:accordion_item.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid "Why is there a minimum donation?"
msgstr "Varför finns ett minimibelopp för donationer?"

#: content/donation/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/donation/
msgid ""
"Find answers to the most common questions about donating to the Tor Project, "
"a 501(c)(3) nonprofit."
msgstr ""
"Svar på de vanligaste frågorna om donationer till The Tor Project, en ideell "
"organisation enligt 501(c)(3)."

#: content/errorpages/404/contents.lr:errorpage.help_text
#: https://support.torproject.org/errorpages/404/
msgid ""
"If you think this is a mistake, please send us a [bug report](https://"
"support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/)."
msgstr ""
"Om du tror att detta är ett misstag kan du skicka en [felrapport](https://"
"support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/)."

#: content/errorpages/404/contents.lr:errorpage.help_text
#: https://support.torproject.org/errorpages/404/
msgid ""
"It may have been moved or deleted, or there could be a typo in the address."
msgstr ""
"Sidan kan ha flyttats eller tagits bort, eller så kan adressen innehålla ett "
"skrivfel."

#: content/errorpages/404/contents.lr:errorpage.help_text
#: https://support.torproject.org/errorpages/404/
msgid "The page you requested does not exist."
msgstr "Sidan du begärde finns inte."

#: content/errorpages/404/contents.lr:errorpage.link_text
#: https://support.torproject.org/errorpages/404/
msgid "Return home"
msgstr "Tillbaka till startsidan"

#: content/errorpages/404/contents.lr:errorpage.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/errorpages/404/
msgid "Page not found"
msgstr "Sidan hittades inte"

#: content/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/
msgid ""
"There are different ways you can contact the Tor Project and what "
"information to include to help us resolve your issue quickly."
msgstr ""
"Det finns olika sätt att kontakta The Tor Project och olika uppgifter som "
"bör följa med för att vi snabbt ska kunna lösa problemet."

#: content/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/contents.lr:article.longer_title
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/
msgid ""
"How to contact the Tor Project team to report bugs, security issues, or "
"share feedback"
msgstr ""
"Så kontaktar du The Tor Project för att rapportera fel och säkerhetsproblem "
"eller lämna återkoppling"

#: content/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/contents.lr:article.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/
msgid "How to Report a Bug or Give Feedback"
msgstr "Rapportera ett fel eller lämna återkoppling"

#: content/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/
msgid "A Tor support specialist will assist you."
msgstr "En supportspecialist för Tor hjälper dig."

#: content/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/
msgid "A screenshot of the problem"
msgstr "En skärmbild av problemet"

#: content/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/contents.lr:content.content
#: content/get-in-touch/user-support/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/user-support/
msgid ""
"After sending a message, our support agents will guide you and help "
"troubleshoot your issue."
msgstr ""
"Efter att ha skickat ett meddelande kommer våra supportagenter att guida dig "
"och hjälpa till att felsöka ditt problem."

#: content/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/contents.lr:content.content
#: content/get-in-touch/user-support/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/user-support/
msgid "At the moment, for the fastest response, please write in English."
msgstr "För tillfället, för snabbast svar, skriv på engelska."

#: content/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/
msgid ""
"Before you ask, please review our [discussion guidelines](https://"
"forum.torproject.org/t/welcome-to-the-tor-project-forum/)."
msgstr ""
"Läs våra [diskussionsriktlinjer](https://forum.torproject.org/t/welcome-to-"
"the-tor-project-forum/) innan du frågar."

#: content/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/
msgid "Blog post comments"
msgstr "Kommentarer till blogginlägg"

#: content/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/contents.lr:content.content
#: content/get-in-touch/user-support/contents.lr:content.content
#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/getting-bridges/contents.lr:tab.title
#: content/tor-vpn/encountering-issues/feedback-and-support/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/user-support/
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/getting-bridges/
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-vpn/encountering-issues/feedback-and-support/
msgid "Email"
msgstr "E-post"

#: content/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/
msgid "Email Lists"
msgstr "E-postlistor"

#: content/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/
msgid "Feedback template"
msgstr "Mall för återkoppling"

#: content/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/contents.lr:content.content
#: content/get-in-touch/user-support/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/user-support/
msgid "First, check if the bug is already known."
msgstr "Kontrollera först om felet redan är känt."

#: content/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/
msgid ""
"For feedback or issues related to running a Tor relay: [tor-relays](https://"
"lists.torproject.org/mailman3/postorius/lists/tor-"
"relays.lists.torproject.org/)"
msgstr ""
"För återkoppling eller problem som gäller drift av ett Tor-relä: [tor-relays]"
"(https://lists.torproject.org/mailman3/postorius/lists/tor-"
"relays.lists.torproject.org/)"

#: content/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/
msgid ""
"For reporting issues or feedback using email lists, we recommend that you do "
"so on the one that is related to what you would like to report. A complete "
"directory of our mailing lists can be found [here](https://"
"lists.torproject.org/mailman3/postorius/lists/?count=100)."
msgstr ""
"När du rapporterar problem eller lämnar återkoppling via e-postlistor "
"rekommenderar vi att du använder den lista som hör till ämnet. En "
"fullständig katalog över e-postlistorna finns [här](https://"
"lists.torproject.org/mailman3/postorius/lists/?count=100)."

#: content/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/
msgid ""
"For the fastest response, please write in English, Spanish, and/or "
"Portuguese if you can."
msgstr ""
"Skriv helst på engelska, spanska och/eller portugisiska om du kan, så får du "
"snabbast svar."

#: content/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/
msgid "How to Reach Us"
msgstr "Så når du oss"

#: content/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/contents.lr:content.content
#: content/get-in-touch/user-support/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/user-support/
msgid ""
"If none of these languages works for you, please write in any language you "
"feel comfortable with, but keep in mind it will take us a bit longer to "
"answer as we will need help with translation to understand it."
msgstr ""
"Om inget av dessa språk fungerar för dig, skriv på vilket språk du känner "
"dig bekväm med, men tänk på att det kan ta lite längre tid för oss att svara "
"eftersom vi behöver hjälp med översättningen för att förstå det."

#: content/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/
msgid ""
"If there is not a blog post related to your issue, please contact us another "
"way."
msgstr ""
"Om det inte finns något blogginlägg om problemet kontaktar du oss på annat "
"sätt."

#: content/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/
msgid "If you found a bug, please use GitLab."
msgstr "Använd GitLab om du har hittat ett fel."

#: content/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/
msgid ""
"If you need help installing or troubleshooting Tor Browser and the [Tor "
"Forum](https://forum.torproject.org) is blocked or censored where you are, "
"you can reach out to us on Telegram [https://t.me/TorProjectSupportBot]"
"(https://t.me/TorProjectSupportBot)."
msgstr ""
"Om du behöver hjälp med att installera eller felsöka Tor Browser och [Tor "
"Forum](https://forum.torproject.org) är blockerat eller censurerat där du "
"befinner dig kan du kontakta oss på Telegram via [https://t.me/"
"TorProjectSupportBot](https://t.me/TorProjectSupportBot)."

#: content/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/
msgid ""
"If you want to encrypt your mail, you can get the OpenPGP public key for "
"this address from [keys.openpgp.org](https://keys.openpgp.org/search?"
"q=security%40torproject.org). Here is the current fingerprint:"
msgstr ""
"Om du vill kryptera e-posten kan du hämta den offentliga OpenPGP-nyckeln för "
"adressen från [keys.openpgp.org](https://keys.openpgp.org/search?"
"q=security%40torproject.org). Det aktuella fingeravtrycket är:"

#: content/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/
msgid ""
"If you wish to participate in our [bug bounty program](https://hackerone.com/"
"torproject), please be aware, submitting a security issue to a third-party "
"website carries certain risks that we cannot control, as a result we'd "
"prefer the report directly."
msgstr ""
"Om du vill delta i vårt [belöningsprogram för fel](https://hackerone.com/"
"torproject) bör du känna till att rapportering av ett säkerhetsproblem via "
"en tredjepartswebbplats medför risker som vi inte kan styra över. Vi "
"föredrar därför att få rapporten direkt."

#: content/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/
msgid "If you've found a security issue, please email security@torproject.org."
msgstr ""
"Om du har hittat ett säkerhetsproblem skriver du till "
"security@torproject.org."

#: content/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/contents.lr:content.content
#: content/get-in-touch/user-support/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/user-support/
msgid ""
"In the subject line of your email, please tell us what you're reporting."
msgstr ""
"I ämnesraden i ditt e-postmeddelande, berätta för oss vad du rapporterar."

#: content/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/contents.lr:content.content
#: content/get-in-touch/user-support/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/user-support/
msgid ""
"Issues related to our websites should be filed under the [Web issue tracker]"
"(https://gitlab.torproject.org/groups/tpo/web/-/work_items/)."
msgstr ""
"Problem med våra webbplatser ska rapporteras i [ärendehanteraren för webben]"
"(https://gitlab.torproject.org/groups/tpo/web/-/work_items/)."

#: content/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/
msgid ""
"Learn how to connect to [OFTC servers](../../get-in-touch/chat-with-us/)."
msgstr ""
"Läs om hur du ansluter till [OFTC-servrar](../../get-in-touch/chat-with-us/)."

#: content/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/
msgid "Matrix/IRC"
msgstr "Matrix/IRC"

#: content/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/
msgid "Operating System you are using"
msgstr "Operativsystemet du använder"

#: content/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/
msgid ""
"Or you can report bugs or send us feedback anonymously through [Anon Ticket]"
"(https://anonticket.torproject.org) without needing to create an account."
msgstr ""
"Du kan också rapportera fel eller lämna återkoppling anonymt via [Anon "
"Ticket](https://anonticket.torproject.org) utan att skapa ett konto."

#: content/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/
msgid "Report a security issue"
msgstr "Rapportera ett säkerhetsproblem"

#: content/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/
msgid ""
"Send us an email to [frontdesk@torproject.org]"
"(mailto:frontdesk@torproject.org)."
msgstr ""
"Skicka e-post till [frontdesk@torproject.org]"
"(mailto:frontdesk@torproject.org)."

#: content/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/contents.lr:content.content
#: content/get-in-touch/user-support/contents.lr:content.content
#: content/tor-vpn/encountering-issues/feedback-and-support/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/user-support/
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-vpn/encountering-issues/feedback-and-support/
msgid "Signal"
msgstr "Signal"

#: content/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/contents.lr:content.content
#: content/get-in-touch/user-support/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/user-support/
msgid ""
"Sometimes when we receive emails without subject lines, they're marked as "
"spam and we don't see them."
msgstr ""
"Ibland när vi får e-postmeddelanden utan ämnesrader markeras de som "
"skräppost och vi ser dem inte."

#: content/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/
msgid ""
"Step by step of how you got to the issue, so we can reproduce it (e.g. I "
"opened the browser, typed a url, clicked on (i) icon, then my browser "
"crashed)"
msgstr ""
"En stegvis beskrivning av hur problemet uppstod så att vi kan återskapa det "
"(exempel: Jag öppnade webbläsaren, skrev en URL, klickade på ikonen (i), och "
"sedan kraschade webbläsaren)"

#: content/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/
msgid "The log"
msgstr "Loggen"

#: content/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/contents.lr:content.content
#: content/get-in-touch/user-support/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/user-support/
msgid ""
"The more specific your subject line is (e.g. \"Connection failure\", "
"\"feedback on website\", \"feedback on Tor Browser, \"I need a bridge\"), "
"the easier it will be for us to understand and follow up."
msgstr ""
"Ju mer specifik din ämnesrad är (t.ex. \"Anslutningsfel\", \"återkoppling om "
"webbplatsen\", \"återkoppling om Tor Browser\", \"Jag behöver en bro\"), "
"desto lättare blir det för oss att förstå och följa upp."

#: content/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/contents.lr:content.content
#: content/get-in-touch/user-support/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/user-support/
msgid ""
"There are several ways to reach us, so please use what works best for you."
msgstr ""
"Det finns flera sätt att nå oss så använd det som fungerar bäst för dig."

#: content/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/contents.lr:content.content
#: content/get-in-touch/user-support/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/user-support/
msgid ""
"This service is only available for text messages; videos or calls are not "
"supported."
msgstr ""
"Den här tjänsten är endast tillgänglig för textmeddelanden; videor eller "
"samtal stöds inte."

#: content/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/
msgid ""
"To create a new issue, please [request a new account](https://"
"anonticket.torproject.org/) to access Tor Project's GitLab instance and "
"[find the right repository](https://gitlab.torproject.org/tpo) to report "
"your issue."
msgstr ""
"För att skapa ett nytt ärende [begär du ett nytt konto](https://"
"anonticket.torproject.org/) för åtkomst till The Tor Projects GitLab-instans "
"och [hittar rätt kodförråd](https://gitlab.torproject.org/tpo) där problemet "
"ska rapporteras."

#: content/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/
msgid "Tor Browser Security Level"
msgstr "Tor Browsers säkerhetsnivå"

#: content/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/
msgid "Tor Browser version"
msgstr "Tor Browser-version"

#: content/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/contents.lr:content.content
#: content/get-in-touch/user-support/contents.lr:content.content
#: content/tor-vpn/encountering-issues/feedback-and-support/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/user-support/
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-vpn/encountering-issues/feedback-and-support/
msgid "Tor Forum"
msgstr "Tor-forum"

#: content/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/
msgid ""
"Tor relies on the support of users and volunteers around the world to help "
"us improve our software and resources, so your feedback is extremely "
"valuable to us (and to all Tor users)."
msgstr ""
"Tor förlitar sig på stöd från användare och volontärer runt om i världen för "
"att hjälpa oss att förbättra vår programvara och resurser, så din feedback "
"är oerhört värdefull för oss (och för alla Tor-användare)."

#: content/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/
msgid ""
"We may not respond right away, but we do check the backlog and will get back "
"to you when we can."
msgstr ""
"Vi kanske inte svarar direkt, men vi går igenom kön och återkommer när vi "
"kan."

#: content/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/
msgid ""
"We recommend asking for help on the [Tor Forum](https://"
"forum.torproject.org)."
msgstr ""
"Vi rekommenderar att du ber om hjälp på [Tor Forum](https://"
"forum.torproject.org)."

#: content/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/contents.lr:content.content
#: content/get-in-touch/user-support/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/user-support/
msgid ""
"We track all Tor Browser related issues at [Tor Browser issue tracker]"
"(https://gitlab.torproject.org/tpo/applications/tor-browser/-/work_items/)."
msgstr ""
"Vi följer alla Tor Browser-relaterade problem i [Tor Browsers "
"ärendehanterare](https://gitlab.torproject.org/tpo/applications/tor-"
"browser/-/work_items/)."

#: content/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/contents.lr:content.content
#: content/get-in-touch/user-support/contents.lr:content.content
#: content/tor-vpn/encountering-issues/feedback-and-support/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/user-support/
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-vpn/encountering-issues/feedback-and-support/
msgid "WhatsApp"
msgstr "WhatsApp"

#: content/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/
msgid ""
"When sending us feedback or reporting a bug, please include as many of these "
"as possible:"
msgstr ""
"När du lämnar återkoppling eller rapporterar ett fel bör du ta med så många "
"som möjligt av följande uppgifter:"

#: content/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/
msgid ""
"You can always leave comments on the blog post related to the issue or "
"feedback you want to report."
msgstr ""
"Du kan alltid lämna en kommentar till blogginlägget som gäller problemet "
"eller återkopplingen."

#: content/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/contents.lr:content.content
#: content/get-in-touch/user-support/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/user-support/
msgid ""
"You can contact our team by sending a text message to our Signal number, "
"[+17787431312](https://signal.me/#p/+17787431312), or Signal username, "
"`@torsupport.89`."
msgstr ""
"Du kan kontakta vårt team genom att skicka ett textmeddelande till vårt "
"Signal-nummer, [+17787431312](https://signal.me/#p/+17787431312), eller "
"Signal-användarnamnet, `@torsupport.89`."

#: content/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/
msgid ""
"You can find us in the #tor channel on OFTC or on [#tor:matrix.org](https://"
"matrix.to/#/#tor:matrix.org) to give us feedback or report bugs/issues."
msgstr ""
"Du hittar oss i kanalen #tor på OFTC eller i [#tor:matrix.org](https://"
"matrix.to/#/#tor:matrix.org), där du kan lämna återkoppling eller rapportera "
"fel och problem."

#: content/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/contents.lr:content.content
#: content/get-in-touch/user-support/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/user-support/
msgid ""
"You can reach our support team with a text message to our WhatsApp number: "
"[+447421000612](https://wa.me/447421000612)."
msgstr ""
"Du kan nå vårt supportteam via sms till vårt WhatsApp-nummer: [+447421000612]"
"(https://wa.me/447421000612)."

#: content/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/contents.lr:content.content
#: content/get-in-touch/user-support/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/user-support/
msgid ""
"You can search and read all the issues at [https://gitlab.torproject.org/]"
"(https://gitlab.torproject.org/groups/tpo/-/work_items/)."
msgstr ""
"Du kan söka och läsa alla problem på [https://gitlab.torproject.org/]"
"(https://gitlab.torproject.org/groups/tpo/-/work_items/)."

#: content/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/
msgid "You will need to create an account to submit a new topic."
msgstr "Du måste skapa ett konto för att publicera ett nytt ämne."

#: content/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/contents.lr:content.content
#: content/get-in-touch/user-support/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/user-support/
msgid ""
"[Signal](https://signal.org/download/) is a free and privacy-focused "
"messaging app."
msgstr ""
"[Signal](https://signal.org/download/) är en gratis och integritetsfokuserad "
"meddelandeapp."

#: content/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/contents.lr:tab.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/bug-or-feedback/
msgid "Reporting issues"
msgstr "Rapportera problem"

#: content/get-in-touch/chat-with-us/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/chat-with-us/
msgid ""
"This article explains how to chat directly with Tor developers, relay "
"operators, and community members via Matrix or IRC."
msgstr ""
"Artikeln förklarar hur du kan chatta direkt med Tor-utvecklare, "
"reläoperatörer och medlemmar i gemenskapen via Matrix eller IRC."

#: content/get-in-touch/chat-with-us/contents.lr:article.longer_title
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/chat-with-us/
msgid "How to join conversations with Tor Project teams on Matrix and IRC"
msgstr "Så deltar du i samtal med The Tor Projects team på Matrix och IRC"

#: content/get-in-touch/chat-with-us/contents.lr:article.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/chat-with-us/
msgid "Chat with Tor developers"
msgstr "Chatta med Tor-utvecklare"

#: content/get-in-touch/chat-with-us/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/chat-with-us/
msgid "/nick yournick"
msgstr "/nick dittnamn"

#: content/get-in-touch/chat-with-us/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/chat-with-us/
msgid "1. Using an IRC client, log onto OFTC (irc.oftc.net)."
msgstr "1. Logga in på OFTC (irc.oftc.net) med en IRC-klient."

#: content/get-in-touch/chat-with-us/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/chat-with-us/
msgid ""
"1. When you register an account, NickServ will give you a link to a web page "
"where you can verify your account."
msgstr ""
"1. När du registrerar ett konto ger NickServ dig en länk till en webbsida "
"där kontot kan verifieras."

#: content/get-in-touch/chat-with-us/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/chat-with-us/
msgid ""
"2. If all is well, you will receive a message confirming the nickname "
"verification:"
msgstr ""
"2. Om allt fungerar får du ett meddelande som bekräftar att smeknamnet har "
"verifierats:"

#: content/get-in-touch/chat-with-us/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/chat-with-us/
msgid "2. Type: `/msg nickserv REGISTER yournewpassword your@email.address`"
msgstr "2. Skriv: `/msg nickserv REGISTER yournewpassword your@email.address`"

#: content/get-in-touch/chat-with-us/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/chat-with-us/
msgid "3. Hit enter."
msgstr "3. Tryck på Retur."

#: content/get-in-touch/chat-with-us/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/chat-with-us/
msgid ""
"After registering your nickname, to gain access to the #tor and other "
"protected channels, your nickname must be **verified**."
msgstr ""
"När smeknamnet har registrerats måste det **verifieras** för att du ska få "
"åtkomst till #tor och andra skyddade kanaler."

#: content/get-in-touch/chat-with-us/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/chat-with-us/
msgid "Check out our [list of channels](https://www.torproject.org/contact/)."
msgstr "Se vår [kanallista](https://www.torproject.org/contact/)."

#: content/get-in-touch/chat-with-us/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/chat-with-us/
msgid "Every time you log on to IRC, to identify your registered nick, type:"
msgstr ""
"Varje gång du loggar in på IRC identifierar du ditt registrerade smeknamn "
"genom att skriva:"

#: content/get-in-touch/chat-with-us/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/chat-with-us/
msgid ""
"For a long time, the Tor Project has been running many day-to-day activities "
"using the IRC network known as [OFTC](https://www.oftc.net/)."
msgstr ""
"The Tor Project har under lång tid genomfört många dagliga aktiviteter i IRC-"
"nätverket [OFTC](https://www.oftc.net/)."

#: content/get-in-touch/chat-with-us/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/chat-with-us/
msgid ""
"For regular Tor users, it means that you can chat with us using a friendly "
"App like [Element](https://app.element.io)."
msgstr ""
"För vanliga Tor-användare innebär det att du kan chatta med oss genom en "
"lättanvänd app som [Element](https://app.element.io)."

#: content/get-in-touch/chat-with-us/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/chat-with-us/
msgid "Here's how to reach #tor and other registered channels."
msgstr "Så når du #tor och andra registrerade kanaler."

#: content/get-in-touch/chat-with-us/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/chat-with-us/
msgid "If all goes well, you will receive a message that you are registered."
msgstr "Om allt fungerar får du ett meddelande om att du är registrerad."

#: content/get-in-touch/chat-with-us/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/chat-with-us/
msgid "If so, just go with it but remember you are user_ and not user."
msgstr ""
"Följ i så fall anvisningen, men kom ihåg att ditt namn är användare_ och "
"inte användare."

#: content/get-in-touch/chat-with-us/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/chat-with-us/
msgid "Joining a IRC channel"
msgstr "Anslut till en IRC-kanal"

#: content/get-in-touch/chat-with-us/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/chat-with-us/
msgid ""
"OFTC often doesn't allow people to use their webchat over Tor, but you can "
"use an IRC client to [connect using Tor](https://www.oftc.net/Tor/)."
msgstr ""
"OFTC tillåter ofta inte att deras webbchatt används över Tor, men du kan "
"använda en IRC-klient för att [ansluta via Tor](https://www.oftc.net/Tor/)."

#: content/get-in-touch/chat-with-us/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/chat-with-us/
msgid ""
"Once you have a Matrix account, you can either [join the Tor Matrix Space]"
"(https://matrix.to/#/#tor-space:matrix.org) to browse the Tor rooms, or "
"directly join the [#tor:matrix.org user support](https://matrix.to/#/"
"#tor:matrix.org) room."
msgstr ""
"När du har ett Matrix-konto kan du antingen [gå med i Tor Matrix Space]"
"(https://matrix.to/#/#tor-space:matrix.org) för att bläddra bland Tor-rummen "
"eller gå direkt till rummet för användarsupport, [#tor:matrix.org](https://"
"matrix.to/#/#tor:matrix.org)."

#: content/get-in-touch/chat-with-us/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/chat-with-us/
msgid ""
"One of these is the Matrix.org Foundation, which allows people to register "
"an account for free."
msgstr ""
"En av leverantörerna är Matrix.org Foundation, där du kan registrera ett "
"kostnadsfritt konto."

#: content/get-in-touch/chat-with-us/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/chat-with-us/
msgid ""
"People may be able to answer right away, or there may be a bit of a delay "
"(some people are listed on the channel but are away from their keyboards and "
"record channel activities to read later)."
msgstr ""
"Någon kanske svarar direkt, men det kan också dröja en stund. Vissa personer "
"visas i kanalen men är borta från tangentbordet och sparar kanalens "
"aktivitet för att läsa senare."

#: content/get-in-touch/chat-with-us/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/chat-with-us/
msgid "Please, don't ask to ask, just ask your question."
msgstr "Fråga inte om du får fråga – ställ bara din fråga."

#: content/get-in-touch/chat-with-us/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/chat-with-us/
msgid "Register your nickname"
msgstr "Registrera ditt smeknamn"

#: content/get-in-touch/chat-with-us/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/chat-with-us/
msgid ""
"The Tor community is opening up its day-to-day conversations by bridging our "
"IRC community to the Matrix network."
msgstr ""
"Tor-gemenskapen öppnar sina dagliga samtal genom att koppla samman IRC-"
"gemenskapen med Matrix-nätverket."

#: content/get-in-touch/chat-with-us/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/chat-with-us/
msgid ""
"The [#tor:matrix.org](https://matrix.to/#/#tor:matrix.org) room or the #tor "
"IRC channel are connected: whichever platform you chose, your message will "
"be shared on both platforms."
msgstr ""
"Rummet [#tor:matrix.org](https://matrix.to/#/#tor:matrix.org) och IRC-"
"kanalen #tor är sammankopplade: oavsett vilken plattform du väljer delas "
"meddelandet på båda."

#: content/get-in-touch/chat-with-us/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/chat-with-us/
msgid ""
"The link will expire after one hour, but you can ask for a new link by "
"typing: `/msg nickserv REVERIFY`"
msgstr ""
"Länken upphör att gälla efter en timme, men du kan begära en ny genom att "
"skriva: `/msg nickserv REVERIFY`"

#: content/get-in-touch/chat-with-us/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/chat-with-us/
msgid "The system may register you as your nick_ instead of your nick."
msgstr "Systemet kan registrera dig som dittnamn_ i stället för dittnamn."

#: content/get-in-touch/chat-with-us/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/chat-with-us/
msgid "To join #tor IRC channel, you can just type `/join #tor` and hit enter."
msgstr ""
"För att ansluta till IRC-kanalen #tor skriver du `/join #tor` och trycker på "
"Retur."

#: content/get-in-touch/chat-with-us/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/chat-with-us/
msgid ""
"To join the conversation with Tor contributors on Matrix, you need a Matrix "
"account. Several providers can get you one."
msgstr ""
"För att delta i samtal med Tor-bidragsgivare på Matrix behöver du ett Matrix-"
"konto. Det finns flera leverantörer."

#: content/get-in-touch/chat-with-us/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/chat-with-us/
msgid "Verify your nickname"
msgstr "Verifiera smeknamnet"

#: content/get-in-touch/chat-with-us/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/chat-with-us/
msgid ""
"You can register an account on [app.element.io](https://app.element.io)."
msgstr ""
"Du kan registrera ett konto på [app.element.io](https://app.element.io)."

#: content/get-in-touch/chat-with-us/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/chat-with-us/
msgid "You will need to solve a Captcha in order to verify your account."
msgstr "Du måste lösa en captcha för att verifiera kontot."

#: content/get-in-touch/chat-with-us/contents.lr:tab.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/chat-with-us/
msgid "IRC"
msgstr "IRC"

#: content/get-in-touch/chat-with-us/contents.lr:tab.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/chat-with-us/
msgid "Matrix"
msgstr "Matrix"

#: content/get-in-touch/user-support/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/user-support/
msgid ""
"Find out how to contact the Tor Project for support, bug reports, and "
"feedback."
msgstr ""
"Läs om hur du kontaktar The Tor Project för support, felrapporter och "
"återkoppling."

#: content/get-in-touch/user-support/contents.lr:article.longer_title
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/user-support/
msgid "How to get help, report a bug or give feedback to the Tor Project"
msgstr ""
"Så får du hjälp, rapporterar ett fel eller lämnar återkoppling till The Tor "
"Project"

#: content/get-in-touch/user-support/contents.lr:article.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/user-support/
msgid "Tor User Support"
msgstr "Användarsupport för Tor"

#: content/get-in-touch/user-support/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/user-support/
msgid "1. Operating System you are using"
msgstr "1. Operativsystem du använder"

#: content/get-in-touch/user-support/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/user-support/
msgid "1. [@GetTor_Bot](https://t.me/GetTor_Bot) to download Tor Browser."
msgstr "1. [@GetTor_Bot](https://t.me/GetTor_Bot) för att hämta Tor Browser."

#: content/get-in-touch/user-support/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/user-support/
msgid "10. Is Tor censored in your region?"
msgstr "10. Är Tor censurerat i din region?"

#: content/get-in-touch/user-support/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/user-support/
msgid ""
"11. If Tor did connect, how much time did it take to bootstrap? Any effects "
"on browsing speed?"
msgstr ""
"11. Om Tor anslöt, hur lång tid tog det att starta upp? Några effekter på "
"surfhastigheten?"

#: content/get-in-touch/user-support/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/user-support/
msgid "2. Tor Browser version"
msgstr "2. Tor Browser-version"

#: content/get-in-touch/user-support/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/user-support/
msgid "2. [@GetBridgesBot](https://t.me/GetBridgesBot) to get obfs4 bridges."
msgstr ""
"2. [@GetBridgesBot](https://t.me/GetBridgesBot) för att hämta obfs4-broar."

#: content/get-in-touch/user-support/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/user-support/
msgid "3. Tor Browser Security Level"
msgstr "3. Säkerhetsnivå för Tor Browser"

#: content/get-in-touch/user-support/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/user-support/
msgid "3. [@TorProject](https://t.me/TorProject) to get the latest news."
msgstr ""
"3. [@TorProject](https://t.me/TorProject) för att få de senaste nyheterna."

#: content/get-in-touch/user-support/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/user-support/
msgid ""
"4. Step by step of how you got to the issue, so we can reproduce it (e.g. I "
"opened the browser, typed a url, clicked on a option in settings, then my "
"browser crashed)"
msgstr ""
"4. Beskriv steg för steg hur problemet uppstod så att vi kan återskapa det "
"(exempelvis: jag öppnade webbläsaren, skrev en URL, klickade på ett "
"alternativ i inställningarna och sedan kraschade webbläsaren)"

#: content/get-in-touch/user-support/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/user-support/
msgid "4. [@TorProjectSupportBot](https://t.me/TorProjectSupportBot) for help."
msgstr ""
"4. [@TorProjectSupportBot](https://t.me/TorProjectSupportBot) för hjälp."

#: content/get-in-touch/user-support/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/user-support/
msgid "5. A screenshot of the problem"
msgstr "5. En skärmdump av problemet"

#: content/get-in-touch/user-support/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/user-support/
msgid ""
"6. Console logs on Tor Browser Desktop (can be opened by Ctrl+Shift+J on "
"Windows/Linux and Cmd+Shift+J on macOS)"
msgstr ""
"6. Konsolloggar på Tor Browser för skrivbordet (kan öppnas med Ctrl+Skift+J "
"i Windows/Linux och Cmd+Skift+J i macOS)"

#: content/get-in-touch/user-support/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/user-support/
msgid "7. Tor logs (Settings > Connection > Advanced > View the Tor logs)"
msgstr ""
"7. Tor-loggar (Inställningar > Anslutning > Avancerat > Visa Tor-loggarna)"

#: content/get-in-touch/user-support/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/user-support/
msgid "8. Region you're connecting to Tor from."
msgstr "8. Region du ansluter till Tor från."

#: content/get-in-touch/user-support/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/user-support/
msgid ""
"9. Region selected from Connection Assist (if it's a Connection Assist "
"related issue)"
msgstr ""
"9. Region vald från Anslutningshjälp (om det är ett problem relaterat till "
"Anslutningshjälp)"

#: content/get-in-touch/user-support/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/user-support/
msgid ""
"At the moment, the Telegram support channel is available in English, Russian "
"and Farsi."
msgstr ""
"För närvarande är Telegrams supportkanal tillgänglig på engelska, ryska och "
"farsi."

#: content/get-in-touch/user-support/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/user-support/
msgid ""
"Currently, our support channel is available in English, Russian, Farsi and "
"focuses on helping Tor users in censored regions."
msgstr ""
"För närvarande är vår supportkanal tillgänglig på engelska, ryska och farsi "
"och fokuserar på att hjälpa Tor-användare i censurerade regioner."

#: content/get-in-touch/user-support/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/user-support/
msgid ""
"For the fastest response, please write in English, Russian, Farsi, Spanish, "
"Hindi, Bangla and/or Portuguese if you can."
msgstr ""
"För snabbast möjliga svar, skriv på engelska, ryska, farsi, spanska, hindi, "
"bengali och/eller portugisiska om du kan."

#: content/get-in-touch/user-support/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/user-support/
msgid "Friday to Sunday: the helpline is closed."
msgstr "Fredag till söndag: hjälplinjen är stängd."

#: content/get-in-touch/user-support/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/user-support/
msgid "How to reach us"
msgstr "Så når du oss"

#: content/get-in-touch/user-support/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/user-support/
msgid "IRC and Matrix"
msgstr "IRC och Matrix"

#: content/get-in-touch/user-support/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/user-support/
msgid ""
"If you found a bug, please use [GitLab](https://anonticket.torproject.org/)."
msgstr ""
"Använd [GitLab](https://anonticket.torproject.org/) om du har hittat ett fel."

#: content/get-in-touch/user-support/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/user-support/
msgid ""
"If you need help with circumventing censorship, please select from the menu "
"options which region you are connecting from as it will be easier for us to "
"follow up."
msgstr ""
"Om du behöver hjälp med att kringgå censur väljer du i menyn vilken region "
"du ansluter från, så blir det enklare för oss att följa upp."

#: content/get-in-touch/user-support/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/user-support/
msgid "Learn how to connect to [IRC / Matrix](../chat-with-us/)."
msgstr "Läs om hur du ansluter till [IRC/Matrix](../chat-with-us/)."

#: content/get-in-touch/user-support/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/user-support/
msgid ""
"Monday to Thursday: our user support channels on email, Telegram, WhatsApp, "
"and Signal are operational."
msgstr ""
"Måndag till torsdag: våra användarsupportkanaler på e-post, Telegram, "
"WhatsApp och Signal är öppna."

#: content/get-in-touch/user-support/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/user-support/
msgid "Please rest assured our team will get back to your messages on Monday."
msgstr "Du kan vara säker på att teamet svarar på dina meddelanden på måndag."

#: content/get-in-touch/user-support/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/user-support/
msgid ""
"Please review our [discussion guidelines](https://forum.torproject.org/t/"
"welcome-to-the-tor-project-forum/) and check the existing topics before "
"asking."
msgstr ""
"Granska våra [diskussionsriktlinjer](https://forum.torproject.org/t/welcome-"
"to-the-tor-project-forum/) och kontrollera befintliga ämnen innan du frågar."

#: content/get-in-touch/user-support/contents.lr:content.content
#: content/tor-vpn/encountering-issues/feedback-and-support/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/user-support/
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-vpn/encountering-issues/feedback-and-support/
msgid ""
"Send us an email to [frontdesk@torproject.org]"
"(mailto:frontdesk@torproject.org)"
msgstr ""
"Skicka ett e-postmeddelande till [frontdesk@torproject.org]"
"(mailto:frontdesk@torproject.org)"

#: content/get-in-touch/user-support/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/user-support/
msgid ""
"The service is only available for text messages; videos, or calls are not "
"supported."
msgstr ""
"Tjänsten är endast tillgänglig för textmeddelanden; videor eller samtal "
"stöds inte."

#: content/get-in-touch/user-support/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/user-support/
msgid ""
"To create a new issue, please [request a new account](https://"
"anonticket.torproject.org/user/gitlab-account/create/) to access Tor "
"Project's GitLab instance and [find the right repository](https://"
"gitlab.torproject.org/tpo) to report your issue."
msgstr ""
"För att skapa ett nytt ärende, vänligen [begär ett nytt konto](https://"
"anonticket.torproject.org/user/gitlab-account/create/) för att komma åt Tor "
"Projects GitLab-instans och [hitta rätt arkiv](https://gitlab.torproject.org/"
"tpo) för att rapportera ditt ärende."

#: content/get-in-touch/user-support/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/user-support/
msgid "Tor user support team office hours"
msgstr "Tor-användarsupportteamets öppettider"

#: content/get-in-touch/user-support/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/user-support/
msgid "We have several official Telegram bots and channels:"
msgstr "Vi har flera officiella Telegram-botar och -kanaler:"

#: content/get-in-touch/user-support/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/user-support/
msgid ""
"We recommend asking for help on the [Tor Forum](https://"
"forum.torproject.org/)."
msgstr ""
"Vi rekommenderar att du ber om hjälp på [Tor Forum](https://"
"forum.torproject.org/)."

#: content/get-in-touch/user-support/contents.lr:content.content
#: content/tor-vpn/encountering-issues/feedback-and-support/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/user-support/
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-vpn/encountering-issues/feedback-and-support/
msgid ""
"When sending us a support request, feedback or reporting a bug, please "
"include as much information possible:"
msgstr ""
"När du skickar en supportförfrågan, lämnar återkoppling eller rapporterar "
"ett fel bör du ta med så mycket information som möjligt:"

#: content/get-in-touch/user-support/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/user-support/
msgid ""
"You can find us in the `#tor` channel on OFTC or [Tor User Support channel]"
"(https://matrix.to/#/#tor:matrix.org) on Matrix. We may not respond right "
"away, but we do check the backlog and will get back to you when we can."
msgstr ""
"Du hittar oss i kanalen `#tor` på OFTC eller i [Tor-användarsupportkanalen]"
"(https://matrix.to/#/#tor:matrix.org) på Matrix. Vi svarar kanske inte "
"direkt, men läser tidigare meddelanden och återkommer när vi kan."

#: content/get-in-touch/user-support/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/user-support/
msgid "You will need to create a account to submit a new topic."
msgstr "Du måste skapa ett konto för att publicera ett nytt ämne."

#: content/get-in-touch/user-support/contents.lr:tab.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/user-support/
msgid "User support"
msgstr "Användarsupport"

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"\"Tor log\" is an automatically-generated list of [Tor](#tor-network-core-"
"tor)'s activity that can help diagnose problems."
msgstr ""
"En ”Tor-logg” är en automatiskt genererad lista över [Tors](#tor-network-"
"core-tor) aktivitet som kan hjälpa till att diagnostisera problem."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"\"little-t tor\" is one way of referring to tor the network daemon, as "
"opposed to Tor Browser or Tor Project."
msgstr ""
"”little-t tor” är ett sätt att syfta på nätverksdemonen tor, till skillnad "
"från Tor Browser eller The Tor Project."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid "**Orfox is no longer maintained or supported**."
msgstr "**Orfox underhålls eller stöds inte längre**."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"A browser history is a record of requests made while using a [web browser]"
"(#web-browser), and includes information like websites visited and when."
msgstr ""
"Webbläsarhistorik är en förteckning över förfrågningar som har gjorts i en "
"[webbläsare](#web-browser), med uppgifter som besökta webbplatser och "
"tidpunkter."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"A cryptographic hash value is the result of a mathematical algorithm that "
"maps data to a bit string of a fixed size."
msgstr ""
"Ett kryptografiskt hashvärde är resultatet av en matematisk algoritm som "
"avbildar data till en bitsträng med fast storlek."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"A cryptographic signature proves the authenticity of a message or file. It "
"is created by the holder of the private portion of a [public key "
"cryptography](#public-key-cryptography) key pair and can be verified by the "
"corresponding public key. If you download software from torproject.org, you "
"will find it as signature files (.asc). These are PGP signatures, so you can "
"verify that the file you have downloaded is exactly the one that we intended "
"you to get."
msgstr ""
"En kryptografisk signatur bevisar att ett meddelande eller en fil är äkta. "
"Den skapas av innehavaren av den privata delen av ett nyckelpar för "
"[kryptografi med offentliga nycklar](#public-key-cryptography) och kan "
"verifieras med motsvarande offentliga nyckel. När du hämtar programvara från "
"torproject.org finns signaturen i filer med ändelsen .asc. Det är PGP-"
"signaturer som gör att du kan kontrollera att den hämtade filen är exakt den "
"fil vi avsåg att du skulle få."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"A daemon is a computer program that runs as a background process, rather "
"than being under the direct control of a user."
msgstr ""
"En demon är ett datorprogram som körs som en bakgrundsprocess i stället för "
"under direkt kontroll av en användare."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"A device on a network that offers a service, such as file and web page "
"storage, email or chat."
msgstr ""
"En enhet i ett nätverk som erbjuder en tjänst, exempelvis lagring av filer "
"och webbsidor, e-post eller chatt."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"A feature in Tor Browser that when required will offer to automatically "
"apply the bridge configuration which works best in the user's location."
msgstr ""
"En funktion i Tor Browser som vid behov erbjuder sig att automatiskt använda "
"den brokonfiguration som fungerar bäst där användaren befinner sig."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"A firewall is a network security system that monitors and controls incoming "
"and outgoing network [traffic](#traffic)."
msgstr ""
"En brandvägg är ett nätverkssäkerhetssystem som övervakar och styr "
"inkommande och utgående [trafik](#traffic)."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"A hashring is a distributed structure used to store a set of keys and "
"associated values."
msgstr ""
"En hashring är en distribuerad struktur som används för att lagra en "
"uppsättning nycklar och tillhörande värden."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"A path through the [Tor network](#tor-network-core-tor) built by [clients]"
"(#client) consisting of randomly selected nodes."
msgstr ""
"En väg genom [Tor-nätverket](#tor-network-core-tor) som byggs av [klienter]"
"(#client) och består av slumpmässigt valda noder."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"A proxy is a middle man between a [client](#client) (like a [web browser]"
"(#web-browser)) and a service (like a [web server](#server))."
msgstr ""
"En proxy är en mellanhand mellan en [klient](#client), exempelvis en "
"[webbläsare](#web-browser), och en tjänst, exempelvis en [webbserver]"
"(#server)."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid "A public-key cryptography system uses pairs of mathematical keys."
msgstr ""
"Ett system för kryptografi med offentliga nycklar använder par av "
"matematiska nycklar."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"A publicly-listed node in the [Tor network](#tor-network-core-tor) that "
"forwards [traffic](#traffic) on behalf of [clients](#client), and that "
"registers itself with the [directory authorities](#directory-authority)."
msgstr ""
"En offentligt listad nod i [Tor-nätverket](#tor-network-core-tor) som "
"vidarebefordrar [trafik](#traffic) åt [klienter](#client) och registrerar "
"sig hos [katalogauktoriteterna](#directory-authority)."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"A session refers to a conversation between two devices communicating on a "
"network."
msgstr "En session är en kommunikation mellan två enheter i ett nätverk."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"A short, four emoji visualization which can be used to identify the right "
"bridge address at a glance."
msgstr ""
"En kort visuell representation med fyra emojier som gör det möjligt att "
"snabbt känna igen rätt bro-adress."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"A single onion service is an onion service that can be configured for "
"services that do not require anonymity, but want to offer it for clients "
"connecting to their service."
msgstr ""
"En enkel onion-tjänst är en onion-tjänst som kan konfigureras för tjänster "
"som inte behöver anonymitet men vill erbjuda anonymitet till klienter som "
"ansluter till tjänsten."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"A special-purpose [relay](#relay) that maintains a list of currently-running "
"relays and periodically publishes a [consensus](#consensus) together with "
"the other directory authorities."
msgstr ""
"Ett specialiserat [relä](#relay) som håller en lista över reläer som körs "
"för närvarande och regelbundet publicerar ett [konsensusdokument]"
"(#consensus) tillsammans med de andra katalogauktoriteterna."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid "A special-purpose relay that maintains the list of [bridges](#bridge)."
msgstr "Ett specialiserat relä som underhåller listan över [broar](#bridge)."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"A standardized Internet domain name used by onion services that end "
"in .onion and is designed to be [self-authenticating](#self-authenticating-"
"address)."
msgstr ""
"Ett standardiserat internetdomännamn som används av onion-tjänster, slutar "
"på .onion och är utformat för att vara [självautentiserande](#self-"
"authenticating-address)."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"A web application (web app), is an application that the [client](#client) "
"runs in a [web browser](#web-browser)."
msgstr ""
"Ett webbprogram (en webbapp) är ett program som [klienten](#client) kör i en "
"[webbläsare](#web-browser)."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"A web browser (commonly referred to as a browser) is a software application "
"for retrieving, presenting, and browsing information resources on the World "
"Wide Web."
msgstr ""
"En webbläsare är ett program för att hämta, visa och navigera bland "
"informationsresurser på webben."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"A website mirror is a one-to-one copy of a website that you can find under "
"other web addresses."
msgstr ""
"En webbplatsspegel är en identisk kopia av en webbplats som finns på andra "
"URL:er."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"Add-ons, extensions, and plugins are components that can be added to [web "
"browsers](#web-browser) to give them new features."
msgstr ""
"Tillägg och insticksmoduler är komponenter som kan läggas till i [webbläsare]"
"(#web-browser) för att ge dem nya funktioner."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"Additionally, the private key can be used to create a [signature]"
"(#cryptographic-signature) to prove the identity of the creator of a message "
"or other files."
msgstr ""
"Den privata nyckeln kan dessutom användas för att skapa en [signatur]"
"(#cryptographic-signature) som styrker identiteten hos den som skapade ett "
"meddelande eller andra filer."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"Although similar in meaning to [onion service](#onion-services), but, onion "
"site refers exclusively to websites."
msgstr ""
"Begreppet liknar [onion-tjänst](#onion-services), men onion-webbplats syftar "
"enbart på webbplatser."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"An Internet Protocol address (IP address) is a numerical (or alpha-numeric "
"in the case of IPv6) label assigned to each device (e.g., computer, printer) "
"participating in a computer network that uses the Internet Protocol for "
"communication."
msgstr ""
"En IP-adress är en numerisk etikett (eller alfanumerisk för IPv6) som "
"tilldelas varje enhet, exempelvis dator eller skrivare, i ett datornätverk "
"som använder internetprotokollet för kommunikation."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"An Internet service provider (ISP) is an organization that provides services "
"for accessing and using the Internet."
msgstr ""
"En internetleverantör (ISP) är en organisation som tillhandahåller tjänster "
"för åtkomst till och användning av internet."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"An [HTTP](#http) cookie (also called web cookie, Internet cookie, browser "
"cookie or simply cookie) is a small piece of data sent from a website and "
"stored on the user's computer by the user's [web browser](#web-browser) "
"while the user is browsing."
msgstr ""
"En [HTTP-kaka](#http), även kallad webbkaka, internetkaka, webbläsarkaka "
"eller bara kaka, är en liten datamängd som en webbplats skickar och som "
"användarens [webbläsare](#web-browser) lagrar på datorn medan användaren "
"surfar."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"An antivirus software is used to prevent, detect and remove malicious "
"software."
msgstr ""
"Antivirusprogram används för att förhindra, upptäcka och ta bort skadlig "
"programvara."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"An iOS app which is open source, uses Tor routing, and is developed by "
"someone who works closely with the Tor Project."
msgstr ""
"En iOS-app med öppen källkod som använder Tor-routning och utvecklas av "
"någon som samarbetar nära med The Tor Project."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid "An onion site is a website that is only accessible via Tor."
msgstr "En onion-webbplats är en webbplats som endast är åtkomlig via Tor."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"Antivirus software can interfere with [Tor](#tor-network-core-tor) running "
"on your computer."
msgstr ""
"Antivirusprogram kan störa [Tor](#tor-network-core-tor) när det körs på "
"datorn."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"Any person can [encrypt](#encryption) a message using the public key of the "
"receiver but only the receiver in possession of the private key is able to "
"decrypt the message."
msgstr ""
"Vem som helst kan [kryptera](#encryption) ett meddelande med mottagarens "
"offentliga nyckel, men endast mottagaren som har den privata nyckeln kan "
"dekryptera meddelandet."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"App can also refer to software that you install on mobile [operating systems]"
"(#operating-system-os)."
msgstr ""
"App kan även syfta på programvara som installeras i mobila [operativsystem]"
"(#operating-system-os)."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: content/tor-browser/encountering-issues/troubleshooting/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/encountering-issues/troubleshooting/
msgid ""
"At the bottom of the page, next to the \"View the Tor logs\" text, click the "
"button \"View Logs...\"."
msgstr ""
"Klicka längst ned på sidan på knappen ”Visa loggar…” bredvid texten ”Visa "
"Tor-loggarna”."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"Atlas is a web application to learn about currently running Tor [relays]"
"(#relay)."
msgstr ""
"Atlas är ett webbprogram för att få information om [Tor-reläer](#relay) som "
"körs för närvarande."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/using-bridges/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/using-bridges/
msgid ""
"Bridge-mojis are **human-readable bridge identifiers** and do **not** "
"represent the quality of connection to the Tor network or the state of the "
"bridge."
msgstr ""
"Bro-emojier är **läsbara identifierare för broar** och anger **inte** "
"kvaliteten på anslutningen till Tor-nätverket eller brons status."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"But be careful when translating, because the actual onion addresses finish "
"with .onion, in English."
msgstr ""
"Var försiktig vid översättning, eftersom de faktiska onion-adresserna slutar "
"på det engelska ordet .onion."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"By clicking or tapping on the icon, it reveals a menu with options or "
"additional pages."
msgstr ""
"När du klickar eller trycker på ikonen visas en meny med alternativ eller "
"ytterligare sidor."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"By default, Tor Browser does not keep any [browsing history](#browsing-"
"history)."
msgstr ""
"Som standard sparar Tor Browser ingen [webbläsarhistorik](#browsing-history)."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid "By default, [Tor Browser](#tor-browser) does not store cookies."
msgstr "Som standard lagrar [Tor Browser](#tor-browser) inga kakor."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"Captchas are a challenge-response test used in computing to determine "
"whether the user is human or not."
msgstr ""
"Captcha är ett utmanings- och svarstest som används inom databehandling för "
"att avgöra om användaren är en människa."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid "Checksums are [hash](#hash) values of files."
msgstr "Kontrollsummor är filers [hashvärden](#hash)."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"Compass is a web application to learn about currently running [Tor relays]"
"(#relay) in bulk."
msgstr ""
"Compass är ett webbprogram för att hämta samlad information om [Tor-reläer]"
"(#relay) som körs för närvarande."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) allows an attacker to add malicious functionality "
"or behavior to a website when they shouldn't have the ability to do so."
msgstr ""
"Cross-site scripting (XSS) gör det möjligt för en angripare att lägga till "
"skadlig funktionalitet eller skadligt beteende på en webbplats trots att "
"angriparen inte borde kunna göra det."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"Domain fronting is a censorship circumvention technique which masks the site "
"you are connecting to."
msgstr ""
"Domänfrontning är en metod för att kringgå censur genom att dölja vilken "
"webbplats du ansluter till."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid "Element used for offering dynamic/interactive content via websites."
msgstr ""
"Ett element som används för att erbjuda dynamiskt eller interaktivt innehåll "
"på webbplatser."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"F-Droid is a repository of FOSS (free and open source software) applications "
"for Android."
msgstr ""
"F-Droid är ett programvaruarkiv för fria Android-appar med öppen källkod."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"FTE (format-transforming encryption) was a pluggable transport that "
"disguised [Tor traffic](#traffic) as ordinary web (HTTP) traffic."
msgstr ""
"FTE (formatomvandlande kryptering) var en pluggbar transport som fick [Tor-"
"trafik](#traffic) att se ut som vanlig webbtrafik (HTTP)."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"Fingerprinting is the process of collecting information about a device or "
"service to make educated guesses about its identity or characteristics."
msgstr ""
"Fingeravtryck är en process där information om en enhet eller tjänst samlas "
"in för att göra kvalificerade antaganden om dess identitet eller egenskaper."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"Firefox is available for Windows, macOS and Linux [operating systems]"
"(#operating-system-os), with its mobile version available for Android and "
"iOS."
msgstr ""
"Firefox finns för [operativsystemen](#operating-system-os) Windows, macOS "
"och Linux, och mobilversionen finns för Android och iOS."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"Flash Player is a [browser plugin](#add-on-extension-or-plugin) for Internet "
"[applications](#app) to watch audio and video content."
msgstr ""
"Flash Player är en [insticksmodul för webbläsare](#add-on-extension-or-"
"plugin) som används av internet[program](#app) för ljud- och videoinnehåll."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"For more information please read the MetricsPort section on the article "
"about [overloaded relays](../relays/performance/overloaded/)."
msgstr ""
"Mer information finns i avsnittet om MetricsPort i artikeln om "
"[överbelastade reläer](../relays/performance/overloaded/)."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"For more information see this [blogpost about domain fronting](https://"
"blog.torproject.org/domain-fronting-critical-open-web)."
msgstr ""
"Mer information finns i detta [blogginlägg om domänfrontning](https://"
"blog.torproject.org/domain-fronting-critical-open-web)."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"For more information, see [how you can verify signatures](../tor-browser/"
"getting-started/verifying-tor-browser/)."
msgstr ""
"Mer information finns i [anvisningarna för att verifiera signaturer](../tor-"
"browser/getting-started/verifying-tor-browser/)."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"For someone monitoring the network, it makes the [traffic](#traffic) look "
"like a regular HTTPS connection to a webpage server giving the impression "
"that the user is simply browsing the web."
msgstr ""
"För den som övervakar nätverket ser [trafiken](#traffic) ut som en vanlig "
"HTTPS-anslutning till en webbserver, vilket ger intrycket att användaren "
"bara surfar på webben."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"Former name for \"[onion services](#onion-services)\", sometimes still in "
"use in [Tor](#tor-network-core-tor) documentation or communication."
msgstr ""
"Ett tidigare namn på [onion-tjänster](#onion-services), som fortfarande "
"ibland används i dokumentation eller kommunikation om [Tor](#tor-network-"
"core-tor)."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"From the perspective of a censor, it appears like you are connecting to a "
"major service which would be costly for a censor to block, like Microsoft or "
"Google."
msgstr ""
"Ur en censors perspektiv ser det ut som om du ansluter till en stor tjänst "
"som är kostsam att blockera, exempelvis Microsoft eller Google."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"GetTor is a service that automatically responds to messages (Email, "
"Telegram) with links to the latest version of [Tor Browser](#tor-browser), "
"hosted at a variety of locations, such as Dropbox, Google Drive and GitHub."
msgstr ""
"GetTor är en tjänst som automatiskt svarar på meddelanden via e-post eller "
"Telegram med länkar till den senaste versionen av [Tor Browser](#tor-"
"browser), som finns på flera platser, exempelvis Dropbox, Google Drive och "
"GitHub."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"HTTPS Everywhere is a [Firefox](#firefox), Chrome, and Opera [extension]"
"(#add-on-extension-or-plugin) that makes [HTTPS](#https) the default on "
"websites that have set up HTTPS but have not made it the default."
msgstr ""
"HTTPS Everywhere är ett [tillägg](#add-on-extension-or-plugin) för [Firefox]"
"(#firefox), Chrome och Opera som gör [HTTPS](#https) till standard på "
"webbplatser som har konfigurerat HTTPS men inte gjort det till standard."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid "HTTPS Everywhere is installed in Tor Browser for Android."
msgstr "HTTPS Everywhere är installerat i Tor Browser för Android."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid "Hash values serve to verify the integrity of data."
msgstr "Hashvärden används för att verifiera dataintegritet."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"However, it does not make you anonymous, or completely hide your destination "
"like [Tor Browser](#tor-browser) does."
msgstr ""
"Det gör dig dock inte anonym och döljer inte destinationen fullständigt på "
"samma sätt som [Tor Browser](#tor-browser)."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"Hypertext Transfer Protocol Secure is the [encrypted](#encryption) version "
"of the HTTP channel used to transfer files and data between devices on a "
"network."
msgstr ""
"Hypertext Transfer Protocol Secure är den [krypterade](#encryption) "
"versionen av HTTP-kanalen som används för att överföra filer och data mellan "
"enheter i ett nätverk."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: content/tor-browser/features/onion-services/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/features/onion-services/
msgid ""
"If the website that you are visiting has an onion site available, a purple "
"suggestion pill will prompt at the URL bar in Tor Browser displaying "
"\".onion available\"."
msgstr ""
"Om webbplatsen som du besöker har en onion-version visar Tor Browser en lila "
"förslagsruta med texten ”.onion tillgänglig” i URL-fältet."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"If you don't see this option and you have [Tor Browser](#tor-browser) open, "
"you can navigate to the [hamburger menu (\"≡\")](#hamburger-menu), then "
"click on \"Settings\", and finally on \"Connection\" in the side bar."
msgstr ""
"Om alternativet inte visas när [Tor Browser](#tor-browser) är öppet kan du "
"gå till [hamburgermenyn (”≡”)](#hamburger-menu), klicka på ”Inställningar” "
"och sedan på ”Anslutning” i sidofältet."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"If you have downloaded the software without errors, the given checksum and "
"the checksum of your downloaded file will be identical."
msgstr ""
"Om programvaran har hämtats utan fel är den angivna kontrollsumman identisk "
"med kontrollsumman för den hämtade filen."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid "If you want to control core Tor with python, this is for you."
msgstr "Det här är biblioteket för dig som vill styra kärnan i Tor med Python."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"In Tor terms, a single document compiled and voted on by the [directory "
"authorities](#directory-authority) once per hour, ensuring that all [clients]"
"(#client) have the same information about the [relays](#relay) that make up "
"the [Tor network](#tor-network-core-tor)."
msgstr ""
"I Tor-sammanhang är detta ett enskilt dokument som sammanställs och röstas "
"fram av [katalogauktoriteterna](#directory-authority) en gång i timmen, så "
"att alla [klienter](#client) har samma information om [reläerna](#relay) som "
"utgör [Tor-nätverket](#tor-network-core-tor)."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"In [Tor](#tor-network-core-tor) terms, a \"hop\" refers to [traffic]"
"(#traffic) moving between [relays](#relay) in a [circuit](#circuit)."
msgstr ""
"I [Tor](#tor-network-core-tor) syftar ett ”hopp” på att [trafik](#traffic) "
"rör sig mellan [reläer](#relay) i en [krets](#circuit)."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"In [Tor](#tor-network-core-tor), a client is a node in the Tor network, "
"typically running on behalf of one user, that routes application connections "
"over a series of [relays](#relay)."
msgstr ""
"I [Tor](#tor-network-core-tor) är en klient en nod i Tor-nätverket, normalt "
"körd för en användares räkning, som leder programanslutningar genom en serie "
"[reläer](#relay)."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"In [public key cryptography](#public-key-cryptography), a public key "
"fingerprint is a sequence of bytes that is used to identify and authenticate "
"a corresponding longer [public key](#public-key)."
msgstr ""
"Inom [kryptografi med offentliga nycklar](#public-key-cryptography) är ett "
"fingeravtryck för en offentlig nyckel en följd av byte som används för att "
"identifiera och autentisera en motsvarande längre [offentlig nyckel](#public-"
"key)."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"In addition, Tor Browser is designed to prevent websites from "
"\"[fingerprinting](#browser-fingerprinting)\" or identifying you based on "
"your browser configuration."
msgstr ""
"Tor Browser är dessutom utformad för att hindra webbplatser från att skapa "
"ett [fingeravtryck](#browser-fingerprinting) eller identifiera dig utifrån "
"webbläsarens konfiguration."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"In order to prevent the blocking of proxy IP addresses, Snowflake involves a "
"large number of volunteer proxies, which also makes them hard to pin point."
msgstr ""
"För att förhindra att proxyservrarnas IP-adresser blockeras använder "
"Snowflake ett stort antal frivilliga proxyservrar, vilket också gör dem "
"svåra att kartlägga."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"In the case of Tor, the keys are generally derived from the name of an onion "
"service, and the values are information a client needs to connect to that "
"service."
msgstr ""
"I Tor härrör nycklarna i allmänhet från namnet på en onion-tjänst, och "
"värdena är information som en klient behöver för att ansluta till tjänsten."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"In the second case, Tor Launcher will take you through a series of "
"configuration options."
msgstr ""
"I det andra fallet leder Tor Launcher dig genom en serie "
"konfigurationsalternativ."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"Instead of connecting directly to the service, a client sends the message to "
"the proxy. The proxy makes the request on behalf of the client, and passes "
"the response back to the client."
msgstr ""
"I stället för att ansluta direkt till tjänsten skickar klienten meddelandet "
"till proxyn. Proxyn gör förfrågan åt klienten och skickar tillbaka svaret."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid "It achieves this by adding margins to the browser window."
msgstr "Detta uppnås genom att marginaler läggs till runt webbläsarfönstret."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid "It aims to preserve your privacy and anonymity."
msgstr "Målet är att bevara din integritet och anonymitet."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"It answers the question of whether there was a [Tor](#tor-network-core-tor) "
"relay running on a given IP address on a given date."
msgstr ""
"Tjänsten svarar på frågan om ett [Tor-relä](#tor-network-core-tor) kördes på "
"en viss IP-adress ett visst datum."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"It ensures that DNS requests are handled safely and explicitly rejects any "
"[traffic](#traffic) other than TCP from the application you're using."
msgstr ""
"Den ser till att DNS-förfrågningar hanteras säkert och avvisar uttryckligen "
"all [trafik](#traffic) från programmet utom TCP."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid "It has been replaced by Tor Browser for Android."
msgstr "Programmet har ersatts av Tor Browser för Android."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"It has three components; the Snowflake client, the Snowflake proxy (the two "
"together known as the Snowflake peers) and the broker."
msgstr ""
"Systemet har tre komponenter: Snowflake-klienten, Snowflake-proxyn "
"(tillsammans kallade Snowflake-parterna) och förmedlaren."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"It is a general purpose [proxy](#proxy) that sits at the layer 5 of the OSI "
"model and uses the tunneling method."
msgstr ""
"Det är en allmän [proxy](#proxy) på lager 5 i OSI-modellen som använder "
"tunnelmetoden."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid "It is a type of [pluggable transport](#pluggable-transports)."
msgstr "Det är en typ av [pluggbar transport](#pluggable-transports)."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"It is an [add-on](#add-on-extension-or-plugin) for the Chrome or Chromium "
"browsers that allows you to download several security and privacy programs, "
"including [Tor Browser](#tor-browser), from different sources."
msgstr ""
"Det är ett [tillägg](#add-on-extension-or-plugin) för Chrome eller Chromium "
"som låter dig hämta flera säkerhets- och integritetsprogram, däribland [Tor "
"Browser](#tor-browser), från olika källor."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid "It is not used anymore."
msgstr "Det används inte längre."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"It is used mainly by Tor relay operators to gather metrics and other "
"relevant information in order to diagnose problems and bottlenecks, or to "
"monitor the relay's performance."
msgstr ""
"Det används främst av Tor-reläoperatörer för att samla in mätvärden och "
"annan relevant information för att diagnostisera problem och flaskhalsar "
"eller övervaka reläets prestanda."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"It offers you the option to connect directly to the [Tor network](#tor-"
"network-core-tor), or to configure Tor Browser for your connection."
msgstr ""
"Det ger dig möjlighet att ansluta direkt till [Tor-nätverket](#tor-network-"
"core-tor) eller konfigurera Tor Browser för din anslutning."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"It protects you by bouncing your communications around a distributed network "
"of [relays](#relay) run by volunteers all around the world: it prevents "
"somebody watching your Internet connection from learning what sites you "
"visit, and it prevents the sites you visit from learning your physical "
"location."
msgstr ""
"Det skyddar dig genom att låta kommunikationen studsa genom ett distribuerat "
"nätverk av [reläer](#relay) som drivs av volontärer över hela världen: den "
"som övervakar internetanslutningen kan inte se vilka webbplatser du besöker, "
"och webbplatserna kan inte se var du befinner dig fysiskt."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"It sends the traffic through the Tor network instead of sending it from your "
"IP address into the open network."
msgstr ""
"Det skickar trafiken genom Tor-nätverket i stället för att skicka den från "
"din IP-adress till det öppna nätverket."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"It supported Jabber (XMPP), IRC, Google Talk, Facebook Chat, Twitter, Yahoo, "
"and others; enabled Off-the-Record (OTR) Messaging automatically; and had an "
"easy-to-use graphical user interface localized into multiple languages."
msgstr ""
"Programmet stödde Jabber (XMPP), IRC, Google Talk, Facebook Chat, Twitter, "
"Yahoo och andra tjänster, aktiverade automatiskt Off-the-Record-meddelanden "
"(OTR) och hade ett lättanvänt grafiskt gränssnitt på flera språk."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"It uses [domain fronting](#domain-fronting) to help you circumvent "
"censorship."
msgstr ""
"Det använder [domänfrontning](#domain-fronting) för att hjälpa dig kringgå "
"censur."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"It was installed over 14 million times, and maintained over 1 million active "
"users."
msgstr ""
"Det installerades mer än 14 miljoner gånger och hade över en miljon aktiva "
"användare."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"It's a icon with three horizontal lines usually on the top-left corner or "
"top-right corner of the screen."
msgstr ""
"Det är en ikon med tre vågräta linjer, vanligtvis i skärmens övre vänstra "
"eller högra hörn."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"It's designed as one-way-function which means the value is easy to calculate "
"in one direction but infeasible to invert."
msgstr ""
"Funktionen är utformad som en envägsfunktion: värdet är lätt att beräkna i "
"ena riktningen men i praktiken omöjligt att invertera."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"JavaScript is a programming language that websites use to offer interactive "
"elements such as video, animation, audio, and status timelines."
msgstr ""
"JavaScript är ett programmeringsspråk som webbplatser använder för "
"interaktiva element såsom video, animeringar, ljud och statusflöden."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"Just like in Google Play one can browse, install and keep track of updates "
"on the device using F-Droid."
msgstr ""
"Precis som i Google Play kan du bläddra bland och installera appar samt "
"hålla reda på uppdateringar på enheten med F-Droid."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"Letterboxing is a Tor Browser feature that conceals a user's real window "
"size from websites."
msgstr ""
"Letterboxing är en Tor Browser-funktion som döljer användarens verkliga "
"fönsterstorlek för webbplatser."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"Like ordinary Tor [relays](#relay), bridges are run by volunteers; unlike "
"ordinary relays, however, they are not listed publicly, so an adversary "
"cannot identify them easily."
msgstr ""
"Precis som vanliga Tor-[reläer](#relay) drivs broar av volontärer. Till "
"skillnad från vanliga reläer är de dock inte offentligt listade, så en "
"angripare kan inte enkelt identifiera dem."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"Major web browsers include [Firefox](#firefox), Chrome, Internet Explorer, "
"and Safari."
msgstr ""
"Bland de vanligaste webbläsarna finns [Firefox](#firefox), Chrome, Internet "
"Explorer och Safari."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"Many services that use Flash also offer an HTML5 alternative, which should "
"work in Tor Browser."
msgstr ""
"Många tjänster som använder Flash erbjuder även ett HTML5-alternativ, vilket "
"bör fungera i Tor Browser."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid "Meek connects you to the Tor network through a big cloud provider."
msgstr "Meek ansluter dig till Tor-nätverket genom en stor molnleverantör."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid "MetricsPort provides an interface to the underlying Tor relay metrics."
msgstr ""
"MetricsPort tillhandahåller ett gränssnitt till Tor-reläets underliggande "
"mätvärden."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"Moat also employs a [Captcha](#captcha) to prevent a censor from quickly "
"blocking all of the bridges."
msgstr ""
"Moat använder också en [captcha](#captcha) för att hindra en censor från att "
"snabbt blockera alla broar."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"Moat is an interactive tool you can use to get [bridges](#bridge) from "
"within [Tor Browser](#tor-browser)."
msgstr ""
"Moat är ett interaktivt verktyg som du kan använda för att hämta [broar]"
"(#bridge) inifrån [Tor Browser](#tor-browser)."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"Most [onion services](#onion-services) use six hops in a circuit (with the "
"exception of [single onion services](#single-onion-service)), and never an "
"exit node."
msgstr ""
"De flesta [onion-tjänster](#onion-services) använder sex hopp i en krets "
"(med undantag för [enkla onion-tjänster](#single-onion-service)) och aldrig "
"en utgångsnod."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"Most circuits consist of three nodes - a guard or bridge, a [middle relay]"
"(#middle-relay), and an [exit](#exit)."
msgstr ""
"De flesta kretsar består av tre noder: en vakt eller bro, ett [mellanrelä]"
"(#middle-relay) och en [utgång](#exit)."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"Most websites use numerous third-party services, including advertising and "
"analytics trackers, which collect data about your [IP address](#ip-address), "
"[web browser](#web-browser), [system](#operating-system-os) and your "
"browsing behavior itself, all of which can link your activity across "
"different sites."
msgstr ""
"De flesta webbplatser använder många tredjepartstjänster, däribland reklam- "
"och analysspårare som samlar in uppgifter om din [IP-adress](#ip-address), "
"[webbläsare](#web-browser), ditt [system](#operating-system-os) och själva "
"surfbeteendet. Dessa uppgifter kan koppla samman dina aktiviteter på olika "
"webbplatser."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"Mozilla Firefox is a free and open-source [web browser](#web-browser) "
"developed by the Mozilla Foundation and its subsidiary, the Mozilla "
"Corporation."
msgstr ""
"Mozilla Firefox är en fri [webbläsare](#web-browser) med öppen källkod som "
"utvecklas av Mozilla Foundation och dess dotterbolag Mozilla Corporation."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"NOTE: This is not as safe as connecting to the [onion services](#onion-"
"services) via Tor Browser, and will remove all [Tor](#tor-network-core-tor)-"
"related protections the [client](#client) would otherwise have."
msgstr ""
"OBS! Detta är inte lika säkert som att ansluta till [onion-tjänster](#onion-"
"services) via Tor Browser och tar bort alla [Tor](#tor-network-core-tor)-"
"relaterade skydd som [klienten](#client) annars skulle ha."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"New Identity can also help if Tor Browser is having trouble connecting to a "
"particular site, similarly to \"[New Tor Circuit for this Site](#new-tor-"
"circuit-for-this-site)\"."
msgstr ""
"Ny identitet kan också hjälpa när Tor Browser har problem att ansluta till "
"en viss webbplats, ungefär som [Ny Tor-krets för den här webbplatsen](#new-"
"tor-circuit-for-this-site)."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"New Identity is a [Tor Browser](#tor-browser) feature if you want to prevent "
"your subsequent browser activity from being linkable to what you were doing "
"before."
msgstr ""
"Ny identitet är en funktion i [Tor Browser](#tor-browser) som du kan använda "
"för att hindra senare webbläsaraktivitet från att kopplas till det du gjorde "
"tidigare."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"NoScript allows you to control the [JavaScript](#javascript) that runs on "
"individual web pages, or to block it entirely."
msgstr ""
"Med NoScript kan du styra vilket [JavaScript](#javascript) som körs på "
"enskilda webbsidor eller blockera det helt."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"OONI stands for \"[Open Observatory of Network Interference](https://"
"ooni.org/)\", it is a global observation network for detecting [censorship]"
"(#network-censorship), surveillance and [traffic](#traffic) manipulation on "
"the internet."
msgstr ""
"OONI står för [Open Observatory of Network Interference](https://ooni.org/) "
"och är ett globalt observationsnätverk som upptäcker [censur](#network-"
"censorship), övervakning och manipulering av [trafik](#traffic) på internet."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"Obfs3 is a [pluggable transport](#pluggable-transports) that makes [Tor]"
"(#tor-network-core-tor) [traffic](#traffic) look random, so that it does not "
"look like Tor or any other protocol."
msgstr ""
"Obfs3 är en [pluggbar transport](#pluggable-transports) som får [Tor](#tor-"
"network-core-tor)-[trafik](#traffic) att se slumpmässig ut, så att den "
"varken ser ut som Tor eller något annat protokoll."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid "Obfs3 is not supported anymore."
msgstr "Obfs3 stöds inte längre."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"Obfs4 bridges are less likely to be blocked than obfs3 [bridges](#bridge)."
msgstr "Obfs4-broar löper mindre risk att blockeras än obfs3-[broar](#bridge)."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"Obfs4 is a [pluggable transport](#pluggable-transports) that makes [Tor]"
"(#tor-network-core-tor) [traffic](#traffic) look random like obfs3, and also "
"prevents censors from finding bridges by Internet scanning."
msgstr ""
"Obfs4 är en [pluggbar transport](#pluggable-transports) som får [Tor](#tor-"
"network-core-tor)-[trafik](#traffic) att se slumpmässig ut, ungefär som "
"obfs3, och dessutom hindrar censuraktörer från att hitta broar genom "
"internetskanning."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"On Tor Browser for Desktop, you can view your current Tor circuit by "
"clicking on the [Tor circuit icon](../tor-browser/features/managing-"
"identities) in the URL bar."
msgstr ""
"I Tor Browser för dator kan du se den aktuella Tor-kretsen genom att klicka "
"på [Tor-kretsikonen](../tor-browser/features/managing-identities) i "
"adressfältet."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"Onion services (formerly known as \"[hidden services](#hidden-services)\") "
"are services (like websites) that are only accessible through the [Tor "
"network](#tor-network-core-tor)."
msgstr ""
"Onion-tjänster (tidigare kallade [dolda tjänster](#hidden-services)) är "
"tjänster, exempelvis webbplatser, som endast kan nås genom [Tor-nätverket]"
"(#tor-network-core-tor)."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: content/tor-browser/features/onion-services/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/features/onion-services/
msgid ""
"Onion-Location is a non-standard HTTP header that websites can use to "
"advertise their onion counterpart."
msgstr ""
"Onion-Location är ett icke-standardiserat HTTP-huvud som webbplatser kan "
"använda för att informera om sin onion-motsvarighet."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"Onionoo provides the data for other applications and websites "
"([metrics.torproject.org](https://metrics.torproject.org/)) which in turn "
"present Tor network status information to humans."
msgstr ""
"Onionoo tillhandahåller data till andra program och webbplatser, exempelvis "
"[metrics.torproject.org](https://metrics.torproject.org/), som i sin tur "
"visar information om Tor-nätverkets status för människor."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"Orbot uses [Tor](#tor-network-core-tor) to [encrypt](#encryption) your "
"Internet [traffic](#traffic) and hide it by bouncing through a series of "
"computers around the world."
msgstr ""
"Orbot använder [Tor](#tor-network-core-tor) för att [kryptera](#encryption) "
"din internet[trafik](#traffic) och döljer den genom att låta den studsa "
"genom en serie datorer runt om i världen."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"Ordinary internet domain names require site owners to trust and be approved "
"by a Certificate Authority (CA) for this binding, and they are subject to "
"hijack by the CA and typically by many other parties as well."
msgstr ""
"Vanliga internetdomännamn kräver att webbplatsägaren litar på och godkänns "
"av en certifikatutfärdare (CA) för denna koppling, och de kan kapas av "
"certifikatutfärdaren och vanligtvis även av många andra parter."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"Orfox was first released 23 September 2015 by [The Guardian Project](https://"
"guardianproject.info/apps/info.guardianproject.orfox/)."
msgstr ""
"Orfox gavs först ut den 23 september 2015 av [The Guardian Project](https://"
"guardianproject.info/apps/info.guardianproject.orfox/)."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"Originally used to transfer only web pages, it is now relied upon to deliver "
"many forms of data and communication."
msgstr ""
"Protokollet användes ursprungligen endast för att överföra webbsidor men "
"används nu för många slags data och kommunikation."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"Other open tabs and windows from the same website will use the new circuit "
"as well once they are reloaded."
msgstr ""
"Andra öppna flikar och fönster från samma webbplats använder också den nya "
"kretsen när de läses in på nytt."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"Over the next three years, Orfox continuously improved and became a popular "
"way for people to browse the internet with more privacy than standard "
"browsers, and Orfox was crucial for helping people circumvent censorship and "
"access blocked sites and critical resources."
msgstr ""
"Under de kommande tre åren förbättrades Orfox kontinuerligt och blev ett "
"populärt sätt för människor att surfa på internet med mer integritet än "
"vanliga webbläsare, och Orfox var avgörande för att hjälpa människor att "
"kringgå censur och få åtkomst till blockerade webbplatser och viktiga "
"resurser."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"People often use `tpo` to abbreviate `torproject.org` when writing "
"hostnames. For example, `blog.tpo` is an abbreviation for "
"`blog.torproject.org`."
msgstr ""
"När värdnamn skrivs förkortas `torproject.org` ofta till `tpo`. `blog.tpo` "
"är exempelvis en förkortning av `blog.torproject.org`."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"Reference: [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hamburger_button](https://"
"en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hamburger_button)"
msgstr ""
"Referens: [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hamburger_button](https://"
"en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hamburger_button)"

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid "SOCKS5 is an Internet protocol used by Tor."
msgstr "SOCKS5 är ett internetprotokoll som används av Tor."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"SSL encrypts data that is being transferred, preventing third parties from "
"accessing the data as it is being sent."
msgstr ""
"SSL krypterar data under överföringen och hindrar tredje parter från att "
"komma åt dem medan de skickas."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"ScrambleSuit is similar to the obfs4 [pluggable transport](#pluggable-"
"transports) but has a different set of [bridges](#bridge)."
msgstr ""
"ScrambleSuit liknar den [pluggbara transporten](#pluggable-transports) obfs4 "
"men använder en annan uppsättning [broar](#bridge)."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"Secure sockets layer (SSL) is a standard Internet security protocol that is "
"used to secure an internet connection and protect sensitive data being "
"transmitted between two systems."
msgstr ""
"Secure Sockets Layer (SSL) är ett standardprotokoll för internetsäkerhet som "
"skyddar en internetanslutning och känsliga data som överförs mellan två "
"system."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"Selecting it will cause the currently active tab or window to be reloaded "
"over a new [Tor circuit](#circuit)."
msgstr ""
"När alternativet väljs läses den aktiva fliken eller det aktiva fönstret in "
"på nytt över en ny [Tor-krets](#circuit)."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"Selecting it will close all your open tabs and windows, clear all private "
"information such as [cookies](#cookie) and [browsing history](#browsing-"
"history), and use New [Tor circuits](#circuit) for all connections."
msgstr ""
"När alternativet väljs stängs alla öppna flikar och fönster, all privat "
"information såsom [kakor](#cookie) och [webbläsarhistorik](#browsing-"
"history) rensas och nya [Tor-kretsar](#circuit) används för alla "
"anslutningar."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"Since Tor Browser 11.5, HTTPS-Only Mode is enabled by default for desktop, "
"and HTTPS Everywhere is no longer bundled with Tor Browser."
msgstr ""
"Sedan Tor Browser 11.5 är HTTPS Only-läget aktiverat som standard på "
"datorer, och HTTPS Everywhere ingår inte längre i Tor Browser."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"Single onion services use only three hops in the [circuit](#circuit) rather "
"than the typical six hops for onion services."
msgstr ""
"Enkla onion-tjänster använder endast tre hopp i [kretsen](#circuit), i "
"stället för de sex hopp som onion-tjänster normalt använder."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"Snowflake can allow an open browser tab to act as an ephemeral Tor bridge."
msgstr ""
"Snowflake kan låta en öppen webbläsarflik fungera som en tillfällig Tor-bro."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"Some languages such as Arabic *transliterate* the word Tor, تور. That is, "
"they write Tor with other characters."
msgstr ""
"Vissa språk, exempelvis arabiska, *translittererar* ordet Tor som تور. Det "
"innebär att Tor skrivs med andra tecken."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"Sometimes people have trouble connecting to [Tor](#tor-network-core-tor) "
"because their firewall blocks Tor connections."
msgstr ""
"Ibland har människor svårt att ansluta till [Tor](#tor-network-core-tor) "
"eftersom deras brandvägg blockerar Tor-anslutningar."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"Sometimes the direct access to the [Tor network](#tor-network-core-tor) is "
"blocked by your [Internet Service Provider (ISP)](#internet-service-provider-"
"isp) or by a government."
msgstr ""
"Ibland blockeras direktåtkomst till [Tor-nätverket](#tor-network-core-tor) "
"av din [internetleverantör (ISP)](#internet-service-provider-isp) eller en "
"regering."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid "Spelling notes:  All in caps, as it is an acronym."
msgstr ""
"Stavningsanmärkning: Skrivs helt med versaler eftersom det är en akronym."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid "Spelling notes: No need to capitalize."
msgstr "Stavningsanmärkning: Behöver inte inledas med versal."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid "Spelling notes: Note that this is not `hashing`."
msgstr "Stavningsanmärkning: Observera att detta inte är `hashing`."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"Spelling notes: Only capitalize first letter, as Captcha is now considered a "
"noun."
msgstr ""
"Stavningsanmärkning: Skriv endast den första bokstaven med versal, eftersom "
"Captcha numera betraktas som ett substantiv."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid "Spelling notes: The second `T` is capitalized when possible: GetTor."
msgstr ""
"Stavningsanmärkning: Det andra `T`:et skrivs med versal när det är möjligt: "
"GetTor."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"Spelling notes: Tor Browser. Sometimes also mentioned as \"tbb\". Not 'TOR "
"Browser'."
msgstr ""
"Stavningsanmärkning: Tor Browser. Nämns ibland även som ”tbb”. Inte ”TOR "
"Browser”."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"Stem is a Python (programming language) controller library for core [Tor]"
"(#tor-network-core-tor)."
msgstr ""
"Stem är ett styrbibliotek i Python för kärnan i [Tor](#tor-network-core-tor)."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid "TPI is an acronym for The Tor Project, Inc."
msgstr "TPI är en akronym för The Tor Project, Inc."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"Tails is a \"live\" [operating system](#operating-system-os), that you can "
"start on almost any computer from a DVD, USB stick, or SD card."
msgstr ""
"Tails är ett ”live”-baserat [operativsystem](#operating-system-os) som kan "
"startas på nästan vilken dator som helst från en DVD, ett USB-minne eller "
"ett SD-kort."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"The ExoneraTor service maintains a database of [relay](#relay) [IP addresses]"
"(#ip-address) that have been part of the Tor network."
msgstr ""
"Tjänsten ExoneraTor underhåller en databas med [IP-adresser](#ip-address) "
"till [reläer](#relay) som har ingått i Tor-nätverket."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"The IP address is the location address of the device, similar to the "
"addresses of physical locations."
msgstr ""
"IP-adressen är enhetens platsadress, ungefär som adresser till fysiska "
"platser."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"The Sybil attack in computer security is an attack wherein a reputation "
"system is subverted by creating a large number of identities, and using them "
"to gain a disproportionately large influence in the network."
msgstr ""
"En Sybil-attack inom datasäkerhet innebär att ett anseendesystem undergrävs "
"genom att ett stort antal identiteter skapas och används för att få ett "
"oproportionerligt stort inflytande i nätverket."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"The Tor Project can refer to either The Tor Project Inc, a 501(c)3 US "
"nonprofit responsible for maintaining the Tor software, or the Tor Project "
"community made up of thousands of volunteers from all over the world who "
"help create Tor."
msgstr ""
"The Tor Project kan syfta på antingen The Tor Project, Inc., en amerikansk "
"ideell organisation enligt 501(c)(3) som ansvarar för underhållet av Tor-"
"programvaran, eller Tor-gemenskapen med tusentals volontärer från hela "
"världen som hjälper till att skapa Tor."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"The Tor Project participates in the Google Season of Docs, which is a "
"program for technical writers."
msgstr ""
"The Tor Project deltar i Google Season of Docs, ett program för tekniska "
"skribenter."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"The Tor Project participates in the Google Summer of Code, which is a summer "
"program for university students."
msgstr ""
"The Tor Project deltar i Google Summer of Code, ett sommarprogram för "
"universitetsstudenter."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"The [Hypertext Transfer Protocol (HTTP)](#http) is a channel used to send "
"files and data between devices on a network."
msgstr ""
"[Hypertext Transfer Protocol (HTTP)](#http) är en kanal som används för att "
"skicka filer och data mellan enheter i ett nätverk."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"The [NoScript](#noscript) [extension](#add-on-extension-or-plugin) in [Tor "
"Browser](#tor-browser) can be used to manage JavaScript on different "
"websites."
msgstr ""
"[NoScript](#noscript)-[tillägget](#add-on-extension-or-plugin) i [Tor "
"Browser](#tor-browser) kan användas för att hantera JavaScript på olika "
"webbplatser."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"The [public key](#public-key) can be disseminated widely while its "
"corresponding [private key](#private-key) is known only by the owner of the "
"key pair."
msgstr ""
"Den [offentliga nyckeln](#public-key) kan spridas brett, medan motsvarande "
"[privata nyckel](#private-key) endast är känd av nyckelparets ägare."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"The anonymizing [relay](#relay) monitor (formerly arm, now nyx) is a "
"terminal status monitor for [Tor](#tor-network-core-tor), intended for "
"command-line usage. This is a tool for monitoring the core Tor process on a "
"system, often useful for relay operators."
msgstr ""
"[Anonymizing Relay Monitor](#relay) (tidigare arm, nu nyx) är en "
"terminalbaserad statusövervakare för [Tor](#tor-network-core-tor), avsedd "
"för kommandoraden. Verktyget övervakar kärnprocessen Tor på ett system och "
"är ofta användbart för reläoperatörer."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"The applications that you run with SOCKS5 will be aware of the tunneling, "
"but you can prevent identity correlation if set up correctly."
msgstr ""
"Program som körs med SOCKS5 känner till tunneln, men korrekt konfigurering "
"kan förhindra att identiteter korreleras."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"The circuit begins with either a [bridge](#bridge) or a [guard](#guard)."
msgstr "Kretsen börjar med antingen en [bro](#bridge) eller en [vakt](#guard)."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid "The core [Tor](#tor-network-core-tor) configuration file."
msgstr "Den centrala konfigurationsfilen för [Tor](#tor-network-core-tor)."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"The feature helps prevent [fingerprinting](#browser-fingerprinting) users "
"based on their window or screen size."
msgstr ""
"Funktionen motverkar att användare identifieras med [fingeravtryck](#browser-"
"fingerprinting) utifrån fönster- eller skärmstorleken."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"The first [relay](#relay) in the [Tor circuit](#circuit), unless using a "
"[bridge](#bridge). When using a bridge, the bridge takes the place of the "
"guard."
msgstr ""
"Det första [reläet](#relay) i [Tor-kretsen](#circuit), om ingen [bro]"
"(#bridge) används. När en bro används ersätter den vakten."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"The format automatically guarantees that the onion address is bound to the "
"key used to protect connections to the [onion site](#onion-site)."
msgstr ""
"Formatet garanterar automatiskt att onion-adressen är kopplad till nyckeln "
"som skyddar anslutningarna till [onion-webbplatsen](#onion-site)."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"The last [relay](#relay) in the [Tor circuit](#circuit) which sends [traffic]"
"(#traffic) out onto the public Internet."
msgstr ""
"Det sista [reläet](#relay) i [Tor-kretsen](#circuit), som skickar [trafiken]"
"(#traffic) ut på det offentliga internet."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"The main system software that manages computer hardware and software "
"resources and provides common services for computer programs."
msgstr ""
"Den centrala systemprogramvaran som hanterar datorns maskinvaru- och "
"programvaruresurser och tillhandahåller gemensamma tjänster åt datorprogram."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"The middle position in the [Tor circuit](#circuit). Non-exit relays can "
"function as either a \"middle\" or a \"[guard](#guard)\" for different users."
msgstr ""
"Den mellersta positionen i [Tor-kretsen](#circuit). Reläer som inte är "
"utgångar kan fungera som antingen ”mellanrelä” eller [vakt](#guard) för "
"olika användare."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"The most used desktop operating systems are Windows, macOS and Linux. "
"Android and iOS are the dominant mobile operating systems."
msgstr ""
"De mest använda operativsystemen för datorer är Windows, macOS och Linux. "
"Android och iOS dominerar på mobila enheter."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"The operators of the websites and services that you use, and anyone watching "
"them, will see a connection coming from the Tor network instead of your real "
"[(IP) address](#ip-address), and will not know who you are unless you "
"explicitly identify yourself."
msgstr ""
"Operatörerna för webbplatserna och tjänsterna du använder, samt den som "
"övervakar dem, ser en anslutning från Tor-nätverket i stället för din "
"verkliga [(IP-)adress](#ip-address) och vet inte vem du är om du inte "
"uttryckligen identifierar dig."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"The private portion of a [public/private key pair](#public-key-cryptography)."
msgstr ""
"Den privata delen av ett [offentligt/privat nyckelpar](#public-key-"
"cryptography)."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"The process of taking a piece of data and scrambling it into a secret code "
"that can only be read by the intended recipient."
msgstr ""
"Processen att ta data och omvandla dem till en hemlig kod som endast den "
"avsedda mottagaren kan läsa."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"The public portion of a [public/private key pair](#public-key-cryptography)."
msgstr ""
"Den offentliga delen av ett [offentligt/privat nyckelpar](#public-key-"
"cryptography)."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid "The service only communicates with and sees the proxy."
msgstr "Tjänsten kommunicerar endast med och ser proxyn."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"The service you are connecting to (website, chat service, email provider, "
"etc.) will see the [IP address](#ip-address) of the exit."
msgstr ""
"Tjänsten som du ansluter till, exempelvis en webbplats, chattjänst eller e-"
"postleverantör, ser utgångens [IP-adress](#ip-address)."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"The set of available [onion services](#onion-services). For example, you can "
"say \"my site is in onionspace\" instead of \"my site is in the Dark Web.\""
msgstr ""
"Mängden tillgängliga [onion-tjänster](#onion-services). Du kan till exempel "
"säga ”min webbplats finns i onion-rymden” i stället för ”min webbplats finns "
"på darknet”."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"The specialized address format of [onion addresses](#onion-address) is self-"
"authenticating."
msgstr ""
"Det särskilda adressformatet för [onion-adresser](#onion-address) är "
"självautentiserande."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/using-bridges/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/using-bridges/
msgid ""
"The string of emoji characters **cannot be used as input**. Users are "
"required to provide the complete bridge address to be able to connect with a "
"bridge."
msgstr ""
"Emoji-strängen **kan inte användas som indata**. Du måste ange hela bro-"
"adressen för att kunna ansluta till bron."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"The way most people use Tor is with [Tor Browser](#tor-browser) which is a "
"version of [Firefox](#firefox) that fixes many privacy issues."
msgstr ""
"De flesta använder Tor med [Tor Browser](#tor-browser), en version av "
"[Firefox](#firefox) som åtgärdar många integritetsproblem."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid "These websites use the .onion Top Level Domain (TLD)."
msgstr "Dessa webbplatser använder toppdomänen .onion."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"This [extension](#add-on-extension-or-plugin) configures Thunderbird to make "
"connections over [Tor](#tor-network-core-tor)."
msgstr ""
"Det här [tillägget](#add-on-extension-or-plugin) konfigurerar Thunderbird "
"för att ansluta genom [Tor](#tor-network-core-tor)."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"This can be useful in situations where an [Internet Service Provider (ISP)]"
"(#internet-service-provider-isp) or other authority is actively blocking "
"connections to the [Tor network](#tor-network-core-tor)."
msgstr ""
"Det kan vara användbart när en [internetleverantör (ISP)](#internet-service-"
"provider-isp) eller annan myndighet aktivt blockerar anslutningar till [Tor-"
"nätverket](#tor-network-core-tor)."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"This helps ensure the data or message being sent is only read by the sending "
"and receiving party."
msgstr ""
"Det bidrar till att endast den sändande och mottagande parten kan läsa data "
"eller meddelandet."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"This is done by converting the pdf to raw pixel data and then back to pdf."
msgstr ""
"Det görs genom att omvandla PDF-filen till råa bildpunktsdata och sedan "
"tillbaka till PDF."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid "This is the key that can be disseminated to others."
msgstr "Detta är nyckeln som får spridas till andra."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"This is the key that must be kept private, and not disseminated to others."
msgstr "Detta är nyckeln som måste hållas privat och inte spridas till andra."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"This option does not clear any private information or unlink your activity, "
"nor does it affect your current connections to other websites."
msgstr ""
"Alternativet rensar ingen privat information, bryter inte kopplingen till "
"din aktivitet och påverkar inte dina aktuella anslutningar till andra "
"webbplatser."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"This option is useful if the [exit](#exit) you are using is unable to "
"connect to the website you require, or is not loading it properly."
msgstr ""
"Alternativet är användbart om [utgången](#exit) du använder inte kan ansluta "
"till den webbplats du behöver eller inte läser in den korrekt."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid "This service is often useful when dealing with law enforcement."
msgstr ""
"Tjänsten är ofta användbar vid kontakter med brottsbekämpande myndigheter."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"This set of volunteer relays is called the Tor network. Sometimes the "
"software associated with this network is called Core Tor, and sometimes "
"[\"little-t tor\"](#little-t-tor)."
msgstr ""
"Denna uppsättning reläer som drivs av volontärer kallas Tor-nätverket. "
"Programvaran som hör till nätverket kallas ibland Core Tor och ibland "
"[”little-t tor”](#little-t-tor)."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid "This signature can be verified by the public key."
msgstr "Signaturen kan verifieras med den offentliga nyckeln."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"This traffic filter is based on predetermined rules. A firewall typically "
"establishes a barrier between a trusted, secure internal network and another "
"outside network but it can also be used as a content filter in the sense of "
"[censorship](#network-censorship)."
msgstr ""
"Trafikfiltret bygger på förutbestämda regler. En brandvägg skapar vanligtvis "
"en barriär mellan ett betrott, säkert internt nätverk och ett annat externt "
"nätverk, men kan även användas som innehållsfilter i betydelsen [censur]"
"(#network-censorship)."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"To determine a relay's throughput, special relays called bandwidth "
"authorities take periodic measurements of the [relays](#relay) in the "
"[consensus](#consensus)."
msgstr ""
"För att fastställa ett reläs kapacitet gör särskilda reläer, så kallade "
"bandbreddsauktoriteter, regelbundna mätningar av [reläerna](#relay) i "
"[konsensusdokumentet](#consensus)."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"To learn more about this type of relays, please read [What are Entry Guards?]"
"(../about-tor/how-tor-works/entry-guards/)."
msgstr ""
"Läs [Vad är ingångsvakter?](../about-tor/how-tor-works/entry-guards/) om du "
"vill veta mer om denna typ av relä."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"Tools that [Tor](#tor-network-core-tor) can use to disguise the [traffic]"
"(#traffic) it sends out."
msgstr ""
"Verktyg som [Tor](#tor-network-core-tor) kan använda för att dölja den "
"[trafik](#traffic) som skickas."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid "Tor Browser comes with one add-on installed: [NoScript](#noscript)."
msgstr ""
"Tor Browser levereras med ett installerat tillägg: [NoScript](#noscript)."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"Tor Browser includes some circumvention tools for getting around these "
"blocks, including [bridges](#bridge), [pluggable transports](#pluggable-"
"transports), and [GetTor](#gettor)."
msgstr ""
"Tor Browser innehåller verktyg för att kringgå sådana blockeringar, bland "
"annat [broar](#bridge), [pluggbara transporter](#pluggable-transports) och "
"[GetTor](#gettor)."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"Tor Browser is available on F-Droid. Follow these [steps](../tor-browser/"
"getting-started/installing/#android) if you prefer installing the app "
"through F-Droid."
msgstr ""
"Tor Browser finns i F-Droid. Följ dessa [steg](../tor-browser/getting-"
"started/installing/#android) om du föredrar att installera appen via F-Droid."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"Tor Browser uses the [Tor network](#tor-network-core-tor) to protect your "
"privacy and anonymity."
msgstr ""
"Tor Browser använder [Tor-nätverket](#tor-network-core-tor) för att skydda "
"din integritet och anonymitet."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"Tor Browser will warn you that all activity and downloads will be stopped, "
"so take this into account before clicking \"New Identity\" (accessible "
"through the small sparkly broom icon at the top-right of the screen)."
msgstr ""
"Tor Browser varnar dig om att all aktivitet och alla hämtningar stoppas. "
"Tänk på detta innan du klickar på ”Ny identitet”, som nås via den lilla "
"glittrande kvastikonen längst upp till höger på skärmen."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid "Tor Messenger is not in development anymore."
msgstr "Tor Messenger utvecklas inte längre."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"Tor Messenger was a cross-platform chat program that aimed to be secure by "
"default and send all of its [traffic](#traffic) over [Tor](#tor-network-core-"
"tor)."
msgstr ""
"Tor Messenger var ett plattformsoberoende chattprogram som hade målet att "
"vara säkert som standard och skicka all [trafik](#traffic) genom [Tor](#tor-"
"network-core-tor)."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"Tor launcher is no longer used in Tor Browser since the [10.5 release]"
"(https://blog.torproject.org/new-release-tor-browser-105)."
msgstr ""
"Tor Launcher används inte längre i Tor Browser sedan [version 10.5](https://"
"blog.torproject.org/new-release-tor-browser-105)."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"Tor2web is a project to let users access [onion services](#onion-services) "
"without using the [Tor Browser](#tor-browser)."
msgstr ""
"Tor2web är ett projekt som låter användare komma åt [onion-tjänster](#onion-"
"services) utan att använda [Tor Browser](#tor-browser)."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"Torsocks allows you to use many applications in a safer way with [Tor](#tor-"
"network-core-tor)."
msgstr ""
"Med Torsocks kan du använda många program på ett säkrare sätt med [Tor](#tor-"
"network-core-tor)."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"Traffic is the data sent and received by [clients](#client) and [servers]"
"(#server)."
msgstr ""
"Trafik är de data som skickas och tas emot av [klienter](#client) och "
"[servrar](#server)."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"Translation notes:  **Do not translate \"Tor\", however you can translate "
"\"Browser\"**. Example in Spanish: Navegador Tor (altering the order because "
"is more natural like that in Spanish.)"
msgstr ""
"Översättningsanmärkning: **Översätt inte ”Tor”, men ”Browser” kan "
"översättas**. Exempel på spanska: Navegador Tor (med omvänd ordning eftersom "
"det är naturligare på spanska)."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid "Translation notes:  Do not translate."
msgstr "Översättningsanmärkning: Översätt inte."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"Translation notes: Can be partially or totally translated, i.e. for Spanish "
"'dirección cebolla' or 'dirección onion'."
msgstr ""
"Översättningsanmärkning: Kan översättas helt eller delvis, exempelvis "
"spanska ”dirección cebolla” eller ”dirección onion”."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid "Translation notes: Do not translate or transliterate."
msgstr "Översättningsanmärkning: Översätt eller translitterera inte."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid "Translation notes: Do not translate this application name."
msgstr "Översättningsanmärkning: Översätt inte programnamnet."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid "Translation notes: Do not translate."
msgstr "Översättningsanmärkning: Översätt inte."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"Translation notes: Project name. Do not translate \"Onion\", however you can "
"translate \"Browser\". Ex: Navegador Onion."
msgstr ""
"Översättningsanmärkning: Projektnamn. Översätt inte ”Onion”, men ”Browser” "
"kan översättas. Exempel: Navegador Onion."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"Translation notes: See how it appears on your language's Tor Browser. Keep "
"in English if there is no version of Tor Browser in your [language](../tor-"
"browser/getting-started/languages/)."
msgstr ""
"Översättningsanmärkning: Kontrollera hur termen visas i Tor Browser på ditt "
"språk. Behåll engelskan om Tor Browser inte finns på ditt [språk](../tor-"
"browser/getting-started/languages/)."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"Translation notes: You can translate this term if it sounds better on your "
"language."
msgstr ""
"Översättningsanmärkning: Termen kan översättas om det låter bättre på ditt "
"språk."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"Transmitted data which is [encrypted](#encryption) directly from origin to "
"destination is called end-to-end encryption."
msgstr ""
"Data som [krypteras](#encryption) direkt från källa till destination kallas "
"totalsträckskrypterade."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"Unfortunately, JavaScript can also enable attacks on the security of the "
"[web browser](#web-browser), which might lead to deanonymization."
msgstr ""
"JavaScript kan tyvärr även möjliggöra attacker mot [webbläsarens](#web-"
"browser) säkerhet som kan leda till avanonymisering."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"Unique behavior or responses can be used to identify the device or service "
"analyzed."
msgstr ""
"Unika beteenden eller svar kan användas för att identifiera den analyserade "
"enheten eller tjänsten."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"Using [Tor Browser](#tor-browser) means that your session data will be wiped "
"when you close the [web browser](#web-browser)."
msgstr ""
"När du använder [Tor Browser](#tor-browser) rensas sessionsdata när du "
"stänger [webbläsaren](#web-browser)."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"WebTunnel is a censorship-resistant [pluggable transport](#pluggable-"
"transports) designed to mimic encrypted web traffic (HTTPS)."
msgstr ""
"WebTunnel är en censurresistent [pluggbar transport](#pluggable-transports) "
"som är utformad för att efterlikna krypterad webbtrafik (HTTPS)."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"When something goes wrong with Tor, you may see an option with the error "
"message to \"copy Tor log to clipboard\"."
msgstr ""
"När något går fel med Tor kan felmeddelandet innehålla alternativet ”kopiera "
"Tor-loggen till urklippet”."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"When using [Tor Browser](#tor-browser), your ISP cannot see what websites "
"you're visiting."
msgstr ""
"När du använder [Tor Browser](#tor-browser) kan internetleverantören inte se "
"vilka webbplatser du besöker."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: content/tor-browser/features/onion-services/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/features/onion-services/
msgid ""
"When you click on \".onion available\", the website will be reloaded and "
"redirected to its onion counterpart."
msgstr ""
"När du klickar på \".onion tillgänglig\" laddas webbplatsen om och "
"omdirigeras till dess motsvarighet i Onion."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"When you run [Tor Browser](#tor-browser) for the first time, you see the Tor "
"Launcher window."
msgstr ""
"När du kör [Tor Browser](#tor-browser) för första gången visas fönstret Tor "
"Launcher."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"You can reconfigure or disable your firewall and restart Tor to test this."
msgstr ""
"Du kan konfigurera om eller inaktivera brandväggen och starta om Tor för att "
"testa detta."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"You may need to consult the documentation for your antivirus software if you "
"do not know how to allow Tor."
msgstr ""
"Du kan behöva läsa dokumentationen till antivirusprogrammet om du inte vet "
"hur Tor tillåts."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"You should never enable Flash to run in [Tor Browser](#tor-browser) as it is "
"unsafe."
msgstr ""
"Aktivera aldrig Flash i [Tor Browser](#tor-browser), eftersom det är osäkert."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"You should not install any additional add-ons on Tor Browser because that "
"can compromise some of its privacy features."
msgstr ""
"Installera inga ytterligare tillägg i Tor Browser, eftersom det kan äventyra "
"vissa av webbläsarens integritetsfunktioner."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"You should see an option to copy the log to your clipboard, which you can "
"then paste to a document to show whoever is helping you troubleshoot."
msgstr ""
"Det bör finnas ett alternativ för att kopiera loggen till urklippet. Sedan "
"kan du klistra in den i ett dokument och visa den för personen som hjälper "
"dig med felsökningen."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"Your internet activity, including the names and addresses of the websites "
"you visit, will be hidden from your [Internet Service Provider (ISP)]"
"(#internet-service-provider-isp) and anyone watching your connection locally."
msgstr ""
"Din internetaktivitet, inklusive namn och adresser till webbplatserna du "
"besöker, döljs för din [internetleverantör (ISP)](#internet-service-provider-"
"isp) och den som övervakar anslutningen lokalt."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"[Cookies](#cookie) are only valid for a single [session](#session) (until "
"Tor Browser is exited or a [New Identity](#new-identity) is requested)."
msgstr ""
"[Kakor](#cookie) är endast giltiga under en enda [session](#session), tills "
"Tor Browser avslutas eller en [ny identitet](#new-identity) begärs."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"[Dangerzone](https://github.com/firstlookmedia/dangerzone) converts any "
"document (even pdf) to pdf, when the document is potentially dangerous or "
"from an untrustworthy source."
msgstr ""
"[Dangerzone](https://github.com/firstlookmedia/dangerzone) omvandlar "
"dokument, även PDF-filer, till PDF när dokumentet kan vara farligt eller "
"kommer från en opålitlig källa."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"[Learn more about Onion Browser](https://blog.torproject.org/tor-heart-onion-"
"browser-and-more-ios-tor)"
msgstr ""
"[Läs mer om Onion Browser](https://blog.torproject.org/tor-heart-onion-"
"browser-and-more-ios-tor)"

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid "[Learn more about Tails](https://tails.net/)."
msgstr "[Läs mer om Tails](https://tails.net/)."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"[Onion services](https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/overview/) "
"offer advantages over ordinary services on the non-private web, including: "
"location hiding, end-to-end authentication, end-to-end encryption, and NAT "
"punching."
msgstr ""
"[Onion-tjänster](https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/overview/) "
"har flera fördelar jämfört med vanliga tjänster på den icke-privata webben, "
"bland annat dold plats, autentisering från ände till ände, "
"totalsträckskryptering och genomträngning av NAT."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"[Onionoo](https://metrics.torproject.org/onionoo.html) is a web-based "
"protocol to learn about currently running [Tor relays](#relay) and [bridges]"
"(#bridge)."
msgstr ""
"[Onionoo](https://metrics.torproject.org/onionoo.html) är ett webbaserat "
"protokoll för information om [Tor-reläer](#relay) och [broar](#bridge) som "
"körs för närvarande."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"[Orbot](https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?"
"id=org.torproject.android) is a free [app](#app) from The Guardian Project "
"that empowers other apps on your device to use the internet more securely."
msgstr ""
"[Orbot](https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?"
"id=org.torproject.android) är en fri [app](#app) från The Guardian Project "
"som gör det möjligt för andra appar på enheten att använda internet säkrare."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"[Pluggable transports](#pluggable-transports) are a type of bridge that "
"helps disguise the fact that you are using Tor."
msgstr ""
"[Pluggbara transporter](#pluggable-transports) är en typ av bro som hjälper "
"till att dölja att du använder Tor."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"[Read more about Orfox](https://blog.torproject.org/orfox-paved-way-tor-"
"browser-android/)."
msgstr ""
"[Läs mer om Orfox](https://blog.torproject.org/orfox-paved-way-tor-browser-"
"android/)."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"[Read more about using moat](../tor-browser/circumvention/getting-bridges/)."
msgstr ""
"[Läs mer om att använda Moat](../tor-browser/circumvention/getting-bridges/)."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"[Snowflake](https://snowflake.torproject.org) is a pluggable transport which "
"provides censorship circumvention and access to a free and open internet."
msgstr ""
"[Snowflake](https://snowflake.torproject.org) är en pluggbar transport som "
"hjälper till att kringgå censur och ger åtkomst till ett fritt och öppet "
"internet."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"[The Guardian Project](https://guardianproject.info/) is a group of software "
"developers, activists and designers that create easy to use, secure, "
"opensource mobile apps and operating system enhancements."
msgstr ""
"[The Guardian Project](https://guardianproject.info/) är en grupp "
"programutvecklare, aktivister och formgivare som skapar lättanvända, säkra "
"mobilappar och förbättringar av operativsystem med öppen källkod."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"[The Orbot app](https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?"
"id=org.torproject.android) provided by The Guardian Project helps route "
"other apps on your android device over the Tor network."
msgstr ""
"[Appen Orbot](https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?"
"id=org.torproject.android) från The Guardian Project hjälper till att leda "
"andra appar på din Android-enhet genom Tor-nätverket."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"[Tor Browser](#tor-browser) deletes your browsing history after you close "
"your [session](#session)."
msgstr ""
"[Tor Browser](#tor-browser) tar bort webbläsarhistoriken när du stänger "
"[sessionen](#session)."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"[Tor Browser](#tor-browser) includes an [add-on](#add-on-extension-or-"
"plugin) called NoScript, accessed by clicking the [hamburger menu (\"≡\")]"
"(#hamburger-menu) at the top-right of the screen, then navigating to \"Add-"
"ons and themes\"."
msgstr ""
"[Tor Browser](#tor-browser) innehåller ett [tillägg](#add-on-extension-or-"
"plugin) som heter NoScript. Du når det genom att klicka på [hamburgermenyn "
"(”≡”)](#hamburger-menu) längst upp till höger på skärmen och sedan välja "
"”Tillägg och teman”."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"[Tor Browser](#tor-browser) is built from a modified version of Firefox ESR "
"(Extended Support Release)."
msgstr ""
"[Tor Browser](#tor-browser) bygger på en modifierad version av Firefox ESR "
"(Extended Support Release)."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"[Tor Browser](#tor-browser) obscures your location by making it look like "
"your [traffic](#traffic) is coming from an IP address that is not your own."
msgstr ""
"[Tor Browser](#tor-browser) döljer din plats genom att få [trafiken]"
"(#traffic) att se ut att komma från en annan IP-adress än din egen."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"[Tor Browser](#tor-browser) prevents a lot of this activity from happening."
msgstr "[Tor Browser](#tor-browser) förhindrar en stor del av denna aktivitet."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid "[Tor Browser](#tor-browser) prevents fingerprinting."
msgstr "[Tor Browser](#tor-browser) motverkar fingeravtryck."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"[Tor Metrics](https://metrics.torproject.org/) archives historical data "
"about the Tor ecosystem, collects data from the public Tor network and "
"related services, and assists in developing novel approaches to safe, "
"privacy preserving data collection."
msgstr ""
"[Tor Metrics](https://metrics.torproject.org/) arkiverar historiska data om "
"Tor-ekosystemet, samlar in data från det offentliga Tor-nätverket och "
"närliggande tjänster samt bidrar till utvecklingen av nya metoder för säker "
"och integritetsbevarande datainsamling."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"[Tor](#tor-network-core-tor) users are often served Captchas because Tor "
"[relays](#relay) make so many requests that sometimes websites have a hard "
"time determining whether or not those requests are coming from humans or "
"bots."
msgstr ""
"[Tor](#tor-network-core-tor)-användare får ofta captcha-utmaningar eftersom "
"Tor-[reläer](#relay) gör så många förfrågningar att webbplatser ibland har "
"svårt att avgöra om de kommer från människor eller robotar."

#: content/glossary/contents.lr:accordion_item.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/glossary/
msgid ""
"[Tor](#tor-network-core-tor) uses three layers of encryption in the Tor "
"[circuit](#circuit); each [relay](#relay) decrypts one layer before passing "
"the request on to the next relay."
msgstr ""
"[Tor](#tor-network-core-tor) använder tre krypteringslager i Tor-[kretsen]"
"(#circuit). Varje [relä](#relay) dekrypterar ett lager innan förfrågan "
"skickas vidare till nästa relä."

