msgid "Does Mullvad collect or store any of my browser or personal data?"
msgstr ""
"Samlar eller lagrar Mullvad några uppgifter om min webbläsare eller mina "
"personuppgifter?"

#: content/mullvad-browser/faqs/does-mullvad-store-collect-data/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/mullvad-browser/faqs/does-mullvad-store-collect-data/
msgid ""
"Please contact Mullvad Browser user support for any further questions: "
"[support@mullvadvpn.net](mailto:support@mullvadvpn.net)."
msgstr ""
"Kontakta Mullvad Browsers användarsupport med ytterligare frågor: "
"[support@mullvadvpn.net](mailto:support@mullvadvpn.net)."

#: content/mullvad-browser/faqs/does-this-mean-tor-browser-going-away/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/mullvad-browser/faqs/does-this-mean-tor-browser-going-away/
msgid "No, Tor Browser is here to stay."
msgstr "Nej, Tor Browser finns kvar."

#: content/mullvad-browser/faqs/does-this-mean-tor-browser-going-away/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/mullvad-browser/faqs/does-this-mean-tor-browser-going-away/
msgid "Therefore Tor Browser will continue to exist."
msgstr "Tor Browser kommer därför att fortsätta finnas."

#: content/mullvad-browser/faqs/does-this-mean-tor-browser-going-away/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/mullvad-browser/faqs/does-this-mean-tor-browser-going-away/
msgid ""
"We know that millions of users around the world rely on Tor Browser and "
"other solutions that the Tor Project offers to safely connect to the "
"internet, to browse anonymously online and to circumvent censorship."
msgstr ""
"Vi vet att miljontals användare över hela världen förlitar sig på Tor "
"Browser och andra lösningar från The Tor Project för att ansluta säkert till "
"internet, surfa anonymt och kringgå censur."

#: content/mullvad-browser/faqs/does-this-mean-tor-browser-going-away/contents.lr:article.longer_title
#: content/mullvad-browser/faqs/does-this-mean-tor-browser-going-away/contents.lr:article.title
#: content/mullvad-browser/faqs/does-this-mean-tor-browser-going-away/contents.lr:tab.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/mullvad-browser/faqs/does-this-mean-tor-browser-going-away/
msgid "Does this mean Tor Browser is going away?"
msgstr "Betyder detta att Tor Browser försvinner?"

#: content/mullvad-browser/faqs/does-this-mean-tor-browser-going-away/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/mullvad-browser/faqs/does-this-mean-tor-browser-going-away/
msgid ""
"The development of Mullvad Browser will actually help make Tor Browser "
"stronger because it allows us to continue to address legacy issues and code, "
"and fix vulnerabilities."
msgstr ""
"Utvecklingen av Mullvad Browser bidrar i själva verket till att göra Tor "
"Browser starkare genom att ge oss möjlighet att fortsätta åtgärda äldre "
"problem och kod samt rätta säkerhetsbrister."

#: content/mullvad-browser/faqs/does-this-mean-tor-browser-going-away/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/mullvad-browser/faqs/does-this-mean-tor-browser-going-away/
msgid ""
"There are a lot of reasons to continue to maintain and improve Tor Browser, "
"it is still one of the few solutions that provides anonymity online because "
"of its use of the Tor network."
msgstr ""
"Det finns många skäl att fortsätta underhålla och förbättra Tor Browser. "
"Tack vare användningen av Tor-nätverket är den fortfarande en av få "
"lösningar som ger anonymitet på nätet."

#: content/mullvad-browser/faqs/does-this-mean-tor-browser-going-away/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/mullvad-browser/faqs/does-this-mean-tor-browser-going-away/
msgid ""
"This combination is a powerful one and sometimes one of the few options that "
"censored and surveilled users have in their region to freely and safely "
"access the internet."
msgstr ""
"Kombinationen är kraftfull och ibland ett av få alternativ som användare i "
"censurerade och övervakade regioner har för att fritt och säkert få åtkomst "
"till internet."

#: content/mullvad-browser/faqs/does-this-mean-tor-browser-going-away/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/mullvad-browser/faqs/does-this-mean-tor-browser-going-away/
msgid ""
"This is also a free solution for all, making it an affordable solution for "
"people at risk."
msgstr ""
"Det är dessutom en kostnadsfri lösning för alla, vilket gör den ekonomiskt "
"tillgänglig för människor som är utsatta."

#: content/mullvad-browser/faqs/does-this-mean-tor-browser-will-get-less-attention/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/mullvad-browser/faqs/does-this-mean-tor-browser-will-get-less-attention/
msgid ""
"Not at all, we are continuing to invest on improving the usability of Tor "
"Browser, as we have done in the last 5 years with major releases that "
"included user experience improvements."
msgstr ""
"Inte alls. Vi fortsätter att investera i Tor Browsers användbarhet, precis "
"som vi har gjort under de senaste fem åren genom stora utgåvor med "
"förbättrad användarupplevelse."

#: content/mullvad-browser/faqs/does-this-mean-tor-browser-will-get-less-attention/contents.lr:article.longer_title
#: content/mullvad-browser/faqs/does-this-mean-tor-browser-will-get-less-attention/contents.lr:article.title
#: content/mullvad-browser/faqs/does-this-mean-tor-browser-will-get-less-attention/contents.lr:tab.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/mullvad-browser/faqs/does-this-mean-tor-browser-will-get-less-attention/
msgid "Does this mean Tor Browser will get less attention?"
msgstr "Betyder detta att Tor Browser får mindre uppmärksamhet?"

#: content/mullvad-browser/faqs/does-this-mean-tor-browser-will-get-less-attention/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/mullvad-browser/faqs/does-this-mean-tor-browser-will-get-less-attention/
msgid "It has not affected our attention and dedication to Tor Browser."
msgstr "Det har inte påverkat vårt fokus på eller engagemang för Tor Browser."

#: content/mullvad-browser/faqs/does-this-mean-tor-browser-will-get-less-attention/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/mullvad-browser/faqs/does-this-mean-tor-browser-will-get-less-attention/
msgid ""
"The development of Mullvad Browser has helped us address legacy issues and "
"code, and fix vulnerabilities."
msgstr ""
"Utvecklingen av Mullvad Browser har hjälpt oss att åtgärda äldre problem och "
"kod samt rätta säkerhetsbrister."

#: content/mullvad-browser/faqs/does-this-mean-tor-browser-will-get-less-attention/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/mullvad-browser/faqs/does-this-mean-tor-browser-will-get-less-attention/
msgid ""
"We are also working hard on bringing Tor Browser for Android up to par with "
"the desktop version's features."
msgstr ""
"Vi arbetar också intensivt med att ge Tor Browser för Android samma "
"funktioner som datorversionen."

#: content/mullvad-browser/faqs/relationship-between-mullvad-vpn-tor/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/mullvad-browser/faqs/relationship-between-mullvad-vpn-tor/
msgid "Mullvad has been part of the Tor community for many years now."
msgstr "Mullvad har ingått i Tor-gemenskapen i många år."

#: content/mullvad-browser/faqs/relationship-between-mullvad-vpn-tor/contents.lr:article.longer_title
#: content/mullvad-browser/faqs/relationship-between-mullvad-vpn-tor/contents.lr:article.title
#: content/mullvad-browser/faqs/relationship-between-mullvad-vpn-tor/contents.lr:tab.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/mullvad-browser/faqs/relationship-between-mullvad-vpn-tor/
msgid "What is the relationship between Mullvad VPN and the Tor Project?"
msgstr "Vilken relation har Mullvad VPN och The Tor Project?"

#: content/mullvad-browser/faqs/relationship-between-mullvad-vpn-tor/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/mullvad-browser/faqs/relationship-between-mullvad-vpn-tor/
msgid ""
"They are a Shallot Level member (highest membership tier) of the [Tor "
"Project membership program](https://www.torproject.org/about/membership/) "
"and have been a founding member of the Tor Project's Membership Program."
msgstr ""
"Mullvad är medlem på Shallot-nivå, den högsta medlemsnivån, i [The Tor "
"Projects medlemsprogram](https://www.torproject.org/about/membership/) och "
"var en av programmets grundande medlemmar."

#: content/mullvad-browser/faqs/relationship-between-mullvad-vpn-tor/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/mullvad-browser/faqs/relationship-between-mullvad-vpn-tor/
msgid ""
"When Mullvad approached us to jointly develop a browser, we said yes because "
"there is great value alignment between our two organizations in our efforts "
"to make privacy-enhancing technologies more widely available and make mass-"
"surveillance impractical."
msgstr ""
"När Mullvad föreslog att vi gemensamt skulle utveckla en webbläsare tackade "
"vi ja, eftersom våra organisationer delar starka värderingar i arbetet för "
"att göra integritetsförbättrande teknik mer allmänt tillgänglig och "
"massövervakning opraktisk."

#: content/mullvad-browser/faqs/what-is-difference-mullvad-browser-tor-browser/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/mullvad-browser/faqs/what-is-difference-mullvad-browser-tor-browser/
msgid ""
"Mullvad Browser is free and open-source software that connects to the "
"internet (if you use it together with Mullvad VPN) through the encrypted VPN "
"tunnels and VPN servers of Mullvad."
msgstr ""
"Mullvad Browser är fri programvara med öppen källkod som, om den används "
"tillsammans med Mullvad VPN, ansluter till internet genom Mullvads "
"krypterade VPN-tunnlar och VPN-servrar."

#: content/mullvad-browser/faqs/what-is-difference-mullvad-browser-tor-browser/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/mullvad-browser/faqs/what-is-difference-mullvad-browser-tor-browser/
msgid ""
"You can use it without or with any VPN, but you should make sure to use a "
"VPN provider you can trust."
msgstr ""
"Du kan använda webbläsaren utan VPN eller med vilken VPN-tjänst som helst, "
"men välj en leverantör som du litar på."

#: content/mullvad-browser/faqs/what-is-difference-mullvad-browser-tor-browser/contents.lr:article.longer_title
#: content/mullvad-browser/faqs/what-is-difference-mullvad-browser-tor-browser/contents.lr:article.title
#: content/mullvad-browser/faqs/what-is-difference-mullvad-browser-tor-browser/contents.lr:tab.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/mullvad-browser/faqs/what-is-difference-mullvad-browser-tor-browser/
msgid "What is the difference between Mullvad Browser and Tor Browser?"
msgstr "Vad är skillnaden mellan Mullvad Browser och Tor Browser?"

#: content/mullvad-browser/faqs/what-is-difference-mullvad-browser-tor-browser/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/mullvad-browser/faqs/what-is-difference-mullvad-browser-tor-browser/
msgid ""
"Access to Onion Services (i.e. onionsites, Onion-Location redirects, onion "
"authentication, and SecureDrop integration)"
msgstr ""
"Åtkomst till onion-tjänster, det vill säga onion-webbplatser, omdirigeringar "
"via Onion-Location, onion-autentisering och SecureDrop-integrering"

#: content/mullvad-browser/faqs/what-is-difference-mullvad-browser-tor-browser/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/mullvad-browser/faqs/what-is-difference-mullvad-browser-tor-browser/
msgid ""
"As a benefit of connecting to the internet using the Tor network, various "
"Tor specific features are closely integrated with our own browser that "
"Mullvad Browser does not offer, including:"
msgstr ""
"Eftersom Tor Browser ansluter till internet genom Tor-nätverket är flera Tor-"
"specifika funktioner nära integrerade i webbläsaren och saknas i Mullvad "
"Browser, bland annat:"

#: content/mullvad-browser/faqs/what-is-difference-mullvad-browser-tor-browser/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/mullvad-browser/faqs/what-is-difference-mullvad-browser-tor-browser/
msgid ""
"Aside from the way that both browsers connect users to the internet (Tor "
"network vs trusted VPN connection) the differences between both browsers are "
"very small and come down to individual preference and use cases for the end-"
"user."
msgstr ""
"Bortsett från hur webbläsarna ansluter användaren till internet (Tor-"
"nätverket respektive en betrodd VPN-anslutning) är skillnaderna små och "
"handlar främst om användarens preferenser och användningsfall."

#: content/mullvad-browser/faqs/what-is-difference-mullvad-browser-tor-browser/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/mullvad-browser/faqs/what-is-difference-mullvad-browser-tor-browser/
msgid ""
"Built-in censorship circumvention with a unique UX found in Tor Browser's "
"connection settings and connection assist"
msgstr ""
"Inbyggt censurkringgående med ett unikt gränssnitt i Tor Browsers "
"anslutningsinställningar och anslutningshjälp"

#: content/mullvad-browser/faqs/what-is-difference-mullvad-browser-tor-browser/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/mullvad-browser/faqs/what-is-difference-mullvad-browser-tor-browser/
msgid "Circuit isolation and the integration with new-identity"
msgstr "Kretsisolering och integrering med Ny identitet"

#: content/mullvad-browser/faqs/what-is-difference-mullvad-browser-tor-browser/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/mullvad-browser/faqs/what-is-difference-mullvad-browser-tor-browser/
msgid ""
"Our objective with this collaboration is to provide more choice for online "
"privacy (e.g., minimize fingerprinting and try to prevent linkability) to "
"users at all levels."
msgstr ""
"Målet med samarbetet är att ge användare på alla nivåer fler alternativ för "
"integritet på nätet, exempelvis minimerade fingeravtryck och motverkad "
"sammankoppling."

#: content/mullvad-browser/faqs/what-is-mullvad-browser/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/mullvad-browser/faqs/what-is-mullvad-browser/
msgid ""
"Mullvad Browser is Tor Browser without the Tor Network - that allows anyone "
"to take advantage of all the privacy features Tor created."
msgstr ""
"Mullvad Browser är Tor Browser utan Tor-nätverket och låter alla dra nytta "
"av integritetsfunktionerna som Tor har skapat."

#: content/mullvad-browser/faqs/what-is-mullvad-browser/contents.lr:article.longer_title
#: content/mullvad-browser/faqs/what-is-mullvad-browser/contents.lr:article.title
#: content/mullvad-browser/faqs/what-is-mullvad-browser/contents.lr:tab.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/mullvad-browser/faqs/what-is-mullvad-browser/
msgid "What is Mullvad Browser?"
msgstr "Vad är Mullvad Browser?"

#: content/mullvad-browser/faqs/what-is-mullvad-browser/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/mullvad-browser/faqs/what-is-mullvad-browser/
msgid ""
"By default, Mullvad Browser has private mode enabled, blocks third-party "
"trackers and cookies."
msgstr ""
"Som standard använder Mullvad Browser privat läge och blockerar spårare och "
"kakor från tredje part."

#: content/mullvad-browser/faqs/what-is-mullvad-browser/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/mullvad-browser/faqs/what-is-mullvad-browser/
msgid ""
"If people want to connect the browser with a VPN they trust, they can easily "
"do so."
msgstr ""
"Den som vill ansluta webbläsaren till en betrodd VPN-tjänst kan enkelt göra "
"det."

#: content/mullvad-browser/faqs/what-is-mullvad-browser/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/mullvad-browser/faqs/what-is-mullvad-browser/
msgid ""
"It is distributed by Mullvad and can be downloaded on their [website]"
"(https://mullvad.net/browser)."
msgstr ""
"Webbläsaren distribueras av Mullvad och kan hämtas från deras [webbplats]"
"(https://mullvad.net/browser)."

#: content/mullvad-browser/faqs/what-is-mullvad-browser/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/mullvad-browser/faqs/what-is-mullvad-browser/
msgid ""
"The browser is free and open-source and is developed by the Tor Project in "
"collaboration with Mullvad VPN."
msgstr ""
"Webbläsaren är fri programvara med öppen källkod och utvecklas av The Tor "
"Project i samarbete med Mullvad VPN."

#: content/mullvad-browser/faqs/what-is-mullvad-browser/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/mullvad-browser/faqs/what-is-mullvad-browser/
msgid ""
"The browser's 'out-of-the-box' configurations and settings will mask many "
"parameters and features commonly used to extract information from a person's "
"device, including fonts, rendered content, and several hardware APIs."
msgstr ""
"Webbläsarens standardkonfiguration och inställningar döljer många parametrar "
"och funktioner som ofta används för att hämta information från en persons "
"enhet, bland annat teckensnitt, renderat innehåll och flera maskinvaru-"
"API:er."

#: content/mullvad-browser/faqs/when-use-mullvad-browser/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/mullvad-browser/faqs/when-use-mullvad-browser/
msgid ""
"You should use Mullvad Browser if you are looking for a privacy enhanced "
"browser solution to connect with your trusted VPN."
msgstr ""
"Använd Mullvad Browser om du söker en integritetsförbättrad webbläsare som "
"kan anslutas till en betrodd VPN-tjänst."

#: content/mullvad-browser/faqs/when-use-mullvad-browser/contents.lr:article.longer_title
#: content/mullvad-browser/faqs/when-use-mullvad-browser/contents.lr:article.title
#: content/mullvad-browser/faqs/when-use-mullvad-browser/contents.lr:tab.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/mullvad-browser/faqs/when-use-mullvad-browser/
msgid "When should I use Mullvad Browser?"
msgstr "När bör jag använda Mullvad Browser?"

#: content/mullvad-browser/faqs/when-use-mullvad-browser/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/mullvad-browser/faqs/when-use-mullvad-browser/
msgid ""
"Its default settings and features are intended to combat mass surveillance, "
"data mining and tracking, or other privacy violations that are commonly "
"employed by big tech companies."
msgstr ""
"Standardinställningarna och funktionerna är avsedda att motverka "
"massövervakning, datautvinning, spårning och andra integritetsintrång som "
"ofta används av stora teknikföretag."

#: content/mullvad-browser/faqs/when-use-mullvad-browser/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/mullvad-browser/faqs/when-use-mullvad-browser/
msgid ""
"While Mullvad Browser offers similar privacy protections to Tor Browser, it "
"is best suited for the threat model of corporate mass-surveillance by big "
"tech companies."
msgstr ""
"Mullvad Browser erbjuder liknande integritetsskydd som Tor Browser men är "
"bäst lämpad för hotmodellen med företagsdriven massövervakning från stora "
"teknikföretag."

#: content/mullvad-browser/faqs/where-to-get-support/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/mullvad-browser/faqs/where-to-get-support/
msgid "Instructions to contact support and report issues."
msgstr "Anvisningar för att kontakta supporten och rapportera problem."

#: content/mullvad-browser/faqs/where-to-get-support/contents.lr:article.longer_title
#: content/mullvad-browser/faqs/where-to-get-support/contents.lr:article.title
#: content/mullvad-browser/faqs/where-to-get-support/contents.lr:tab.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/mullvad-browser/faqs/where-to-get-support/
msgid "Where can I get support for Mullvad Browser?"
msgstr "Var får jag support för Mullvad Browser?"

#: content/mullvad-browser/faqs/where-to-get-support/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/mullvad-browser/faqs/where-to-get-support/
msgid ""
"For any and all support inquiries, please email: [support@mullvadvpn.net]"
"(mailto:support@mullvadvpn.net)."
msgstr ""
"Skicka alla supportfrågor till [support@mullvadvpn.net]"
"(mailto:support@mullvadvpn.net)."

#: content/mullvad-browser/faqs/where-to-get-support/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/mullvad-browser/faqs/where-to-get-support/
msgid ""
"User support is available via email or via [Github issues](https://"
"github.com/mullvad/mullvad-browser/issues)."
msgstr ""
"Användarsupport finns via e-post och [GitHub-ärenden](https://github.com/"
"mullvad/mullvad-browser/issues)."

#: content/mullvad-browser/faqs/why-tor-project-develop-this-browser/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/mullvad-browser/faqs/why-tor-project-develop-this-browser/
msgid ""
"Mullvad Browser fills a gap in the market for those who want to run a "
"privacy-focused browser as good as Tor Browser but with a trusted VPN "
"instead of the Tor Network."
msgstr ""
"Mullvad Browser fyller en lucka för dem som vill använda en "
"integritetsinriktad webbläsare som är lika bra som Tor Browser men med en "
"betrodd VPN-tjänst i stället för Tor-nätverket."

#: content/mullvad-browser/faqs/why-tor-project-develop-this-browser/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/mullvad-browser/faqs/why-tor-project-develop-this-browser/
msgid ""
"This partnership contributes to providing people with more free privacy "
"options for web browsing while challenging the current business model of "
"exploiting people's data."
msgstr ""
"Samarbetet ger människor fler kostnadsfria integritetsalternativ för "
"webbsurfning och utmanar samtidigt den rådande affärsmodellen där människors "
"data exploateras."

#: content/mullvad-browser/faqs/why-tor-project-develop-this-browser/contents.lr:article.longer_title
#: content/mullvad-browser/faqs/why-tor-project-develop-this-browser/contents.lr:article.title
#: content/mullvad-browser/faqs/why-tor-project-develop-this-browser/contents.lr:tab.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/mullvad-browser/faqs/why-tor-project-develop-this-browser/
msgid "Why did the Tor Project decide to develop this browser for Mullvad VPN?"
msgstr ""
"Varför beslutade The Tor Project att utveckla denna webbläsare för Mullvad "
"VPN?"

#: content/mullvad-browser/faqs/why-tor-project-develop-this-browser/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/mullvad-browser/faqs/why-tor-project-develop-this-browser/
msgid ""
"It demonstrates that it is possible to develop free technology solutions "
"that prioritize the protection of user privacy."
msgstr ""
"Det visar att det går att utveckla fria tekniska lösningar som prioriterar "
"skyddet av användarnas integritet."

#: content/mullvad-browser/faqs/why-tor-project-develop-this-browser/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/mullvad-browser/faqs/why-tor-project-develop-this-browser/
msgid ""
"Mullvad shares the same values around internet privacy and freedom and is "
"dedicated to making privacy-enhancing technologies more widely available and "
"rendering mass-surveillance impractical."
msgstr ""
"Mullvad delar våra värderingar om internetintegritet och frihet och arbetar "
"för att göra integritetsförbättrande teknik mer allmänt tillgänglig och "
"massövervakning opraktisk."

#: content/mullvad-browser/faqs/why-tor-project-develop-this-browser/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/mullvad-browser/faqs/why-tor-project-develop-this-browser/
msgid ""
"Over the last couple of years, the Tor Project has launched a number of "
"[initiatives to increase adoption of our technologies](https://"
"wiki.mozilla.org/Security/Tor_Uplift) and made [significant improvements]"
"(https://blog.torproject.org/tor-browser-advancing-privacy-innovation/) to "
"the usability of our own products."
msgstr ""
"Under de senaste åren har The Tor Project lanserat flera [initiativ för att "
"öka användningen av vår teknik](https://wiki.mozilla.org/Security/"
"Tor_Uplift) och gjort [betydande förbättringar](https://blog.torproject.org/"
"tor-browser-advancing-privacy-innovation/) av användbarheten i våra egna "
"produkter."

#: content/mullvad-browser/faqs/why-tor-project-develop-this-browser/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/mullvad-browser/faqs/why-tor-project-develop-this-browser/
msgid ""
"This joint project with Mullvad has contributed to addressing legacy code "
"issues for Tor Browser and allowed the allocation of dedicated resources to "
"make necessary improvements that benefit both Tor and Mullvad Browsers."
msgstr ""
"Det gemensamma projektet med Mullvad har bidragit till att åtgärda äldre "
"kodproblem i Tor Browser och gjort det möjligt att avsätta särskilda "
"resurser för nödvändiga förbättringar som gynnar både Tor Browser och "
"Mullvad Browser."

#: content/mullvad-browser/faqs/why-trust-mullvad-browser/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/mullvad-browser/faqs/why-trust-mullvad-browser/
msgid ""
"Unlike other browsers on the market, Mullvad Browser's business model does "
"not rely on capitalizing on users' behavioral data."
msgstr ""
"Till skillnad från andra webbläsare på marknaden bygger Mullvad Browsers "
"affärsmodell inte på att tjäna pengar på användarnas beteendedata."

#: content/mullvad-browser/faqs/why-trust-mullvad-browser/contents.lr:article.longer_title
#: content/mullvad-browser/faqs/why-trust-mullvad-browser/contents.lr:article.title
#: content/mullvad-browser/faqs/why-trust-mullvad-browser/contents.lr:tab.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/mullvad-browser/faqs/why-trust-mullvad-browser/
msgid "Why should I trust Mullvad Browser?"
msgstr "Varför ska jag lita på Mullvad Browser?"

#: content/mullvad-browser/faqs/why-trust-mullvad-browser/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/mullvad-browser/faqs/why-trust-mullvad-browser/
msgid ""
"Mullvad Browser was developed by the Tor Project who have a proven track "
"record of building and deploying free and open-source privacy preserving "
"technologies such as Tor Browser, Onion Services, the Tor network etc. that "
"have helped millions of people from at-risk communities defend their right "
"to privacy and anonymity online."
msgstr ""
"Mullvad Browser utvecklades av The Tor Project, som har lång erfarenhet av "
"att bygga och distribuera fri integritetsbevarande teknik med öppen källkod, "
"såsom Tor Browser, onion-tjänster och Tor-nätverket. Dessa verktyg har "
"hjälpt miljontals människor i utsatta gemenskaper att försvara sin rätt till "
"integritet och anonymitet på nätet."

#: content/mullvad-browser/faqs/why-trust-mullvad-browser/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/mullvad-browser/faqs/why-trust-mullvad-browser/
msgid ""
"Mullvad makes money by selling their VPN, they are not in the business of "
"selling user data from the browser."
msgstr ""
"Mullvad tjänar pengar på sin VPN-tjänst och säljer inte användardata från "
"webbläsaren."

#: content/offline/tor-browser/contents.lr:offline.content
#: content/tor-browser/contents.lr:product.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/offline/tor-browser/
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/
msgid ""
"The Tor Browser user manual guides you through getting started, configuring "
"censorship circumvention, exploring key features like fingerprinting "
"protections and onion services, and troubleshooting common issues."
msgstr ""
"Tor Browsers användarhandbok hjälper dig att komma igång, konfigurera "
"censurkringgående, utforska viktiga funktioner som skydd mot fingeravtryck "
"och onion-tjänster samt felsöka vanliga problem."

#: content/offline/tor-browser/contents.lr:offline.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/offline/tor-browser/
msgid "Tor Browser manual"
msgstr "Handbok för Tor Browser"

#: content/offline/tor-vpn/contents.lr:offline.content
#: content/tor-vpn/contents.lr:product.content
#: content/tor-vpn/getting-started/about-tor-vpn/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/offline/tor-vpn/
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-vpn/
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-vpn/getting-started/about-tor-vpn/
msgid "Do not rely on it for anything other than testing."
msgstr "Använd den inte till något annat än testning."

#: content/offline/tor-vpn/contents.lr:offline.content
#: content/tor-vpn/contents.lr:product.content
#: content/tor-vpn/getting-started/about-tor-vpn/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/offline/tor-vpn/
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-vpn/
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-vpn/getting-started/about-tor-vpn/
msgid ""
"It may leak information and should not be relied on for anything sensitive."
msgstr "Den kan läcka information och bör inte användas för något känsligt."

#: content/offline/tor-vpn/contents.lr:offline.content
#: content/tor-vpn/contents.lr:product.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/offline/tor-vpn/
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-vpn/
msgid "⚠️ **WARNING**: Tor VPN is beta software."
msgstr "⚠️ **VARNING**: Tor VPN är betaprogramvara."

#: content/offline/tor-vpn/contents.lr:offline.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/offline/tor-vpn/
msgid "Tor VPN manual"
msgstr "Handbok för Tor VPN"

#: content/relays/contents.lr:product.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/
msgid "Relays FAQ"
msgstr "Vanliga frågor om reläer"

#: content/relays/getting-started/better-anonymity/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/getting-started/better-anonymity/
msgid ""
"Running a relay can increase your anonymity against some attacks, but it "
"also carries risks and trade-offs that depend on your threat model."
msgstr ""
"Att driva ett relä kan förbättra anonymiteten mot vissa attacker, men medför "
"också risker och avvägningar som beror på din hotmodell."

#: content/relays/getting-started/better-anonymity/contents.lr:article.longer_title
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/getting-started/better-anonymity/
msgid "Does running a relay improve your anonymity when using Tor?"
msgstr "Förbättras anonymiteten när du använder Tor om du driver ett relä?"

#: content/relays/getting-started/better-anonymity/contents.lr:article.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/getting-started/better-anonymity/
msgid "Running a relay and using Tor"
msgstr "Driva ett relä och använda Tor"

#: content/relays/getting-started/better-anonymity/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/getting-started/better-anonymity/
msgid ""
"(In this case they still don't know your destinations unless they are "
"watching them too, but you're no better off than if you were an ordinary "
"client.)"
msgstr ""
"(I detta fall känner de fortfarande inte till destinationerna om de inte "
"också övervakar dem, men du har inget bättre skydd än en vanlig klient.)"

#: content/relays/getting-started/better-anonymity/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/getting-started/better-anonymity/
msgid "A lot of that depends on the attacks you are most worried about."
msgstr "Mycket beror på vilka attacker du oroar dig mest för."

#: content/relays/getting-started/better-anonymity/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/getting-started/better-anonymity/
msgid ""
"First, while we only have a few hundred relays, the fact that you're running "
"one might signal to an attacker that you place a high value on your "
"anonymity."
msgstr ""
"För det första kan det faktum att du driver ett relä, när nätverket bara har "
"några hundra reläer, signalera till en angripare att du värdesätter din "
"anonymitet högt."

#: content/relays/getting-started/better-anonymity/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/getting-started/better-anonymity/
msgid "For most users, we think it's a smart move."
msgstr "För de flesta användare anser vi att det är ett klokt val."

#: content/relays/getting-started/better-anonymity/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/getting-started/better-anonymity/
msgid ""
"It is an open research question whether the benefits outweigh the risks."
msgstr "Det är en öppen forskningsfråga om fördelarna överväger riskerna."

#: content/relays/getting-started/better-anonymity/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/getting-started/better-anonymity/
msgid ""
"Running a Tor relay can offer some additional anonymity benefits compared to "
"being a regular user, but it also introduces specific risks and trade-offs "
"depending on your threat model."
msgstr ""
"Att driva ett Tor-relä kan ge vissa ytterligare anonymitetsfördelar jämfört "
"med att vara en vanlig användare, men det medför även särskilda risker och "
"avvägningar beroende på hotmodellen."

#: content/relays/getting-started/better-anonymity/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/getting-started/better-anonymity/
msgid ""
"Second, there are some more esoteric attacks that are not as well-understood "
"or well-tested that involve making use of the knowledge that you're running "
"a relay -- for example, an attacker may be able to \"observe\" whether "
"you're sending traffic even if they can't actually watch your network, by "
"relaying traffic through your Tor relay and noticing changes in traffic "
"timing."
msgstr ""
"För det andra finns mer esoteriska attacker som är mindre väl förstådda och "
"testade och som utnyttjar vetskapen om att du driver ett relä. En angripare "
"kan exempelvis ”observera” om du skickar trafik, även utan att direkt "
"övervaka nätverket, genom att skicka trafik genom ditt Tor-relä och upptäcka "
"förändringar i trafiktidpunkterna."

#: content/relays/getting-started/better-anonymity/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/getting-started/better-anonymity/
msgid ""
"The simplest example is an attacker who owns a small number of Tor relays."
msgstr ""
"Det enklaste exemplet är en angripare som äger ett litet antal Tor-reläer."

#: content/relays/getting-started/better-anonymity/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/getting-started/better-anonymity/
msgid "There are also some downsides to running a Tor relay."
msgstr "Det finns även nackdelar med att driva ett Tor-relä."

#: content/relays/getting-started/better-anonymity/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/getting-started/better-anonymity/
msgid ""
"There are some cases where it doesn't seem to help: if an attacker can watch "
"all of your incoming and outgoing traffic, then it's easy for them to learn "
"which connections were relayed and which started at you."
msgstr ""
"I vissa fall verkar det inte hjälpa: om en angripare kan övervaka all "
"inkommande och utgående trafik är det enkelt att avgöra vilka anslutningar "
"som vidarebefordrades och vilka som började hos dig."

#: content/relays/getting-started/better-anonymity/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/getting-started/better-anonymity/
msgid ""
"They will see a connection from you, but they won't be able to know whether "
"the connection originated at your computer or was relayed from somebody else."
msgstr ""
"De ser en anslutning från dig men kan inte veta om den uppstod på din dator "
"eller vidarebefordrades från någon annan."

#: content/relays/getting-started/better-anonymity/contents.lr:tab.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/getting-started/better-anonymity/
msgid "Better Anonymity"
msgstr "Bättre anonymitet"

#: content/relays/getting-started/contents.lr:section.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/getting-started/
msgid "How to run Tor relays and bridges"
msgstr "Så driver du Tor-reläer och broar"

#: content/relays/getting-started/my-family/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/getting-started/my-family/
msgid ""
"You can run more than one Tor relay to contribute additional bandwidth to "
"the network, but you must configure them properly to maintain user anonymity "
"and network diversity."
msgstr ""
"Du kan driva mer än ett Tor-relä för att bidra med mer bandbredd till "
"nätverket, men de måste konfigureras korrekt för att bevara användarnas "
"anonymitet och nätverkets mångfald."

#: content/relays/getting-started/my-family/contents.lr:article.longer_title
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/getting-started/my-family/
msgid "How to safely run more than one Tor relay"
msgstr "Så driver du flera Tor-reläer på ett säkert sätt"

#: content/relays/getting-started/my-family/contents.lr:article.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/getting-started/my-family/
msgid "Running multiple relays"
msgstr "Driva flera reläer"

#: content/relays/getting-started/my-family/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/getting-started/my-family/
msgid ""
"But please don't run more than a few dozen on the same network, since part "
"of the goal of the Tor network is dispersal and diversity."
msgstr ""
"Kör dock inte fler än några tiotal i samma nätverk, eftersom ett av Tor-"
"nätverkets mål är spridning och mångfald."

#: content/relays/getting-started/my-family/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/getting-started/my-family/
msgid ""
"If you do decide to run more than one relay, please set the \"MyFamily\" "
"config option in the torrc of each relay, listing all the relays (comma-"
"separated) that are under your control:"
msgstr ""
"Om du bestämmer dig för att driva flera reläer anger du "
"konfigurationsalternativet ”MyFamily” i torrc för varje relä och listar alla "
"reläer du styr, avgränsade med kommatecken:"

#: content/relays/getting-started/my-family/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/getting-started/my-family/
msgid ""
"If you want to run several relays to donate more to the network, we're happy "
"with that."
msgstr ""
"Vi uppskattar om du vill driva flera reläer och bidra mer till nätverket."

#: content/relays/getting-started/my-family/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/getting-started/my-family/
msgid ""
"That way, Tor clients will know to avoid using more than one of your relays "
"in a single circuit."
msgstr ""
"Då vet Tor-klienterna att de inte ska använda mer än ett av dina reläer i "
"samma krets."

#: content/relays/getting-started/my-family/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/getting-started/my-family/
msgid ""
"You should set MyFamily if you have administrative control of the computers "
"or of their network, even if they're not all in the same geographic location."
msgstr ""
"Ange MyFamily om du har administrativ kontroll över datorerna eller deras "
"nätverk, även om de inte finns på samma geografiska plats."

#: content/relays/getting-started/my-family/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/getting-started/my-family/
msgid ""
"where each fingerprint is the 40 character identity fingerprint (without "
"spaces)."
msgstr ""
"där varje fingeravtryck är det 40 tecken långa identitetsfingeravtrycket "
"utan blanksteg."

#: content/relays/getting-started/my-family/contents.lr:tab.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/getting-started/my-family/
msgid "Relay family"
msgstr "Reläfamilj"

#: content/relays/getting-started/run-exit-from-home/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/getting-started/run-exit-from-home/
msgid ""
"Running an exit relay from your home connection can expose you to serious "
"legal, privacy, and operational risks."
msgstr ""
"Att driva ett utgångsrelä via hemmets internetanslutning kan utsätta dig för "
"allvarliga juridiska, integritetsmässiga och driftsrelaterade risker."

#: content/relays/getting-started/run-exit-from-home/contents.lr:article.longer_title
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/getting-started/run-exit-from-home/
msgid "Why you should avoid running an exit relay from your home network"
msgstr "Varför du bör undvika att driva ett utgångsrelä från hemnätverket"

#: content/relays/getting-started/run-exit-from-home/contents.lr:article.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/getting-started/run-exit-from-home/
msgid "Running an exit relay from home"
msgstr "Driva ett utgångsrelä hemma"

#: content/relays/getting-started/run-exit-from-home/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/getting-started/run-exit-from-home/
msgid ""
"For that reason, it's best not to run your exit relay in your home or using "
"your home internet connection."
msgstr ""
"Därför är det bäst att inte driva utgångsreläet hemma eller via hemmets "
"internetanslutning."

#: content/relays/getting-started/run-exit-from-home/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/getting-started/run-exit-from-home/
msgid ""
"Have a separate IP address for your exit relay, and don't route your own "
"traffic through it."
msgstr ""
"Använd en separat IP-adress för utgångsreläet och led inte din egen trafik "
"genom det."

#: content/relays/getting-started/run-exit-from-home/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/getting-started/run-exit-from-home/
msgid ""
"If law enforcement becomes interested in traffic from your exit relay, it's "
"possible that officers will seize your computer."
msgstr ""
"Om brottsbekämpande myndigheter intresserar sig för trafik från "
"utgångsreläet kan de beslagta datorn."

#: content/relays/getting-started/run-exit-from-home/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/getting-started/run-exit-from-home/
msgid ""
"Instead, consider running your exit relay in a commercial facility that is "
"supportive of Tor."
msgstr ""
"Överväg i stället att driva utgångsreläet i en kommersiell anläggning som "
"stöder Tor."

#: content/relays/getting-started/run-exit-from-home/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/getting-started/run-exit-from-home/
msgid ""
"Of course, you should avoid keeping any sensitive or personal information on "
"the computer hosting your exit relay."
msgstr ""
"Förvara naturligtvis ingen känslig eller personlig information på datorn som "
"är värd för utgångsreläet."

#: content/relays/getting-started/run-exit-from-home/contents.lr:tab.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/getting-started/run-exit-from-home/
msgid "Exit relay from home"
msgstr "Utgångsrelä hemma"

#: content/relays/getting-started/what-is-a-bridge/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/getting-started/what-is-a-bridge/
msgid ""
"Bridges are non-public Tor relays that aren't listed in the public "
"directory, making them harder for ISPs or governments to block."
msgstr ""
"Broar är icke-offentliga Tor-reläer som inte listas i den offentliga "
"katalogen, vilket gör dem svårare för internetleverantörer och regeringar "
"att blockera."

#: content/relays/getting-started/what-is-a-bridge/contents.lr:article.longer_title
#: content/relays/getting-started/what-is-a-bridge/contents.lr:article.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/getting-started/what-is-a-bridge/
msgid "What is a bridge"
msgstr "Vad är en bro?"

#: content/relays/getting-started/what-is-a-bridge/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/getting-started/what-is-a-bridge/
msgid ""
"A bridge is just a normal relay with a slightly different configuration."
msgstr "En bro är ett vanligt relä med en något annorlunda konfiguration."

#: content/relays/getting-started/what-is-a-bridge/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/getting-started/what-is-a-bridge/
msgid ""
"Because bridge IP addresses aren't publicly listed, they are less likely to "
"be automatically blocklisted by online services."
msgstr ""
"Eftersom broarnas IP-adresser inte listas offentligt är det mindre sannolikt "
"att nättjänster automatiskt lägger dem i blockeringslistor."

#: content/relays/getting-started/what-is-a-bridge/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/getting-started/what-is-a-bridge/
msgid ""
"Bridge relays are Tor relays that are not listed in the public Tor directory."
msgstr ""
"Broreläer är Tor-reläer som inte listas i den offentliga Tor-katalogen."

#: content/relays/getting-started/what-is-a-bridge/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/getting-started/what-is-a-bridge/
msgid ""
"Bridges are useful for Tor users connecting from censored networks or under "
"oppressive regimes."
msgstr ""
"Broar är användbara för Tor-användare som ansluter från censurerade nätverk "
"eller under förtryckande regimer."

#: content/relays/getting-started/what-is-a-bridge/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/getting-started/what-is-a-bridge/
msgid ""
"If you have a residential connection and want to become a relay operator, we "
"recommend running a bridge."
msgstr ""
"Om du har en internetanslutning i hemmet och vill bli reläoperatör "
"rekommenderar vi att du driver en bro."

#: content/relays/getting-started/what-is-a-bridge/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/getting-started/what-is-a-bridge/
msgid ""
"See [How do I run a bridge](https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/"
"bridge/) for instructions."
msgstr ""
"Anvisningar finns i [Så driver du en bro](https://community.torproject.org/"
"relay/setup/bridge/)."

#: content/relays/getting-started/what-is-a-bridge/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/getting-started/what-is-a-bridge/
msgid ""
"That means that ISPs or governments trying to block access to the Tor "
"network can't simply block all bridges."
msgstr ""
"Det innebär att internetleverantörer och regeringar som försöker blockera "
"Tor-nätverket inte bara kan blockera alla broar."

#: content/relays/getting-started/what-is-a-bridge/contents.lr:tab.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/getting-started/what-is-a-bridge/
msgid "Bridges"
msgstr "Broar"

#: content/relays/getting-started/what-type-of-relays-are-most-needed/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/getting-started/what-type-of-relays-are-most-needed/
msgid ""
"Bridges are the most needed relay type to help users bypass censorship, "
"followed by diverse exit relays and fast guard relays."
msgstr ""
"Broar är den relätyp som behövs mest för att hjälpa användare kringgå "
"censur, följt av geografiskt varierade utgångsreläer och snabba vaktreläer."

#: content/relays/getting-started/what-type-of-relays-are-most-needed/contents.lr:article.longer_title
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/getting-started/what-type-of-relays-are-most-needed/
msgid "What type of relays are most needed?"
msgstr "Vilka typer av reläer behövs mest?"

#: content/relays/getting-started/what-type-of-relays-are-most-needed/contents.lr:article.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/getting-started/what-type-of-relays-are-most-needed/
msgid "Relay types most needed"
msgstr "Relätyper som behövs mest"

#: content/relays/getting-started/what-type-of-relays-are-most-needed/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/getting-started/what-type-of-relays-are-most-needed/
msgid "**Bridges** are currently the most needed relay type."
msgstr "**Broar** är för närvarande den relätyp som behövs mest."

#: content/relays/getting-started/what-type-of-relays-are-most-needed/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/getting-started/what-type-of-relays-are-most-needed/
msgid ""
"**Exit relays** in diverse geographic locations are also important, but they "
"come with the highest legal exposure and risk."
msgstr ""
"**Utgångsreläer** på varierade geografiska platser är också viktiga, men "
"medför störst juridisk exponering och risk."

#: content/relays/getting-started/what-type-of-relays-are-most-needed/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/getting-started/what-type-of-relays-are-most-needed/
msgid "**You should not run an exit relay from your home network.**"
msgstr "**Du bör inte driva ett utgångsrelä från hemnätverket.**"

#: content/relays/getting-started/what-type-of-relays-are-most-needed/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/getting-started/what-type-of-relays-are-most-needed/
msgid "Here are the types of relays that are most needed:"
msgstr "Följande typer av reläer behövs mest:"

#: content/relays/getting-started/what-type-of-relays-are-most-needed/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/getting-started/what-type-of-relays-are-most-needed/
msgid ""
"If you're looking to contribute with minimal legal risk, **fast guard "
"relays** (non-exit relays) are also extremely valuable to the network."
msgstr ""
"Om du vill bidra med minimal juridisk risk är **snabba vaktreläer** (reläer "
"som inte är utgångsreläer) också mycket värdefulla för nätverket."

#: content/relays/getting-started/what-type-of-relays-are-most-needed/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/getting-started/what-type-of-relays-are-most-needed/
msgid ""
"Running a relay is one of the most impactful ways to support the Tor network."
msgstr ""
"Att driva ett relä är ett av de mest verkningsfulla sätten att stödja Tor-"
"nätverket."

#: content/relays/getting-started/what-type-of-relays-are-most-needed/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/getting-started/what-type-of-relays-are-most-needed/
msgid ""
"They help people in censored regions to connect to Tor when the Tor network "
"is blocked."
msgstr ""
"De hjälper människor i censurerade regioner att ansluta till Tor när Tor-"
"nätverket är blockerat."

#: content/relays/getting-started/what-type-of-relays-are-most-needed/contents.lr:tab.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/getting-started/what-type-of-relays-are-most-needed/
msgid "Type of relays"
msgstr "Typer av reläer"

#: content/relays/legal-and-abuse/contents.lr:section.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/legal-and-abuse/
msgid "Legal and Abuse"
msgstr "Juridik och missbruk"

#: content/relays/legal-and-abuse/ddos/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/legal-and-abuse/ddos/
msgid ""
"Because Tor only transports correctly formed TCP streams on a one-for-one "
"basis, it is not an effective tool for launching ordinary DDoS or bandwidth-"
"amplification attacks."
msgstr ""
"Eftersom Tor endast transporterar korrekt utformade TCP-strömmar en-till-en "
"är det inte ett effektivt verktyg för vanliga DDoS- eller "
"bandbreddsförstärkningsattacker."

#: content/relays/legal-and-abuse/ddos/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/legal-and-abuse/ddos/
msgid ""
"Tor does not support the kinds of traffic (like raw UDP packets) that "
"typical DDoS attacks rely on, and it does not amplify outbound bandwidth."
msgstr ""
"Tor stöder inte den typ av trafik, exempelvis råa UDP-paket, som vanliga "
"DDoS-attacker bygger på och förstärker inte utgående bandbredd."

#: content/relays/legal-and-abuse/ddos/contents.lr:article.longer_title
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/legal-and-abuse/ddos/
msgid "Can Tor be used to launch distributed denial-of-service (DDoS) attacks?"
msgstr "Kan Tor användas för distribuerade överbelastningsattacker (DDoS)?"

#: content/relays/legal-and-abuse/ddos/contents.lr:article.title
#: content/relays/legal-and-abuse/ddos/contents.lr:tab.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/legal-and-abuse/ddos/
msgid "DDoS attacks and Tor"
msgstr "DDoS-attacker och Tor"

#: content/relays/legal-and-abuse/ddos/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/legal-and-abuse/ddos/
msgid ""
"(You can't do specialized forms of this attack like SYN flooding either.)"
msgstr ""
"(Du kan inte heller utföra specialiserade varianter av attacken, exempelvis "
"SYN-översvämning.)"

#: content/relays/legal-and-abuse/ddos/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/legal-and-abuse/ddos/
msgid ""
"But because Tor only transports correctly formed TCP streams, not all IP "
"packets, you cannot send UDP packets over Tor."
msgstr ""
"Eftersom Tor bara transporterar korrekt utformade TCP-strömmar och inte alla "
"IP-paket går det inte att skicka UDP-paket via Tor."

#: content/relays/legal-and-abuse/ddos/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/legal-and-abuse/ddos/
msgid ""
"Distributed denial of service (DDoS) attacks typically rely on having a "
"group of thousands of computers all sending floods of traffic to a victim."
msgstr ""
"Distribuerade överbelastningsattacker (DDoS) bygger vanligen på att "
"tusentals datorer samtidigt skickar stora trafikmängder till ett offer."

#: content/relays/legal-and-abuse/ddos/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/legal-and-abuse/ddos/
msgid ""
"Since the goal is to overpower the bandwidth of the victim, they typically "
"send UDP packets since those don't require handshakes or coordination."
msgstr ""
"Eftersom målet är att överbelasta offrets bandbredd skickas vanligtvis UDP-"
"paket, då de inte kräver handskakningar eller samordning."

#: content/relays/legal-and-abuse/ddos/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/legal-and-abuse/ddos/
msgid ""
"So in general, attackers who control enough bandwidth to launch an effective "
"DDoS attack can do it just fine without Tor."
msgstr ""
"Angripare som kontrollerar tillräckligt mycket bandbredd för en effektiv "
"DDoS-attack klarar sig därför i allmänhet lika bra utan Tor."

#: content/relays/legal-and-abuse/ddos/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/legal-and-abuse/ddos/
msgid ""
"So ordinary DDoS attacks are not possible over Tor. Tor also doesn't allow "
"bandwidth amplification attacks against external sites:"
msgstr ""
"Vanliga DDoS-attacker är alltså inte möjliga via Tor. Tor tillåter inte "
"heller bandbreddsförstärkningsattacker mot externa webbplatser:"

#: content/relays/legal-and-abuse/ddos/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/legal-and-abuse/ddos/
msgid ""
"you need to send in a byte for every byte that the Tor network will send to "
"your destination."
msgstr ""
"du måste skicka in en byte för varje byte som Tor-nätverket skickar till "
"destinationen."

#: content/relays/legal-and-abuse/exit-relay-abuse/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/legal-and-abuse/exit-relay-abuse/
msgid ""
"By configuring your relay's exit policy, you control exactly which outbound "
"connections-if any-are allowed."
msgstr ""
"Genom att konfigurera reläets utgångspolicy styr du exakt vilka utgående "
"anslutningar, om några, som tillåts."

#: content/relays/legal-and-abuse/exit-relay-abuse/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/legal-and-abuse/exit-relay-abuse/
msgid ""
"While the Tor Project actively monitors for and removes bad relays, we "
"cannot and do not monitor individual users' activity by design."
msgstr ""
"Tor-projektet övervakar aktivt nätverket och tar bort skadliga reläer, men "
"avsiktligt kan och ska vi inte övervaka enskilda användares aktiviteter."

#: content/relays/legal-and-abuse/exit-relay-abuse/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/legal-and-abuse/exit-relay-abuse/
msgid ""
"You can still contribute bandwidth to Tor without exposing yourself to exit "
"relay abuse complaints."
msgstr ""
"Du kan ändå bidra med bandbredd till Tor utan att utsätta dig för klagomål "
"om missbruk via utgångsreläer."

#: content/relays/legal-and-abuse/exit-relay-abuse/contents.lr:article.longer_title
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/legal-and-abuse/exit-relay-abuse/
msgid ""
"How to contribute bandwidth to Tor safely and what to know about abuse issues"
msgstr ""
"Så bidrar du säkert med bandbredd till Tor och vad du behöver veta om "
"missbruksfrågor"

#: content/relays/legal-and-abuse/exit-relay-abuse/contents.lr:article.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/legal-and-abuse/exit-relay-abuse/
msgid "Running a relay and understanding abuse concerns"
msgstr "Driva ett relä och förstå missbruksrisker"

#: content/relays/legal-and-abuse/exit-relay-abuse/contents.lr:content.content
#: content/relays/running/relay-stability/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/legal-and-abuse/exit-relay-abuse/
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/relay-stability/
msgid ""
"Each Tor relay has an exit policy that specifies what sort of outbound "
"connections are allowed or refused from that relay."
msgstr ""
"Varje Tor-relä har en utgångspolicy som anger vilka typer av utgående "
"anslutningar som tillåts eller nekas från reläet."

#: content/relays/legal-and-abuse/exit-relay-abuse/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/legal-and-abuse/exit-relay-abuse/
msgid ""
"However, by design we cannot see or control what individual users do on the "
"network."
msgstr ""
"Avsiktligt kan vi däremot inte se eller styra vad enskilda användare gör i "
"nätverket."

#: content/relays/legal-and-abuse/exit-relay-abuse/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/legal-and-abuse/exit-relay-abuse/
msgid ""
"If there are any resources that your computer can't reach (for example, you "
"are behind a restrictive firewall or content filter), please explicitly "
"reject them in your exit policy  otherwise Tor users will be impacted too."
msgstr ""
"Om det finns resurser som din dator inte kan nå, exempelvis på grund av en "
"restriktiv brandvägg eller ett innehållsfilter, ska du uttryckligen neka dem "
"i utgångspolicyn. Annars påverkas även Tor-användare."

#: content/relays/legal-and-abuse/exit-relay-abuse/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/legal-and-abuse/exit-relay-abuse/
msgid ""
"If you do allow any exit connections, make sure name resolution works (that "
"is, your computer can resolve Internet addresses correctly)."
msgstr ""
"Om du tillåter några utgångsanslutningar måste du kontrollera att "
"namnuppslagningen fungerar, det vill säga att datorn kan slå upp "
"internetadresser korrekt."

#: content/relays/legal-and-abuse/exit-relay-abuse/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/legal-and-abuse/exit-relay-abuse/
msgid ""
"If you want to avoid most if not all abuse potential, set it to \"reject "
"&#42;:&#42;\"."
msgstr ""
"Om du vill undvika nästan all risk för missbruk anger du \"reject "
"&#42;:&#42;\"."

#: content/relays/legal-and-abuse/exit-relay-abuse/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/legal-and-abuse/exit-relay-abuse/
msgid ""
"In parallel, Tor has a dedicated Network Health team investigating bad relay "
"behavior and removing malicious relays from the network."
msgstr ""
"Samtidigt har Tor ett särskilt nätverkshälsoteam som undersöker skadligt "
"reläbeteende och tar bort illvilliga reläer från nätverket."

#: content/relays/legal-and-abuse/exit-relay-abuse/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/legal-and-abuse/exit-relay-abuse/
msgid ""
"Learn more about [our users and Tor's beneficial use cases](https://"
"community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/)."
msgstr ""
"Läs mer om [våra användare och Tors samhällsnyttiga användningsområden]"
"(https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/)."

#: content/relays/legal-and-abuse/exit-relay-abuse/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/legal-and-abuse/exit-relay-abuse/
msgid ""
"Read the Support entry on issues you might encounter if you use the default "
"exit policy, and then read Mike Perry's [tips for running an exit node with "
"minimal harassment](https://blog.torproject.org/blog/tips-running-exit-node)."
msgstr ""
"Läs supportavsnittet om problem du kan stöta på med standardpolicyn för "
"utgångar och sedan Mike Perrys [tips för att driva ett utgångsrelä med "
"minsta möjliga besvär](https://blog.torproject.org/blog/tips-running-exit-"
"node)."

#: content/relays/legal-and-abuse/exit-relay-abuse/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/legal-and-abuse/exit-relay-abuse/
msgid ""
"The default exit policy allows access to many popular services (e.g. web "
"browsing), but restricts some due to abuse potential (e.g. mail) and some "
"since the Tor network can't handle the load (e.g. default file-sharing "
"ports)."
msgstr ""
"Standardpolicyn för utgångar tillåter åtkomst till många populära tjänster, "
"exempelvis webbsurfning, men begränsar vissa på grund av missbruksrisken, "
"exempelvis e-post, och andra eftersom Tor-nätverket inte klarar "
"belastningen, exempelvis standardportar för fildelning."

#: content/relays/legal-and-abuse/exit-relay-abuse/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/legal-and-abuse/exit-relay-abuse/
msgid ""
"The exit policies are propagated to Tor clients via the directory, so "
"clients will automatically avoid picking exit relays that would refuse to "
"exit to their intended destination."
msgstr ""
"Utgångspolicyerna distribueras till Tor-klienterna via katalogen, så "
"klienterna undviker automatiskt utgångsreläer som skulle neka anslutning "
"till den avsedda destinationen."

#: content/relays/legal-and-abuse/exit-relay-abuse/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/legal-and-abuse/exit-relay-abuse/
msgid ""
"This design overwhelmingly enables beneficial uses-such as for human rights "
"defenders, journalists, domestic-violence survivors, whistleblowers, and "
"even law-enforcement officers."
msgstr ""
"Den här konstruktionen möjliggör i överväldigande grad samhällsnyttig "
"användning, bland annat för människorättsförsvarare, journalister, personer "
"utsatta för våld i nära relationer, visselblåsare och även brottsbekämpande "
"myndigheter."

#: content/relays/legal-and-abuse/exit-relay-abuse/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/legal-and-abuse/exit-relay-abuse/
msgid ""
"This setting means that your relay will be used for relaying traffic inside "
"the Tor network, but not for connections to external websites or other "
"services."
msgstr ""
"Inställningen innebär att reläet används för att vidarebefordra trafik inom "
"Tor-nätverket, men inte för anslutningar till externa webbplatser eller "
"andra tjänster."

#: content/relays/legal-and-abuse/exit-relay-abuse/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/legal-and-abuse/exit-relay-abuse/
msgid ""
"This way each relay can decide the services, hosts, and networks it wants to "
"allow connections to, based on abuse potential and its own situation."
msgstr ""
"På så sätt kan varje relä, utifrån missbruksrisken och sin egen situation, "
"bestämma vilka tjänster, värdar och nätverk det vill tillåta anslutningar "
"till."

#: content/relays/legal-and-abuse/exit-relay-abuse/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/legal-and-abuse/exit-relay-abuse/
msgid "You can change your exit policy by editing your torrc file."
msgstr "Du kan ändra utgångspolicyn genom att redigera filen torrc."

#: content/relays/legal-and-abuse/exit-relay-abuse/contents.lr:tab.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/legal-and-abuse/exit-relay-abuse/
msgid "Exit policies"
msgstr "Utgångspolicyer"

#: content/relays/legal-and-abuse/exit-relay-expectations/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/legal-and-abuse/exit-relay-expectations/
msgid ""
"Because your IP address appears as the source of Tor users' traffic, you may "
"receive abuse complaints, DMCA notices, or face service blocks."
msgstr ""
"Eftersom din IP-adress visas som källa för Tor-användarnas trafik kan du få "
"klagomål om missbruk, DMCA-meddelanden eller bli blockerad av tjänster."

#: content/relays/legal-and-abuse/exit-relay-expectations/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/legal-and-abuse/exit-relay-expectations/
msgid ""
"Operating a Tor exit relay is one of the most meaningful ways to support the "
"network, but it also brings public visibility."
msgstr ""
"Att driva ett Tor-utgångsrelä är ett av de mest betydelsefulla sätten att "
"stödja nätverket, men det medför också offentlig synlighet."

#: content/relays/legal-and-abuse/exit-relay-expectations/contents.lr:article.longer_title
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/legal-and-abuse/exit-relay-expectations/
msgid ""
"Understanding potential complaints and best practices for operating an exit "
"relay"
msgstr "Förstå möjliga klagomål och bästa praxis för att driva ett utgångsrelä"

#: content/relays/legal-and-abuse/exit-relay-expectations/contents.lr:article.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/legal-and-abuse/exit-relay-expectations/
msgid "What to expect when running a Tor exit relay"
msgstr "Vad du kan förvänta dig när du driver ett Tor-utgångsrelä"

#: content/relays/legal-and-abuse/exit-relay-expectations/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/legal-and-abuse/exit-relay-expectations/
msgid ""
"(If you have a spare IP not used for other activities, you might consider "
"running your Tor relay on it.)"
msgstr ""
"(Om du har en extra IP-adress som inte används till något annat kan du "
"överväga att köra Tor-reläet på den.)"

#: content/relays/legal-and-abuse/exit-relay-expectations/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/legal-and-abuse/exit-relay-expectations/
msgid "Abuse complaints may come in a variety of forms. For example:"
msgstr "Klagomål om missbruk kan förekomma i många former. Exempel:"

#: content/relays/legal-and-abuse/exit-relay-expectations/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/legal-and-abuse/exit-relay-expectations/
msgid ""
"For a complete set of template responses to different abuse complaint types, "
"see the [collection of templates](https://community.torproject.org/relay/"
"community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/)."
msgstr ""
"En fullständig uppsättning svarsmallar för olika slags klagomål finns i "
"[samlingen med mallar](https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-"
"resources/tor-abuse-templates/)."

#: content/relays/legal-and-abuse/exit-relay-expectations/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/legal-and-abuse/exit-relay-expectations/
msgid ""
"If you run a Tor relay that allows exit connections (such as the default "
"exit policy), it's probably safe to say that you will eventually hear from "
"somebody."
msgstr ""
"Om du driver ett Tor-relä som tillåter utgångsanslutningar, såsom "
"standardpolicyn, är det sannolikt att någon förr eller senare kontaktar dig."

#: content/relays/legal-and-abuse/exit-relay-expectations/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/legal-and-abuse/exit-relay-expectations/
msgid ""
"In general, it's advisable not to use your home internet connection to "
"provide a Tor relay."
msgstr ""
"I allmänhet rekommenderas du att inte använda internetanslutningen hemma för "
"att driva ett Tor-relä."

#: content/relays/legal-and-abuse/exit-relay-expectations/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/legal-and-abuse/exit-relay-expectations/
msgid ""
"Some hosting providers are friendlier than others when it comes to Tor "
"exits. For a listing see the [good and bad ISPs page](https://"
"community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/good-bad-isps/)."
msgstr ""
"Vissa webbhotellsleverantörer är mer välvilligt inställda till Tor-utgångar "
"än andra. Se förteckningen på sidan om [bra och dåliga internetleverantörer]"
"(https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/good-bad-isps/)."

#: content/relays/legal-and-abuse/exit-relay-expectations/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/legal-and-abuse/exit-relay-expectations/
msgid ""
"Somebody connects to Hotmail, and sends a ransom note to a company. The FBI "
"sends you a polite email, you explain that you run a Tor relay, and they say "
"\"oh well\" and leave you alone. [Port 80]"
msgstr ""
"Någon ansluter till Hotmail och skickar ett utpressningsbrev till ett "
"företag. FBI skickar ett artigt e-postmeddelande, du förklarar att du driver "
"ett Tor-relä och de säger ungefär ”jaha” och lämnar dig i fred. [Port 80]"

#: content/relays/legal-and-abuse/exit-relay-expectations/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/legal-and-abuse/exit-relay-expectations/
msgid ""
"Somebody connects to an IRC network and makes a nuisance of himself. Your "
"ISP gets polite mail about how your computer has been compromised; and/or "
"your computer gets DDoSed. [Port 6667]"
msgstr ""
"Någon ansluter till ett IRC-nätverk och stör. Din internetleverantör får ett "
"artigt meddelande om att datorn har utsatts för intrång och/eller så utsätts "
"datorn för en DDoS-attack. [Port 6667]"

#: content/relays/legal-and-abuse/exit-relay-expectations/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/legal-and-abuse/exit-relay-expectations/
msgid ""
"Somebody tries to get you shut down by using Tor to connect to Google groups "
"and post spam to Usenet, and then sends an angry mail to your ISP about how "
"you're destroying the world. [Port 80]"
msgstr ""
"Någon försöker få ditt relä avstängt genom att använda Tor för att ansluta "
"till Google Grupper och skicka skräppost till Usenet, och skickar sedan ett "
"argt meddelande till internetleverantören om hur du förstör världen. [Port "
"80]"

#: content/relays/legal-and-abuse/exit-relay-expectations/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/legal-and-abuse/exit-relay-expectations/
msgid ""
"Somebody uses Tor to download a Vin Diesel movie, and your ISP gets a DMCA "
"takedown notice. See EFF's [Tor DMCA Response Template](https://"
"community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/tor-"
"dmca-response/), which explains why your ISP can probably ignore the notice "
"without any liability."
msgstr ""
"Någon använder Tor för att hämta en film med Vin Diesel och din "
"internetleverantör får ett DMCA-meddelande om nedtagning. Se EFF:s "
"[svarsmall för Tor och DMCA](https://community.torproject.org/relay/"
"community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/tor-dmca-response/), som förklarar "
"varför internetleverantören sannolikt kan ignorera meddelandet utan ansvar."

#: content/relays/legal-and-abuse/exit-relay-expectations/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/legal-and-abuse/exit-relay-expectations/
msgid ""
"This might happen regardless of your exit policy, because some groups don't "
"seem to know or care that Tor has exit policies."
msgstr ""
"Det kan inträffa oavsett utgångspolicy, eftersom vissa grupper inte verkar "
"känna till eller bry sig om att Tor har utgångspolicyer."

#: content/relays/legal-and-abuse/exit-relay-expectations/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/legal-and-abuse/exit-relay-expectations/
msgid ""
"You can also proactively reduce the amount of abuse you get by following "
"[these tips for running an exit node with minimal harassment](https://"
"blog.torproject.org/blog/tips-running-exit-node) and [running a reduced exit "
"policy](https://gitlab.torproject.org/legacy/trac/-/wikis/doc/"
"ReducedExitPolicy)."
msgstr ""
"Du kan också förebyggande minska mängden missbruk genom att följa [tipsen "
"för att driva ett utgångsrelä med minsta möjliga besvär](https://"
"blog.torproject.org/blog/tips-running-exit-node) och [använda en begränsad "
"utgångspolicy](https://gitlab.torproject.org/legacy/trac/-/wikis/doc/"
"ReducedExitPolicy)."

#: content/relays/legal-and-abuse/exit-relay-expectations/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/legal-and-abuse/exit-relay-expectations/
msgid ""
"You might also find that your Tor relay's IP is blocked from accessing some "
"Internet sites/services."
msgstr ""
"Du kan även upptäcka att Tor-reläets IP-adress är blockerad från vissa "
"webbplatser eller tjänster på internet."

#: content/relays/legal-and-abuse/exit-relay-expectations/contents.lr:tab.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/legal-and-abuse/exit-relay-expectations/
msgid "Expectations"
msgstr "Förväntningar"

#: content/relays/legal-and-abuse/legal-support/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/legal-and-abuse/legal-support/
msgid ""
"If you've received an abuse complaint, a subpoena, or have other legal "
"concerns related to Tor traffic, please consult the external legal resources "
"linked below."
msgstr ""
"Om du har fått ett klagomål om missbruk, en stämning eller har andra "
"juridiska frågor om Tor-trafik bör du vända dig till de externa juridiska "
"resurser som länkas nedan."

#: content/relays/legal-and-abuse/legal-support/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/legal-and-abuse/legal-support/
msgid "Tor Project developers cannot provide legal advice."
msgstr "Tor-projektets utvecklare kan inte ge juridisk rådgivning."

#: content/relays/legal-and-abuse/legal-support/contents.lr:article.longer_title
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/legal-and-abuse/legal-support/
msgid ""
"Where to get legal help if you receive complaints about Tor traffic or "
"alleged abuse"
msgstr ""
"Här får du juridisk hjälp om du får klagomål om Tor-trafik eller påstått "
"missbruk"

#: content/relays/legal-and-abuse/legal-support/contents.lr:article.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/legal-and-abuse/legal-support/
msgid "I have legal questions about Tor abuse"
msgstr "Jag har juridiska frågor om missbruk via Tor"

#: content/relays/legal-and-abuse/legal-support/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/legal-and-abuse/legal-support/
msgid ""
"If you need to check if a certain IP address was acting as a Tor exit node "
"at a certain date and time, you can use the [ExoneraTor tool](https://"
"exonerator.torproject.org/) to query the historic Tor relay lists and get an "
"answer."
msgstr ""
"Med verktyget [ExoneraTor](https://exonerator.torproject.org/) kan du "
"kontrollera om en viss IP-adress fungerade som Tor-utgångsrelä vid ett visst "
"datum och klockslag genom att söka i historiska förteckningar över Tor-"
"reläer."

#: content/relays/legal-and-abuse/legal-support/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/legal-and-abuse/legal-support/
msgid ""
"Please read the [legal FAQ written by EFF lawyers](https://"
"community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/), and "
"contact EFF directly if you have any further legal questions."
msgstr ""
"Läs den [juridiska FAQ som skrivits av EFF:s jurister](https://"
"community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/) och "
"kontakta EFF direkt om du har fler juridiska frågor."

#: content/relays/legal-and-abuse/legal-support/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/legal-and-abuse/legal-support/
msgid ""
"There's a growing [legal directory](https://blog.torproject.org/blog/start-"
"tor-legal-support-directory) of people who may be able to help you."
msgstr ""
"Det finns en växande [juridisk katalog](https://blog.torproject.org/blog/"
"start-tor-legal-support-directory) med personer som kanske kan hjälpa dig."

#: content/relays/legal-and-abuse/legal-support/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/legal-and-abuse/legal-support/
msgid ""
"We can answer technical questions, but we're not the ones to talk to about "
"legal questions or concerns."
msgstr ""
"Vi kan besvara tekniska frågor, men vi är inte rätt instans för juridiska "
"frågor eller farhågor."

#: content/relays/legal-and-abuse/legal-support/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/legal-and-abuse/legal-support/
msgid "We're only the developers."
msgstr "Vi är bara utvecklarna."

#: content/relays/legal-and-abuse/legal-support/contents.lr:tab.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/legal-and-abuse/legal-support/
msgid "Legal questions"
msgstr "Juridiska frågor"

#: content/relays/legal-and-abuse/spammers-and-tor/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/legal-and-abuse/spammers-and-tor/
msgid ""
"Because almost all Tor exit relays block outgoing mail ports by default, Tor "
"is not a practical way to send spam."
msgstr ""
"Eftersom nästan alla Tor-utgångsreläer som standard blockerar utgående e-"
"postportar är Tor inte ett praktiskt sätt att skicka skräppost."

#: content/relays/legal-and-abuse/spammers-and-tor/contents.lr:article.longer_title
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/legal-and-abuse/spammers-and-tor/
msgid "Does Tor make it easier to send spam or control botnets?"
msgstr "Gör Tor det enklare att skicka skräppost eller styra botnät?"

#: content/relays/legal-and-abuse/spammers-and-tor/contents.lr:article.title
#: content/relays/legal-and-abuse/spammers-and-tor/contents.lr:tab.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/legal-and-abuse/spammers-and-tor/
msgid "Spammers and Tor"
msgstr "Spammare och Tor"

#: content/relays/legal-and-abuse/spammers-and-tor/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/legal-and-abuse/spammers-and-tor/
msgid ""
"Also, remember that many of their more subtle communication mechanisms (like "
"spoofed UDP packets) can't be used over Tor, because it only transports "
"correctly-formed TCP connections."
msgstr ""
"Kom också ihåg att många av deras mer subtila kommunikationsmetoder, "
"exempelvis förfalskade UDP-paket, inte kan användas via Tor eftersom endast "
"korrekt utformade TCP-anslutningar transporteras."

#: content/relays/legal-and-abuse/spammers-and-tor/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/legal-and-abuse/spammers-and-tor/
msgid ""
"First of all, the default Tor exit policy rejects all outgoing port 25 "
"(SMTP) traffic."
msgstr ""
"För det första nekar standardpolicyn för Tor-utgångar all utgående trafik på "
"port 25 (SMTP)."

#: content/relays/legal-and-abuse/spammers-and-tor/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/legal-and-abuse/spammers-and-tor/
msgid ""
"In short, Tor isn't useful for spamming, because nearly all Tor relays "
"refuse to deliver the mail."
msgstr ""
"Kort sagt är Tor inte användbart för skräppost, eftersom nästan alla Tor-"
"reläer vägrar leverera e-post."

#: content/relays/legal-and-abuse/spammers-and-tor/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/legal-and-abuse/spammers-and-tor/
msgid ""
"It's possible that some relay operators will enable port 25 on their "
"particular exit node, in which case that computer will allow outgoing mails; "
"but that individual could just set up an open mail relay too, independent of "
"Tor."
msgstr ""
"Enskilda reläoperatörer kan aktivera port 25 på sitt utgångsrelä, varvid "
"datorn tillåter utgående e-post. Samma person skulle dock lika gärna kunna "
"konfigurera ett öppet e-postrelä oberoende av Tor."

#: content/relays/legal-and-abuse/spammers-and-tor/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/legal-and-abuse/spammers-and-tor/
msgid "Of course, it's not all about delivering the mail."
msgstr "Det handlar förstås inte enbart om att leverera e-post."

#: content/relays/legal-and-abuse/spammers-and-tor/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/legal-and-abuse/spammers-and-tor/
msgid "So sending spam mail through Tor isn't going to work by default."
msgstr "Att skicka skräppost via Tor fungerar alltså inte som standard."

#: content/relays/legal-and-abuse/spammers-and-tor/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/legal-and-abuse/spammers-and-tor/
msgid ""
"Spammers can use Tor to connect to open HTTP proxies (and from there to SMTP "
"servers); to connect to badly written mail-sending CGI scripts; and to "
"control their botnets — that is, to covertly communicate with armies of "
"compromised computers that deliver the spam."
msgstr ""
"Spammare kan använda Tor för att ansluta till öppna HTTP-proxyservrar och "
"därifrån till SMTP-servrar, till dåligt skrivna CGI-skript för att skicka e-"
"post och för att styra sina botnät, det vill säga kommunicera i hemlighet "
"med stora mängder komprometterade datorer som levererar skräpposten."

#: content/relays/legal-and-abuse/spammers-and-tor/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/legal-and-abuse/spammers-and-tor/
msgid ""
"This is a shame, but notice that spammers are already doing great without "
"Tor."
msgstr "Det är beklagligt, men spammare klarar sig redan utmärkt utan Tor."

#: content/relays/performance/bandwidth-limits/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/bandwidth-limits/
msgid "These options also apply to bridges."
msgstr "Alternativen gäller även för broar."

#: content/relays/performance/bandwidth-limits/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/bandwidth-limits/
msgid ""
"Tor relays can be configured to cap the total amount of data they send and "
"receive over a set period using options in torrc."
msgstr ""
"Tor-reläer kan konfigureras så att den totala mängden data som skickas och "
"tas emot under en viss period begränsas med alternativ i torrc."

#: content/relays/performance/bandwidth-limits/contents.lr:article.longer_title
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/bandwidth-limits/
msgid "How to limit the total amount of bandwidth your Tor relay uses"
msgstr "Så begränsar du den totala bandbredd som Tor-reläet använder"

#: content/relays/performance/bandwidth-limits/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/bandwidth-limits/
msgid ""
"Example: Let's say you want to allow 50 GB of traffic every day in each "
"direction and the accounting should reset at noon each day:"
msgstr ""
"Exempel: Anta att du vill tillåta 50 GB trafik per dag i vardera riktningen "
"och att redovisningen ska nollställas klockan 12 varje dag:"

#: content/relays/performance/bandwidth-limits/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/bandwidth-limits/
msgid ""
"For example, if you have 50 GB to offer each way, you might set your "
"RelayBandwidthRate to 1000 KBytes: this way your relay will always be useful "
"for at least half of each day."
msgstr ""
"Om du exempelvis kan erbjuda 50 GB i vardera riktningen kan du ange "
"RelayBandwidthRate till 1000 KBytes. Då är reläet alltid användbart under "
"minst halva dagen."

#: content/relays/performance/bandwidth-limits/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/bandwidth-limits/
msgid ""
"If you have only a small amount of bandwidth to donate compared to your "
"connection speed, we recommend you use daily accounting, so you don't end up "
"using your entire monthly quota in the first day."
msgstr ""
"Om du bara kan donera en liten mängd bandbredd i förhållande till "
"anslutningens hastighet rekommenderar vi daglig redovisning, så att hela "
"månadskvoten inte förbrukas den första dagen."

#: content/relays/performance/bandwidth-limits/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/bandwidth-limits/
msgid ""
"It will keep track of how quickly it used its quota in the last period, and "
"choose a random point in the new interval to wake up."
msgstr ""
"Tor registrerar hur snabbt kvoten användes under föregående period och "
"väljer en slumpmässig tidpunkt i det nya intervallet för att vakna."

#: content/relays/performance/bandwidth-limits/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/bandwidth-limits/
msgid ""
"Just divide your monthly amount by 30. You might also consider rate limiting "
"to spread your usefulness over more of the day: if you want to offer X GB in "
"each direction, you could set your RelayBandwidthRate to 20*X KBytes."
msgstr ""
"Dela bara månadsmängden med 30. Du kan också överväga en hastighetsgräns för "
"att fördela nyttan över en större del av dagen. Om du vill erbjuda X GB i "
"vardera riktningen kan du ange RelayBandwidthRate till 20*X KBytes."

#: content/relays/performance/bandwidth-limits/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/bandwidth-limits/
msgid ""
"Note that your relay won't wake up exactly at the beginning of each "
"accounting period."
msgstr ""
"Observera att reläet inte vaknar exakt i början av varje redovisningsperiod."

#: content/relays/performance/bandwidth-limits/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/bandwidth-limits/
msgid ""
"RelayBandwidthBurst 5000 KBytes # allow higher bursts but maintain average"
msgstr ""
"RelayBandwidthBurst 5000 KBytes # tillåt högre toppar men bibehåll "
"genomsnittet"

#: content/relays/performance/bandwidth-limits/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/bandwidth-limits/
msgid ""
"The accounting options in the torrc file allow you to specify the maximum "
"amount of bytes your relay uses for a time period."
msgstr ""
"Med redovisningsalternativen i torrc-filen kan du ange den största mängd "
"byte som reläet använder under en tidsperiod."

#: content/relays/performance/bandwidth-limits/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/bandwidth-limits/
msgid ""
"This specifies the maximum amount of data your relay will send during an "
"accounting period, and the maximum amount of data your relay will receive "
"during an accounting period."
msgstr ""
"Det anger den största mängd data som reläet skickar under en "
"redovisningsperiod och den största mängd data som reläet tar emot under "
"perioden."

#: content/relays/performance/bandwidth-limits/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/bandwidth-limits/
msgid ""
"This specifies when the accounting should reset. For instance, to setup a "
"total amount of bytes served for a week (that resets every Wednesday at "
"10:00am), you would use:"
msgstr ""
"Det anger när redovisningen ska nollställas. Om du till exempel vill ange en "
"total datamängd per vecka som nollställs varje onsdag klockan 10 använder du:"

#: content/relays/performance/bandwidth-limits/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/bandwidth-limits/
msgid ""
"This way we avoid having hundreds of relays working at the beginning of each "
"month but none still up by the end."
msgstr ""
"På så sätt undviker vi att hundratals reläer är aktiva i början av månaden "
"men att inga återstår i slutet."

#: content/relays/performance/bandwidth-limits/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/bandwidth-limits/
msgid ""
"When the accounting period resets (from AccountingStart), then the counters "
"for AccountingMax are reset to 0."
msgstr ""
"När redovisningsperioden nollställs enligt AccountingStart återställs även "
"räknarna för AccountingMax till 0."

#: content/relays/performance/bandwidth-shaping/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/bandwidth-shaping/
msgid "Tor relays can limit or smooth out bandwidth usage."
msgstr "Tor-reläer kan begränsa eller jämna ut bandbreddsanvändningen."

#: content/relays/performance/bandwidth-shaping/contents.lr:article.longer_title
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/bandwidth-shaping/
msgid "How to control and shape bandwidth usage on your Tor relay"
msgstr "Så styr och formar du bandbreddsanvändningen för Tor-reläet"

#: content/relays/performance/bandwidth-shaping/contents.lr:article.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/bandwidth-shaping/
msgid "Bandwidth shaping options"
msgstr "Alternativ för bandbreddsformning"

#: content/relays/performance/bandwidth-shaping/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/bandwidth-shaping/
msgid ""
"**BandwidthBurst** is a pool of bytes used to fulfill requests during short "
"periods of traffic above BandwidthRate but still keeps the average over a "
"long period to BandwidthRate."
msgstr ""
"**BandwidthBurst** är en pott med byte som används för att tillgodose "
"begäranden under korta perioder med trafik över BandwidthRate, samtidigt som "
"det långsiktiga genomsnittet hålls på BandwidthRate."

#: content/relays/performance/bandwidth-shaping/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/bandwidth-shaping/
msgid ""
"**BandwidthRate** is the maximum long-term bandwidth allowed (bytes per "
"second)."
msgstr ""
"**BandwidthRate** är den högsta tillåtna långsiktiga bandbredden (byte per "
"sekund)."

#: content/relays/performance/bandwidth-shaping/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/bandwidth-shaping/
msgid ""
"A [script to do this](https://gitlab.torproject.org/tpo/core/tor/-/raw/"
"maint-0.3.5/contrib/operator-tools/linux-tor-prio.sh) can be found in the "
"Tor source distribution's contrib directory."
msgstr ""
"Ett [skript för detta](https://gitlab.torproject.org/tpo/core/tor/-/raw/"
"maint-0.3.5/contrib/operator-tools/linux-tor-prio.sh) finns i katalogen "
"contrib i Tors källdistribution."

#: content/relays/performance/bandwidth-shaping/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/bandwidth-shaping/
msgid ""
"A low Rate but a high Burst enforces a long-term average while still "
"allowing more traffic during peak times if the average hasn't been reached "
"lately."
msgstr ""
"Ett lågt Rate-värde men ett högt Burst-värde tvingar fram ett långsiktigt "
"genomsnitt men tillåter samtidigt mer trafik vid belastningstoppar om "
"genomsnittet inte nyligen har uppnåtts."

#: content/relays/performance/bandwidth-shaping/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/bandwidth-shaping/
msgid ""
"Additionally, there are hibernation options where you can tell Tor to only "
"serve a certain amount of bandwidth per time period (such as 100 GB per "
"month). These are covered in the [hibernation entry](../bandwidth-limits/)."
msgstr ""
"Dessutom finns vilolägesalternativ som låter dig ange att Tor bara ska "
"tillhandahålla en viss mängd bandbredd per tidsperiod, exempelvis 100 GB per "
"månad. Dessa beskrivs i [avsnittet om viloläge](../bandwidth-limits/)."

#: content/relays/performance/bandwidth-shaping/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/bandwidth-shaping/
msgid ""
"For example, if you choose \"BandwidthBurst 500 KBytes\" and also use that "
"for your BandwidthRate, then you will never use more than 500 kilobytes per "
"second; but if you choose a higher BandwidthBurst (like 5 MBytes), it will "
"allow more bytes through until the pool is empty."
msgstr ""
"Om du till exempel väljer ”BandwidthBurst 500 KBytes” och även använder det "
"värdet för BandwidthRate används aldrig mer än 500 kilobyte per sekund. Om "
"du väljer ett högre BandwidthBurst, exempelvis 5 MBytes, släpps fler byte "
"igenom tills potten är tom."

#: content/relays/performance/bandwidth-shaping/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/bandwidth-shaping/
msgid ""
"For example, you might want to choose \"BandwidthRate 10 MBytes\" for 10 "
"megabytes per second (a fast connection), or \"BandwidthRate 500 KBytes\" "
"for 500 kilobytes per second (a decent cable connection)."
msgstr ""
"Du kan exempelvis välja ”BandwidthRate 10 MBytes” för 10 megabyte per "
"sekund, vilket motsvarar en snabb anslutning, eller ”BandwidthRate 500 "
"KBytes” för 500 kilobyte per sekund, vilket motsvarar en hygglig "
"kabelanslutning."

#: content/relays/performance/bandwidth-shaping/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/bandwidth-shaping/
msgid ""
"If you have an asymmetric connection (upload less than download) such as a "
"cable modem, you should set BandwidthRate to less than your smaller "
"bandwidth (Usually that's the upload bandwidth)."
msgstr ""
"Om anslutningen är asymmetrisk, med lägre uppladdnings- än "
"hämtningshastighet, exempelvis via kabelmodem, ska BandwidthRate anges lägre "
"än den lägre bandbredden, vanligen uppladdningsbandbredden."

#: content/relays/performance/bandwidth-shaping/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/bandwidth-shaping/
msgid ""
"Linux-based Tor nodes have another option at their disposal: they can "
"prioritize Tor traffic below other traffic on their machine, so that their "
"own personal traffic is not impacted by Tor load."
msgstr ""
"Linux-baserade Tor-noder har ytterligare ett alternativ: de kan prioritera "
"Tor-trafik lägre än annan trafik på datorn, så att den egna trafiken inte "
"påverkas av Tor-belastningen."

#: content/relays/performance/bandwidth-shaping/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/bandwidth-shaping/
msgid "Note that BandwidthRate and BandwidthBurst are in **Bytes**, not Bits."
msgstr ""
"Observera att BandwidthRate och BandwidthBurst anges i **byte**, inte bit."

#: content/relays/performance/bandwidth-shaping/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/bandwidth-shaping/
msgid ""
"Otherwise, you could drop many packets during periods of maximum bandwidth "
"usage - you may need to experiment with which values make your connection "
"comfortable."
msgstr ""
"Annars kan många paket tappas under perioder med maximal "
"bandbreddsanvändning. Du kan behöva prova dig fram till värden som fungerar "
"bra för anslutningen."

#: content/relays/performance/bandwidth-shaping/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/bandwidth-shaping/
msgid "The minimum BandwidthRate setting is 75 kilobytes per second."
msgstr ""
"Det lägsta tillåtna värdet för BandwidthRate är 75 kilobyte per sekund."

#: content/relays/performance/bandwidth-shaping/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/bandwidth-shaping/
msgid "Then set BandwidthBurst to the same as BandwidthRate."
msgstr "Ange sedan samma värde för BandwidthBurst som för BandwidthRate."

#: content/relays/performance/bandwidth-shaping/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/bandwidth-shaping/
msgid "There are two options you can add to your torrc file:"
msgstr "Det finns två alternativ som du kan lägga till i torrc-filen:"

#: content/relays/performance/bandwidth-shaping/contents.lr:tab.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/bandwidth-shaping/
msgid "Bandwidth shaping"
msgstr "Bandbreddsformning"

#: content/relays/performance/contents.lr:section.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/
msgid "Relay performance"
msgstr "Reläprestanda"

#: content/relays/performance/hibernation/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/hibernation/
msgid ""
"If you run a relay and a client in the same Tor process, and have some "
"bandwidth limits, once your relay hits its limit and goes into hibernation, "
"your client connections stop too."
msgstr ""
"Om du kör ett relä och en klient i samma Tor-process och har "
"bandbreddsgränser slutar även klientanslutningarna när reläet når gränsen "
"och går i viloläge."

#: content/relays/performance/hibernation/contents.lr:article.longer_title
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/hibernation/
msgid "Why limiting bandwidth on your Tor relay can stop you from browsing"
msgstr "Därför kan en bandbreddsgräns för Tor-reläet hindra dig från att surfa"

#: content/relays/performance/hibernation/contents.lr:article.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/hibernation/
msgid "Bandwidth limits affecting browsing"
msgstr "Bandbreddsgränser påverkar surfningen"

#: content/relays/performance/hibernation/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/hibernation/
msgid "Bandwidth soft limit reached; commencing hibernation."
msgstr "Den mjuka bandbreddsgränsen har nåtts. Viloläge inleds."

#: content/relays/performance/hibernation/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/hibernation/
msgid ""
"Create a new client torrc file from the torrc.sample and ensure it uses a "
"different log file from the relay."
msgstr ""
"Skapa en ny torrc-fil för klienten från torrc.sample och se till att den "
"använder en annan loggfil än reläet."

#: content/relays/performance/hibernation/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/hibernation/
msgid ""
"In Linux/BSD/macOS, changing the startup scripts to `Tor.client` and "
"`Tor.relay` may make separation of configs easier."
msgstr ""
"I Linux, BSD och macOS kan det bli enklare att separera konfigurationerna om "
"startskripten ändras till `Tor.client` och `Tor.relay`."

#: content/relays/performance/hibernation/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/hibernation/
msgid "In the relay Tor torrc file, simply set the SocksPort to 0."
msgstr "Ange helt enkelt SocksPort till 0 i reläets torrc-fil."

#: content/relays/performance/hibernation/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/hibernation/
msgid ""
"Modify the Tor client and relay startup scripts to include `-f /path/to/"
"correct/torrc`."
msgstr ""
"Ändra startskripten för Tor-klienten och reläet så att de innehåller `-f /"
"path/to/correct/torrc`."

#: content/relays/performance/hibernation/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/hibernation/
msgid "No new connections will be accepted"
msgstr "Inga nya anslutningar tas emot"

#: content/relays/performance/hibernation/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/hibernation/
msgid "One naming convention may be torrc.client and torrc.relay."
msgstr "En möjlig namnkonvention är torrc.client och torrc.relay."

#: content/relays/performance/hibernation/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/hibernation/
msgid ""
"One way to do this (if you are starting from a working relay setup) is as "
"follows:"
msgstr ""
"Ett sätt att göra detta, om du utgår från en fungerande reläkonfiguration, "
"är följande:"

#: content/relays/performance/hibernation/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/hibernation/
msgid ""
"The solution is to run two Tor processes - one relay and one client, each "
"with its own config."
msgstr ""
"Lösningen är att köra två Tor-processer, ett relä och en klient, med var sin "
"konfiguration."

#: content/relays/performance/hibernation/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/hibernation/
msgid ""
"Thus you may find that you are unable to browse as soon as your Tor goes "
"into hibernation, signaled by this entry in the log:"
msgstr ""
"Du kan därför upptäcka att det inte längre går att surfa när Tor går i "
"viloläge, vilket anges med följande post i loggen:"

#: content/relays/performance/hibernation/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/hibernation/
msgid ""
"When you run a Tor relay and a Tor client in the same process, the "
"parameters set in `AccountingMax` and `BandwidthRate` apply to **both** "
"relay and client functions."
msgstr ""
"När du kör ett Tor-relä och en Tor-klient i samma process gäller "
"parametrarna `AccountingMax` och `BandwidthRate` för **både** relä- och "
"klientfunktionerna."

#: content/relays/performance/low-traffic/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/low-traffic/
msgid "New relays ramp up gradually as Bandwidth Authorities measure them."
msgstr ""
"Nya reläer ökar trafiken gradvis medan bandbreddsauktoriteterna mäter dem."

#: content/relays/performance/low-traffic/contents.lr:article.longer_title
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/low-traffic/
msgid "Why isn't my relay getting much traffic?"
msgstr "Varför får mitt relä så lite trafik?"

#: content/relays/performance/low-traffic/contents.lr:article.title
#: content/relays/performance/low-traffic/contents.lr:tab.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/low-traffic/
msgid "Understanding low usage on your relay"
msgstr "Förstå låg användning av reläet"

#: content/relays/performance/low-traffic/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/low-traffic/
msgid ""
"If you've been running a relay for a while and still having issues then try "
"asking on the [tor-relays list](https://lists.torproject.org/mailman3/"
"postorius/lists/tor-relays.lists.torproject.org/)."
msgstr ""
"Om reläet har varit igång ett tag och problemet kvarstår kan du fråga på "
"[sändlistan tor-relays](https://lists.torproject.org/mailman3/postorius/"
"lists/tor-relays.lists.torproject.org/)."

#: content/relays/performance/low-traffic/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/low-traffic/
msgid "If your relay is relatively new then give it time."
msgstr "Om reläet är relativt nytt bör du ge det tid."

#: content/relays/performance/low-traffic/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/low-traffic/
msgid ""
"The lifecycle of a new relay is explained in more depth in [this blog post]"
"(https://blog.torproject.org/blog/lifecycle-of-a-new-relay)."
msgstr ""
"Ett nytt reläs livscykel beskrivs utförligare i [det här blogginlägget]"
"(https://blog.torproject.org/blog/lifecycle-of-a-new-relay)."

#: content/relays/performance/low-traffic/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/low-traffic/
msgid ""
"Tor decides which relays it uses heuristically based on reports from "
"Bandwidth Authorities. These authorities take measurements of your relay's "
"capacity and, over time, directs more traffic there until it reaches an "
"optimal load."
msgstr ""
"Tor väljer reläer heuristiskt utifrån rapporter från "
"bandbreddsauktoriteterna. De mäter reläets kapacitet och leder med tiden mer "
"trafik dit tills en optimal belastning uppnås."

#: content/relays/performance/overloaded/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/overloaded/
msgid "Relay Search shows an amber dot when a relay/bridge is overloaded."
msgstr ""
"Relay Search visar en bärnstensfärgad punkt när ett relä eller en bro är "
"överbelastad."

#: content/relays/performance/overloaded/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/overloaded/
msgid ""
"This page explains what triggers that state, how long it persists, and "
"practical steps to investigate and resolve it."
msgstr ""
"Den här sidan förklarar vad som utlöser tillståndet, hur länge det kvarstår "
"och vilka praktiska åtgärder du kan vidta för att undersöka och lösa "
"problemet."

#: content/relays/performance/overloaded/contents.lr:article.longer_title
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/overloaded/
msgid "Understanding \"overloaded\" status and how to diagnose it"
msgstr "Förstå statusen ”överbelastad” och hur den diagnostiseras"

#: content/relays/performance/overloaded/contents.lr:article.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/overloaded/
msgid "Overloaded relays and bridges"
msgstr "Överbelastade reläer och broar"

#: content/relays/performance/overloaded/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/overloaded/
msgid ""
"**Note:** If you are running a powerful server with lots of RAM then you "
"might end up in an overloaded state due to the default queue size limit of "
"8GB even though you still have plenty of RAM unused. Add an appropriate "
"`MaxMemInQueues` entry to your `torrc` configuration in that case."
msgstr ""
"**Obs!** Om du kör en kraftfull server med mycket RAM-minne kan reläet ändå "
"bli överbelastat på grund av den standardmässiga gränsen på 8 GB för köns "
"storlek, trots att mycket RAM-minne är oanvänt. Lägg då till en lämplig post "
"för `MaxMemInQueues` i konfigurationen `torrc`."

#: content/relays/performance/overloaded/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/overloaded/
msgid ""
"**Note:** every user on that server will be able to access those relay "
"metrics in the example above."
msgstr ""
"**Obs!** I exemplet ovan kan alla användare på servern komma åt "
"relämätvärdena."

#: content/relays/performance/overloaded/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/overloaded/
msgid "/* Capped. */"
msgstr "/* Begränsat. */"

#: content/relays/performance/overloaded/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/overloaded/
msgid "/* Minimum value. */"
msgstr "/* Minsta värde. */"

#: content/relays/performance/overloaded/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/overloaded/
msgid ""
"1. Check <https://torprojectstatus.org/> for any known issues in the \"Tor "
"Network\" category."
msgstr ""
"1. Kontrollera <https://torprojectstatus.org/> för kända problem i kategorin "
"”Tor Network”."

#: content/relays/performance/overloaded/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/overloaded/
msgid ""
"2. Consider [tuning `sysctl` for your system](#tuning-sysctl-for-network-"
"memory-and-cpu-load) for network, memory and CPU load."
msgstr ""
"2. Överväg att [justera `sysctl` för systemet](#tuning-sysctl-for-network-"
"memory-and-cpu-load) med avseende på nätverk, minne och processorbelastning."

#: content/relays/performance/overloaded/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/overloaded/
msgid ""
"3. Consider [enabling `MetricsPort`](#metricsport) to understand what is "
"happening."
msgstr ""
"3. Överväg att [aktivera `MetricsPort`](#metricsport) för att förstå vad som "
"händer."

#: content/relays/performance/overloaded/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/overloaded/
msgid ""
"4GB is advised, although of course it doesn't hurt to add more RAM if you "
"can."
msgstr ""
"4 GB rekommenderas, men det skadar förstås inte att lägga till mer RAM-minne "
"om du kan."

#: content/relays/performance/overloaded/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/overloaded/
msgid "An Out-Of-Memory invocation indicates a RAM problem."
msgstr ""
"Om minnesbristshanteraren aktiveras tyder det på ett problem med RAM-minnet."

#: content/relays/performance/overloaded/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/overloaded/
msgid "And then you will be able to easily retrieve the metrics with:"
msgstr "Sedan kan du enkelt hämta mätvärdena med:"

#: content/relays/performance/overloaded/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/overloaded/
msgid ""
"Any counter in the \"*_dns_error_total\" realm (apart from the one for "
"successful queries) indicates a potential DNS related problem."
msgstr ""
"Alla räknare i kategorin ”*_dns_error_total”, förutom räknaren för lyckade "
"frågor, tyder på ett möjligt DNS-problem."

#: content/relays/performance/overloaded/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/overloaded/
msgid ""
"Because tor takes the total memory on the system when it starts, if the "
"overall system has many other applications running using RAM, it ends up "
"eating too much memory."
msgstr ""
"Eftersom Tor beräknar den totala mängden minne i systemet när det startar "
"kan det använda för mycket minne om många andra program samtidigt använder "
"RAM-minne."

#: content/relays/performance/overloaded/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/overloaded/
msgid "DNS timeout issues and errors only apply to Exit nodes."
msgstr "Tidsgränser och fel för DNS gäller endast utgångsreläer."

#: content/relays/performance/overloaded/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/overloaded/
msgid "Enabling MetricsPort"
msgstr "Aktivera MetricsPort"

#: content/relays/performance/overloaded/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/overloaded/
msgid ""
"For a more detailed explanation about ``MetricsPort`` and "
"``MetricsPortPolicy`` see tor's man page."
msgstr ""
"En utförligare förklaring av ``MetricsPort`` och ``MetricsPortPolicy`` finns "
"på Tors manualsida."

#: content/relays/performance/overloaded/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/overloaded/
msgid ""
"Here is an example of what output enabling ``MetricsPort`` will produce (we "
"omitted any congestion control related metrics as we still need to stabilize "
"that interface):"
msgstr ""
"Här är ett exempel på utdata när ``MetricsPort`` är aktiverad. Mätvärden för "
"överbelastningskontroll har utelämnats eftersom gränssnittet ännu behöver "
"stabiliseras:"

#: content/relays/performance/overloaded/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/overloaded/
msgid ""
"However, we realized during the 0.4.7 release cycle that DNS errors are way "
"too noisy and contain too many false positives to be useful for overload "
"reporting purposes."
msgstr ""
"Under utgivningscykeln för 0.4.7 insåg vi dock att DNS-fel är alltför "
"brusiga och innehåller för många falska positiva resultat för att vara "
"användbara vid rapportering av överbelastning."

#: content/relays/performance/overloaded/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/overloaded/
msgid ""
"If the number of opened sockets is close to or the same as total sockets "
"available then this indicates the relay is running out of sockets."
msgstr ""
"Om antalet öppna socketar ligger nära eller är lika med det totala antalet "
"tillgängliga socketar håller reläet på att få slut på socketar."

#: content/relays/performance/overloaded/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/overloaded/
msgid ""
"If this counter is incremented by some noticeable value over a short period "
"of time, the relay is congested."
msgstr "Om räknaren ökar märkbart under en kort period är reläet överbelastat."

#: content/relays/performance/overloaded/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/overloaded/
msgid ""
"If you are experiencing TCP port exhaustion consider expanding your local "
"port range."
msgstr "Överväg att utöka det lokala portintervallet om TCP-portarna tar slut."

#: content/relays/performance/overloaded/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/overloaded/
msgid "If you notice that your relay is overloaded please:"
msgstr "Om du märker att reläet är överbelastat:"

#: content/relays/performance/overloaded/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/overloaded/
msgid ""
"If you noticed that the tor process is leaking memory, please report the "
"issue either via [Tor GitLab](https://gitlab.torproject.org) or sending an "
"email to the [tor-relays mailing list](https://lists.torproject.org/mailman3/"
"postorius/lists/tor-relays.lists.torproject.org/)."
msgstr ""
"Om du märker att Tor-processen läcker minne rapporterar du problemet via "
"[Tor GitLab](https://gitlab.torproject.org) eller genom att skicka ett e-"
"postmeddelande till [sändlistan tor-relays](https://lists.torproject.org/"
"mailman3/postorius/lists/tor-relays.lists.torproject.org/)."

#: content/relays/performance/overloaded/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/overloaded/
msgid ""
"If your relay is still overloaded and you don't know why, please get in "
"touch with [network-report@torproject.org](mailto:network-"
"report@torproject.org)."
msgstr ""
"Kontakta [network-report@torproject.org](mailto:network-"
"report@torproject.org) om reläet fortfarande är överbelastat och du inte vet "
"varför."

#: content/relays/performance/overloaded/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/overloaded/
msgid "If your server is running at capacity this will likely be triggered."
msgstr "Det här utlöses sannolikt om servern körs med full kapacitet."

#: content/relays/performance/overloaded/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/overloaded/
msgid ""
"In general, set a very strict access policy with ``MetricsPortPolicy`` and "
"consider using your operating systems firewall features for defense in depth."
msgstr ""
"Ange i allmänhet en mycket strikt åtkomstpolicy med ``MetricsPortPolicy`` "
"och överväg att använda operativsystemets brandväggsfunktioner som ett extra "
"skyddslager."

#: content/relays/performance/overloaded/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/overloaded/
msgid ""
"In this case the OS could OOM tor, without tor even noticing memory pressure."
msgstr ""
"I så fall kan operativsystemet avsluta Tor på grund av minnesbrist utan att "
"Tor ens märker minnestrycket."

#: content/relays/performance/overloaded/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/overloaded/
msgid ""
"It can happen that this pool starts dropping work due to memory or CPU "
"pressure and this will trigger an overload state."
msgstr ""
"Det kan hända att den här poolen börjar tappa arbete på grund av minnes- "
"eller processortryck, vilket utlöser ett överbelastningstillstånd."

#: content/relays/performance/overloaded/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/overloaded/
msgid ""
"It is likely being used as a Guard by a big onion service or for an ongoing "
"DDoS on the network."
msgstr ""
"Reläet används sannolikt som vakt av en stor onion-tjänst eller i en "
"pågående DDoS-attack mot nätverket."

#: content/relays/performance/overloaded/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/overloaded/
msgid ""
"It's important to understand that **exposing the tor MetricsPort publicly is "
"dangerous for the Tor network users**, which is why that port is not enabled "
"by default and its access has to be governed by an access policy."
msgstr ""
"Det är viktigt att förstå att **det är farligt för Tor-nätverkets användare "
"att exponera Tors MetricsPort offentligt**. Därför är porten inte aktiverad "
"som standard och åtkomsten måste styras med en åtkomstpolicy."

#: content/relays/performance/overloaded/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/overloaded/
msgid ""
"Keep in mind that tuning `sysctl` as described is not permanent and will be "
"lost upon restart."
msgstr ""
"Kom ihåg att den beskrivna justeringen av `sysctl` inte är permanent utan "
"försvinner vid omstart."

#: content/relays/performance/overloaded/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/overloaded/
msgid "Let's assume you are the only user on a server that runs a Tor relay."
msgstr "Anta att du är den enda användaren på en server som kör ett Tor-relä."

#: content/relays/performance/overloaded/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/overloaded/
msgid "Let's find out what some of these lines actually mean:"
msgstr "Låt oss se vad några av raderna faktiskt betyder:"

#: content/relays/performance/overloaded/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/overloaded/
msgid "MetricsPort output"
msgstr "Utdata från MetricsPort"

#: content/relays/performance/overloaded/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/overloaded/
msgid ""
"Note that if a relay reaches an overloaded state we show it for 72 hours "
"after the relay has recovered."
msgstr ""
"Observera att statusen som överbelastad visas i 72 timmar efter att reläet "
"har återhämtat sig."

#: content/relays/performance/overloaded/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/overloaded/
msgid ""
"On relay search we show an amber dot next to the relay nickname when it is "
"overloaded."
msgstr ""
"I Relay Search visas en bärnstensfärgad punkt bredvid reläets smeknamn när "
"det är överbelastat."

#: content/relays/performance/overloaded/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/overloaded/
msgid "One might notice that tor could be called by the OS OOM handler itself."
msgstr ""
"Det kan hända att operativsystemets minnesbristshanterare avslutar Tor-"
"processen."

#: content/relays/performance/overloaded/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/overloaded/
msgid ""
"Please take extra precaution and care when opening this port, and close it "
"when you are done debugging."
msgstr ""
"Var extra försiktig när du öppnar porten och stäng den när felsökningen är "
"klar."

#: content/relays/performance/overloaded/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/overloaded/
msgid ""
"Relay overload information has been added to relay descriptors since 0.4.6+ "
"but it was not until Tor >= 0.4.7.1-alpha that an interface to the "
"underlying relay metrics was available: the metrics port."
msgstr ""
"Information om reläöverbelastning har funnits i relädeskriptorer sedan "
"version 0.4.6+, men först i Tor >= 0.4.7.1-alpha blev ett gränssnitt till de "
"underliggande relämätvärdena tillgängligt: mätvärdesporten."

#: content/relays/performance/overloaded/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/overloaded/
msgid "TCP port exhaustion"
msgstr "Slut på TCP-portar"

#: content/relays/performance/overloaded/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/overloaded/
msgid "That is considered an overload state."
msgstr "Det betraktas som ett överbelastningstillstånd."

#: content/relays/performance/overloaded/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/overloaded/
msgid ""
"The \"onion skins\" are the cryptographic work that needs to be done on the "
"famous \"onion layers\" in every circuits."
msgstr ""
"”Onion-skalen” är det kryptografiska arbete som måste utföras på de välkända "
"”onion-lagren” i varje krets."

#: content/relays/performance/overloaded/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/overloaded/
msgid "The relay might need more RAM or it is leaking memory."
msgstr "Reläet kan behöva mer RAM-minne eller läcka minne."

#: content/relays/performance/overloaded/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/overloaded/
msgid "The solution is to increase ``ulimit -n`` for the tor process."
msgstr "Lösningen är att höja ``ulimit -n`` för Tor-processen."

#: content/relays/performance/overloaded/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/overloaded/
msgid "These lines indicate the relay is running out of TCP ports."
msgstr "De här raderna visar att reläet håller på att få slut på TCP-portar."

#: content/relays/performance/overloaded/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/overloaded/
msgid ""
"This means that one or many of the following load metrics have been "
"triggered:"
msgstr ""
"Det innebär att ett eller flera av följande belastningsmätvärden har utlösts:"

#: content/relays/performance/overloaded/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/overloaded/
msgid ""
"Thus, let's say tor thinks it can use 2GB in total then at 1.5GB of memory "
"usage, it will start freeing memory."
msgstr ""
"Om Tor exempelvis tror att det totalt kan använda 2 GB börjar det frigöra "
"minne vid 1,5 GB minnesanvändning."

#: content/relays/performance/overloaded/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/overloaded/
msgid ""
"To avoid an overloaded state we recommend to run a relay above 2GB of RAM on "
"64bit."
msgstr ""
"För att undvika överbelastning rekommenderar vi att reläet körs på ett 64-"
"bitars system med mer än 2 GB RAM-minne."

#: content/relays/performance/overloaded/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/overloaded/
msgid ""
"To estimate the amount of memory it has available, when tor starts, it will "
"use `MaxMemInQueues` or, if not set, will look at the total RAM available on "
"the system and apply this algorithm:"
msgstr ""
"När Tor startar uppskattas det tillgängliga minnet med `MaxMemInQueues` "
"eller, om det inte är angivet, genom att kontrollera systemets totala RAM-"
"minne och använda följande algoritm:"

#: content/relays/performance/overloaded/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/overloaded/
msgid ""
"To understand the well-being of Tor relays and the Tor network it is vital "
"to provide and have access to relay metrics."
msgstr ""
"Tillgång till mätvärden för reläer är avgörande för att förstå hur Tor-"
"reläerna och Tor-nätverket mår."

#: content/relays/performance/overloaded/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/overloaded/
msgid ""
"Tor has its own OOM handler and it is invoked when 75%, of the total memory "
"tor thinks is available, is reached."
msgstr ""
"Tor har en egen minnesbristshanterare som aktiveras när 75 procent av den "
"mängd minne som Tor bedömer vara tillgänglig har använts."

#: content/relays/performance/overloaded/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/overloaded/
msgid ""
"Tor is sadly single threaded _except_ for when the \"onion skins\" are "
"processed."
msgstr "Tor är tyvärr enkeltrådat, _förutom_ när ”onion-skalen” bearbetas."

#: content/relays/performance/overloaded/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/overloaded/
msgid ""
"Tor provides access to the metrics port via a torrc configuration option "
"called ``MetricsPort``."
msgstr ""
"Tor ger åtkomst till mätvärdesporten via konfigurationsalternativet "
"``MetricsPort`` i torrc."

#: content/relays/performance/overloaded/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/overloaded/
msgid "Try to tune ``sysctl`` as [described above](#tcp-port-exhaustion)."
msgstr ""
"Försök justera ``sysctl`` enligt [beskrivningen ovan](#tcp-port-exhaustion)."

#: content/relays/performance/overloaded/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/overloaded/
msgid "Tuning `sysctl` for network, memory and CPU load"
msgstr "Justera `sysctl` för nätverks-, minnes- och processorbelastning"

#: content/relays/performance/overloaded/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/overloaded/
msgid ""
"We therefore don't use them anymore for that purpose starting with 0.4.6.9 "
"and 0.4.7.4-alpha. However, we still keep DNS metrics around to give the "
"relay operator insight into what is going on with their relay."
msgstr ""
"Från och med 0.4.6.9 och 0.4.7.4-alpha använder vi därför inte längre DNS-"
"felen för det ändamålet. DNS-mätvärdena behålls dock så att reläoperatören "
"kan se vad som händer med reläet."

#: content/relays/performance/overloaded/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/overloaded/
msgid ""
"When a relay starts seeing \"dropped\", it is a CPU/RAM problem usually."
msgstr ""
"När ett relä börjar rapportera ”dropped” beror det vanligen på processor- "
"eller minnesproblem."

#: content/relays/performance/overloaded/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/overloaded/
msgid ""
"When tor processes the layers we use a thread pool and outsource all of that "
"work to that pool."
msgstr ""
"När Tor bearbetar lagren används en trådpool som allt arbete överförs till."

#: content/relays/performance/overloaded/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/overloaded/
msgid "You can do that with"
msgstr "Det kan du göra med"

#: content/relays/performance/overloaded/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/overloaded/
msgid "You can enable the metrics port adding this to your torrc file:"
msgstr ""
"Du kan aktivera mätvärdesporten genom att lägga till följande i torrc-filen:"

#: content/relays/performance/overloaded/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/overloaded/
msgid ""
"You can encrypt your email using [network-report OpenPGP key](https://"
"keys.openpgp.org/vks/v1/by-fingerprint/"
"01F062062766826E8D1B71771F095787CFDBF2DE)."
msgstr ""
"Du kan kryptera e-postmeddelandet med [OpenPGP-nyckeln för network-report]"
"(https://keys.openpgp.org/vks/v1/by-fingerprint/"
"01F062062766826E8D1B71771F095787CFDBF2DE)."

#: content/relays/performance/overloaded/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/overloaded/
msgid ""
"You need to add the configuration to `/etc/sysctl.conf` or to a file in `/"
"etc/sysctl.d/` to make it permanent."
msgstr ""
"Lägg till konfigurationen i `/etc/sysctl.conf` eller i en fil under `/etc/"
"sysctl.d/` för att göra den permanent."

#: content/relays/performance/overloaded/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/overloaded/
msgid ""
"[Any Tor OOM invocation due to memory pressure](#tor-relay-load-oom-bytes-"
"total)"
msgstr ""
"[Alla aktiveringar av Tors minnesbristshanterare på grund av minnestryck]"
"(#tor-relay-load-oom-bytes-total)"

#: content/relays/performance/overloaded/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/overloaded/
msgid ""
"[Any ntor onionskins are dropped](#tor-relay-load-onionskins-total-type-ntor-"
"action-dropped-0)"
msgstr ""
"[Alla ntor-onion-skal som tappas](#tor-relay-load-onionskins-total-type-ntor-"
"action-dropped-0)"

#: content/relays/performance/overloaded/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/overloaded/
msgid "[TCP port exhaustion](#tcp-port-exhaustion)"
msgstr "[Slut på TCP-portar](#tcp-port-exhaustion)"

#: content/relays/performance/overloaded/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/overloaded/
msgid "or"
msgstr "eller"

#: content/relays/performance/overloaded/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/overloaded/
msgid "which are by default in a Prometheus format."
msgstr "som som standard använder Prometheus-format."

#: content/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/
msgid ""
"If your Tor relay seems slow or under-utilized, there are several possible "
"causes - from system limits to network peering to Tor's own bandwidth "
"measurements - and practical steps you can take to diagnose and improve its "
"speed."
msgstr ""
"Om Tor-reläet verkar långsamt eller underutnyttjat kan orsaken vara allt "
"från systemgränser och nätverkspeering till Tors egna bandbreddsmätningar. "
"Det finns flera praktiska sätt att diagnostisera och förbättra hastigheten."

#: content/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/contents.lr:article.longer_title
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/
msgid "Why your Tor relay might be slow and how to improve its performance"
msgstr "Därför kan Tor-reläet vara långsamt och så förbättrar du prestandan"

#: content/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/contents.lr:article.title
#: content/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/contents.lr:tab.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/
msgid "Slow Tor relay"
msgstr "Långsamt Tor-relä"

#: content/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/
msgid ""
"(We want enough relays to so that each relay is loaded at 10%. Then Tor "
"would be almost as fast as the wider Internet)."
msgstr ""
"(Vi vill ha tillräckligt många reläer för att varje relä bara ska belastas "
"till 10 procent. Då skulle Tor vara nästan lika snabbt som internet i "
"övrigt.)"

#: content/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/
msgid ""
"Alternatively, you can run [relay_bw](https://gitlab.torproject.org/juga/"
"relay_bw) to test your relay using 2 hops circuits, in a similar way as "
"[sbws](https://tpo.pages.torproject.net/network-health/sbws/) does."
msgstr ""
"Du kan också köra [relay_bw](https://gitlab.torproject.org/juga/relay_bw) "
"för att testa reläet med kretsar på två hopp, på ungefär samma sätt som "
"[sbws](https://tpo.pages.torproject.net/network-health/sbws/)."

#: content/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/
msgid "Are there more than 2 relays on its IPv4 address?"
msgstr "Finns det fler än två reläer på samma IPv4-adress?"

#: content/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/
msgid ""
"BitTorrent wants bulk downloads, which requires using all the bandwidth."
msgstr ""
"BitTorrent är utformat för stora hämtningar och kräver därför att all "
"bandbredd används."

#: content/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/
msgid ""
"But Tor has users all over the world, and our users connect to one or two "
"Guard relays at random."
msgstr ""
"Tor har däremot användare över hela världen, och användarna ansluter "
"slumpmässigt till ett eller två vaktreläer."

#: content/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/
msgid "But Tor's goals are different to protocols like BitTorrent."
msgstr "Tors mål skiljer sig från protokoll som BitTorrent."

#: content/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/
msgid "Check RAM, CPU, and socket/file descriptor usage on your relay"
msgstr ""
"Kontrollera reläets användning av RAM-minne, processor, socketar och "
"filbeskrivare"

#: content/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/
msgid ""
"Check each of the votes for your relay on [consensus-health (large page)]"
"(https://consensus-health.torproject.org/consensus-health.html), and check "
"the median."
msgstr ""
"Kontrollera varje katalogauktoritets röst för reläet på [consensus-health "
"(stor sida)](https://consensus-health.torproject.org/consensus-health.html) "
"och kontrollera medianen."

#: content/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/
msgid ""
"Check the Internet peering (bandwidth, latency) from your relay's provider "
"to other relays."
msgstr ""
"Kontrollera internetpeeringen, både bandbredd och latens, mellan reläets "
"leverantör och andra reläer."

#: content/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/
msgid "Does it have the wrong IPv4 or IPv6 address?"
msgstr "Har reläet fel IPv4- eller IPv6-adress?"

#: content/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/
msgid "Doing Your Own Relay Measurements"
msgstr "Göra egna relämätningar"

#: content/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/
msgid "Finding Out what is Limiting a Relay"
msgstr "Ta reda på vad som begränsar reläet"

#: content/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/
msgid "For this, you can use `curl`, eg:"
msgstr "Du kan använda `curl`, exempelvis:"

#: content/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/
msgid ""
"For this, you need to configure a tor client to use use your relay as entry."
msgstr ""
"För detta måste en Tor-klient konfigureras så att reläet används som ingång."

#: content/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/
msgid ""
"Here is some more detail and some examples: [Drop in consensus weight]"
"(https://archive.torproject.org/websites/lists.torproject.org/pipermail/tor-"
"relays/2016-November/010913.html) and [Rampup speed of Exit relay](https://"
"archive.torproject.org/websites/lists.torproject.org/pipermail/tor-relays/"
"2016-October/010784.html)."
msgstr ""
"Fler detaljer och exempel finns i [Drop in consensus weight](https://"
"archive.torproject.org/websites/lists.torproject.org/pipermail/tor-relays/"
"2016-November/010913.html) och [Rampup speed of Exit relay](https://"
"archive.torproject.org/websites/lists.torproject.org/pipermail/tor-relays/"
"2016-October/010784.html)."

#: content/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/
msgid "Here's how to find out which measurement is limiting your relay:"
msgstr "Så tar du reda på vilken mätning som begränsar reläet:"

#: content/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/
msgid "How to fix it"
msgstr "Så åtgärdar du det"

#: content/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/
msgid ""
"If it's the bandwidth rate, increase the BandwidthRate/Burst or "
"RelayBandwidthRate/Burst in your torrc."
msgstr ""
"Om bandbreddshastigheten begränsar höjer du BandwidthRate/Burst eller "
"RelayBandwidthRate/Burst i torrc."

#: content/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/
msgid ""
"If it's the median measured bandwidth, your relay looks slow from a majority "
"of bandwidth authorities."
msgstr ""
"Om den uppmätta medianbandbredden begränsar ser reläet långsamt ut för en "
"majoritet av bandbreddsauktoriteterna."

#: content/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/
msgid ""
"If it's the observed bandwidth, your relay won't ask for more bandwidth "
"until it sees itself getting faster."
msgstr ""
"Om den observerade bandbredden begränsar begär reläet inte mer bandbredd "
"förrän det själv ser att det blivit snabbare."

#: content/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/
msgid ""
"If your relay doesn't have `Guard` flag or it has `Guard` and `Exit` flags, "
"you can't set your relay as an entry node (see https://gitlab.torproject.org/"
"tpo/core/tor/-/work_items/22204), but you can set it as your bridge, even if "
"it is not a bridge."
msgstr ""
"Om reläet saknar flaggan `Guard` eller har både `Guard` och `Exit` kan det "
"inte anges som ingångsnod (se https://gitlab.torproject.org/tpo/core/tor/-/"
"work_items/22204), men det kan anges som bro även om det inte är en bro."

#: content/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/
msgid ""
"If your relay has only `Guard` flag, set `EntryNodes` with your relay "
"fingerprint in `torrc`."
msgstr ""
"Om reläet endast har flaggan `Guard` anger du `EntryNodes` med reläets "
"fingeravtryck i `torrc`."

#: content/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/
msgid "If your relay is not marked Running by some directory authorities:"
msgstr "Om vissa katalogauktoriteter inte markerar reläet som Running:"

#: content/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/
msgid ""
"If your relay thinks it is slow, or the bandwidth authorities think it is "
"slow, you can test the bandwidth yourself:"
msgstr ""
"Om reläet självt eller bandbreddsauktoriteterna bedömer att det är långsamt "
"kan du testa bandbredden själv:"

#: content/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/
msgid "Is its IPv4 or IPv6 address unreachable from some networks?"
msgstr "Går reläets IPv4- eller IPv6-adress inte att nå från vissa nätverk?"

#: content/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/
msgid ""
"It will have diagnostics for relays that don't get measured, and relays that "
"have low measurements."
msgstr ""
"Där visas diagnostik för reläer som inte mäts och reläer med låga mätvärden."

#: content/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/
msgid "It's normal for most relays to be loaded at 30%-80% of their capacity."
msgstr ""
"Det är normalt att de flesta reläer belastas till 30–80 procent av sin "
"kapacitet."

#: content/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/
msgid "Keep increasing the data volume until the bandwidth stops increasing."
msgstr "Öka datamängden tills bandbredden slutar öka."

#: content/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/
msgid ""
"Look up your relay on [Metrics](https://metrics.torproject.org/rs.html)."
msgstr "Slå upp reläet i [Metrics](https://metrics.torproject.org/rs.html)."

#: content/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/
msgid "Lots of things can slow down a relay. Here's how to track them down."
msgstr "Många saker kan göra ett relä långsammare. Så här hittar du orsaken."

#: content/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/
msgid "Most providers tell you the maximum speed of your local connection."
msgstr ""
"De flesta leverantörer anger den högsta hastigheten för den lokala "
"anslutningen."

#: content/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/
msgid ""
"Other times, it is the network that is slow: the relay has bad peering to "
"most other tor relays, or is a long distance away."
msgstr ""
"I andra fall är nätverket långsamt: reläet har dålig peering med de flesta "
"andra Tor-reläer eller ligger långt bort."

#: content/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/
msgid ""
"Otherwise, check your relay's observed bandwidth and bandwidth rate (limit)."
msgstr ""
"Kontrollera annars reläets observerade bandbredd och bandbreddshastighet, "
"det vill säga gränsen."

#: content/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/
msgid "Provider Limits"
msgstr "Leverantörsgränser"

#: content/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/
msgid ""
"Relay bandwidth can be limited by a relay's own observed bandwidth, or by "
"the directory authorities' measured bandwidth."
msgstr ""
"Reläets bandbredd kan begränsas av dess egen observerade bandbredd eller av "
"den bandbredd som katalogauktoriteterna mäter."

#: content/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/
msgid "Relays outside North America and Western Europe are usually slower."
msgstr "Reläer utanför Nordamerika och Västeuropa är vanligtvis långsammare."

#: content/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/
msgid "Relays transiting via Comcast have been slow at times."
msgstr "Reläer vars trafik passerar Comcast har periodvis varit långsamma."

#: content/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/
msgid ""
"Run a test using tor and [chutney](https://gitlab.torproject.org/tpo/core/"
"chutney/-/blob/c4f6789ad2558dcbfeb7d024c6481d8112bfb6c2/README.md#L143) to "
"find out how fast tor can get on your CPU."
msgstr ""
"Kör ett test med Tor och [chutney](https://gitlab.torproject.org/tpo/core/"
"chutney/-/blob/c4f6789ad2558dcbfeb7d024c6481d8112bfb6c2/README.md#L143) för "
"att ta reda på hur snabbt Tor kan köras på processorn."

#: content/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/
msgid "Run a test using tor to see how fast tor can get on your network"
msgstr "Kör ett test med Tor för att se hur snabbt Tor kan köras i nätverket"

#: content/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/
msgid ""
"So even if all relay operators set their advertised bandwidth to their local "
"connection speed, we would still need bandwidth authorities to balance the "
"load between different parts of the Internet."
msgstr ""
"Även om alla reläoperatörer angav den lokala anslutningshastigheten som "
"annonserad bandbredd skulle bandbreddsauktoriteter fortfarande behövas för "
"att balansera belastningen mellan olika delar av internet."

#: content/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/
msgid "So we need to know how well each relay can connect to the entire world."
msgstr "Vi måste därför veta hur väl varje relä kan ansluta till hela världen."

#: content/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/
msgid ""
"Sometimes, a relay is slow because its processor is slow or its connections "
"are limited."
msgstr ""
"Ibland är reläet långsamt för att processorn är långsam eller anslutningarna "
"är begränsade."

#: content/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/
msgid "System Limits"
msgstr "Systemgränser"

#: content/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/
msgid ""
"That will give you some idea of how much traffic your relay can sustain."
msgstr "Det ger en uppfattning om hur mycket trafik reläet klarar."

#: content/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/
msgid ""
"The smallest of these figures is limiting the bandwidth allocated to the "
"relay."
msgstr ""
"Det lägsta av dessa värden begränsar den bandbredd som tilldelas reläet."

#: content/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/
msgid "Then download a large file using your `SocksPort` as a socks proxy."
msgstr ""
"Hämta sedan en stor fil genom att använda din `SocksPort` som SOCKS-proxy."

#: content/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/
msgid ""
"Then mouse over the bandwidth heading to see the observed bandwidth and "
"relay bandwidth rate."
msgstr ""
"Håll sedan muspekaren över rubriken för bandbredd för att visa observerad "
"bandbredd och reläets bandbreddshastighet."

#: content/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/
msgid "This is good for clients: an overloaded relay has high latency."
msgstr "Det är bra för klienterna: ett överbelastat relä har hög latens."

#: content/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/
msgid "To set your relay as a bridge, add to your `torrc`:"
msgstr "Lägg till följande i `torrc` för att ange reläet som en bro:"

#: content/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/
msgid "Tor Network Limits"
msgstr "Gränser i Tor-nätverket"

#: content/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/
msgid ""
"Tor logs some of these when it starts. Others can be viewed using top or "
"similar tools."
msgstr ""
"Tor loggar vissa av dessa värden när det startar. Andra kan visas med top "
"eller liknande verktyg."

#: content/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/
msgid ""
"Tor manages bandwidth across the entire network. It does a reasonable job "
"for most relays."
msgstr ""
"Tor hanterar bandbredden i hela nätverket och gör ett rimligt bra jobb för "
"de flesta reläer."

#: content/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/
msgid ""
"Tor wants low-latency web pages, which requires fast connections with "
"headroom."
msgstr ""
"Tor är avsett för webbsidor med låg latens, vilket kräver snabba "
"anslutningar med ledig kapacitet."

#: content/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/
msgid ""
"Using different `user`/`password` guarantees different circuits. You can use "
"`$RANDOM`."
msgstr ""
"Olika `user`/`password` garanterar olika kretsar. Du kan använda `$RANDOM`."

#: content/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/
msgid ""
"We're working on a [new bandwidth scanner](https://sbws.readthedocs.io/), "
"which is easier to understand and maintain."
msgstr ""
"Vi arbetar på en [ny bandbreddsskanner](https://sbws.readthedocs.io/) som är "
"enklare att förstå och underhålla."

#: content/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/
msgid "What is a normal relay load?"
msgstr "Vad är en normal reläbelastning?"

#: content/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/
msgid "Why does Tor need bandwidth scanners?"
msgstr "Varför behöver Tor bandbreddsskannrar?"

#: content/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/
msgid "Why relay load varies"
msgstr "Därför varierar reläbelastningen"

#: content/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/
msgid "You need to work out why it is slow."
msgstr "Du måste ta reda på varför reläet är långsamt."

#: content/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/
msgid "You need to work out why they measure it slow."
msgstr "Du måste ta reda på varför de mäter det som långsamt."

#: content/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/relay-is-slow/
msgid ""
"curl https://target/path --proxy socks5h://<user>:<password>@127.0.0.1:"
"<socks-port>"
msgstr ""
"curl https://target/path --proxy socks5h://<user>:<password>@127.0.0.1:"
"<socks-port>"

#: content/relays/performance/relay-writes-more-bytes/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/relay-writes-more-bytes/
msgid ""
"Tor relays often appear to transmit more bytes than they receive because of "
"directory responses and how Tor packages data into cells."
msgstr ""
"Tor-reläer verkar ofta skicka fler byte än de tar emot på grund av "
"katalogsvar och hur Tor packar data i celler."

#: content/relays/performance/relay-writes-more-bytes/contents.lr:article.longer_title
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/relay-writes-more-bytes/
msgid "Why does my relay write more bytes onto the network than it reads?"
msgstr "Varför skriver reläet fler byte till nätverket än det läser?"

#: content/relays/performance/relay-writes-more-bytes/contents.lr:article.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/relay-writes-more-bytes/
msgid "Relay bandwidth difference"
msgstr "Skillnad i reläets bandbredd"

#: content/relays/performance/relay-writes-more-bytes/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/relay-writes-more-bytes/
msgid ""
"Another minor exception shows up when you operate as an exit node, and you "
"read a few bytes from an exit connection (for example, an instant messaging "
"or ssh connection) and wrap it up into an entire 512 byte cell for transport "
"through the Tor network."
msgstr ""
"Ett annat mindre undantag uppstår när du fungerar som utgångsrelä, läser "
"några få byte från en utgångsanslutning, exempelvis en anslutning för "
"snabbmeddelanden eller SSH, och packar dem i en hel cell på 512 byte för "
"transport genom Tor-nätverket."

#: content/relays/performance/relay-writes-more-bytes/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/relay-writes-more-bytes/
msgid ""
"If you open your DirPort, then Tor clients will ask you for a copy of the "
"directory."
msgstr "Om du öppnar DirPort begär Tor-klienter en kopia av katalogen."

#: content/relays/performance/relay-writes-more-bytes/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/relay-writes-more-bytes/
msgid ""
"The request they make (an HTTP GET) is quite small, and the response is "
"sometimes quite large."
msgstr ""
"Begäran, en HTTP GET, är ganska liten medan svaret ibland är mycket stort."

#: content/relays/performance/relay-writes-more-bytes/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/relay-writes-more-bytes/
msgid ""
"This probably accounts for most of the difference between your \"write\" "
"byte count and your \"read\" byte count."
msgstr ""
"Det förklarar sannolikt större delen av skillnaden mellan antalet skrivna "
"och lästa byte."

#: content/relays/performance/relay-writes-more-bytes/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/performance/relay-writes-more-bytes/
msgid ""
"You're right, for the most part a byte into your Tor relay means a byte out, "
"and vice versa. But there are a few exceptions:"
msgstr ""
"Du har rätt: för det mesta innebär en byte in till Tor-reläet en byte ut och "
"omvänt. Det finns dock några undantag:"

#: content/relays/running/bridge-distribution-method/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/bridge-distribution-method/
msgid ""
"Bridge operators can view and control how their bridges are distributed to "
"users."
msgstr ""
"Brooperatörer kan visa och styra hur deras broar distribueras till "
"användarna."

#: content/relays/running/bridge-distribution-method/contents.lr:article.longer_title
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/bridge-distribution-method/
msgid "How to choose and change your bridge's distribution method"
msgstr "Så väljer och ändrar du brons distributionsmetod"

#: content/relays/running/bridge-distribution-method/contents.lr:article.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/bridge-distribution-method/
msgid "Bridge distribution method"
msgstr "Brons distributionsmetod"

#: content/relays/running/bridge-distribution-method/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/bridge-distribution-method/
msgid ""
"Bridge operators can check which mechanism their bridge is using, on the "
"[Relay Search](https://metrics.torproject.org/rs.html)."
msgstr ""
"Brooperatörer kan kontrollera vilken mekanism bron använder i [Relay Search]"
"(https://metrics.torproject.org/rs.html)."

#: content/relays/running/bridge-distribution-method/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/bridge-distribution-method/
msgid ""
"Bridges are distributed via five mechanisms : HTTPS, Email, Telegram, "
"Settings and Reserved."
msgstr ""
"Broar distribueras genom fem mekanismer: HTTPS, e-post, Telegram, "
"inställningar och reserverad distribution."

#: content/relays/running/bridge-distribution-method/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/bridge-distribution-method/
msgid ""
"Enter the bridge's `<HASHED FINGERPRINT>` in the form and click \"Search\"."
msgstr "Ange brons `<HASHED FINGERPRINT>` i formuläret och klicka på ”Search”."

#: content/relays/running/bridge-distribution-method/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/bridge-distribution-method/
msgid "Operators can also choose which distribution method their bridge uses."
msgstr "Operatörer kan även välja vilken distributionsmetod bron ska använda."

#: content/relays/running/bridge-distribution-method/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/bridge-distribution-method/
msgid ""
"Read more on the Bridges [post-install](https://community.torproject.org/"
"relay/setup/bridge/post-install/) guide."
msgstr ""
"Läs mer i [guiden för åtgärder efter installation av broar](https://"
"community.torproject.org/relay/setup/bridge/post-install/)."

#: content/relays/running/bridge-distribution-method/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/bridge-distribution-method/
msgid ""
"To change the method, modify the `BridgeDistribution` setting in the torrc "
"file to one of these: https, email, telegram, settings, none, any."
msgstr ""
"Ändra metoden genom att ange någon av följande inställningar för "
"`BridgeDistribution` i torrc-filen: https, email, telegram, settings, none "
"eller any."

#: content/relays/running/bridge-distribution-method/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/bridge-distribution-method/
msgid ""
"You can find a description of each distributor in the [Bridge distribution "
"documentation](https://gitlab.torproject.org/tpo/anti-censorship/rdsys/-/"
"blob/main/doc/distributors.md)."
msgstr ""
"En beskrivning av varje distributör finns i [dokumentationen om "
"brodistribution](https://gitlab.torproject.org/tpo/anti-censorship/rdsys/-/"
"blob/main/doc/distributors.md)."

#: content/relays/running/bridge-distribution-method/contents.lr:tab.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/bridge-distribution-method/
msgid "Bridge distribution"
msgstr "Brodistribution"

#: content/relays/running/configure-outgoing-filters/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/configure-outgoing-filters/
msgid ""
"Tor relays must allow unrestricted outgoing connections to maintain network "
"integrity, and exit relays must not filter traffic passing through them."
msgstr ""
"Tor-reläer måste tillåta obegränsade utgående anslutningar för att bevara "
"nätverkets integritet, och utgångsreläer får inte filtrera trafik som "
"passerar genom dem."

#: content/relays/running/configure-outgoing-filters/contents.lr:article.longer_title
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/configure-outgoing-filters/
msgid "How to configure outgoing filters on your Tor relay"
msgstr "Så konfigurerar du utgående filter för Tor-reläet"

#: content/relays/running/configure-outgoing-filters/contents.lr:article.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/configure-outgoing-filters/
msgid "Outgoing filters on relays"
msgstr "Utgående filter på reläer"

#: content/relays/running/configure-outgoing-filters/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/configure-outgoing-filters/
msgid ""
"All outgoing connections must be allowed, so that each relay can communicate "
"with every other relay."
msgstr ""
"Alla utgående anslutningar måste tillåtas så att varje relä kan kommunicera "
"med alla andra reläer."

#: content/relays/running/configure-outgoing-filters/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/configure-outgoing-filters/
msgid ""
"Exit relays found to be filtering traffic will get the [BadExit](https://"
"community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/bad-relays/) flag once "
"detected."
msgstr ""
"Utgångsreläer som visar sig filtrera trafik får flaggan [BadExit](https://"
"community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/bad-relays/) när detta "
"upptäcks."

#: content/relays/running/configure-outgoing-filters/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/configure-outgoing-filters/
msgid ""
"Exit relays must not filter the traffic that passes through them to the "
"internet."
msgstr ""
"Utgångsreläer får inte filtrera trafiken som passerar genom dem till "
"internet."

#: content/relays/running/configure-outgoing-filters/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/configure-outgoing-filters/
msgid ""
"Exit relays that filter some traffic would likely forfeit those protections."
msgstr ""
"Utgångsreläer som filtrerar viss trafik skulle sannolikt förlora dessa "
"rättsliga skydd."

#: content/relays/running/configure-outgoing-filters/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/configure-outgoing-filters/
msgid ""
"In many jurisdictions, Tor relay operators are legally protected by the same "
"common carrier regulations that prevent internet service providers from "
"being held liable for third-party content that passes through their network."
msgstr ""
"I många jurisdiktioner skyddas Tor-reläoperatörer juridiskt av samma regler "
"för allmänna kommunikationstjänster som hindrar internetleverantörer från "
"att hållas ansvariga för innehåll från tredje part som passerar deras "
"nätverk."

#: content/relays/running/configure-outgoing-filters/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/configure-outgoing-filters/
msgid "Tor promotes free network access without interference."
msgstr "Tor främjar fri nätverksåtkomst utan ingrepp."

#: content/relays/running/configure-outgoing-filters/contents.lr:tab.title
#: content/relays/running/fixing-relay-ip-address/contents.lr:article.title
#: content/relays/running/fixing-relay-ip-address/contents.lr:tab.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/configure-outgoing-filters/
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/fixing-relay-ip-address/
msgid "Relay IP address"
msgstr "Reläets IP-adress"

#: content/relays/running/contents.lr:section.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/
msgid "Running relays"
msgstr "Driva reläer"

#: content/relays/running/default-exit-ports/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/default-exit-ports/
msgid ""
"Tor exit relays have a default exit policy that blocks some high-risk or "
"abuse-prone ports but allows most other ports unless the operator changes "
"the configuration."
msgstr ""
"Tor-utgångsreläer har en standardpolicy som blockerar vissa portar med hög "
"risk eller missbruksrisk, men tillåter de flesta andra portar om operatören "
"inte ändrar konfigurationen."

#: content/relays/running/default-exit-ports/contents.lr:article.longer_title
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/default-exit-ports/
msgid "Which ports are allowed by default on Tor exit relays?"
msgstr "Vilka portar tillåts som standard på Tor-utgångsreläer?"

#: content/relays/running/default-exit-ports/contents.lr:article.title
#: content/relays/running/default-exit-ports/contents.lr:tab.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/default-exit-ports/
msgid "Default exit ports"
msgstr "Standardportar för utgångar"

#: content/relays/running/default-exit-ports/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/default-exit-ports/
msgid ""
"By default, Tor exit relays block some IP ranges and a number of ports that "
"are commonly abused, but allow most other ports."
msgstr ""
"Som standard blockerar Tor-utgångsreläer vissa IP-intervall och ett antal "
"portar som ofta missbrukas, men tillåter de flesta andra portar."

#: content/relays/running/default-exit-ports/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/default-exit-ports/
msgid ""
"Relay operators can override this policy in their `torrc` configuration or "
"even modify the source code to adjust it."
msgstr ""
"Reläoperatörer kan åsidosätta policyn i konfigurationen `torrc` eller till "
"och med ändra källkoden."

#: content/relays/running/fixing-relay-ip-address/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/fixing-relay-ip-address/
msgid ""
"If Tor detects the wrong IP address for your relay, you can correct it by "
"checking your hostname settings or specifying the desired address in torrc."
msgstr ""
"Om Tor identifierar fel IP-adress för reläet kan du rätta den genom att "
"kontrollera värdnamnsinställningarna eller ange önskad adress i torrc."

#: content/relays/running/fixing-relay-ip-address/contents.lr:article.longer_title
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/fixing-relay-ip-address/
msgid "How to fix a Tor relay picking the wrong IP address"
msgstr "Så rättar du ett Tor-relä som väljer fel IP-adress"

#: content/relays/running/fixing-relay-ip-address/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/fixing-relay-ip-address/
msgid ""
"Also, if you have many addresses, you might also want to set "
"\"OutboundBindAddress\" so external connections come from the IP you intend "
"to present to the world."
msgstr ""
"Om du har många adresser kan du även ange ”OutboundBindAddress” så att "
"externa anslutningar kommer från den IP-adress som du vill visa utåt."

#: content/relays/running/fixing-relay-ip-address/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/fixing-relay-ip-address/
msgid ""
"If that doesn't fix it, you should use the \"Address\" config option to "
"specify the IP address you want it to pick. If your computer is behind a NAT "
"and it only has an internal IP address, see the following Support entry on "
"dynamic IP addresses."
msgstr ""
"Om det inte löser problemet använder du konfigurationsalternativet ”Address” "
"för att ange vilken IP-adress som ska väljas. Om datorn finns bakom NAT och "
"endast har en intern IP-adress läser du följande supportavsnitt om dynamiska "
"IP-adresser."

#: content/relays/running/fixing-relay-ip-address/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/fixing-relay-ip-address/
msgid ""
"Tor guesses its IP address by asking the computer for its hostname, and then "
"resolving that hostname. Often people have old entries in their /etc/hosts "
"file that point to old IP addresses."
msgstr ""
"Tor gissar IP-adressen genom att fråga datorn efter värdnamnet och sedan slå "
"upp det. Många har gamla poster i filen /etc/hosts som pekar på tidigare IP-"
"adresser."

#: content/relays/running/guard-relay-traffic-drop/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/guard-relay-traffic-drop/
msgid "This is normal behavior in Tor's design."
msgstr "Det är normalt och följer Tors konstruktion."

#: content/relays/running/guard-relay-traffic-drop/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/guard-relay-traffic-drop/
msgid ""
"When a relay first becomes a Guard, it may see a temporary drop in traffic "
"as clients gradually rotate in new Guards."
msgstr ""
"När ett relä först blir vakt kan trafiken tillfälligt minska medan "
"klienterna gradvis byter till nya vakter."

#: content/relays/running/guard-relay-traffic-drop/contents.lr:article.longer_title
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/guard-relay-traffic-drop/
msgid "Why new Guard relays experience temporary drops in traffic"
msgstr "Därför minskar trafiken tillfälligt för nya vaktreläer"

#: content/relays/running/guard-relay-traffic-drop/contents.lr:article.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/guard-relay-traffic-drop/
msgid "Guard relay traffic usage"
msgstr "Trafikanvändning för vaktreläer"

#: content/relays/running/guard-relay-traffic-drop/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/guard-relay-traffic-drop/
msgid ""
"Read more details in this [blog post](https://blog.torproject.org/blog/"
"lifecycle-of-a-new-relay) or in [Changing of the Guards: A Framework for "
"Understanding and Improving Entry Guard Selection in Tor](https://"
"www.freehaven.net/anonbib/cache/wpes12-cogs.pdf)."
msgstr ""
"Fler detaljer finns i [det här blogginlägget](https://blog.torproject.org/"
"blog/lifecycle-of-a-new-relay) och i [Changing of the Guards: A Framework "
"for Understanding and Improving Entry Guard Selection in Tor](https://"
"www.freehaven.net/anonbib/cache/wpes12-cogs.pdf)."

#: content/relays/running/guard-relay-traffic-drop/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/guard-relay-traffic-drop/
msgid ""
"Since it's now a guard, clients are using it less in other positions, but "
"not many clients have rotated their existing guards out to use it as a guard "
"yet."
msgstr ""
"Eftersom reläet nu är en vakt använder klienterna det mer sällan i andra "
"positioner, samtidigt som få klienter ännu har bytt ut sina befintliga "
"vakter för att använda det som vakt."

#: content/relays/running/guard-relay-traffic-drop/contents.lr:tab.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/guard-relay-traffic-drop/
msgid "Guard relay traffic"
msgstr "Trafik för vaktreläer"

#: content/relays/running/ipv6-relay/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/ipv6-relay/
msgid "However, Tor still requires an IPv4 address to run a relay."
msgstr ""
"Tor kräver dock fortfarande en IPv4-adress för att ett relä ska kunna köras."

#: content/relays/running/ipv6-relay/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/ipv6-relay/
msgid ""
"Tor has partial IPv6 support, and relay operators are encouraged to enable "
"IPv6 alongside IPv4 when possible."
msgstr ""
"Tor har partiellt stöd för IPv6 och reläoperatörer uppmuntras att aktivera "
"IPv6 tillsammans med IPv4 när det är möjligt."

#: content/relays/running/ipv6-relay/contents.lr:article.longer_title
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/ipv6-relay/
msgid "Using IPv6 on your Tor relay"
msgstr "Använda IPv6 på Tor-reläet"

#: content/relays/running/ipv6-relay/contents.lr:article.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/ipv6-relay/
msgid "IPv6 on relays"
msgstr "IPv6 på reläer"

#: content/relays/running/ipv6-relay/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/ipv6-relay/
msgid ""
"For the time being Tor will require IPv4 addresses on relays, you can not "
"run a Tor relay on a host with IPv6 addresses only."
msgstr ""
"Tills vidare kräver Tor IPv4-adresser på reläer. Du kan inte köra ett Tor-"
"relä på en värd som endast har IPv6-adresser."

#: content/relays/running/ipv6-relay/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/ipv6-relay/
msgid ""
"Tor [has partial support for IPv6](https://blog.torproject.org/state-of-ipv6-"
"support-tor-network) and we encourage every relay operator to [enable IPv6 "
"functionality](https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/) "
"in their torrc configuration files when IPv6 connectivity is available."
msgstr ""
"Tor [har partiellt stöd för IPv6](https://blog.torproject.org/state-of-ipv6-"
"support-tor-network), och vi uppmuntrar alla reläoperatörer att [aktivera "
"IPv6](https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/) i sina "
"torrc-filer när IPv6-anslutning finns."

#: content/relays/running/relay-offline-keys/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/relay-offline-keys/
msgid ""
"Offline ed25519 keys let relay operators keep their most sensitive identity "
"key offline for better security while using a short-lived signing key on the "
"running relay."
msgstr ""
"Med frånkopplade ed25519-nycklar kan reläoperatören hålla den känsligaste "
"identitetsnyckeln frånkopplad och använda en kortlivad signeringsnyckel på "
"det aktiva reläet."

#: content/relays/running/relay-offline-keys/contents.lr:article.longer_title
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/relay-offline-keys/
msgid ""
"How offline ed25519 identity keys work and what relay operators should know"
msgstr ""
"Så fungerar frånkopplade ed25519-identitetsnycklar och detta bör "
"reläoperatörer känna till"

#: content/relays/running/relay-offline-keys/contents.lr:article.title
#: content/relays/running/relay-offline-keys/contents.lr:tab.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/relay-offline-keys/
msgid "Offline ed25519 identity keys"
msgstr "Frånkopplade ed25519-identitetsnycklar"

#: content/relays/running/relay-offline-keys/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/relay-offline-keys/
msgid ""
"A medium term signing key named \"ed25519_signing_secret_key\" is generated "
"for Tor to use."
msgstr ""
"En medellång signeringsnyckel med namnet ”ed25519_signing_secret_key” skapas "
"för Tor."

#: content/relays/running/relay-offline-keys/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/relay-offline-keys/
msgid ""
"Also, a certificate is generated named \"ed25519_signing_cert\" which is "
"signed by the primary identity secret key and confirms that the medium term "
"signing key is valid for a certain period of time."
msgstr ""
"Dessutom skapas ett certifikat med namnet ”ed25519_signing_cert” som "
"signeras med den primära hemliga identitetsnyckeln och bekräftar att den "
"medellånga signeringsnyckeln är giltig under en viss period."

#: content/relays/running/relay-offline-keys/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/relay-offline-keys/
msgid ""
"If you want to use this feature, you can consult our more [detailed guide]"
"(https://gitlab.torproject.org/legacy/trac/-/wikis/doc/TorRelaySecurity/"
"OfflineKeys) on the topic."
msgstr ""
"Om du vill använda funktionen finns en [utförligare guide](https://"
"gitlab.torproject.org/legacy/trac/-/wikis/doc/TorRelaySecurity/OfflineKeys) "
"om ämnet."

#: content/relays/running/relay-offline-keys/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/relay-offline-keys/
msgid ""
"If you want your relay to run unattended for longer time without having to "
"manually do the medium term signing key renewal on regular basis, best to "
"leave the primary identity secret key in DataDirectory/keys, just make a "
"backup in case you'll need to reinstall it."
msgstr ""
"Om reläet ska kunna köras obevakat under längre tid utan att "
"signeringsnyckeln med medellång giltighet behöver förnyas manuellt "
"regelbundet är det bäst att lämna den primära hemliga identitetsnyckeln i "
"DataDirectory/keys. Säkerhetskopiera den för den händelse att den behöver "
"återställas."

#: content/relays/running/relay-offline-keys/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/relay-offline-keys/
msgid "In simple words, it works like this:"
msgstr "Förenklat fungerar det så här:"

#: content/relays/running/relay-offline-keys/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/relay-offline-keys/
msgid ""
"Offline ed25519 identity keys allow you to protect your relay's long-term "
"identity key by keeping it offline and using a medium-term signing key "
"instead."
msgstr ""
"Med frånkopplade ed25519-identitetsnycklar kan reläets långsiktiga "
"identitetsnyckel skyddas genom att hållas frånkopplad medan en "
"signeringsnyckel med medellång giltighet används."

#: content/relays/running/relay-offline-keys/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/relay-offline-keys/
msgid ""
"The default validity is 30 days, but this can be customized by setting "
"\"SigningKeyLifetime N days|weeks|months\" in torrc."
msgstr ""
"Standardgiltigheten är 30 dagar, men den kan anpassas med "
"”SigningKeyLifetime N days|weeks|months” i torrc."

#: content/relays/running/relay-offline-keys/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/relay-offline-keys/
msgid ""
"There is a primary ed25519 identity secret key file named "
"\"ed25519_master_id_secret_key\"."
msgstr ""
"Det finns en primär hemlig ed25519-identitetsnyckelfil med namnet "
"”ed25519_master_id_secret_key”."

#: content/relays/running/relay-offline-keys/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/relay-offline-keys/
msgid ""
"There is also a primary public key named \"ed25519_master_id_public_key\", "
"which is the actual identity of the relay advertised in the network."
msgstr ""
"Det finns också en primär offentlig nyckel med namnet "
"”ed25519_master_id_public_key”, som är reläets egentliga identitet och "
"annonseras i nätverket."

#: content/relays/running/relay-offline-keys/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/relay-offline-keys/
msgid "This feature is optional, you don't need to use it unless you want to."
msgstr "Funktionen är valfri och behöver bara användas om du vill."

#: content/relays/running/relay-offline-keys/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/relay-offline-keys/
msgid ""
"This is the most important one, so make sure you keep a backup in a secure "
"place - the file is sensitive and should be protected."
msgstr ""
"Det här är den viktigaste nyckeln. Säkerhetskopiera den på en säker plats. "
"Filen är känslig och måste skyddas."

#: content/relays/running/relay-offline-keys/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/relay-offline-keys/
msgid ""
"This one is not sensitive and can be easily computed from "
"\"ed5519_master_id_secret_key\"."
msgstr ""
"Den här är inte känslig och kan enkelt beräknas från "
"”ed5519_master_id_secret_key”."

#: content/relays/running/relay-offline-keys/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/relay-offline-keys/
msgid ""
"Tor could encrypt it for you if you generate it manually and enter a "
"password when asked."
msgstr ""
"Tor kan kryptera den åt dig om du skapar den manuellt och anger ett lösenord "
"när du blir ombedd."

#: content/relays/running/relay-offline-keys/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/relay-offline-keys/
msgid ""
"Tor will only need access to the medium term signing key and certificate as "
"long as they are valid, so the primary identity secret key can be kept "
"outside DataDirectory/keys, on a storage media or a different computer."
msgstr ""
"Tor behöver bara åtkomst till den medellånga signeringsnyckeln och "
"certifikatet så länge de är giltiga. Den primära hemliga identitetsnyckeln "
"kan därför förvaras utanför DataDirectory/keys, på ett lagringsmedium eller "
"en annan dator."

#: content/relays/running/relay-offline-keys/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/relay-offline-keys/
msgid ""
"You'll have to manually renew the medium term signing key and certificate "
"before they expire otherwise the Tor process on the relay will exit upon "
"expiration."
msgstr ""
"Du måste förnya den medellånga signeringsnyckeln och certifikatet manuellt "
"innan de upphör att gälla. Annars avslutas Tor-processen på reläet när "
"giltighetstiden löper ut."

#: content/relays/running/relay-stability/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/relay-stability/
msgid ""
"Occasional downtime is fine, though frequent disconnections can disrupt "
"users."
msgstr ""
"Enstaka driftstopp är inget problem, men täta avbrott kan störa användarna."

#: content/relays/running/relay-stability/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/relay-stability/
msgid ""
"Tor relays don't need to be online 24/7, but the more stable they are, the "
"more useful they become to the network."
msgstr ""
"Tor-reläer behöver inte vara uppkopplade dygnet runt, men ju stabilare de "
"är, desto mer användbara blir de för nätverket."

#: content/relays/running/relay-stability/contents.lr:article.longer_title
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/relay-stability/
msgid "How stable does my relay need to be for the Tor network?"
msgstr "Hur stabilt måste mitt relä vara för Tor-nätverket?"

#: content/relays/running/relay-stability/contents.lr:article.title
#: content/relays/running/relay-stability/contents.lr:tab.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/relay-stability/
msgid "Relay stability"
msgstr "Relästabilitet"

#: content/relays/running/relay-stability/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/relay-stability/
msgid ""
"If you are uncomfortable allowing people to exit from your relay, you can "
"set it up to only allow connections to other Tor relays."
msgstr ""
"Om du inte vill låta människor använda reläet som utgång kan du konfigurera "
"det så att endast anslutningar till andra Tor-reläer tillåts."

#: content/relays/running/relay-stability/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/relay-stability/
msgid "It's fine if the relay goes offline sometimes."
msgstr "Det är inget problem om reläet ibland är frånkopplat."

#: content/relays/running/relay-stability/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/relay-stability/
msgid ""
"Just try to make sure it's not too often, since connections using the relay "
"when it disconnects will break."
msgstr ""
"Försök bara se till att det inte händer alltför ofta, eftersom anslutningar "
"som använder reläet bryts när det kopplas från."

#: content/relays/running/relay-stability/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/relay-stability/
msgid "The directories notice this quickly and stop advertising the relay."
msgstr "Katalogerna upptäcker detta snabbt och slutar annonsera reläet."

#: content/relays/running/relay-stability/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/relay-stability/
msgid "We aim to make setting up a Tor relay easy and convenient:"
msgstr ""
"Vi strävar efter att göra det enkelt och smidigt att konfigurera ett Tor-"
"relä:"

#: content/relays/running/relay-stability/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/relay-stability/
msgid ""
"Your relay will passively estimate and advertise its recent bandwidth "
"capacity, so high-bandwidth relays will attract more users than low-"
"bandwidth ones. Therefore, having low-bandwidth relays is useful too."
msgstr ""
"Reläet uppskattar passivt och annonserar sin senaste bandbreddskapacitet. "
"Reläer med hög bandbredd lockar därför fler användare än reläer med låg "
"bandbredd, men även reläer med låg bandbredd är användbara."

#: content/relays/running/same-relay-identity/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/same-relay-identity/
msgid ""
"When you upgrade or move your Tor relay to a new system, you can preserve "
"its identity and reputation by copying its key files."
msgstr ""
"När du uppgraderar eller flyttar Tor-reläet till ett nytt system kan "
"identiteten och anseendet bevaras genom att nyckelfilerna kopieras."

#: content/relays/running/same-relay-identity/contents.lr:article.longer_title
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/same-relay-identity/
msgid "How to keep your Tor relay identity when upgrading or moving it"
msgstr "Så behåller du Tor-reläets identitet när det uppgraderas eller flyttas"

#: content/relays/running/same-relay-identity/contents.lr:article.title
#: content/relays/running/same-relay-identity/contents.lr:tab.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/same-relay-identity/
msgid "Keeping relay identity"
msgstr "Bevara reläets identitet"

#: content/relays/running/same-relay-identity/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/same-relay-identity/
msgid ""
"For simplicity, just copying over the entire DataDirectory should work too."
msgstr ""
"För enkelhetens skull bör det även fungera att kopiera hela DataDirectory."

#: content/relays/running/same-relay-identity/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/same-relay-identity/
msgid ""
"If you are a bridge operator, also make sure to keep `pt_state/`. It "
"contains data required for your bridge to keep working with the same bridge "
"line."
msgstr ""
"Om du driver en bro måste du även behålla `pt_state/`. Den innehåller data "
"som krävs för att bron ska fortsätta fungera med samma brorad."

#: content/relays/running/same-relay-identity/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/same-relay-identity/
msgid ""
"When upgrading your Tor relay, or moving it to a different computer, be sure "
"to keep the same identity keys (stored in `keys/"
"ed25519_master_id_secret_key` and `keys/secret_id_key` in your "
"DataDirectory)."
msgstr ""
"När du uppgraderar Tor-reläet eller flyttar det till en annan dator måste du "
"behålla samma identitetsnycklar, som finns i `keys/"
"ed25519_master_id_secret_key` och `keys/secret_id_key` i DataDirectory."

#: content/relays/running/same-relay-identity/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/same-relay-identity/
msgid ""
"You may wish to keep backups of these identity keys, plus pt_state for a "
"bridge, so you can restore the relay if something goes wrong."
msgstr ""
"Säkerhetskopiera gärna identitetsnycklarna och, för en bro, även pt_state så "
"att reläet kan återställas om något går fel."

#: content/relays/running/supporting-tor-relays/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/supporting-tor-relays/
msgid ""
"If you're unable to operate your own Tor relay, you can still strengthen the "
"network by donating to independent organizations that run relays."
msgstr ""
"Om du inte kan driva ett eget Tor-relä kan du ändå stärka nätverket genom "
"att donera till oberoende organisationer som driver reläer."

#: content/relays/running/supporting-tor-relays/contents.lr:article.longer_title
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/supporting-tor-relays/
msgid "Ways to support Tor relays if you can't run one yourself"
msgstr "Sätt att stödja Tor-reläer om du inte kan driva ett själv"

#: content/relays/running/supporting-tor-relays/contents.lr:article.title
#: content/relays/running/supporting-tor-relays/contents.lr:tab.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/supporting-tor-relays/
msgid "Supporting Tor Relays"
msgstr "Stöd Tor-reläer"

#: content/relays/running/supporting-tor-relays/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/supporting-tor-relays/
msgid ""
"At the same time though, economies of scale for bandwidth mean that "
"combining many small donations into several larger relays is more efficient "
"at improving network performance."
msgstr ""
"Samtidigt innebär skalfördelar för bandbredd att det är effektivare för "
"nätverkets prestanda att samla många små donationer till några större reläer."

#: content/relays/running/supporting-tor-relays/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/supporting-tor-relays/
msgid ""
"Improving anonymity and improving performance are both worthwhile goals, so "
"however you can help is great!"
msgstr ""
"Både bättre anonymitet och högre prestanda är värdefulla mål, så all hjälp "
"är uppskattad!"

#: content/relays/running/supporting-tor-relays/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/supporting-tor-relays/
msgid ""
"Note that there can be a tradeoff here between anonymity and performance."
msgstr ""
"Observera att det kan finnas en avvägning mellan anonymitet och prestanda."

#: content/relays/running/supporting-tor-relays/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/supporting-tor-relays/
msgid ""
"The Tor network's anonymity comes in part from diversity, so if you are in a "
"position to run your own relay, you will be improving Tor's anonymity more "
"than by donating."
msgstr ""
"Tor-nätverkets anonymitet bygger delvis på mångfald. Om du kan driva ett "
"eget relä förbättrar du därför Tors anonymitet mer än genom att donera."

#: content/relays/running/supporting-tor-relays/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/supporting-tor-relays/
msgid ""
"These organizations are not the same as [The Tor Project, Inc](https://"
"donate.torproject.org/), but we consider that a good thing."
msgstr ""
"Organisationerna är inte samma sak som [The Tor Project, Inc](https://"
"donate.torproject.org/), vilket vi ser som positivt."

#: content/relays/running/supporting-tor-relays/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/supporting-tor-relays/
msgid "They're run by nice people who are part of the Tor community."
msgstr "De drivs av trevliga personer som ingår i Tor-gemenskapen."

#: content/relays/running/supporting-tor-relays/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/relays/running/supporting-tor-relays/
msgid ""
"We have a [list of organizations that run Tor relays](https://"
"community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/relay-associations/) that "
"are happy to turn your donations into better speed and anonymity for the Tor "
"network."
msgstr ""
"Vi har en [förteckning över organisationer som driver Tor-reläer](https://"
"community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/relay-associations/) och "
"gärna omvandlar dina donationer till bättre hastighet och anonymitet i Tor-"
"nätverket."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/
msgid ""
"In some countries, Internet service providers or national firewalls block "
"direct access to the Tor network."
msgstr ""
"I vissa länder blockerar internetleverantörer eller nationella brandväggar "
"direkt åtkomst till Tor-nätverket."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/
msgid ""
"This page offers country-specific guidance on getting Tor Browser connected "
"when access is censored."
msgstr ""
"Den här sidan ger landsspecifik vägledning om hur Tor Browser ansluts när "
"åtkomsten censureras."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/
msgid ""
"Tor Browser includes built-in support for bridges and other circumvention "
"tools, but in censored regions you may still need to select or request a "
"bridge to connect successfully."
msgstr ""
"Tor Browser har inbyggt stöd för broar och andra kringgåendeverktyg, men i "
"censurerade regioner kan du ändå behöva välja eller begära en bro för att "
"ansluta."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/contents.lr:article.longer_title
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/
msgid ""
"How to bypass censorship and connect to Tor from different countries or "
"regions"
msgstr ""
"Så kringgår du censur och ansluter till Tor från olika länder eller regioner"

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/contents.lr:article.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/
msgid "Connecting to Tor from censored regions"
msgstr "Ansluta till Tor från censurerade regioner"

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/
msgid ""
"**(Optional but recommended)**. [Verify](../../getting-started/verifying-tor-"
"browser/) Tor Browser's signature."
msgstr ""
"**(Valfritt men rekommenderat.)** [Verifiera](../../getting-started/"
"verifying-tor-browser/) Tor Browsers signatur."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/
msgid "**Using Snowflake with Tor Browser for Android**"
msgstr "**Använda Snowflake med Tor Browser för Android**"

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/
msgid "**Using Snowflake with Tor Browser for Desktop**"
msgstr "**Använda Snowflake med Tor Browser för datorer**"

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/
msgid ""
"**[Snowflake](../../../anti-censorship/what-is-snowflake/):** uses ephemeral "
"proxies to connect to the Tor network."
msgstr ""
"**[Snowflake](../../../anti-censorship/what-is-snowflake/):** använder "
"tillfälliga proxyservrar för att ansluta till Tor-nätverket."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/
msgid ""
"**meek:** makes it look like you are browsing a website instead of using Tor."
msgstr ""
"**meek:** får det att se ut som om du besöker en webbplats i stället för att "
"använda Tor."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/
msgid ""
"1. Click \"Settings\" in the hamburger menu (≡) and then go to "
"\"Connection\" in the sidebar."
msgstr ""
"1. Klicka på ”Inställningar” i hamburgermenyn (≡) och gå sedan till "
"”Anslutning” i sidofältet."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/
msgid "1. Direct connection"
msgstr "1. Direktanslutning"

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/
msgid "1. Get Tor Browser safely"
msgstr "1. Hämta Tor Browser säkert"

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/
msgid "1. Tap \"Configure connection\" when on the \"Connect to Tor\" screen."
msgstr "1. Tryck på ”Konfigurera anslutningen” på skärmen ”Anslut till Tor”."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/
msgid ""
"2. In the \"Bridges\" section, from the option \"Choose from one of Tor "
"Browser's built-in bridges\" select \"Snowflake\"."
msgstr ""
"2. Under ”Broar” väljer du ”Snowflake” i alternativet ”Välj en av Tor "
"Browsers inbyggda broar”."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/
msgid "2. Navigate to the \"Connection\" section in Settings."
msgstr "2. Gå till avsnittet \"Anslutning\" i inställningarna."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/
msgid "2. Try Connection Assist first"
msgstr "2. Prova först anslutningshjälpen"

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/
msgid "2. Using a Tor bridge"
msgstr "2. Använda en Tor-bro"

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/
msgid "3. Bridge options that work in China"
msgstr "3. Broalternativ som fungerar i Kina"

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/
msgid "3. Tap \"Config Bridge\" to configure a bridge."
msgstr "3. Tryck på ”Konfigurera bro” för att konfigurera en bro."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/
msgid "4. Getting help"
msgstr "4. Få hjälp"

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/
msgid "4. With the \"Use a Bridge\" option select \"Snowflake\"."
msgstr "4. Välj ”Snowflake” under alternativet ”Använd en bro”."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/
msgid "5. Return to the \"Connect to Tor\" screen and tap \"Connect\"."
msgstr "5. Gå tillbaka till skärmen ”Anslut till Tor” och tryck på ”Anslut”."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/
msgid ""
"After the installation, Tor Browser will try to connect to the Tor network."
msgstr "Efter installationen försöker Tor Browser ansluta till Tor-nätverket."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/
msgid ""
"At the moment, we aren't aware of any specific bridge blocking mechanism in "
"Belarus, so you can use obfs4, WebTunnel bridges, or snowflake."
msgstr ""
"För närvarande känner vi inte till någon särskild metod som blockerar broar "
"i Belarus, så du kan använda obfs4-, WebTunnel- eller Snowflake-broar."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/contents.lr:content.content
#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/contents.lr:tab.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/
msgid "Belarus"
msgstr "Belarus"

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/
msgid ""
"Below are reliable ways to obtain Tor Browser and connect from within China."
msgstr ""
"Nedan finns tillförlitliga sätt att hämta Tor Browser och ansluta från Kina."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/
msgid ""
"But if that doesn't work, the next step will be to obtain a bridge that "
"works in China."
msgstr ""
"Om det inte fungerar är nästa steg att skaffa en bro som fungerar i Kina."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/contents.lr:content.content
#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/contents.lr:tab.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/
msgid "China"
msgstr "Kina"

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/
msgid "Download Tor Browser"
msgstr "Hämta Tor Browser"

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/
msgid ""
"Find up-to-date instructions on how to circumvent censorship and connect to "
"Tor from Russia on our forum guide: [Tor blocked in Russia - how to "
"circumvent censorship](https://forum.torproject.org/t/tor-blocked-in-russia-"
"how-to-circumvent-censorship/982)."
msgstr ""
"Aktuella anvisningar om hur du kringgår censur och ansluter till Tor från "
"Ryssland finns i vår forumguide: [Tor blocked in Russia - how to circumvent "
"censorship](https://forum.torproject.org/t/tor-blocked-in-russia-how-to-"
"circumvent-censorship/982)."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/
msgid ""
"Follow instructions to [enter the bridge addresses](../using-bridges/) in "
"Tor Browser."
msgstr ""
"Följ anvisningarna för att [ange bro-adresserna](../using-bridges/) i Tor "
"Browser."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/
msgid ""
"From the \"Advanced options\" select \"WebTunnel\", from the dropdown, as "
"the pluggable transport."
msgstr ""
"Välj ”WebTunnel” som pluggbar transport i listrutan under ”Avancerade "
"alternativ”."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/
msgid "Getting support"
msgstr "Få support"

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/
msgid ""
"However, because it has a bandwidth limitation, this option will be quite "
"slow."
msgstr ""
"Eftersom alternativet har en bandbreddsbegränsning blir det dock ganska "
"långsamt."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/
msgid ""
"If Tor is blocked in your location, Connection Assist will try to "
"automatically connect using a bridge or Snowflake."
msgstr ""
"Om Tor är blockerat där du befinner dig försöker anslutningshjälpen ansluta "
"automatiskt med en bro eller Snowflake."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/
msgid ""
"If WebTunnel does not work, you can try the following options from [Tor "
"Browser's built-in bridge menu](../unblocking-tor/#using-pluggable-"
"transports):"
msgstr ""
"Om WebTunnel inte fungerar kan du prova följande alternativ i [Tor Browsers "
"meny med inbyggda broar](../unblocking-tor/#using-pluggable-transports):"

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/
msgid ""
"If that doesn't work, you can send an email to [gettor@torproject.org]"
"(mailto:gettor@torproject.org) with the subject \"windows\", \"macos\", "
"\"linux\" or \"android\" for the respective operating system."
msgstr ""
"Om det inte fungerar skickar du ett e-postmeddelande till "
"[gettor@torproject.org](mailto:gettor@torproject.org) med ämnet ”windows”, "
"”macos”, ”linux” eller ”android” för respektive operativsystem."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/
msgid "If the direct connection doesn't work, try using Snowflake."
msgstr "Om den direkta anslutningen inte fungerar provar du Snowflake."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/
msgid ""
"If the direct connection to the Tor network didn't work, you may need to use "
"a Tor bridge."
msgstr ""
"Om den direkta anslutningen till Tor-nätverket inte fungerar kan du behöva "
"använda en Tor-bro."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/
msgid ""
"If you are connecting to Tor from Belarus, there are several options you can "
"try."
msgstr "Om du ansluter till Tor från Belarus finns flera alternativ att prova."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/
msgid "If you have Tor Browser running:"
msgstr "Om Tor Browser redan körs:"

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/
msgid ""
"If you need help, contact us via [Telegram](https://t.me/"
"TorProjectSupportBot), [WhatsApp](https://wa.me/4474210006120), [Signal]"
"(https://signal.me/#p/+17787431312), or by email [frontdesk@torproject.org]"
"(mailto:frontdesk@torproject.org)."
msgstr ""
"Behöver du hjälp kan du kontakta oss via [Telegram](https://t.me/"
"TorProjectSupportBot), [WhatsApp](https://wa.me/4474210006120), [Signal]"
"(https://signal.me/#p/+17787431312) eller e-post på "
"[frontdesk@torproject.org](mailto:frontdesk@torproject.org)."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/
msgid ""
"If you need help, you can contact our support team on Telegram [Tor Project "
"Support](https://t.me/TorProjectSupportBot) and [Signal](https://signal.me/"
"#p/+17787431312)."
msgstr ""
"Behöver du hjälp kan du kontakta supportteamet på Telegram via [Tor Project "
"Support](https://t.me/TorProjectSupportBot) eller på [Signal](https://"
"signal.me/#p/+17787431312)."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/
msgid ""
"In Turkmenistan, direct access to the Tor network is heavily restricted."
msgstr ""
"I Turkmenistan är direkt åtkomst till Tor-nätverket kraftigt begränsad."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/
msgid ""
"In those cases, switching to WebTunnel bridges hosted on less well-known "
"providers (rather than major hosts like OVH, Hetzner, Linode, or "
"DigitalOcean) can help you bypass these restrictions."
msgstr ""
"I sådana fall kan du kringgå begränsningarna genom att byta till WebTunnel-"
"broar hos mindre kända leverantörer i stället för stora värdar som OVH, "
"Hetzner, Linode eller DigitalOcean."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/
msgid ""
"It's also possible to connect using obfs4 bridges, but users need to find "
"bridges hosted on less-well-known providers rather than major hosting "
"companies, since they are frequently blocked."
msgstr ""
"Det går också att ansluta med obfs4-broar, men användaren behöver hitta "
"broar hos mindre kända leverantörer i stället för stora webbhotellsföretag, "
"eftersom de ofta blockeras."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/
msgid "It's available in Tor Browser and other Tor powered apps like Orbot."
msgstr "Det finns i Tor Browser och andra Tor-baserade appar som Orbot."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/
msgid ""
"Next, tap on 'webtunnel bridges' or type `/webtunnel` and copy the bridge "
"addresses."
msgstr ""
"Tryck sedan på ”webtunnel bridges” eller skriv `/webtunnel` och kopiera bro-"
"adresserna."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/
msgid "Open Tor Browser and click or tap \"Connect\"."
msgstr "Öppna Tor Browser och klicka eller tryck på ”Anslut”."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/
msgid ""
"Or send an email to [frontdesk@torproject.org]"
"(mailto:frontdesk@torproject.org) with the phrase **\"connect cn\"** in the "
"subject of the email."
msgstr ""
"Eller skicka ett e-postmeddelande till [frontdesk@torproject.org]"
"(mailto:frontdesk@torproject.org) med frasen **\"connect cn\"** i ämnesraden."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/contents.lr:content.content
#: content/tor-browser/getting-started/first-launch/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/getting-started/first-launch/
msgid "Other options"
msgstr "Andra alternativ"

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/contents.lr:content.content
#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/contents.lr:tab.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/
msgid "Russia"
msgstr "Ryssland"

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/
msgid ""
"Send a message to [@GetBridgesBot](https://t.me/GetBridgesBot) on Telegram."
msgstr ""
"Skicka ett meddelande till [@GetBridgesBot](https://t.me/GetBridgesBot) på "
"Telegram."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/
msgid ""
"Since December 2021, many Internet providers in Russia have been blocking "
"direct connections to the Tor network, so users generally need to connect "
"through a bridge."
msgstr ""
"Sedan december 2021 har många internetleverantörer i Ryssland blockerat "
"direkta anslutningar till Tor-nätverket, så användarna behöver vanligtvis "
"ansluta via en bro."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/
msgid "Start the chat with the bot and type the command `/obfs4`."
msgstr "Starta chatten med boten och skriv kommandot `/obfs4`."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/
msgid "Start the chat with the bot and type the command `/webtunnel`."
msgstr "Starta chatten med boten och skriv kommandot `/webtunnel`."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/
msgid ""
"Support for WebTunnel bridges is available on Tor Browser for Desktop and "
"Android, Tails and Tor VPN Beta."
msgstr ""
"Stöd för WebTunnel-broar finns i Tor Browser för datorer och Android, Tails "
"och Tor VPN Beta."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/contents.lr:content.content
#: content/tor-browser/getting-started/downloading/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/getting-started/downloading/
msgid "Tap on 'Start' or write `/start` in the chat."
msgstr "Tryck på 'Start' eller skriv `/start` i chatten."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/
msgid ""
"The first and easiest option to try is a direct connection to Tor, which "
"could be available on some ISPs."
msgstr ""
"Det första och enklaste alternativet är att prova en direktanslutning till "
"Tor, som kan fungera hos vissa internetleverantörer."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/
msgid ""
"The most reliable way to connect with Tor Browser is usually through "
"Snowflake, and using AMP cache as the front domain."
msgstr ""
"Det mest tillförlitliga sättet att ansluta med Tor Browser är vanligtvis "
"Snowflake med AMP-cache som frontdomän."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/
msgid ""
"The obfs4 bridge type remains the most widely used in Russia, but some "
"mobile ISPs have begun blocking it through Deep Packet Inspection (DPI)."
msgstr ""
"Brotypen obfs4 är fortfarande vanligast i Ryssland, men vissa "
"mobiloperatörer har börjat blockera den med djup paketinspektion (DPI)."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/
msgid "Then click on \"Get Bridges\"."
msgstr "Klicka sedan på ”Hämta broar”."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/
msgid ""
"To get WebTunnel bridges please use our Telegram bot: [@getbridgesbot]"
"(https://t.me/getbridgesbot)."
msgstr ""
"Använd vår Telegram-bot för att hämta WebTunnel-broar: [@getbridgesbot]"
"(https://t.me/getbridgesbot)."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/
msgid ""
"To get an updated version of Tor Browser, try our Telegram bot: [@GetTor_bot]"
"(https://t.me/gettor_bot)."
msgstr ""
"Prova vår Telegram-bot för att hämta en uppdaterad version av Tor Browser: "
"[@GetTor_bot](https://t.me/gettor_bot)."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/
msgid ""
"To get an updated version of Tor Browser, try the Telegram bot first: "
"[@gettor_bot](https://t.me/gettor_bot)."
msgstr ""
"Prova först Telegram-boten för att hämta en uppdaterad version av Tor "
"Browser: [@gettor_bot](https://t.me/gettor_bot)."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/
msgid ""
"To get obfs4 bridges please use our Telegram bot: [@getbridgesbot](https://"
"t.me/getbridgesbot)."
msgstr ""
"Använd vår Telegram-bot för att hämta obfs4-broar: [@getbridgesbot](https://"
"t.me/getbridgesbot)."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/
msgid "To obtain WebTunnel bridges you can use one of the following methods:"
msgstr "Du kan hämta WebTunnel-broar på något av följande sätt:"

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/
msgid "Try connecting to Tor using **WebTunnel** bridges."
msgstr "Prova att ansluta till Tor med **WebTunnel**-broar."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/contents.lr:content.content
#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/contents.lr:tab.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/
msgid "Turkmenistan"
msgstr "Turkmenistan"

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/
msgid "Visit our [bridges website](https://bridges.torproject.org/options)."
msgstr ""
"Besök vår [webbplats för broar](https://bridges.torproject.org/options)."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/
msgid ""
"WebTunnel makes the traffic look like a regular HTTPS connection to a "
"webpage server giving the impression that the user is simply browsing the "
"web."
msgstr ""
"WebTunnel får trafiken att likna en vanlig HTTPS-anslutning till en "
"webbserver, så att det ser ut som om användaren bara surfar på webben."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/
msgid ""
"When you reach out, include \"private bridge by\" in your message (subject "
"line or chat text) so our team can send you the right instructions more "
"quickly."
msgstr ""
"Ta med ”private bridge by” i meddelandet, i ämnesraden eller chatttexten, så "
"att teamet snabbare kan skicka rätt anvisningar."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/
msgid ""
"When you reach out, include \"private bridge ru\" in your message (subject "
"line or chat text) so our team can send you the right instructions more "
"quickly."
msgstr ""
"Ta med ”private bridge ru” i meddelandet, i ämnesraden eller chatttexten, så "
"att teamet snabbare kan skicka rätt anvisningar."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/connecting-from-censored-regions/
msgid ""
"When you reach out, include \"private bridge tm\" in your message (subject "
"line or chat text) so our team can send you the right instructions more "
"quickly."
msgstr ""
"Ta med ”private bridge tm” i meddelandet, i ämnesraden eller chatttexten, så "
"att teamet snabbare kan skicka rätt anvisningar."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/contents.lr:section.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/
msgid "What to do if the Tor network is blocked."
msgstr "Det här gör du om Tor-nätverket är blockerat."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/contents.lr:section.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/
msgid "Censorship circumvention"
msgstr "Kringgå censur"

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/getting-bridges/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/getting-bridges/
msgid ""
"Because bridge addresses are not public, you will need to request them "
"yourself."
msgstr "Eftersom bro-adresser inte är offentliga måste du själv begära dem."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/getting-bridges/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/getting-bridges/
msgid ""
"You have a few options: moat (inside Tor Browser), the Tor Project website, "
"our Telegram bot, or email."
msgstr ""
"Du har flera alternativ: moat i Tor Browser, Tor-projektets webbplats, vår "
"Telegram-bot eller e-post."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/getting-bridges/contents.lr:article.longer_title
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/getting-bridges/
msgid "Where to find Tor bridges?"
msgstr "Var hittar jag Tor-broar?"

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/getting-bridges/contents.lr:article.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/getting-bridges/
msgid "Getting bridges"
msgstr "Hämta broar"

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/getting-bridges/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/getting-bridges/
msgid ""
"1. Send a message to [@GetBridgesBot](https://t.me/GetBridgesBot) on "
"Telegram."
msgstr ""
"1. Skicka ett meddelande till [@GetBridgesBot](https://t.me/GetBridgesBot) "
"på Telegram."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/getting-bridges/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/getting-bridges/
msgid "1. Visit our [bridges website](https://bridges.torproject.org/options)."
msgstr ""
"1. Besök vår [webbplats för broar](https://bridges.torproject.org/options)."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/getting-bridges/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/getting-bridges/
msgid "2. Click on 'Just give me bridges!' and copy the bridge lines."
msgstr "2. Klicka på ”Just give me bridges!” och kopiera broraderna."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/getting-bridges/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/getting-bridges/
msgid "2. Tap on 'Start' or write `/start` in the chat."
msgstr "2. Tryck på ”Start” eller skriv `/start` i chatten."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/getting-bridges/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/getting-bridges/
msgid ""
"3. Or use advanced options to select the type of [pluggable transport]"
"(../../../glossary/#pluggable-transports) and only get bridges with a [IPv6 "
"address](../../../glossary/#ip-address)."
msgstr ""
"3. Du kan också använda de avancerade alternativen för att välja typ av "
"[pluggbar transport](../../../glossary/#pluggable-transports) och endast få "
"broar med en [IPv6-adress](../../../glossary/#ip-address)."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/getting-bridges/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/getting-bridges/
msgid "3. To get bridges, type `/obfs4` or `/webtunnel`."
msgstr "3. Skriv `/obfs4` eller `/webtunnel` för att få broar."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/getting-bridges/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/getting-bridges/
msgid "4. Copy the bridge addresses."
msgstr "4. Kopiera bro-adresserna."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/getting-bridges/contents.lr:content.content
#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/using-bridges/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/getting-bridges/
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/using-bridges/
msgid "Click \"Connect\" to save your settings."
msgstr "Klicka på ”Anslut” för att spara inställningarna."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/getting-bridges/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/getting-bridges/
msgid "Complete the Captcha and click \"Submit\"."
msgstr "Lös CAPTCHA-testet och klicka på ”Skicka”."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/getting-bridges/contents.lr:content.content
#: content/tor-vpn/circumvention/using-bridges/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/getting-bridges/
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-vpn/circumvention/using-bridges/
msgid ""
"Email [bridges@torproject.org](mailto:bridges@torproject.org) from a Gmail "
"or Riseup email address and copy the bridge addresses received in the email."
msgstr ""
"Skicka ett e-postmeddelande till [bridges@torproject.org]"
"(mailto:bridges@torproject.org) från en Gmail- eller Riseup-adress och "
"kopiera bro-adresserna i svaret."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/getting-bridges/contents.lr:content.content
#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/using-bridges/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/getting-bridges/
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/using-bridges/
msgid ""
"If you're starting Tor Browser for the first time, click on \"Configure "
"Connection\" to open the Tor settings window."
msgstr ""
"Om du startar Tor Browser för första gången klickar du på ”Konfigurera "
"anslutningen” för att öppna Tor-inställningarna."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/getting-bridges/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/getting-bridges/
msgid ""
"In the \"Bridges\" section, locate the option to \"Find more bridges\" and "
"click on \"Request bridges\" for Tor Project to provide a bridge."
msgstr ""
"Leta reda på alternativet ”Hitta fler broar” i avsnittet ”Broar” och klicka "
"på ”Begär broar” för att få en bro från Tor-projektet."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/getting-bridges/contents.lr:content.content
#: content/tor-vpn/circumvention/using-bridges/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/getting-bridges/
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-vpn/circumvention/using-bridges/
msgid "Obtain bridges from the Bridges website"
msgstr "Skaffa broar från Bridges-webbplats"

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/getting-bridges/contents.lr:content.content
#: content/tor-vpn/circumvention/using-bridges/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/getting-bridges/
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-vpn/circumvention/using-bridges/
msgid "Obtain bridges via Email"
msgstr "Skaffa broar via e-post"

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/getting-bridges/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/getting-bridges/
msgid "Obtain bridges via Telegram Bot"
msgstr "Hämta broar via Telegram-boten"

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/getting-bridges/contents.lr:content.content
#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/unblocking-tor/contents.lr:content.content
#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/using-bridges/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/getting-bridges/
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/unblocking-tor/
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/using-bridges/
msgid ""
"Or, if you have Tor Browser running, click on \"Settings\" in the [hamburger "
"menu (≡)](../../../glossary/#hamburger-menu) and then on \"Connection\" in "
"the sidebar."
msgstr ""
"Om Tor Browser redan körs klickar du på ”Inställningar” i [hamburgermenyn "
"(≡)](../../../glossary/#hamburger-menu) och sedan på ”Anslutning” i "
"sidofältet."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/getting-bridges/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/getting-bridges/
msgid "Request bridges from within Tor Browser"
msgstr "Begär broar inifrån Tor Browser"

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/getting-bridges/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/getting-bridges/
msgid "Your setting will automatically be saved once you close the tab."
msgstr "Din inställning sparas automatiskt när du stänger fliken."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/getting-bridges/contents.lr:tab.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/getting-bridges/
msgid "Moat"
msgstr "Moat"

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/getting-bridges/contents.lr:tab.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/getting-bridges/
msgid "Telegram Bot"
msgstr "Telegram-bot"

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/getting-bridges/contents.lr:tab.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/getting-bridges/
msgid "Website"
msgstr "Webbplats"

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/unblocking-tor/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/unblocking-tor/
msgid ""
"Direct access to the Tor network may sometimes be blocked by your Internet "
"Service Provider or by a government. Tor Browser includes some circumvention "
"tools for getting around these blocks. These tools are called \"pluggable "
"transports\"."
msgstr ""
"Direkt åtkomst till Tor-nätverket kan ibland blockeras av "
"internetleverantören eller en regering. Tor Browser innehåller "
"kringgåendeverktyg för att ta sig förbi blockeringarna. Verktygen kallas "
"”pluggbara transporter”."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/unblocking-tor/contents.lr:article.longer_title
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/unblocking-tor/
msgid "What to do if access to Tor is blocked?"
msgstr "Vad gör jag om åtkomsten till Tor är blockerad?"

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/unblocking-tor/contents.lr:article.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/unblocking-tor/
msgid "Unblocking Tor"
msgstr "Häv blockeringen av Tor"

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/unblocking-tor/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/unblocking-tor/
msgid ""
"Bridges help you securely access the Tor network in places where Tor is "
"blocked."
msgstr ""
"Broar hjälper dig att säkert nå Tor-nätverket på platser där Tor är "
"blockerat."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/unblocking-tor/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/unblocking-tor/
msgid ""
"Choose whichever pluggable transport you'd like to use from the menu and "
"click on \"OK\"."
msgstr ""
"Välj vilken pluggbar transport du vill använda från menyn och klicka på "
"\"OK\"."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/unblocking-tor/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/unblocking-tor/
msgid ""
"Currently there are four pluggable transports available, but more are being "
"developed."
msgstr ""
"För närvarande finns det fyra pluggbara transporter tillgängliga, men fler "
"är under utveckling."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/unblocking-tor/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/unblocking-tor/
msgid ""
"Each of the transports listed in Tor Bridge's menu works in a different way, "
"and their effectiveness depends on your individual circumstances."
msgstr ""
"Var och en av transporterna som listas i meny för Tor-broar fungerar på "
"olika sätt, och deras effektivitet beror på dina individuella omständigheter."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/unblocking-tor/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/unblocking-tor/
msgid ""
"If you are trying to circumvent a blocked connection for the first time, you "
"should try the different transports: obfs4, webtunnel, snowflake, or meek."
msgstr ""
"Om du försöker kringgå en blockerad anslutning för första gången bör du "
"prova de olika transporterna: obfs4, WebTunnel, Snowflake eller meek."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/unblocking-tor/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/unblocking-tor/
msgid ""
"If you try all of these options, and none of them gets you online, you will "
"need to request a bridge or manually enter bridge addresses."
msgstr ""
"Om inget av alternativen fungerar måste du begära en bro eller ange bro-"
"adresser manuellt."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/unblocking-tor/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/unblocking-tor/
msgid ""
"In Tor Browser, **Lyrebird** is the name of Tor's program that implements "
"several pluggable transport protocols, including obfs4, meek, Snowflake, and "
"WebTunnel."
msgstr ""
"I Tor Browser är **Lyrebird** namnet på Tors program som implementerar flera "
"protokoll för pluggbara transporter, däribland obfs4, meek, Snowflake och "
"WebTunnel."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/unblocking-tor/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/unblocking-tor/
msgid ""
"It also implements the ability to request bridges and supports Connection "
"Assist."
msgstr "Det kan även begära broar och har stöd för anslutningshjälpen."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/unblocking-tor/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/unblocking-tor/
msgid ""
"Like ordinary Tor relays, bridges are run by volunteers; unlike ordinary "
"relays, however, they are not listed publicly, so an adversary cannot "
"identify them easily."
msgstr ""
"Liksom vanliga Tor-reläer drivs broar av volontärer; till skillnad från "
"vanliga reläer är de dock inte noterade offentligt, så en motståndare kan "
"inte identifiera dem enkelt."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/unblocking-tor/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/unblocking-tor/
msgid ""
"Most pluggable transports, such as obfs4, rely on the use of \"bridge\" "
"relays."
msgstr ""
"De flesta pluggbara transporter, exempelvis obfs4, bygger på användning av "
"”broreläer”."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/unblocking-tor/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/unblocking-tor/
msgid ""
"Once you've selected the pluggable transport, click on \"Connect\" to save "
"your settings."
msgstr ""
"När du har valt den pluggbara transporten klickar du på \"Anslut\" för att "
"spara dina inställningar."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/unblocking-tor/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/unblocking-tor/
msgid ""
"Other pluggable transports, like meek and Snowflake, use different anti-"
"censorship techniques that do not rely on finding bridge addresses. You do "
"not need to obtain bridge addresses in order to use these transports."
msgstr ""
"Andra pluggbara transporter, exempelvis meek och Snowflake, använder andra "
"metoder mot censur som inte kräver att bro-adresser hittas. Du behöver inte "
"skaffa bro-adresser för att använda dem."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/unblocking-tor/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/unblocking-tor/
msgid ""
"Read the [Getting bridges](../getting-bridges/) section to learn how to "
"obtain them."
msgstr ""
"Läs avsnittet [Hämta broar](../getting-bridges/) för att se hur du får dem."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/unblocking-tor/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/unblocking-tor/
msgid ""
"To use a pluggable transport, click \"Configure Connection\" when starting "
"Tor Browser for the first time. Under the \"Bridges\" section, locate the "
"option \"Choose from one of Tor Browser's built-in bridges\" and click on "
"\"Select a Built-In Bridge\" option. From the menu, select whichever "
"pluggable transport you'd like to use."
msgstr ""
"Om du vill använda en pluggbar transport klickar du på ”Konfigurera "
"anslutningen” när Tor Browser startas första gången. Under ”Broar” hittar du "
"alternativet ”Välj en av Tor Browsers inbyggda broar” och klickar på ”Välj "
"en inbyggd bro”. Välj sedan önskad pluggbar transport i menyn."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/unblocking-tor/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/unblocking-tor/
msgid "Types of Pluggable Transport"
msgstr "Typer av pluggbara transporter"

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/unblocking-tor/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/unblocking-tor/
msgid "Using Pluggable Transports"
msgstr "Använda pluggbara transporter"

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/unblocking-tor/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/unblocking-tor/
msgid ""
"Using bridges in combination with pluggable transports helps circumvent "
"blocks against Tor, but may slow down the connection compared to using "
"ordinary Tor relays."
msgstr ""
"Broar tillsammans med pluggbara transporter hjälper till att kringgå "
"blockeringar av Tor, men anslutningen kan bli långsammare än med vanliga Tor-"
"reläer."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/unblocking-tor/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/unblocking-tor/
msgid "What are bridges?"
msgstr "Vad är broar?"

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/unblocking-tor/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/unblocking-tor/
msgid "Which transport should I use?"
msgstr "Vilken transport bör jag använda?"

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/unblocking-tor/contents.lr:content.content
#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/using-bridges/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/unblocking-tor/
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/using-bridges/
msgid "Your settings will automatically be saved once you close the tab."
msgstr "Dina inställningar sparas automatiskt när du stänger fliken."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/unblocking-tor/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/unblocking-tor/
msgid "| Pluggable Transport | Description     |"
msgstr "| Pluggbar transport | Beskrivning     |"

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/unblocking-tor/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/unblocking-tor/
msgid ""
"| Snowflake           | Snowflake routes your connection through volunteer-"
"operated proxies to make it look like you're placing a video call instead of "
"using Tor. |"
msgstr ""
"| Snowflake           | Snowflake leder anslutningen genom volontärdrivna "
"proxyservrar så att det ser ut som om du ringer ett videosamtal i stället "
"för att använda Tor. |"

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/unblocking-tor/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/unblocking-tor/
msgid ""
"| WebTunnel           | WebTunnel masks your Tor connection, making it "
"appear as if you're accessing a website via HTTPS. |"
msgstr ""
"| WebTunnel           | WebTunnel maskerar Tor-anslutningen så att den ser "
"ut som åtkomst till en webbplats via HTTPS. |"

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/unblocking-tor/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/unblocking-tor/
msgid ""
"| meek                | meek transports make it look like you are browsing a "
"major web site instead of using Tor. meek makes it look like you are using a "
"web site from a CDN or cloud provider. |"
msgstr ""
"| meek                | meek-transporter får det att se ut som om du besöker "
"en stor webbplats i stället för att använda Tor. meek får det att se ut som "
"om du använder en webbplats hos ett CDN eller en molnleverantör. |"

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/unblocking-tor/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/unblocking-tor/
msgid ""
"| obfs4               | obfs4 makes Tor traffic look random, and also "
"prevents censors from finding bridges by Internet scanning. obfs4 bridges "
"are less likely to be blocked than its predecessors, obfs3 bridges. |"
msgstr ""
"| obfs4               | obfs4 får Tor-trafiken att se slumpmässig ut och "
"hindrar censuraktörer från att hitta broar genom internetskanning. obfs4-"
"broar blockeras mer sällan än föregångaren obfs3. |"

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/unblocking-tor/contents.lr:figure.text
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/unblocking-tor/
msgid "Configure built-in bridges"
msgstr "Konfigurera inbyggda broar"

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/unblocking-tor/contents.lr:tab.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/unblocking-tor/
msgid "Pluggable Transport"
msgstr "Pluggbar transport"

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/using-bridges/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/using-bridges/
msgid ""
"Bridges are alternative entry nodes to the Tor network that help bypass "
"censorship when direct connections are blocked."
msgstr ""
"Broar är alternativa ingångsnoder till Tor-nätverket som hjälper till att "
"kringgå censur när direktanslutningar blockeras."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/using-bridges/contents.lr:article.description
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/using-bridges/
msgid ""
"Learn how to configure Tor Browser to use bridges on desktop and Android."
msgstr ""
"Lär dig konfigurera Tor Browser för att använda broar på datorer och Android."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/using-bridges/contents.lr:article.longer_title
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/using-bridges/
msgid "Configure Tor Browser to use bridges"
msgstr "Konfigurera Tor Browser för att använda broar"

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/using-bridges/contents.lr:article.title
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/using-bridges/
msgid "Using bridges"
msgstr "Använda broar"

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/using-bridges/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/using-bridges/
msgid ""
"1. Tap on \"Configure Connection\" or tap on 'Settings' (⚙️), scroll down to "
"the \"Connection\" section and tap on \"Config Bridge\"."
msgstr ""
"1. Tryck på ”Konfigurera anslutningen” eller på ”Inställningar” (⚙️), rulla "
"ned till avsnittet ”Anslutning” och tryck på ”Konfigurera bro”."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/using-bridges/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/using-bridges/
msgid ""
"1. Tap on \"Settings\" (⚙️) and then scroll to the \"Connection\" section of "
"the settings."
msgstr ""
"1. Tryck på \"Inställningar\" (⚙️) och bläddra sedan till avsnittet "
"\"Anslutning\" i inställningarna."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/using-bridges/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/using-bridges/
msgid "2. Tap on \"Config Bridge\"."
msgstr "2. Klicka på \"Konfigurera bro\"."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/using-bridges/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/using-bridges/
msgid "2. Toggle on \"Use a Bridge\"."
msgstr "2. Aktivera ”Använd en bro”."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/using-bridges/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/using-bridges/
msgid "3. Tap on \"Provide a Bridge I know\"."
msgstr "3. Tryck på ”Ange en bro som jag känner till”."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/using-bridges/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/using-bridges/
msgid "3. Toggle on \"Use a Bridge\" and select \"Provide a Bridge I know\"."
msgstr ""
"3. Aktivera ”Använd en bro” och välj ”Ange en bro som jag känner till”."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/using-bridges/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/using-bridges/
msgid "4. Enter the bridge address."
msgstr "4. Ange bro-adressen."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/using-bridges/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/using-bridges/
msgid "4. Paste the bridge addresses in the input prompt."
msgstr "4. Klistra in bro-adresserna i inmatningsfältet."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/using-bridges/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/using-bridges/
msgid "BRIDGE-MOJI"
msgstr "BRO-EMOJI"

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/using-bridges/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/using-bridges/
msgid ""
"Each bridge address is represented by a string of emoji characters called "
"Bridge-mojis. The Bridge-mojis can be used to validate that the intended "
"bridge has been added successfully."
msgstr ""
"Varje bro-adress representeras av en emoji-sträng som kallas bro-emojier. De "
"kan användas för att kontrollera att rätt bro har lagts till."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/using-bridges/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/using-bridges/
msgid ""
"If the connection fails, the bridges you received may be down. Please use "
"one of the [methods to obtain more bridges](../getting-bridges), and try "
"again."
msgstr ""
"Om anslutningen misslyckas kan broarna som du fick vara ur funktion. Använd "
"någon av [metoderna för att hämta fler broar](../getting-bridges) och försök "
"igen."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/using-bridges/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/using-bridges/
msgid "If you're starting Tor Browser for the first time:"
msgstr "Om du startar Tor Browser för första gången:"

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/using-bridges/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/using-bridges/
msgid ""
"In the \"Bridges\" section, from the option \"Enter bridge addresses you "
"already know\" click on \"Add new bridges\" and enter each bridge address on "
"a separate line."
msgstr ""
"Klicka under ”Broar” på ”Lägg till nya broar” vid alternativet ”Ange bro-"
"adresser som du redan känner till” och ange varje bro-adress på en egen rad."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/using-bridges/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/using-bridges/
msgid "Or, if you have Tor Browser running:"
msgstr "Om Tor Browser redan körs:"

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/using-bridges/contents.lr:content.content
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/using-bridges/
msgid ""
"The bridge addresses can be shared using the QR code or by copying the "
"entire address."
msgstr ""
"Bro-adresser kan delas med QR-koden eller genom att hela adressen kopieras."

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/using-bridges/contents.lr:figure.text
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/using-bridges/
msgid "Bridge QR code"
msgstr "Brons QR-kod"

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/using-bridges/contents.lr:figure.text
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/using-bridges/
msgid "Bridge-moji"
msgstr "Bro-emoji"

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/using-bridges/contents.lr:figure.text
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/using-bridges/
msgid "Enter bridge addresses manually"
msgstr "Ange bro-adresser manuellt"

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/using-bridges/contents.lr:figure.text
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/using-bridges/
msgid "Provide a bridge on Tor Browser for Android"
msgstr "Ange en bro i Tor Browser för Android"

#: content/tor-browser/circumvention/using-bridges/contents.lr:figure.text
#: https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/circumvention/using-bridges/
msgid "Provide bridge addresses on Tor Browser for Android"
msgstr "Ange bro-adresser i Tor Browser för Android"

